      "description": "The Visiting PhD Fellowship gives registered doctoral students a three-month placement at UNU-WIDER in Helsinki to use the institute's resources and facilities for their PhD dissertation or thesis research on developing economies. Fellows prepare one or more research papers and present a seminar on their findings, and may have the opportunity to publish in the WIDER Working Paper Series. UNU-WIDER provides a return travel grant, medical insurance for the stay, and a monthly stipend of EUR 2,100 to cover living expenses during the fellowship period in Helsinki.",
