        "official_details": {
          "description": "The United Nations University World Institute for Development Economics Research (UNU-WIDER), together with the National Treasury of South Africa, is requesting research proposals under the third phase of the Southern Africa - Towards Inclusive Economic Development (SA-TIED) programme. The call invites South Africa-based and international researchers to submit proposals to conduct research primarily, but not exclusively, using the South African tax administrative data. Papers generated will be published as part of the workstreams on public revenue mobilisation for inclusive development and on poverty, inequality, and labour markets.",
          "purpose": [
            "Investigate the determinants of revenue collection in South Africa and the effects of the tax structure on economic growth and inequality",
            "Examine how people and firms respond to tax policy design and tax administration processes",
            "Address inclusivity of South Africa's growth path and policy options to promote inclusive growth",
            "Explore individual and structural constraints on self-employment and informal sector activity",
            "Assess the Social Relief of Distress grant as a potential platform into productive livelihoods",
            "Examine asset inequality, infrastructure as redistribution, and immigration in the South African labour market",
            "Produce policy-relevant recommendations that can be taken forward in a further phase of work"
