          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "U.S. citizens only. Applicants must reside/study at a U.S. institution and may not study in an overseas destination of which they are a citizen.",
          "international_eligibility": "No permanent residents or international students are eligible for the Boren Scholarships; the application eligibility section states only U.S. citizens are eligible. ROTC cadets, midshipmen and members of the military Reserves or National Guard may apply if in inactive, non-drilling status. Veterans of the U.S. armed forces are encouraged to apply and receive selection preference when other factors are equivalent.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "Boren Scholarships applicants must be matriculated in an associate's or bachelor's degree program located within the United States and accredited by a body recognized by the U.S. Department of Education at the time of application",
              "They must remain matriculated in an undergraduate degree program for the duration of the scholarship and may not graduate until the scholarship is complete",
              "Only undergraduate STEM majors may propose summer-only awards of 8 weeks or more, at $8,000",
              "Essay 2 (Motivation and Public Service Careers) has a maximum length of 800 words",
              "Two letters of recommendation are required, with a third optional",
