            "phd": [
              "Eligible doctoral programs include PhD, MD and others",
              "Boren Fellows must be matriculated in a graduate degree program by the start date of the fellowship and may not graduate until the fellowship is complete",
              "Boren Fellows are encouraged to conduct research related to graduate theses or dissertations while abroad",
              "At least one of the three letters of recommendation should be from a research advisor at the U.S. institution if a research component is proposed",
              "Boren Fellows with sufficiently advanced skills in the target language may be able to conduct research, internships and other classroom study in that language",
              "The language component is the only required element of a Boren Fellowship proposal; research is additive, not mandatory"
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "Boren Scholars and Fellows must remain matriculated in a degree program at a U.S. post-secondary institution for the duration of their Boren Awards-funded program",
            "To prove matriculation, grantees will be required to submit a signed matriculation form, or may submit a letter from a dean or registrar at their home institution stating that their graduation date will occur after the completion of their Boren Scholarship or Fellowship",
            "The applicant remains in the same overseas destination for the full program; if the program sponsor or overseas institution differs between terms, the applicant is expected to remain in the same overseas destination",
            "If selected, all overseas program proposals are reviewed and approved by the Boren Program Advisor to ensure the program meets Boren Award requirements and is in compliance with Executive Orders; the applicant may be asked to adjust overseas plans, including the number of weekly language hours, internship(s) and/or research performed",
            "Short mid-program trips out of the overseas destination of study are allowed but need to be pre-approved by IIE"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "All Boren Awards-funded programs must include language study within a classroom as a core element for the duration of the grant",
            "The Boren Awards requires that overseas programs contain at least 15-20 weekly language hours",
            "Applicants must complete the Eligibility Determination section to unlock the rest of the application",
            "Two letters of recommendation for Boren Scholarships (a third optional); three for Boren Fellowships",
            "At least one Boren Fellowship letter of recommendation should be from a research advisor at the U.S. institution if proposing research",
            "Essay 1 (National Security): maximum 800 words, single-spaced, written for an educated generalist audience",
            "Essay 2 (Motivation and Public Service Careers): maximum 800 words (Scholarships) or 1000 words (Fellowships), single-spaced",
            "Study Plan Summary: maximum 250 words per programme segment, plus alternate-destination programme descriptions",
            "Weekly contact hours of formal language acquisition must be entered (minimum 15-20)",
            "An alternate study abroad program is required for asterisked (blue) destinations or for Arabic, Mandarin and Russian",
            "Applicants must agree to the policies in the Submission Agreement section in order to actually submit",
            "Boren Scholars must comply with the Fly America Act for Boren-funded airfare and send a photocopy of the passenger receipt page(s) to their airline",
            "The application saves automatically; you can change responses at any time as long as you have not submitted"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "UNOFFICIAL transcript from the current institution - required in order to submit the application",
            "UNOFFICIAL transcripts from up to two additional institutions where you pursued or obtained a previous degree - must be received before the national deadline",
            "Unofficial transcripts MUST include your name, the name of the institution, titles of the courses, and the grades obtained in each",
            "Study Abroad Program Description - a screenshot or PDF from the program's website, or a scanned program brochure; limit this upload to no more than 5 pages",
            "Two letters of recommendation (third optional) for Boren Scholarships; three for Boren Fellowships, submitted by recommenders through the online system",
            "Optional Language Proficiency Evaluation completed by a language instructor, which does not count toward the Letters of Recommendation requirement",
            "Optional letter of affiliation (Boren Fellowship applicants only)"
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "Transcripts must be UNOFFICIAL. Unofficial transcripts MUST include your name, the name of the institution, titles of the courses, and the grades obtained in each.",
            "Transcripts that include sensitive personal identifying information (PII) such as your social security number or your date of birth are NOT ALLOWED; you must redact the identifying information before uploading your transcript",
            "Study Abroad Program Description: create a screenshot or PDF from the program's website, or scan the program brochure; limit the upload to no more than 5 pages. If you have more than one program, upload all descriptions",
            "Letters of recommendation and language evaluations must be submitted via the online application system. You may not upload recommendation letters or language proficiency forms on behalf of your recommenders.",
            "Recommendations or Language Evaluations from a parent, sibling, or other relative will not be accepted",
            "The recommendation letter will not be visible to you - you will only be able to see whether or not it has been submitted",
            "You must submit an unofficial transcript for your current institution in order to submit your application; transcripts from other listed institutions may be submitted after submitting but MUST be received BEFORE the national application deadline",
            "The language proficiency evaluation, if completed, should be assessed using the LinguaFolio Self-Assessment guide",
            "No file-size limit and no accepted file-type list are published on the application instructions pages read; these fields are therefore left unspecified rather than guessed"
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Boren Scholarships criterion 1: Does the applicant provide a clear and compelling explanation of the significance of their overseas destination, region, language, field of study, and overseas study to U.S. national security? Priority organizations (Tier One) are the Departments of War, State, and Homeland Security, as well as the Intelligence Community.",
            "Boren Scholarships criterion 2: Does the applicant demonstrate an understanding of how they might fulfill the one-year federal service requirement and a longer-term commitment to the federal government? Consider the leadership potential the applicant would bring to the federal government.",
            "Boren Scholarships criterion 3: Does the applicant demonstrate a serious commitment to language study, before, during, and after their overseas study? The Boren Awards require a minimum of 15-20 contact hours per week. Does the applicant have realistic expectations for the proficiency level obtainable abroad?",
            "Boren Scholarships criterion 4: Has the applicant proposed a study plan in a preferred overseas destination, region, and language, with a preferred major or field of study, meeting the preferred duration of 25+ weeks? If not, have they made a compelling argument on the basis of U.S. national security?",
            "Boren Scholarships criterion 5: Does the applicant possess the appropriate academic preparation, adaptability, flexibility, and maturity required to succeed abroad?",
            "Boren Fellowships criterion 4 (additional): If proposing research in addition to language study, does the applicant have a comprehensive, clear and feasible overseas plan, with language study being the primary purpose of their overseas plan?",
            "Veteran Preference: Veterans of the U.S. armed forces are encouraged to apply, and selection preference will be given to veterans when other factors are equivalent.",
            "Preference factors: the Boren Awards give preference based on program duration, focus on intensive study of a preferred language in a preferred overseas destination, the applicant's field of study, and applicants with longer-term interest in a federal career."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Applications are evaluated on these criteria by IIE-organized regional merit review panels consisting of faculty members and administrators from colleges and universities across the United States, representing a wide array of fields of study. The regional panels make recommendations for each submitted, eligible application, with final decision-making authority held by the program's federal sponsor, DLNSEO. There is no semi-finalist or interview phase, so everything an applicant would want the selection committee to know should be stated clearly in the essays and other application materials. Applicants are notified if they have been selected in mid-to-late April.",
          "application_method": [
            "Start a new application on the Apply Now page by selecting the overseas location and language you want to study (you may change selections at any time)",
            "Get support from your Boren Awards campus representative and watch the introductory webinar",
            "Choose a programme: apply for a Regional Flagship Language Initiative or select/design your own study programme",
            "Complete the application sections in order (eligibility determination, personal information, academic information, employment history, activities, programme information and budget, essays, language self-assessment, additional information, recommendations, submission agreement, review)",
            "Notify your recommenders through the online system and track their submission status",
            "Click 'Submit Application' on the Review section before the national deadline"
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Create a new application at https://apply.iie.org/borenscholarship (Boren Scholarships) or https://apply.iie.org/borenfellowship (Boren Fellowships)",
            "2. Pass the Eligibility Determination section - you must answer all of these questions to unlock the rest of the application",
            "3. Enter personal information (name, permanent and mailing address, email, telephone, sex as it appears on your birth certificate, birthdate, country of residence, veteran/reservist/active-service status)",
            "4. Enter academic information (academic level, degree type, major, GPA, maximum possible GPA, institution location, dates attended/graduation date) and upload an UNOFFICIAL transcript of the current institution",
            "5. List up to three relevant jobs and up to three relevant activities, 50-100 words each",
            "6. Enter programme information: study abroad city, program sponsor, program name, proposed overseas institution, Study Plan Summary (max 250 words), upload the Study Abroad Program Description (max 5 pages), weekly contact hours of formal language acquisition, and any alternate study abroad program",
            "7. Write and submit Essay 1 (National Security, max 800 words) and Essay 2 (Motivation and Public Service Careers, max 800 words for Scholarships / 1000 words for Fellowships)",
            "8. Complete the Language Self-Assessment for the Boren language plus up to four additional languages",
            "9. Complete Additional Information: up to three overseas countries, up to five honours and awards, optional other scholarships, ROTC participation, how you learned about Boren, prior NSEP participation",
            "10. Add recommenders, select the type (Letter of Recommendation or Language Evaluation), and click 'Send to Recommender'",
            "11. Read and agree to the Submission Agreement policies",
            "12. Review the application, fix any errors flagged, and click 'Submit Application'"
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
