      "english_requirement": null,
      "application_method": [
        "Create a new User ID and Password in the online application system (click 'Create New Account').",
        "Complete all required fields of the online application.",
        "Draft the five essay responses offline in word processing software, spell-check them, and copy and paste into the appropriate areas of the online application.",
        "Request recommendations from three individuals familiar with the applicant's professional and education background and their experience, aptitude or promise relevant to the AEF Programme, entering their names and email addresses on the Request Recommendations page; requests can be made as soon as the application system is accessed, without waiting for the application to be complete.",
        "Confirm that one recommender is a school district official and select the correct Type option (a school headmaster/headmistress or equivalent to a school principal qualifies; choose 'Other' and enter the position title in the Other District Official text box).",
        "Monitor the 'Check Your Status' page to confirm that all three recommendations have been submitted; use the 'Resend Email' button on the Recommendations tab to chase recommenders.",
        "Submit the completed application, including all three letters of recommendation, by 8:00pm Eastern on November 5, 2026.",
        "Check Your Status periodically before the deadline; the applicant is responsible for confirming completeness, as the programme will not tell them what is missing.",
        "If selected as a semi-finalist, travel to Washington, DC on Saturday February 27, 2027, attend orientation on Sunday February 28, and be interviewed Monday March 1 and possibly Tuesday March 2.",
        "Finalists selected for a Congressional office placement return to Washington, DC in mid-June 2027 for a week of placement interviews."
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Applications are first subject to an eligibility and compliance review conducted by the AEF Programme to verify applicant eligibility and ensure all required materials have been provided; only applications meeting all requirements are advanced for merit-based evaluation. Merit review is a thorough, consistent and objective examination by evaluators who must be independent of the applicants and of the sponsoring agencies, applying pre-established criteria in four areas: the applicant's teaching experience, professional accomplishments, demonstrated leadership qualities, and interests as they relate to participating in the AEF Programme. Sponsoring federal agencies then review the highly reviewed applications on overall professional experience and demonstrated leadership qualities, the applicant's interest in and preparedness for the fellowship, alignment of the applicant's experience and subject matter expertise with the interests of the host office, and quality of recommendations, and select the top candidates as semi-finalists to interview in Washington, DC. Semi-finalists are invited to Washington, DC for three days of individual interviews and information sessions. Following interviews, final selections are made at the discretion of the sponsoring federal agencies; finalists are contacted by ORISE regarding offers. DOE selects the finalists for Congressional office placements. Recruitment and selection is done without regard to race, gender, age, colour, religion, national origin, mental or physical disability, or status as a veteran.",
      "notes": "Not deferrable and not renewable: the fellowship is for a single eleven-month period from mid-August with initial programme Orientation, and there is no flexibility in start and end dates. There is no return-home requirement, but relocation to the Washington, DC area is a programme requirement if the Fellow does not already live there. The Fellow cannot maintain a teaching position while serving; a leave of absence must be secured or employment terminated. The AEF Programme does not arrange housing. Fellows receive a monthly stipend and are not considered employees of the hosting office, so they do not earn sick or annual leave, although up to ten personal days and ten sick days are allowed without stipend reduction. All stipends are reportable to the Internal Revenue Service and the AEF Programme does not withhold taxes; fellows may need to file Form 1040-ES and pay estimated income tax. Current and former AEF Fellows are not eligible to apply for a second fellowship. No clinical restriction is published.",
