      "image_alt_text": "Albert Einstein Distinguished Educator Fellowship Program logo",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Albert Einstein Distinguished Educator Fellowship (AEF) Program provides a unique opportunity for accomplished K-12 educators in the fields of science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) to serve in the national education arena. Fellows spend eleven months working in Federal agencies or in U.S. Congressional offices, applying their extensive knowledge and classroom experiences to national education program and/or education policy efforts. At the end of the Fellowship, educators are equipped with access to a national network of education leaders and programs, a better understanding of the challenges and possibilities in STEM education, and a renewed passion for teaching, ready to make significant contributions to the educational community. The Albert Einstein Distinguished Educator Fellowship Act (Fellowship Act Public Law 103-382, Improving America's Schools Act of 1994) was signed into law in November 1994 and gives the DOE the responsibility for managing the program. The DOE Office of Science's Office of Workforce Development for Teachers and Scientists (WDTS) manages this program for DOE in collaboration with the Oak Ridge Institute for Science and Education (ORISE) and other partners.",
          "purpose": [
            "Provide a unique opportunity for accomplished K-12 educators in the fields of science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) to serve in the national education arena.",
            "Allow Fellows to spend eleven months working in Federal agencies or in U.S. Congressional offices, applying their extensive knowledge and classroom experiences to national education program and/or education policy efforts.",
            "Support the intellectual and professional development of K-12 STEM teachers who have the desire to share their education and classroom expertise with Federal agencies and U.S. Congressional offices.",
            "Equip educators with access to a national network of education leaders and programs, a better understanding of the challenges and possibilities in STEM education, and a renewed passion for teaching.",
            "Advance national K-12 STEM education through contributions to programme design, legislation and policy, federal agency partnerships, web-based science education tools, and evaluation of national and regional school reform and teacher preparation programmes.",
            "Inspire the next generation of scientific and technological leaders by strengthening K-12 STEM teaching."
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [],
          "degree_levels": [
            "Not a degree programme; the fellowship is an eleven-month professional appointment for K-12 STEM educators and school district officials"
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Full-time eleven-month appointment in a Federal agency or U.S. Congressional office in Washington, DC",
            "Education policy and/or programme related activities"
          ],
          "degree_award": "Short-term award. No degree is awarded; this is an eleven-month professional fellowship and appointment.",
          "duration": "Eleven months, mid-August through mid-July. The fellowship begins on the third Monday in August with the initial programme Orientation.",
          "application_cycle": "Annual. For the 2027-2028 programme the online application opened August 3, 2026 and closed 8:00pm Eastern on November 5, 2026. The application period typically opens in mid-August, with applications due in mid-November.",
          "deadline_central": "2026-11-05",
          "deadline_central_display": "8:00pm Eastern, November 5, 2026",
          "deadline_institutional": "None published. The application is submitted directly by the applicant through the online application system; the applicant's school or district does not submit anything.",
          "deadline_note": "All parts of the online application, including all three letters of recommendation, must be completed before the deadline. Recommendation letters must be submitted through the online application system; WDTS will not accept mailed or emailed recommendation letters. A limited number of personal and professional travel days are allowed, but dates and length of absence from the host office are subject to AEF Programme guidelines and approval by the sponsoring agency and/or host office.",
          "status": "OPEN",
          "funding_type": "Stipend plus capped travel, education, relocation and health insurance allowances",
          "funding_label": "$8,200 monthly living stipend, plus up to $5,000 travel allowance, up to $1,000 education allowance, up to $3,500 relocation reimbursement, and up to $550/month (individual) or $1,300/month (family) health insurance stipend",
          "funding_amount": 8200,
          "funding_currency": "USD",
          "funding_period": "per month over the eleven-month fellowship",
          "tuition_coverage": null,
          "living_cost_coverage": "A monthly living stipend of $8,200.",
          "travel_coverage": "A travel allowance of up to $5,000 for approved travel requested by the host agency. Limitations on foreign travel will vary by agency. All travel requests must be pre-approved by the AEF Programme prior to making any travel arrangements. The travel allowance is primarily to support travel the host office may require, and Fellows may also use part of it for travel related to their individual Professional Development Plan objectives. Separately, up to $3,500 is reimbursed for relocation inbound and outbound between home and Washington, DC if the distance is more than 50 miles one way.",
          "fully_funded": false,
          "tuition_rule": "Not applicable. The AEF Programme is not a degree programme and no tuition, fees or education costs are involved.",
          "home_tuition_rule": "Not applicable. There is no tuition; the Fellow is on an eleven-month leave of absence from teaching or has terminated employment with their school.",
          "host_institution_fee": null,
          "tax_status": "In general, all stipends paid to the Fellow are reportable to the Internal Revenue Service. The AEF Programme does not withhold taxes from these payments. Fellows will need to consider whether filing Form 1040-ES on a quarterly basis and paying estimated income taxes is necessary in order to avoid late payment penalties. Federal agencies and ORISE cannot give participants tax advice.",
          "covered_expenses": [
            "Monthly living stipend of $8,200.",
            "Up to $5,000 travel allowance for approved travel requested by the host agency.",
            "Up to $1,000 education allowance for approved expenses aligned with the Fellow's individual professional development plan, including courses, conferences, and professional books.",
            "Up to $3,500 reimbursement for moving/relocation expenses for Fellows relocating from outside of the Washington, DC area (distance more than 50 miles one way).",
            "Stipend of up to $550 per month (individual plan) or $1,300 per month (family plan) to offset the cost of health insurance.",
            "Designated office space and agency/office-specific orientation and training.",
            "Official professional development meetings, conferences and field trips organised for Fellows by the AEF Programme.",
            "Mentoring and guidance from AEF Programme staff in developing the individual Professional Development Plan."
          ],
          "not_covered_or_excluded": [
            "Housing: the AEF Programme does not arrange housing for Fellows; only resources and connections to outgoing Fellows are provided.",
            "No tuition or formal education costs are covered, because the programme is not a degree programme.",
            "Salary or continued employment income from the applicant's school: the Fellow is on leave of absence or has terminated employment, and Fellows receive a monthly stipend rather than an employee salary.",
            "Sick and annual leave: Fellows are not employees of the hosting office and do not 'earn' sick or annual leave, though up to ten personal days and up to ten sick days are allowed per year without stipend reduction.",
            "Any travel not pre-approved by the AEF Programme, and any travel beyond the $5,000 allowance or the agency-specific foreign travel limitations.",
            "Any professional development expense beyond the $1,000 education allowance.",
            "Relocation costs for a distance of 50 miles one way or less, and relocation costs beyond the $3,500 cap.",
            "Health insurance costs beyond the $550/month individual or $1,300/month family stipend, including any cost of coverage obtained through the ORISE health insurance plan.",
            "Spouse, partner or dependent employment or schooling costs; family relocation is an individual decision and only capped relocation costs are reimbursed.",
            "Tax liability: the programme does not withhold taxes, so fellows bear their own estimated tax payments and any penalties."
          ],
          "benefits": [
            "Develops a professional development plan to guide individual professional development objectives outside their host office responsibilities with ongoing mentoring provided by the AEF Program.",
            "Receives professional development opportunities throughout the year, including opportunities for Fellows to interact with various organizations, associations and experts who focus on STEM education.",
            "Has designated office space and agency/office-specific orientation and training.",
            "Access to a national network of education leaders and programs at the end of the Fellowship.",
            "Up to ten personal days off per year and up to ten sick days off without reduction in the Fellow's stipend.",
            "Placement in a Federal agency or U.S. Congressional office, with DOE sponsoring up to five placements in congressional offices.",
            "Current sponsoring agencies include the Department of War (DOW), the Department of Energy (DOE), the Library of Congress (LOC), and the U.S. Geological Survey (USGS)."
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Be a U.S. citizen at the time of applying (by the November 5, 2026 application deadline).",
            "Have a minimum of five complete years of full-time classroom teaching experience prior to submitting the application; student teaching does not count toward this minimum full-time teaching requirement.",
            "Have been teaching full-time in a public or private elementary or secondary school for at least five of the last seven years in a science, technology, engineering, or mathematics (STEM) discipline; current employment may be as an educator or district official.",
            "Be currently employed full-time in a public or private elementary or secondary school or school district in the U.S.",
            "Be able to provide a letter of recommendation from a school district official as one of their three required letters of recommendation.",
            "Be able to obtain a leave of absence from teaching in order to participate in the program for the full eleven months.",
            "Applicants must meet all eligibility criteria and submit an application comprised of all required materials by the application deadline."
          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "U.S. citizenship at the time of applying is mandatory.",
            "Five complete years of full-time classroom teaching experience is required prior to submitting the application, and at least five of the last seven years must have been spent teaching STEM full-time in a U.S. public or private elementary or secondary school.",
            "Current full-time employment in a U.S. public or private elementary or secondary school or school district is required; a full-time academic coach at a high school meets this requirement.",
            "The applicant must be able to secure an eleven-month leave of absence, or be prepared to terminate employment.",
            "Relocation to the Washington, DC area is required to fulfil the eleven-month host office appointment and the professional development sessions."
          ],
          "ineligibility_conditions": [
            "Applicants who are not U.S. citizens at the time of applying; permanent resident aliens who expect to obtain citizenship before the fellowship year are not eligible.",
            "Applicants who have not completed five years of full-time classroom teaching by November 5, 2026; student teaching experience does not count toward this requirement.",
            "Applicants whose STEM teaching does not total at least five of the last seven years.",
            "Applicants whose assistant teaching experience is offered in place of full-time classroom teaching; student teaching or assistant teaching does not qualify toward the required five years of full-time classroom teaching experience.",
            "Applicants not currently employed full-time in a U.S. public or private elementary or secondary school or school district, including those teaching outside the country in the current year.",
            "Current and former AEF Program Fellows, who are not eligible to apply for a second fellowship, including applicants who served as a Fellow in a federal agency ten years ago and want a congressional office placement.",
            "Eligible individuals who have already applied three times within a six year period; eligible individuals may apply a maximum of three times within a six year period.",
            "Applicants whose three recommendation letters do not include one from a school district official; department chairs, assistant principals, associate principals and vice-principals do not qualify as school district officials.",
            "Applicants who cannot participate for the entire eleven-month period in Washington, DC.",
            "Incomplete applications or applications missing any required material; only complete applications submitted by the deadline will be considered, and the uploaded materials provide the sole basis for evaluation."
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "U.S. citizenship is required at the time of applying (by the November 5, 2026 deadline). Applicants must currently be employed full-time in a U.S. public or private elementary or secondary school or school district. Teaching experience outside the United States counts toward the five-year total but does not satisfy the current-employment requirement.",
          "international_eligibility": "None. The programme is restricted to U.S. citizens currently employed in U.S. K-12 schools or school districts. Non-U.S. citizens, including permanent resident aliens who have not yet naturalised, are not eligible.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "Not applicable; the programme is not open to undergraduates."
            ],
            "masters": [
              "Not applicable; the programme is not open to master's students. Education background (formal education and continuing education) is a required application field, but the applicant must be an employed K-12 educator, not a graduate student."
            ],
            "phd": [
              "Not applicable; the programme is not open to doctoral students."
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "The applicant must be able to obtain a leave of absence from teaching for the full eleven months; it is not possible to maintain a teaching position while serving as a Fellow.",
            "The Fellow must relocate to the Washington, DC area if they do not currently reside there, in order to fulfil the eleven-month host office appointment and attend professional development sessions.",
            "The applicant must provide a letter of recommendation from a school district official; at an independent school with no district structure, a headmaster/headmistress or equivalent senior executive qualifies, with the position title entered in the Other District Official text box.",
            "The applicant must be currently employed full-time in a U.S. public or private elementary or secondary school or school district; the host employer does not submit the application."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "All applications must be completed online through the online application system; the Check Your Status page keeps applicants informed on application status before and after submission.",
            "Applicants must meet all eligibility requirements.",
            "All applications, including recommendations, are due by the specified application deadline; only complete applications submitted by the deadline will be considered for evaluation and placement.",
            "Materials uploaded into the application system provide the sole basis for evaluation.",
            "Complete all required fields: Contact Information; Education Background (formal education and continuing education); Teaching and Professional Experience; Professional Awards and Recognition; Citizenship Status; Interest in Federal Agency and/or Congressional Office Placement; and Five Essay Questions.",
            "Submit three letters of recommendation online, including one recommendation letter from a school district official.",
            "School district officials do NOT include department chairs, assistant principals, associate principals, or vice-principals.",
            "Applicants must ensure their recommenders have the information for accessing the online Recommender form; recommendation requests can only be sent electronically through the online application system.",
            "Request letters from three individuals familiar with the applicant's professional and education background and their experience, aptitude, or promise relevant to the AEF Program.",
            "All letters of recommendation must be submitted through the online application system by the application deadline; WDTS will not accept mailed or emailed recommendation letters.",
            "Recommendation requests may be made as soon as the applicant accesses the application system; they do not need to wait until the application is complete.",
            "It is the applicant's responsibility to inform recommenders that they must submit their recommendation letters using the online system before the application deadline, and to allow adequate time for them to act.",
            "Essay responses must be provided in the online application system; drafting offline and copying in is recommended because the system logs out after 60 minutes of inactivity.",
            "Provide proof of U.S. citizenship upon accepting a Fellowship offer.",
            "Secure a leave of absence from teaching during the Fellowship year.",
            "Complete the eleven-month full-time appointment (mid-August through mid-July) in Washington, DC.",
            "Meet the Terms and Conditions spelled out in the offer letter of appointment, including requirements for ethical conduct, and financial disclosure and conflict-of-interest.",
            "Participate in the official professional development meetings, conferences, field trips, etc., organized for Fellows by the AEF Program.",
            "Have health care coverage during the Fellowship appointment; Fellows are eligible to participate in the ORISE health insurance plan if they do not have other health insurance coverage.",
            "Establish an individual Professional Development Plan for the year, which must be completed by early October.",
            "Submit the requested written reports, presentations, and surveys related to the Fellowship experience before the published deadlines.",
            "Represent themselves as educators in a responsible and professional manner.",
            "Only use the AEF Program name or the Fellow's affiliation with the AEF Program in an authorized manner.",
            "Give priority to the duties assigned by the host office in managing fellowship responsibilities.",
            "Comply with all legal and ethical requirements subject to the individual appointment; DOE-sponsored Fellows are subject to ORISE ethics guidance.",
            "DOE employees must comply with 10 CFR Part 1010 and the Standards of Ethical Conduct for Employees of the Executive Branch at 5 CFR Part 2635; other sponsoring agencies and host offices must comply with analogous regulations."
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Completed online application with all required fields: contact information; education background (formal education and continuing education); teaching and professional experience; professional awards and recognition; citizenship status; interest in Federal Agency and/or Congressional Office placement.",
            "Responses to five essay questions.",
            "Three letters of recommendation submitted through the online application system, including one from a school district official.",
            "Proof of U.S. citizenship, required upon accepting a Fellowship offer."
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "All applications and all letters of recommendation must be completed and submitted through the online application system; mailed and emailed recommendation letters are not accepted.",
            "No file format, size limit, font or page-count requirement for the essays is published; essay responses are typed into fields in the online application system.",
            "The online application has a 60-minute time-out: if a page is not completed and saved within 60 minutes the system requires the applicant to log in again, so applicants are advised to complete essays offline and copy and paste them in.",
            "Account credentials are case-sensitive; a locked account must be resolved by emailing SC.Einstein@doe.gov.",
            "Recommendation letters are submitted by recommenders through a unique URL sent to them by email; the applicant cannot view the recommendation form or the submitted letter, and a letter once received cannot be removed.",
            "A recommender may be changed before the deadline only if that recommender has not yet submitted a recommendation.",
            "The Request Recommendations page provides six recommender Type options; for personal references such as a parent of a student, select Non-District Non-School Official; for an independent-school senior executive, select Other and enter the position title in the Other District Official text box."
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "The applicant's teaching experience.",
            "Professional accomplishments.",
            "Demonstrated leadership qualities.",
            "Interests as they relate to participating in the AEF Program.",
            "Overall professional experience and demonstrated leadership qualities of the applicant (agency sponsor review).",
            "Applicant's interest in and preparedness for the fellowship (agency sponsor review).",
            "Alignment of the applicant's experience and subject matter expertise with the interests of the host office (agency sponsor review).",
            "Quality of recommendations (agency sponsor review)."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "To be considered, an applicant must meet all eligibility criteria and submit all required materials by the application deadline. An initial eligibility and compliance review is conducted by the AEF Program to verify applicant eligibility and ensure all required materials have been provided; only applications meeting all requirements are advanced for merit-based evaluation and selection, and the materials uploaded and received through the online application system provide the sole basis for evaluation and selection. The merit review is a thorough, consistent and objective examination of eligible applicants based on pre-established criteria; application evaluators must be independent of the applicants and of the sponsoring agencies and must comply with all applicable DOE rules or directives on evaluation and merit review. Applications are evaluated in four areas: teaching experience, professional accomplishments, demonstrated leadership qualities, and interests as they relate to participating in the AEF Program. Following merit review, highly reviewed applications are viewed by the Federal agency sponsors, who evaluate on overall professional experience and demonstrated leadership qualities, interest in and preparedness for the fellowship, alignment of experience and subject matter expertise with host office interests, and quality of recommendations; the sponsors select the top candidates as semi-finalists to interview in Washington, DC. Semi-finalists are invited to Washington, DC for three days for individual interviews and information sessions with one or more sponsoring agencies and/or host offices. Following the semi-finalist interviews, final selections are made at the discretion of the sponsoring Federal agencies; finalists are contacted by ORISE regarding offers from the Federal agencies. DOE selects the finalists for Congressional office placements, who return to Washington, DC in the June-July timeframe for placement interviews with Congressional host offices. The number of Fellowships awarded is contingent upon the availability of funds by the sponsoring agencies; in recent years the program has awarded between ten and twenty Fellowships a year. Recruitment and selection of participants is done without regard to race, gender, age, color, religion, national origin, mental or physical disability, or status as a veteran.",
          "application_method": [
            "Create a new User ID and Password in the online application system.",
            "Complete all required fields of the online application.",
            "Draft the five essay responses offline in word processing software, spell-check them, and copy and paste into the online application.",
            "Request recommendations from three individuals through the Request Recommendations tab, entering names and email addresses; correct Type options for each recommender.",
            "Monitor the Check Your Status page and use the Resend Email button to chase outstanding recommenders.",
            "Submit the application and all three letters of recommendation by 8:00pm Eastern on November 5, 2026.",
            "Check Your Status periodically before the deadline, since the programme will not notify applicants of missing components.",
            "If selected as a semi-finalist, travel to Washington, DC on Saturday February 27, 2027; orientation Sunday February 28; interviews Monday March 1 and possibly Tuesday March 2.",
            "If selected as a finalist, respond promptly to the email and phone call from ORISE, as offers are made from March and candidates have limited time to decide.",
            "If selected for a Congressional office placement, return to Washington, DC for one week in June 2027 for placement interviews."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "Create a new User ID and Password in the online application system (click 'Create New Account').",
            "Complete all required fields: contact information; education background (formal education and continuing education); teaching and professional experience; professional awards and recognition; citizenship status; interest in Federal Agency and/or Congressional Office Placement.",
            "Write the five essay responses offline, spell-check them, and paste them into the online application (the system times out after 60 minutes of inactivity).",
            "On the Request Recommendations tab, request three recommendations from individuals familiar with the applicant's professional and education background and their experience, aptitude, or promise relevant to the AEF Program.",
            "Ensure at least one request is to a school district official (school principal, district superintendent, deputy or assistant superintendent, or district board of education member, or equivalent); department chairs, assistant principals, associate principals and vice-principals do not qualify. At an independent school, select 'Other' and enter the equivalent position title.",
            "For personal references such as a parent of a student, select 'Non-District Non-School Official' from the Type drop-down.",
            "Recommendation requests may be sent as soon as the application system is accessed, before the application is complete; recommenders receive an email with instructions and a unique URL.",
            "Check the Check Your Status page regularly to confirm all three recommendations have been submitted and that the application is complete; resend reminder emails where needed.",
            "Submit the application by 8:00pm Eastern on November 5, 2026. Only complete applications, including all three letters of recommendation, submitted by the deadline are considered.",
            "Application is kept on record for the current year only; there is no carry-over to the following year, and a maximum of three applications within a six year period is allowed.",
            "If selected as a semi-finalist: travel to Washington, DC on February 27, 2027, attend orientation on February 28, and be interviewed on March 1 and possibly March 2.",
            "If selected as a finalist: respond to the offer from ORISE promptly; if selected for a Congressional office placement, return to Washington, DC for one week in mid-June 2027 for placement interviews."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits the application personally through the online application system; no institutional submission route exists.",
            "Recommendation letters are submitted electronically by the recommenders through a unique URL provided by the online application system; WDTS will not accept mailed or emailed recommendation letters.",
            "The applicant's school or district does not submit or certify the application, though a leave of absence must be secured from the employer."
          ],
