      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Chevening ASEAN Scholarship is the ASEAN variant of the UK government-funded Chevening Scholarship programme. Applicants from ASEAN member states or Timor-Leste apply through the standard Chevening Scholarship process and, on top of all standard Chevening benefits, are considered for an enhanced UK programme of exclusive events, priority invitations, the ASEAN Chevening Conference and access to the global Chevening alumni community. Chevening states the scholarship is fully funded, covering a one-year UK master's degree; the highest-ranking applicant(s) from each participating country are considered for the ASEAN element. Chevening does not publish the monthly stipend figure on its public pages - the amount is stated in the applicant's Final Award Letter.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Citizens or residents of an ASEAN member state or Timor-Leste who hold an undergraduate degree qualifying them for a UK master's programme, have at least two years (2,800 hours) of post-degree work experience, can commit to returning home for at least two years, and can apply to three different eligible UK taught master's courses. Opting in for the ASEAN element does not affect your chances of a standard Chevening Scholarship.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Must be a citizen of a Chevening-eligible country or territory (ASEAN member state or Timor-Leste for the ASEAN element), with an undergraduate degree, two years' work experience, three eligible UK master's course choices and a commitment to return home for two years.",
      "eligibility": [
