      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Chevening SIDS Scholarship is the Small Island Developing State variant of the UK government-funded Chevening Scholarship programme. Applicants from Commonwealth SIDS apply through the standard Chevening Scholarship process and must study on courses that address a national development priority or capacity shortage - human rights, democracy and the rule of law; climate change and sustainability; economic recovery and growth; or supportive societies that help people lead peaceful and productive lives. On top of standard Chevening benefits, SIDS scholars receive an enhanced UK programme of exclusive events, an FCDO welcome event where they network with SIDS scholars from the Commonwealth Scholarships Commission and FCDO officials, and eligibility for Chevening Alumni Programme Fund support. Chevening publishes no stipend figure on its public pages; the amount is stated in the applicant's Final Award Letter.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Citizens or residents of a participating Commonwealth Small Island Developing State who hold an undergraduate degree qualifying them for a UK master's programme, have at least two years (2,800 hours) of post-degree work experience, can commit to returning home for at least two years, and can choose three eligible UK taught master's courses relevant to a national development priority or capacity shortage. Opting in for the SIDS element does not affect your chances of a standard Chevening Scholarship.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
