        "Student visa application fee and Immigration Health Surcharge ('you don't need to pay the visa fee or the Immigration Health Surcharge')",
        "Arrival allowance where confirmed in the Final Award Letter",
        "Departure allowance for scholars on a full award",
        "A travel grant"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "SIDS element: exclusive events - 'A series of exclusive events and opportunities designed to enhance your experience in the UK.'",
        "SIDS element: exclusive networking opportunities - an invitation to a welcome event at the Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO), where you network with SIDS scholars from the Commonwealth Scholarships Commission and with FCDO officials.",
        "SIDS element: membership of the global Chevening alumni community after graduation, and eligibility to apply for funding from the Chevening Alumni Programme Fund, which supports regional projects and events led by alumni.",
        "SIDS element: possible invitation to speak or participate in UK-SIDS workshops and events in your area of expertise.",
        "Standard Chevening Scholarship benefits for all Chevening scholars"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Applications must be submitted through the Chevening online application system reached from your own country/territory page.",
        "Opt in to be considered for the Chevening SIDS Scholarship within the standard Chevening Scholarship application.",
        "Choose three different eligible UK master's degree courses in order of preference; duplicate courses at the same university cannot be considered.",
        "Courses must be full-time, taught master's courses (not research-focused MRes programmes), based in the UK, starting in the autumn term (usually September/October) and lasting nine to twelve months.",
        "Courses cannot be part-time, distance learning, a PhD or DPhil, or include more than one month of study outside the UK.",
        "Provide the names and contact details of two referees in the application.",
        "If shortlisted, upload two reference letters and your undergraduate degree certificate to the online application system no later than seven working days before your interview.",
        "If successful at interview, submit at least one unconditional UK university offer by 17:00 BST on 8 July 2027.",
        "Apply for your own student visa; Chevening cannot apply on your behalf."
      ],
      "english_requirement": "The application form must be completed in English: 'If the application form is not completed in English, it will be deemed ineligible.' Chevening also publishes that 'Though an English test score is not required for Chevening, strong English skills are necessary to write a successful application, conduct the interview, and apply to a UK university.' Reference letters must be in English. Separately, UK university applications 'typically requiring: A letter of motivation or personal statement. English language test results. Proof of previous qualifications. Academic and professional references.'",
      "application_method": [
        "Check your eligibility against Chevening's published eligibility criteria and confirm your country is a participating SIDS country.",
        "Read the Chevening application criteria and preparation guidance.",
        "Research and choose three different eligible UK master's courses using the Chevening course finder, making sure they relate to a national development priority or capacity shortage.",
        "Register via the 'apply today' link on your country/territory page on chevening.org, read and consent to the terms and conditions and Privacy Notice, then register your email address and mobile phone number.",
        "Pass the online eligibility checker (you get four more attempts if you fail but believe it was an error).",
        "Note and keep your unique access code.",
        "Complete each application section: personal details, immigration details, education history (up to 15 entries), work history (up to 15 entries), programmes of study (three UK master's choices), and the essay answers.",
        "Opt in to be considered for the Chevening SIDS Scholarship.",
        "Submit; sift against eligibility criteria runs from October 2026.",
        "If shortlisted, upload two reference letters and your undergraduate degree certificate at least seven working days before your interview.",
        "Attend your interview at a British embassy or high commission, March to April 2027.",
        "If successful, secure and upload an unconditional offer by 17:00 BST on 8 July 2027."
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Applications are sifted against the eligibility criteria from October 2026, then independent reading committees assess all eligible applications from mid-October 2026 to January 2027. British embassies and high commissions produce shortlists and interview candidates in March to April 2027; results are announced from mid-June 2027. Applicants are assessed on leadership and influencing skills, the ability to build professional relationships to achieve positive outcomes, the reasons for the course and university choice (linked to UK priorities such as promoting growth and prosperity, building climate resilience, strengthening security and stability, and supporting development for more inclusive and effective societies), and a realistic short, mid and long-term career plan. Chevening states: 'The use of AI software to generate answers in Chevening applications is strictly prohibited.' The official page does not publish a separate SIDS selection weighting, so the SIDS element appears to be applied alongside the standard Chevening assessment.",
      "notes": "Applicants must commit to returning to their home country (country of award) for at least two years after the scholarship ends. SIDS scholars must study on a course addressing a national development priority or capacity shortage. The award is a one-year master's degree; Chevening publishes no deferral or renewal provisions. Reference letters must be uploaded at least seven working days before the interview - 'Failure to do so will result in your application no longer being considered for a Chevening award.' Applicants must not have previously studied in the UK on a UK government-funded scholarship. No clinical or medical restriction is published.",
      "image_url": "https://www.chevening.org/wp-content/themes/chevening/assets/images/logo.png",
      "image_source_url": "https://www.chevening.org/sids-chevening-scholarship/",
      "image_source_type": "official_government",
      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
      "image_alt_text": "Chevening logo",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Chevening SIDS Scholarship is an opportunity for outstanding individuals from Small Island Developing States (SIDS) to pursue a one-year master's degree in the UK. 'As part of the prestigious Chevening Scholarship programme, SIDS applicants can apply for all the standard benefits, with the additional opportunity to be considered for the Chevening SIDS Scholarship.' Applicants are required to study on courses that help to address a national development priority or capacity shortage. In addition to the standard benefits of a Chevening Scholarship, the scheme includes an enhanced UK programme of exclusive events, exclusive networking opportunities including an FCDO welcome event, and membership of the global Chevening alumni community with eligibility for Chevening Alumni Programme Fund support.",
          "purpose": [
            "Enable outstanding individuals from Small Island Developing States to pursue a one-year master's degree in the UK.",
            "Direct study choices towards national development priorities and capacity shortages in SIDS, in the areas Chevening names: human rights, democracy and the rule of law; climate change and sustainability; economic recovery and growth; supportive societies that help people lead peaceful and productive lives.",
            "Build exclusive networking between SIDS Chevening scholars, Commonwealth Scholarships Commission SIDS scholars and FCDO officials through an FCDO welcome event.",
            "Sustain SIDS alumni engagement through Chevening Alumni Programme Fund support and invitations to UK-SIDS workshops and events."
