      "description": "The Chevening Europe Defence and Security Fellowship is funded by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office and delivered by Cranfield University at the Defence Academy of the United Kingdom, Shrivenham. It is a six-week applied programme for mid-career professionals from non-ODA eligible European countries who have leadership responsibilities for national or international security. Fellows study six integrated themes - global leadership in an era of complexity; people, culture and organisations; cyber resilience; AI, governance and emerging technology; decision-making under pressure; and resilience and future leadership - complete a research project, and present their findings to the FCDO in London. The award covers full programme fees, living expenses for the duration including pre-arranged accommodation, and return economy airfare; the stipend figure is not published and is confirmed in the Final Award Letter.",
      "program_type": "Government fellowship",
      "best_fit": "Mid-career professionals who are citizens AND residents of one of the 35 listed European countries, hold a postgraduate qualification or equivalent professional training, have at least five years' relevant professional experience (7,200 hours) in defence, security, government, diplomacy, policing, intelligence, civil protection, resilience, academia, media, energy/infrastructure or international organisations, and can show leadership potential and a commitment to applying what they learn on return.",
      "funding_amount": null,
