      "selection_notes": "Chevening publishes the four general Fellowship objectives - supporting mid-career professionals in positions of leadership and influence, offering dynamic training/professional development/research relevant to professional interests and UK international strategic priorities, increasing the breadth and diversity of Chevening awards, and supporting FCDO foreign policy priorities by creating lasting relationships with future leaders, influencers and decision-makers. For this programme the assessment is against the general Chevening Fellowship criteria plus the published programme-specific requirements, and against the needs of a cohort drawn from the listed European countries. Chevening Fellowships are 'an important element of Britain's public diplomacy effort', and fellows are active in their field or subject. Chevening does not publish a separate scoring framework or interview format for this programme; applications for Chevening Scholarships follow the published sifting, reading committee, embassy shortlist and interview stages, while Chevening states that 'Application timelines for Chevening Fellowships vary.'",
      "notes": "Deferral: 'Applications to defer awards will only be granted in the case of pregnancy.' Extensions: 'Extensions to the original fellowship duration may be permitted in exceptional circumstances, but the total duration must not exceed 12 months. All extensions are subject to the availability of funds and assessed on a case-by-case basis. Extensions are not automatic and should not be assumed.' Return home: 'You are expected to return to your home country for at least one year on completion of your fellowship.' Dependants: 'All Chevening Awards are calculated to support fellow costs only. There are no financial or welfare provisions for dependants of Chevening Fellows. It is strongly advised that Fellows do not bring dependants to the UK', and 'The Chevening Programme will not endorse the visa applications of, nor provide travel for, dependants.' Other conditions: no transfer to any course other than that confirmed in the Final Award Letter; no other publicly funded award during the fellowship period; approval required before any part-time employment or internship outside the approved programme; cannot serve as an official government representative during the fellowship; must not be outside the UK for more than 30 days in total (pro-rata: 3-month tenure up to 7 days outside the UK), and absences without prior notice may suspend the stipend or end the award; must cite Chevening Fellowships in publications; breach may result in withdrawal of the award. Stipend suspension may occur if fellowship terms and conditions are not complied with, if compulsory documentation is not returned, or if the Fellow elects to return home early and submit work from overseas.",
