          "description": "The Chevening Europe Defence and Security Fellowship is funded by the UK Foreign, Commonwealth and Development Office (FCDO) and delivered by Cranfield University at the Defence Academy of the United Kingdom, Shrivenham. It is open to all non-ODA eligible European countries and is designed for mid-career professionals from across Europe who have demonstrated leadership potential in security and defence. Through six weeks of teaching, discussion, practical exercises, site visits, individual research, and collaborative learning, fellows develop practical insight into leadership, organisational resilience, governance, strategic decision-making, cyber resilience, artificial intelligence, and international collaboration. Throughout the programme fellows work on a research project addressing a relevant policy, leadership, organisational, or security challenge, receive academic support, and present their findings to the FCDO in London at the end of the fellowship.",
