            "Programme-specific: demonstrated leadership potential and a commitment to applying the knowledge and networks gained through the fellowship on completion.",
            "The published route into relevant sectors is illustrative, not exhaustive: military personnel and civilian defence staff; government officials, diplomats and international relationship managers; HR, people and organisational development professionals; leaders and managers in defence and security institutions; police, intelligence and emergency planning professionals; cybersecurity, technology and information specialists; energy, infrastructure and supply chain professionals; journalists, researchers and academics; professionals in international organisations and civil society; local authority staff; policy makers and policy advisers. 'The Fellowship welcomes applicants from any field with a connection to defence or security and the ambition to put what they learn into practice.'"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Chevening publishes that 'Application timelines for Chevening Fellowships vary' and does not publish a programme-specific scoring framework, shortlisting route or interview format for this fellowship. The Scholarship scheme's published stages (eligibility sift, reading committee assessment, embassy or high commission shortlist and interview, mid-June results) are published for Chevening Scholarships only and are not asserted here for this fellowship. Applications for the Europe Defence and Security Fellowship close at 11:00 (UTC) on 12 October 2026, earlier than the Chevening Scholarship deadline of 6 October 2026 published on the Chevening Scholarship timeline.",
