      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Pierre Elliott Trudeau Foundation PhD Scholarship is a three-year doctoral award for students with an outstanding academic record whose humanities and social sciences research aligns with at least one of the Foundation's four themes. It provides an annual stipend of up to $50,000 for three years to cover tuition and living expenses related to doctoral studies, plus an annual allowance of up to $20,000 for three years for research and travel. The application period for the 2027 competition runs from September 1 to November 6, 2026, so the competition is open on 2026-10-01. Scholars also gain membership in a multidisciplinary community of Scholars, Fellows and Mentors and structured mentorship programming.",
      "program_type": "Foundation scholarship",
      "best_fit": "First- or second-year PhD students in the humanities and social sciences whose research maps onto one of the Foundation's four themes (Human Rights and Dignity; Responsible Citizenship; Canada and the World; People and their Natural Environment), who already have an outstanding academic record and who want mentorship and a non-academic network alongside funding.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Doctoral students in the first or second year of a PhD at the time of application whose research is broadly humanities/social sciences and aligns with at least one of the Foundation's four themes, who are either a Canadian student enrolled at a Canadian university, a Canadian student enrolled at a university outside Canada, or an international student enrolled at a Canadian university.",
      "eligibility": [
        "At the time of application the applicant must be in the first year or the second year of a PhD program.",
