        "Receive a confirmation email acknowledging submission once your application is received."
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Applications are assessed on academic excellence, the clear alignment of the research project with the Foundation's mission and four founding themes, the rigour of the research proposal, and the ability to share knowledge for the benefit of society. Only applications meeting the programme's eligibility criteria are assessed. Applicants who pass review are notified by email; all other applicants are informed at the end of the application review period. Applicants shortlisted in the selection process are invited to group meetings and individual interviews, conducted in French or English depending on the applicant's preference. Final decisions are approved by the Board of Directors. The application form is removed from the portal once the competition ends; the confirmation email is the only proof of receipt.",
      "notes": "The Scholarship is a three-year program. It is not deferrable in the sense that the value is adjusted: Scholars may accept other awards, but the value of the Trudeau Scholarship is adjusted based on amounts received from other organizations, institutions or universities, and all additional sources of income must be declared annually. Regardless of other funding, every Scholar receives the full annual $20,000 research, travel and networking allowance and a minimum of $25,000 from the annual stipend. For Scholars studying outside Canada who receive external funding in foreign currency, the Foundation converts that amount into Canadian dollars; the location of study does not affect the Scholarship amount. Scholars may work part-time (up to 20 hours per week) while continuing to receive full benefits, including university or campus-based roles such as research assistant, teaching assistant or lecturer. Scholars may suspend the Scholarship for up to one year for parental, medical, personal or professional leave; the Foundation states Scholars are not employees of the Foundation and it does not provide paid parental leave, and payments are paused until the Scholar re-enrols full-time. Funds begin only after Board of Directors approval, signature of the funding agreement and submission of required documentation. The annual Scholarship is disbursed in three instalments per year. There is no return-home requirement for Canadian students studying abroad or for international students.",
