      "description": "The UBC International Scholars Program funds international students who enter UBC directly from secondary school for their first undergraduate degree and who show both exceptional academic achievement and a significant level of financial need. Awards are need-based rather than fixed-value: UBC states that applicants are automatically considered for whichever of four awards they qualify for, and that individual award amounts are not selected by the applicant. Only the Vantage One Excellence Award is described as ranging in value up to the full cost of a student's academic program and living expenses, so full funding is not established for the programme as a whole.",
