      "selection_notes": "UBC states there are no exceptions to the eligibility criteria. As part of the evaluation process a financial assessment is carried out, reviewing documents outlining family gross income, expenses and family assets. Applicants are assessed on demonstrated leadership qualities, exceptional contributions to their communities, and outstanding academic performance (all As or equivalent standard). Applicants may be invited to a video interview to share more about themselves and reflect on past educational and leadership experiences beyond the written application. You do not select which award you wish to receive; the team automatically considers you for the awards you are eligible for. Applicants who apply to the International Scholars Program will not be considered for merit-based awards.",
      "notes": "Non-renewable status, deferral and return-home requirements are not published on the programme page. There is no published clinical restriction, but the following degrees are explicitly not eligible for UBC International Scholars Program awards: Bachelor of Nursing degree (Okanagan and Vancouver), Bachelor of Dental Science in Dental Hygiene, Bachelor of Medical Laboratory Science, Bachelor + Master of Management degree, dual degrees, joint degrees between UBC Okanagan and UBC Vancouver, and joint degrees with other post-secondary institutions. Applicants may only be considered for either UBC's merit-based or its financial need-based award programme. Applicants must hold a Canadian study permit. Applicants started shortly before the deadline are less likely to be successful. Housing should not be applied for until award decisions are released, because the housing application deadline is May 1.",
