          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "Alberta-based: Yes. Organization type: Post-Secondary Students.",
            "Eligible research projects involve developing or advancing an emerging technology (ET) as listed in Alberta Innovates' Applied Digital & Emerging Technology Areas, in natural sciences and engineering, in and of themselves or additionally supporting one or more Thematic Areas of Focus.",
            "The primary objective must be the advancement of the ET itself, rather than improvements in other products.",
            "Thematic Areas of Focus that an ET development project may additionally support: Health, Agricultural, and Life Science Innovation; Advanced Materials, Defence, and Aerospace; Natural Resource Recovery.",
            "At the University of Calgary, the applied digital and emerging technology topics include communications networks and services; Internet of Things (IoT)/Machine-to-machine systems; advanced data management and analytics (Artificial Intelligence/Machine Learning); cybersecurity; human interaction with digital media; quantum computing; automation including robotics; lightweight materials and technologies; additive manufacturing; nanotechnology; and quantum materials.",
            "At the University of Calgary, you are encouraged to apply once you have submitted your admissions application and received your UCID; you are not required to meet the eligibility requirements in the terms of reference when you apply, but you must meet them at the time the award is paid.",
            "Awards are based on merit, and the applicant is directed to read the terms of reference on the awarding agency or donor website."
