          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "Transcript date rule: transcripts must be up-to-date, dated or issued in the fall session of the year of application if currently registered, or after the last term completed if not currently registered.",
            "Transcript issuer rule: transcripts must be issued by the institution's registrar's office, either in paper or electronic format, either to the student or to UCalgary staff. Paper transcripts may be opened and scanned by the student.",
            "Transcript source rule: transcripts from other sources, printed from the student's personal school account, are not accepted.",
            "Transcript scan quality rule: scans must be of high quality and easily legible by reviewers.",
            "Transcript scan content rule: scans must contain grading scales for each institution.",
            "Transcript scan orientation rule: scans must be rotated so text is upright and reads from left to right.",
            "Transcript scan colour rule: scans may be in colour or black and white.",
            "Reference date rule: references used for admission may be used toward the scholarship competition only if written within the eleven months prior to the Faculty of Graduate Studies' February 1 deadline.",
            "Reference reuse rule: new students can use their references from their admission application toward their scholarship application.",
            "Application limit rule: you may create one application per competition each year.",
            "No file size limits are published for the Alberta Innovates programme on the pages read; the transcript scan rules above are the only format rules published."
