          "selection_criteria": [
            "Awards are based on merit.",
            "Ability to clearly articulate how the research aligns with Alberta Innovates' Applied Digital & Emerging Technology Areas.",
            "Ability to articulate how the research can produce potential environmental, health, economic, social and other impacts for Alberta.",
            "Research that develops or advances an emerging technology, where the primary objective is the advancement of the ET itself.",
            "Institutional evaluation: each participating Alberta institution applies its own selection and evaluation processes for students in full-time programmes.",
            "At the University of Calgary, a first-class average is required for the Killam and Open Doctoral categories, defined at UCalgary as a grade point average of 3.5 or higher in the last two years of study; the University of Calgary does not convert scales. This indicator is published for those categories rather than for the Alberta Innovates category."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Selection is institution-specific. Each of the participating Alberta institutions has scholarship application and evaluation processes specific to their institutions for students in programs of full-time study, and students are directed to their faculty of graduate studies for information on evaluation. At the University of Calgary, only one application is required regardless of the number of awards applied for, and successful students may normally hold one GAC scholarship per year across the Open Doctoral and Special Awards categories and will be awarded the highest-value scholarship for which they are eligible. Successful offers are sent by email and also appear in the MyUofC student portal, and unsuccessful notices are not sent.",
          "application_method": [
            "Check with your institution's faculty of graduate studies for full descriptions and application details.",
            "Submit your application to your institution.",
            "Wait for your application to be reviewed."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "Review the Alberta Innovates Graduate Student Scholarships Program Guidelines before applying.",
            "Check with your institution's faculty of graduate studies for the full description and application details, and note the institutional deadline.",
            "At the University of Calgary, submit your admissions application and obtain your UCID.",
            "Wait for the institutional competition to open; at the University of Calgary the Graduate Award Competition opens November 1 of each year.",
