      "description": "The Hanns-Seidel-Stiftung funds international students and doctoral candidates at state or state-recognised higher education institutions in Germany with a monthly stipend plus a study-cost flat rate, together with an ideological and networking programme. The page states that the amount is based on the income and assets of the person responsible for support and that graduates of the second educational path are funded independently of parents. The scholarship does not have to be repaid and there is no legal entitlement to the stated benefits. Double funding with BAföG or other public funds is expressly excluded.",
