      "notes": "The scholarship does not have to be repaid. There is no legal entitlement to the stated benefits; the amount is individually calculated. Double funding by the Hanns-Seidel-Stiftung together with BAföG or other public funds is excluded. Study scholarship holders drop out of the study funding programme on passing their first qualifying examination, although they remain connected to HSS as former scholarship holders. Promotion funding ends in the month of the last examination or defence of the dissertation, and is initially granted for three years, with a six-month extension possible on justified application and up to a maximum of four years in exceptional cases such as illness or pregnancy. The published pages do not state a deferral rule.",
