      "official_source": "Bundesministerium für Forschung, Technologie und Raumfahrt (BMFTR)",
      "official_source_url": "https://www.deutschlandstipendium.de/deutschlandstipendium/de/stipendium/wie-es-funktioniert/wie-es-funktioniert.html",
      "catalogue_url": null,
      "official_updates_url": "https://www.deutschlandstipendium.de/deutschlandstipendium/de/studierende/haeufig-gestellte-fragen/haeufig-gestellte-fragen.html",
      "region": "Germany (applicants of any nationality enrolled at a participating public or state-recognised German university)",
      "duration": "At least two semesters and at most the standard period of study (Regelstudienzeit); the institution reviews continued funding once a year",
      "deadline": "There is no central deadline. The programme page states that students apply to their university and that they should find out the procedure and deadlines directly from the university ('Zum jeweiligen Verfahren und den Fristen erkundigen Sie sich direkt an Ihrer Hochschule'). Deadlines are set by each participating university.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": null,
      "application_period": "No central application period. Applications run through the individual university's own call for applications; universities publish their own deadlines, which the federal programme deliberately does not centralise.",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Deutschlandstipendium is a German public-private scholarship that pays 300 euros a month, income-independent, to high-achieving and socially engaged students at German public and state-recognised universities. Half of the money comes from the federal government and half from private donors, and the university itself selects and pays the scholarship holders. The award is granted for at least two semesters and at most the standard period of study, and can be held in addition to BAföG.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Talented, high-achieving students of any nationality and any subject who are enrolled, or about to enrol, at a German public or state-recognised university that offers the Deutschlandstipendium, and who can show academic performance combined with social commitment or personal initiative.",
      "funding_amount": 300,
      "funding_currency": "EUR",
      "funding_period": "monthly",
      "eligibility_summary": "Students of all nationalities and all subjects at a public or state-recognised German university whose university offers the Deutschlandstipendium, judged on performance, commitment and personal initiative rather than grades alone.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Students of all nationalities and all subject areas",
        "Enrolled at a public or state-recognised university in Germany that offers the Deutschlandstipendium",
        "In principle any degree is eligible, including a second or supplementary degree, a master's programme and a part-time/accompanying dual programme",
        "Part-time students and prospective students awaiting admission can also apply",
        "Scholarship criteria include school and study performance, awards and prizes, previous professional activity and internships, extracurricular or non-academic engagement, and the overcoming of origin-related biographical obstacles"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "300 euros per month, half from the federal government and half from private donors",
        "The scholarship is awarded independently of income",
        "It can be received in addition to BAföG",
        "If a donor contributes more than 150 euros a month, the scholarship holder receives the excess in addition to the regular 300 euros",
        "Paid directly by the university to the scholarship holder"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Entitlement to funding is decided by the university; there is no legal claim to the Deutschlandstipendium",
        "On a change of university within the same subject, a transition semester is granted (funding for one semester) for both domestic and foreign institutions",
        "Funding continues during a subject-related stay abroad, including during a DAAD-funded ERASMUS+ mobility grant"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Apply according to the rules set out in your own university's call for applications",
        "Prospective first-year students may apply if they meet the university's admission requirements and are about to start the programme; for capacity-restricted subjects universities may run a selection process after admission",
        "The awarding decision is made by the university's selection commission, which may include private funders in an advisory capacity",
        "Membership of a university senate or student self-administration body can justify an extension of the maximum funding period (for elected members only)"
      ],
      "english_requirement": null,
      "application_method": [
        "Find out what the Deutschlandstipendium offers you and how it works",
        "Check whether your university participates, using the interactive Deutschlandkarte; in principle all public and state-recognised universities in Germany can take part",
        "Ask the university where you are enrolled or want to enrol about the specific requirements and application procedure",
        "Submit your application with the required evidence to your university",
        "Subscribe to the BMFTR newsletter for current information"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "The Deutschlandstipendium law (StipG) and the scholarship programme ordinance (StipV) set the funding criteria which the universities can shape. The intention is to support gifted and high-performing students; school and study results are an important indication, but the criteria also include awards and prizes, previous professional activity and internships, extracurricular or non-specialist engagement, and the overcoming of origin-related biographical obstacles. The application and selection procedure is intended to take the whole personality of the applicant into account. Refugee experience or experience of political persecution counts among the special social, family or personal hurdles that must be taken into account. Selection is made by the university's own selection commission; there is no central list and no right to the scholarship.",
      "notes": "The money does not have to be repaid. Students with a refugee background can also receive the scholarship if enrolled at a participating university. Funding ends on successful completion of the degree with the announcement of the overall grade, at the latest at the end of the second month after the last examination; otherwise it ends with the end of the month in which the student drops out, changes subject or de-registers. Funding is not continued during a leave of absence for personal or family reasons, but the award period is extended by that period; it does continue for a leave for an abroad semester or a compulsory internship, without extending the award period. The Deutschlandstipendium ends in principle with a successful first degree, including a bachelor's, and universities may set up special selection procedures to ease the transition to master's funding. Temporary suspension is possible (for example during a DAAD-funded period abroad), but the award period is not extended by this. Parallel funding: anyone who already receives a merit- and performance-dependent material grant averaging 30 euros or more a month cannot receive the Deutschlandstipendium; a DAAD full scholarship is not compatible, while a DAAD partial scholarship can run in parallel. The Deutschlandstipendium is not counted towards BAföG; counting applies only if combined scholarship income exceeds a monthly average of 300 euros. It is generally not counted towards other social benefits such as unemployment benefit II, with housing benefit (Wohngeld) as the exception, but it is taken into account in the parents' child maintenance. Tax: under the StipG it generally does not constitute taxable or contribution-liable income; exceptions are possible in certain constellations of private, state-recognised higher education institutions.",
      "image_url": "https://www.deutschlandstipendium.de/SiteGlobals/Frontend/Images/icons/deutschlandstipendium/logo-deutschlandstipendium.jpg?__blob=normal&v=6",
      "image_source_url": "https://www.deutschlandstipendium.de/deutschlandstipendium/de/home/home_node.html",
      "image_source_type": "official_government",
      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
