      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Deutschlandstipendium supports talented and high-achieving students at German public and state-recognised universities. It pays 300 euros a month, income-independent, split equally between the federal government and private donors, and can be held in addition to BAföG. It has been running since the summer semester 2011. The notion of performance behind it is deliberately broad: good grades and study results count, as do the willingness to take responsibility and the successful overcoming of obstacles in one's own life and educational path.",
          "purpose": [
            "Support high-achieving and engaged students and first-year students at German public and state-recognised universities",
            "Combine public funding with private donors in a public-private partnership",
            "Reward achievement, social commitment and personal initiative rather than grades alone",
            "Give scholarship holders room to focus on their university education"
          ],
