            "An aid request outside 0.8 M€-3 M€.",
            "A coordinating institution that is not a French higher education and research institution.",
            "A single project leader (responsable de projet) may carry only one PEPR GFM project.",
            "Members of the programme directorate, of the Scientific Council and of the FPPC may take part in submitted projects with limited responsibility but cannot carry a project nor be a workpackage leader.",
            "Projects that would cause significant environmental harm (DNSH principle, Article 17 of the EU Taxonomy Regulation) are excluded."
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "No nationality condition on the applicants. The obligation is institutional: the coordinating institution must be French, and the beneficiaries are French research organisations and higher education and research institutions.",
          "international_eligibility": "Foreign institutions and companies can join as partners but receive no ANR funding. French research teams can work in any scientific field as long as the project fits the deep-sea challenges, and the AAP explicitly values projects with European network opening.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [],
            "masters": [],
            "phd": [
              "The AAP anticipates the recruitment of doctoral students (doctorants) on the project budget and includes them among the 'personnels contractuels' whose role must be specified in the scientific document.",
              "Evaluation requires that the role of each contractual worker (post-doctorants, doctoral students, technical staff, students) be specified and that it allow assessment of what their contribution to the project brings to their academic or non-academic career path.",
              "Travel budget line: 3-4 travels every 2 years for workpackage leaders or staff in training (doctorate or post-doctorate) must be included in the project budget."
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "The coordinating institution signs the aid contract (contrat attributif d'aide) with the ANR.",
            "The coordinating institution may pass a share of the aid to partner institutions via a convention de reversement.",
            "Where required, the coordinating institution supplies the consortium agreement to the ANR within a maximum of 12 months of contract signature and guarantees coherence between multiple agreements.",
            "All partner institutions contributing means to the project are signatories of the consortium agreement even if they receive no share of the aid.",
            "The project must designate a data referent, an ethics referent and an equity/inclusion referent.",
            "The project must plan a structured maturation phase at the start, with specified duration, budget and responsible persons.",
            "Projects integrating sea campaigns on unprogrammed IR* Flotte means must justify why non-realisation would not undermine the project and must follow the upstream operational feasibility procedure."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Open an account on the ANR submission site as early as possible (login and password required).",
            "Deposit electronically from the project manager's account before the closing date and time.",
            "Only the electronic version of the documents present on the submission site at the closing time is taken into account.",
            "Structure a maturation phase with specified duration, budget and persons, delivering an operational roadmap, ethical issues analysis, ethics charter and Data Management Plan.",
            "Designate a data referent responsible for drafting and updating the PGD and for regular exchange with the PEPR operational cell's data officer.",
            "Identify an ethics referent from submission, participating in PEPR GFM cross-project activities on ethical issues.",
            "Identify one person responsible for equity and inclusion follow-up.",
            "Describe strategies to maintain the interdisciplinary/transdisciplinary dialogue, with a named person responsible for monitoring them.",
            "Justify explicitly the budget sizing, consistent with consortium size, permanent-staff involvement and scientific ambition.",
            "Describe explicit scientific and operational choices to minimise the project's environmental footprint (campaign and equipment pooling, remote-meeting policy, responsible digital practices, procurement policy, limiting long-distance travel).",
            "Justify all new data and sample acquisitions against an inventory of existing data/samples and state the risk-management strategy for sea operations."
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Document scientifique (scientific document): maximum 15 pages, in English, on the published template, with an appendix listing the scientific publications of the last three years by the proposing researchers/teams. Deposit format: unprotected PDF.",
            "Document administratif et financier (administrative and financial document): Excel format, covering the administrative and budget description of the project and incorporating the commitment letters of partner institutions.",
            "Lettres d'engagement des établissements partenaires, signed by the legal representative of each partner, deposited in the 'documents signés' section.",
            "Plan de Gestion de Données (PGD): first version within 6 months of project start, using the ANR-recommended structured DMP OPIDoR template, links (Opidor) to be provided in the project.",
            "Charte éthique interne au consortium, written during the maturation phase.",
            "Compte rendu de la commission ad hoc (CNFH or CNFC) of the IR* Flotte, where a not-yet-programmed fleet campaign is integrated.",
            "Annexe publication (publications annex template, .docx) and Trame du document scientifique (scientific document template, .docx) supplied by the ANR for completion.",
            "Accord de consortium, or a copy of an existing framework contract with equivalent provisions, when required."
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "The scientific document must imperatively follow the model published on the call website and be deposited as an unprotected PDF (PDF non protégé).",
            "The scientific document has a maximum length of 15 pages.",
            "The scientific document must be written in English.",
            "The scientific document must include, in appendix, the list of scientific publications of the last three years of the proposing researchers/teams.",
            "The administrative and financial document is supplied in Excel format (modèle) and must be signed and stamped by each partner institution.",
            "The signature of the commitment letters integrated in the administrative and financial document certifies that partners agree to submit the project under the conditions described in that document and in the scientific document and its appendices.",
            "No size limit, file-type list or translation rule is published beyond the unprotected-PDF and Excel-format requirements; no translation requirement is published for the submission documents.",
            "Documents must be uploaded into the dedicated 'documents de dépôt' and 'documents signés' sections; the submission cannot be validated by the project manager until every document has been uploaded.",
            "The ANR will disregard any file version other than the one present on the submission site at the closing time."
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Ambition scientifique et excellence: the structuring research question goes beyond the documented state of the art and is not a simple continuation, involving opening up disciplines and/or to non-academic stakeholders; all projects must think about their interface with society",
            "Ambition scientifique et excellence: the combination of disciplines is justified by the scientific question, each discipline alone cannot answer the question, and the role of non-academic partners in producing knowledge is justified and not limited to dissemination",
            "Ambition scientifique et excellence: conceptual frameworks of each discipline are put in dialogue and generate results no single discipline would have produced",
            "Ambition scientifique et excellence: existing or newly acquired data and samples are exploited to answer new questions, using new methodologies if needed",
            "Ambition scientifique et excellence: identifying and managing ethical issues is integral to the scientific ambition and excellence",
            "Qualité du consortium: the project leader and co-leaders have recognised expertise in complementary fields and demonstrate capacity to coordinate an ambitious interdisciplinary consortium and/or animate transdisciplinary projects",
            "Qualité du consortium: adequacy between staff and objectives, with the role of each academic and non-academic partner clearly defined, substantive permanent-staff involvement, and a precise role for contractual staff that demonstrates benefit to their career",
            "Qualité du consortium: a structured maturation phase is explicitly described, with duration, budget and persons specified for its deliverables",
            "Qualité du consortium: concrete mechanisms let all consortium members appropriate the research questions (launch seminars, shared glossaries, co-writing processes, disciplinary translation workshops), with procedures for resolving scientific disagreement and explicit strategies to overcome foreseeable limitations (fieldwork, stakeholders, data, interdisciplinarity, transdisciplinarity)",
            "Qualité du consortium: the strategy for inventorying, acquiring and managing data and samples is described and shows what exists, what is missing and why any acquisition fills a real, non-redundant gap",
            "Qualité du consortium: concrete and recurring mechanisms for analysing and implementing ethical follow-up",
            "Qualité du consortium: explicit scientific and operational choices to minimise the project's environmental footprint",
            "Qualité du consortium: sizing coherent with ambition in human resources and budget; the 0.8-3 M€ request is argued and consistent, and budget lines reflect the stated commitments",
            "Inscription dans les défis: the project clearly addresses research issues in at least one PEPR GFM challenge and contributes to the programme's strategic priorities",
            "Impact: expected scientific, economic, environmental and societal impacts are described and the contribution to the domains of the Stratégie nationale d'accélération is argued",
            "Impact: modalities for sharing data and results during and after the project are described, with assured transparency of each partner's contributions",
            "Impact: modalities of open access to scientific data are defined, the PGD strategy integrates FAIR and CARE principles and specifically addresses SHS data, and Opidor PGD links are provided",
            "Impact: dissemination of results in academic and non-academic circles and engagement with the scientific community and the general public are described"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Two-step gatekeeping: only proposals meeting the eligibility criteria reach the committee and can never be funded otherwise. An independent international-dimension committee convened by the ANR, possibly with external experts and possibly hearing project leaders, produces a funding-recommended list and a non-funding list with written justification per project, and may give an opinion on the requested amount. Programme directors not involved in submitted projects then propose to the SGPI the projects that could be financed and at what amount; the Prime Minister, after opinion of the CPMo and the SGPI, decides beneficiaries and amounts, and each project is covered by an ANR contract with the coordinating institution. Committee and external experts commit to ANR deontology and scientific-integrity rules, strict confidentiality, declaration of conflicts of interest, and a ban on using AI tools in the evaluation. The committee composition is published on the call website after selection.",
          "application_method": [
            "Create an account on the ANR France 2030 submission site (https://france2030.agencerecherche.fr/PEPR-GFM-AAP-2026-dossier).",
            "Download the Word template of the scientific document, the Excel administrative and financial annex, and the publications annex template from the call page.",
            "Draft the scientific document in English, max 15 pages, on the template, with the three-year publications appendix.",
            "Gather signed and stamped commitment letters from all partner institutions and the legal representative's signature on the administrative and financial document.",
            "Enter project data online (duration 36-54 months, aid 0.8-3 M€) and upload the files in the 'documents de dépôt' and 'documents signés' sections.",
            "Validate the complete deposit before 17/11/2026 at 11:00 Paris time and retain the electronic acknowledgement of receipt.",
            "Follow updates on the call page, which carries updated information on how the call is proceeding."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Create an account on the ANR submission site as early as possible.",
            "2. Download the scientific document template (Word), the administrative and financial document template (Excel) and the publications annex template.",
            "3. Write the 15-page English scientific document covering the maturation phase, data and samples strategy, ethical issues, human resources, open science and dissemination.",
            "4. Build the budget between 800 k€ and 3 M€ for 36-54 months, explicitly justifying the sizing and including the PEPR GFM governance travel costs.",
            "5. Obtain commitment letters and signatures from all partner institutions, including the legal representative of the coordinating institution.",
            "6. Complete and sign the administrative and financial document.",
            "7. Upload all documents to the call entry and validate the deposit electronically.",
            "8. Confirm receipt of the electronic acknowledgement and monitor the call page for updates."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
