      "description": "The PEPR PROPSY call funds precision-psychiatry research projects in three axes: pre-clinical studies, clinical studies and mixed studies, with an indicative total envelope of about 9 600 000 € for 8 to 16 projects in 2026. The aid is paid as a grant to the coordinating institution and may finance equipment, personnel specifically assigned to the project and associated running costs, so doctoral and post-doctoral positions are recruited on project budgets rather than awarded as individual scholarships. Funded projects must target bipolar disorders, resistant and/or recurrent depressions, psychotic disorders or autism spectrum disorders, and transdiagnostic projects are assessed positively.",
