      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The PEPR PROPSY \"Psychiatrie de précision\" is a national initiative financed under the France 2030 plan, piloted by Inserm and CNRS with the support of the Fondation FondaMental, with a budget of 80 million euros over seven years. Its aim is to transform the care of four disabling disorders: bipolar disorders, resistant and/or recurrent depressions, psychotic disorders and autism spectrum disorders. This 2026 call will finance 8 to 16 projects for a total of about 9 600 000 €, covering pre-clinical studies, clinical studies and/or mixed studies to explore physiopathological mechanisms or identify and validate biomarkers or therapeutic targets in a precision-psychiatry approach. It is one of five work packages of the PEPR, alongside the French Minds longitudinal cohort, mechanisms, new therapeutic strategies, a French biomedical industry in mental health, and training and information actions.",
          "purpose": [
            "Refine the characterisation of psychiatric disorders and clarify their heterogeneity.",
            "Identify new stratification, prognostic and/or treatment-response biomarkers.",
            "Develop innovative therapeutic strategies targeted at a precise mechanism and/or a homogeneous subgroup of patients.",
            "Structure a French biomedical sector in precision psychiatry, encouraging collaboration between public research and the pharmaceutical industry and relying on new medical and digital technologies.",
            "Strengthen training and the attractiveness of professions related to psychiatric care and to research and innovation in precision psychiatry.",
            "Contribute to the transformation and strengthening of French research capacity, its attractiveness, its European and international influence, and its impact on the economy and society.",
            "Produce high-quality research and valorise the resulting research and innovation, accompanying clinical implementation and/or industrialisation.",
