          "selection_criteria": [
            "1) Excellence and ambition: clarity of objectives and research hypotheses",
            "1) Excellence and ambition: innovativeness, ambition, originality, methodological or conceptual rupture compared with the state of the art",
            "1) Excellence and ambition: relevance of the methodology",
            "1) Excellence and ambition: preliminary data",
            "1) Excellence and ambition: project feasibility",
            "2) Consortium, management, means and governance: competence, expertise and involvement of the project leader, including capacity to coordinate ambitious multidisciplinary projects or consortia, academic track record and international recognition",
            "2) Consortium, management, means and governance: quality and complementarity of the scientific consortium with regard to the project objectives, if collaborative",
            "2) Consortium, management, means and governance: adequacy between the human and financial means mobilised (including those requested in the project) and the objectives",
            "2) Consortium, management, means and governance: relevance of the schedule (particularly for long projects), management of scientific risks and alternative solutions, credibility of the proposed milestones",
            "2) Consortium, management, means and governance: relevance and efficiency of project governance (piloting, organisation, animation, setting up of advisory committees), in particular the relevance of integrating patient associations, links with industrial partners, other projects or programmes",
            "3) Impact and outcomes: capacity of the project to address the issues of developing precision psychiatry",
            "3) Impact and outcomes: active strategy to measure the economic and/or societal impact of the work",
            "3) Impact and outcomes: contribution to solutions to pathophysiological, diagnostic or therapeutic issues in psychiatry",
            "3) Impact and outcomes: dissemination strategy (in itinere and ex post) and valorization of results, adherence to FAIR and Open Science principles, and promotion of scientific culture"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Two-step gatekeeping: only proposals meeting the eligibility criteria reach the committee and can never be funded otherwise. An independent international-dimension committee, possibly with external experts and possibly hearing project leaders, reports to the PEPR PROPSY scientific directors with a funding-recommended list, a non-funding list with written justification per project, and possibly an opinion on amounts. The scientific directors propose to the SGPI the projects that could be financed and at what amount; the Prime Minister, after SGPI opinion, decides beneficiaries and amounts, and each project is covered by an ANR contract with the coordinating institution. The committee may call on external experts. Committee members and external experts commit to ANR deontology and scientific-integrity rules, strict confidentiality, declaration of conflicts of interest, and a ban on using AI tools in the evaluation. The committee composition is published on the call website after selection.",
