      "description": "M-ERA.NET Call 2026 (2027 edition for the ANR) is a transnational ERA-NET call co-funded by more than 30 national and regional funding agencies to fund ambitious R&D projects on advanced materials and battery technologies, supporting the European Green Deal and the UN Sustainable Development Goals. The ANR funds only the eligible costs of French partners, paid directly to each partner's national or regional organisation. ANR aid ranges from a 15 000 € minimum up to 180 000 € for a non-coordinating French partner and 250 000 € for a coordinating French partner, with a 350 000 € total cap across several ANR partners, plus an optional additional 20 000 € per project for European project-preparation activities.",
      "program_type": "Research grant",
      "best_fit": "A researcher or institution in France leading or joining a materials or battery-technology consortium of at least three funded partners from at least three different countries, whose pre-proposal was recommended in step 1 and who need French ANR co-funding for a maximum 36-month project in one of the four ANR-eligible topics.",
      "funding_amount": null,
