      "english_requirement": "Pre-proposals and detailed proposals, and Annexe 1, must be written in English (rédigées en langue anglaise). The ANR also states that, on request, a translation of the evaluation criteria may be provided.",
      "application_method": [
        "Register the intended project with the M-ERA.NET Call 2026 submission site before the step 1 pre-proposal deadline of 12/05/2026 at 12:00 CEST (this step is closed).",
        "Submit the pre-proposal form in English on the M-ERA.NET site, clearly stating the topic and, where ANR aid is sought, the TRL levels of each French partner's tasks.",
        "Wait for the M-ERA.NET invitation: the pre-proposal must be recommended by at least three funding agencies from at least three different participating countries.",
        "Prepare the detailed proposal in English on the mandatory template, with Annexe 1 and the CVs of all consortium participants.",
        "For ANR aid, await the email from the ANR with the exact ANR submission link and deadline, then deposit the identical detailed proposal on the ANR submission site.",
        "Validate both deposits before 18/11/2026 at 12:00 CET; the ANR does not require a deposit on its site at step 1.",
        "Communicate and obtain acceptance of any change from the requested funding agencies and the call secretariat at least two weeks before the step 2 closing date."
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Evaluation and selection are centralised at M-ERA.NET level and take place in two steps: step 1 central evaluation of pre-proposals by independent international experts convened by the M-ERA.NET Call Secretariat, with invitations to step 2 issued in ranking order and taking account of the participating agencies' budget capacity; step 2 central evaluation of detailed proposals by independent international experts convened by the same secretariat. Proposals are ranked on the evaluation results and selection follows the ranking. The list of projects recommended for funding is drawn up by the group of participating funders taking account of their respective budget capacities, and the final funding decision is then taken individually by the funders concerned. Results are sent by the call secretariat to the project coordinators. Evaluation modalities and criteria are those of the call text (Guide for proposers) available on the ANR call page and the M-ERA.NET call site; the ANR adds its own horizontal objectives, which are that projects show significant French participation (in coordination or in charge of a substantial part of the work), generate significant opening and diversification of French collaboration networks, and are ambitious with a clear intention of continuity and evolution of the collaboration. During discussions to separate projects of similar scientific quality within the funder group, projects involving a wider and/or more diverse consortium may be favoured.",
      "notes": "This is institutional research funding, not a personal scholarship: nothing is paid to individual students and no tuition, living-cost or travel allowance is established for individuals. The aid is paid to each partner's own national or regional organisation, not centrally. Amounts may not be increased between the two steps: increases are not authorised, and projects that do not respect the aid limits or that do not conform to any budgetary adjustments requested by the ANR are declared ineligible. The 20 000 € European-preparation supplement is conditional on adequate planning and activities within the M-ERA.NET project (a dedicated Work Package and budget under the responsibility of an ANR-funded partner), on the activities actually leading to a research proposal involving consortium members in continuity with the M-ERA.NET work, and on the follow-up proposal targeting clearly identified FP10 calls (not co-funded by the ANR) coordinated by the ANR-funded French partner; it is a subject of a final assessment and a supplementary deliverable to the ANR. Beneficiaries commit to immediate open access to peer-reviewed publications under CC-BY, deposit of the accepted manuscript or publisher version in HAL, a FAIR approach to research data, a PGD within 6 months of the scientific start, deposit of data in a reference thematic repository or recherche.data.gouv, and free-licence release and Software Heritage archiving of software. Any change affecting the whole project (extensions, consortium modifications) must be approved by all partners, their funding agencies and M-ERA.NET. Proposals may be transmitted to other administrations, control bodies and partner funders, and certain national funders are obliged to publish submitted pre-proposals/proposals, which may disclose intellectual-property or business-secret content; applicants are warned to be careful with what they include. The ANR applies the PPST protection of the scientific and technical potential of the nation to projects with foreign public or private partners, and a negative SHFDS/MESR opinion prevents selection without reasons being given.",
      "image_url": "https://anr.fr/fileadmin/images/logos/m-era.net-2022.jpg",
