      "description": "WBI funds researchers from any country who hold a doctorate awarded by a foreign institution to carry out a postdoctoral research programme at a higher-education institution organised or subsidised by the Fédération Wallonie-Bruxelles. The support is a net monthly grant of 2,120 EUR paid for the duration of the research programme, plus return international economy-class travel and health, civil-liability and repatriation insurance. WBI states explicitly that this is a monthly grant and not a salary, and that it is awarded as a mobility allowance. Priority research themes are the Marshall Plan 4.0 competitiveness clusters, though any field including humanities, fundamental or applied sciences will be considered.",
