      "selection_notes": "Five-stage process: administrative verification of admissibility; admissible files passed to the selection jury; jury ranking sent to WBI; WBI allocates the grants according to available budget; WBI communicates results. The jury is composed of members of the Fonds de la Recherche Scientifique (F.R.S.-FNRS), the Direction générale opérationnel 'Economie, emploi et recherche' (DGO6) of the Walloon public service, and WBI. Files are ranked in three categories A–B–C; only files rated A (with sub-categories A- and A+) by at least one jury member can be selected. Selection is based on: link to Marshall Plan 4.0 competitiveness clusters; recommendation letters; academic records; interest of the field for Walloon universities and research centres; scientific publications; added value of the intended mobility; professional career path. Results are normally issued in early June for long-duration grants, early January for short-duration stays of March–July, and early July for short-duration stays of September–February.",
      "notes": "The grant is explicitly NOT a salary ('ne constitue aucunement un salaire') and is awarded as a mobility allowance. Long-duration grants may be renewed once; short-duration grants are renewable only while the 3-year interval between two stays is respected. No return-home obligation is published. Award holders must acknowledge WBI support with the wording 'Avec le soutien de Wallonie-Bruxelles International' and the WBI logo on any public document, and must submit periodic reports, a final mission report and an ALUMNI form. There is no clinical or field restriction published for this programme.",
