      "description": "AFdoc is a new PhD funding scheme launched by the Luxembourg National Research Fund following the entry into force of the new FNR law on 1 August 2026. It supports talented doctoral candidates with a clear link to Luxembourg who undertake PhD projects in established research environments abroad, or through collaborations involving Luxembourg-based companies active in R&D. Funding is granted to the eligible Host Institution, which employs the selected candidate under an employment contract, and may cover up to four years of doctoral training. Based on the salary index applicable on 1 June 2026, the maximum annual salary contribution is EUR 54,574 including employer charges, social security and pension contributions.",
