          "selection_notes": "Eligible proposals are assessed on the scientific quality and potential of the project, the applicant's profile and potential, the quality of the Host Institution, supervision and training environment, and the expected impact of the project. AFdoc is bottom-up: proposals from all fields of research and technological development are eligible and do not need to align with Luxembourg's National Research Priorities, provided they fall within the expertise of the supervisors, the Host Institution and, where applicable, the company partner. One proposal may be submitted per applicant per call. The 2026 call is a pilot call introducing a self-assessment on potential research security aspects, developed in a joint 3LiU-FNR working group and to be presented to prospective PIs by the end of February at the latest. Funding decisions are communicated in March of the following year for the September call and in July for the April call.",
