    {
      "name": "Flanders Trainee Programme (Flanders Traineeship Programme)",
      "country": "Belgium",
      "degree_levels": "Undergraduate, Master's",
      "funding_type": "Stipend",
      "official_source": "Government of Flanders — Flanders Trainee Programme (Departement Buitenlandse Zaken)",
      "official_source_url": "https://www.vlaanderen.be/en/studying/flanders-trainee-programme",
      "catalogue_url": null,
      "official_updates_url": null,
      "region": "Belgium (Government of Flanders). The internship itself is taken at the headquarters or a field office of a qualifying multilateral organisation within the jurisdiction of the Diplomatic Representations of Flanders. Published monthly grant amounts cover Antwerp, Brussels, Luxembourg, Geneva, London, Montreal, Nairobi, New York, Paris, Pretoria, Rome, Strasbourg, The Hague, Vienna, Warsaw, Washington D.C., Bonn, Madrid, Stockholm, Copenhagen, Maputo, Lilongwe and Midrand. Applicants may be of any nationality and resident anywhere, but must hold a Flemish secondary or higher education diploma.",
      "duration": "The grant covers an internship of at least two and up to six months. The internship can be extended to a total duration of six months, or nine months where the internship concerns a project funded by the Government of Flanders.",
      "deadline": "No more grants for 2026: 'You can no longer apply for a grant for internships continuing into 2026. There is no more budget available for 2026. A budget will be available again in 2027. You can reapply for internships taking place in 2027 as from January 2027.' Within a funded budget year: 'You can submit your grant application up to six months in advance until one day before the start of your internship.'",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "month",
      "application_period": "The 2026 budget is exhausted and applications for 2026 are closed. The 2027 budget reopens for applications in January 2027 for internships taking place in 2027, and new internship vacancies will be published on the programme's internships page from late 2026 onwards. Inside a funded budget year the published rule is that you may apply at any time of the year until one day before your internship starts, up to six months in advance, but a grant is only granted while budget remains.",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Flanders Trainee Programme gives young people who hold a secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders financial support for an internship with a multilateral organisation. The grant is made up of a one-off travel allowance and a monthly lump-sum amount for accommodation and living expenses, both set in advance; the monthly amount depends on the host city. Nationality and official place of residence are irrelevant, and the programme targets people interested in global challenges such as climate change, food security or human rights. The 2026 budget is exhausted; a budget is available again for 2027, with applications reopenable from January 2027.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Anyone under 35 with a secondary or higher education diploma earned at a Flemish institution, of any nationality, who has already secured or is about to secure an internship at a qualifying multilateral organisation such as the UN, NATO-adjacent bodies, the OECD, the WHO family, the Council of Europe, the Benelux Union or an EU institution.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": "EUR",
      "funding_period": "month for the living-expense component, plus a one-off travel payment",
      "eligibility_summary": "You must be under 35 when the internship starts, hold a secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders, and have secured an internship of at least two months with an organisation on the published list of qualifying multilateral organisations.",
      "eligibility": [
        "You are younger than 35 on the start date of your internship.",
        "You have obtained a secondary or higher education diploma in Flanders. So your nationality and official place of residence are irrelevant.",
        "You have secured an internship with a multilateral organisation from the published qualifying list.",
        "The internship lasts at least two and up to six months.",
        "The internship must take place at the headquarters or a field office of the organisation, within the areas of jurisdiction of the Diplomatic Representations of Flanders."
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "One-off payment of 200 EUR for travel expenses if the internship is within Europe (all Council of Europe member states, Belarus and Kosovo)",
        "One-off payment of 500 EUR for travel expenses if the internship is located outside Europe",
        "Monthly lump-sum amount for accommodation and living expenses, set annually and multiplied by the number of months your internship is active, varying by host city (published city matrix)",
        "No travel reimbursement if the internship is in Belgium"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "The grant is not a salary but a lump-sum reimbursement of expenses actually borne, so it is not an obstacle to the Flemish Growth Package/child benefit you may still be entitled to for 12 months after finishing your studies",
        "Payment in two instalments: 85% of the total grant after approval, and the remaining 15% after the internship once you submit the internship report and the supervisor's evaluation report",
        "The internship can be extended to a total duration of six months, or nine months where the internship concerns a project funded by the Government of Flanders"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Be under 35 on the internship start date",
        "Hold a secondary or higher education diploma obtained at a Flemish educational institution",
        "Have secured the internship; you may apply up to six months before it starts or after it has started",
        "Your internship supervisor must complete the attestation regarding the internship offer and submit it to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
        "If you apply after the internship has started, the remaining period counted from the first day after you submit must be at least two months",
        "After the internship, submit the personal evaluation form and have your supervisor complete and submit the evaluation form, at the latest two months after the end of the internship",
        "Take part in an intake interview before the internship and a follow-up conversation afterwards",
        "You must not receive a salary from the hosting organisation if you want to keep the Flemish Growth Package/child benefit",
        "Inform the programme if you end the internship early; you may have to repay part of the grant"
      ],
      "english_requirement": null,
      "application_method": [
        "Check you meet the eligibility conditions",
        "Secure an internship at a qualifying multilateral organisation, either through a vacancy published on the programme's internships page or by a spontaneous application",
        "Submit the online application form with the required documents",
        "Have your internship supervisor complete the attestation regarding the internship offer and submit it to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
        "Receive approval once all documents are provided and the requirements are met",
        "Take part in the intake interview with the programme coordinator",
        "During the internship, stay in contact with the coordinator and provide visual material",
        "After the internship, submit the personal evaluation form and the supervisor's evaluation form within two months",
        "Take part in the follow-up conversation with the coordinator"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "No competitive jury or published ranking is described for this programme. The published route is a budget-limited reimbursement scheme: in principle you can apply at any time of the year, but you only get a grant if budget is still available, and if a budget is no longer available for the current year that is announced clearly on the programme website; an application submitted after the budget is gone is not processed and is not kept until a new budget is available. The average administrative turnaround time is three weeks. The grant is reduced by any remuneration or financial allowance you receive for the same internship from another Belgian or foreign government or from the multilateral organisation itself.",
      "notes": "The grant is explicitly not a salary but a lump-sum reimbursement of expenses actually borne, made up of a one-off travel allowance and an expense allowance for accommodation and living expenses. Coverage is partial: it does not pay tuition or course fees, there is no travel payment for an internship in Belgium, and the amounts are capped at a fixed 200 or 500 EUR travel payment plus a city-based monthly living amount. The internship can be extended to a total of six months, or nine months for internships linked to a project funded by the Government of Flanders. If you end the internship early you must inform the programme and may have to repay part of the grant, the amount being determined by the number of days you actually worked. There is no clinical or professional restriction published beyond the requirement that the host be a qualifying multilateral organisation.",
      "image_url": "https://www.vlaanderen.be/img/logo/vlaanderen-logo-en.svg",
      "image_source_url": "https://www.vlaanderen.be/en/studying/flanders-trainee-programme",
      "image_source_type": "official_government",
      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
      "image_alt_text": "Government of Flanders",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Flanders Trainee Programme offers young global citizens financial support for an internship with a multilateral organisation. The grant consists of a one-off amount for travel expenses and a monthly amount for living expenses; both are lump sums, meaning they are set in advance. You must hold a secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders, be under 35 when the internship starts, and secure the internship yourself with an organisation on the published qualifying list.",
          "purpose": [
            "Give young people financial support for an internship with a multilateral organisation",
            "Recruit socially engaged young people interested in global challenges such as climate change, food security or human rights",
            "Give Flemish-trained young people international exposure and, through Flanders' diplomatic representatives abroad, involve them in Flemish foreign policy",
            "Build a network between young Flemish graduates and multilateral organisations"
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [],
          "degree_levels": [
            "Secondary education diploma or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders"
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Internship with a multilateral organisation"
          ],
          "degree_award": "Not a degree award. The programme funds an internship and confers no credit, degree or diploma.",
          "duration": "At least two and up to six months. Extensible to a total duration of six months, or nine months where the internship concerns a project funded by the Government of Flanders.",
          "application_cycle": "Budget-year based rather than a fixed annual call. The 2026 budget is exhausted; a budget is available again in 2027 and you can reapply for internships taking place in 2027 as from January 2027. Inside a funded year applications may be made at any time until one day before the internship starts, up to six months in advance.",
          "deadline_central": null,
          "deadline_central_display": "No more grants for 2026 — 'You can no longer apply for a grant for internships continuing into 2026. There is no more budget available for 2026. A budget will be available again in 2027. You can reapply for internships taking place in 2027 as from January 2027.' Inside a funded year: submit up to six months in advance, until one day before the start of the internship.",
          "deadline_institutional": "None published. The host organisation does not set a deadline; the internship supervisor only has to complete and submit the attestation regarding the internship offer to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be.",
          "deadline_note": "No absolute closing date is published for the 2027 round. The only published timing is that applications for 2027 internships reopen in January 2027, so deadline_date is left null and deadline_precision is set to month to reflect the month-level January 2027 opening. The standing in-year rule is that applications close one day before the internship start date.",
          "status": "UPCOMING",
          "funding_type": "Stipend",
          "funding_label": "One-off travel allowance (200 EUR within Europe / 500 EUR outside Europe) plus a monthly lump-sum expense allowance for accommodation and living expenses, set annually by city and multiplied by the number of active internship months",
          "funding_amount": null,
          "funding_currency": "EUR",
          "funding_period": "month (living-expense component) plus a one-off travel payment",
          "tuition_coverage": "Not applicable. The programme funds an internship with a multilateral organisation, not a course, and no tuition or enrolment fee appears in the published support list.",
          "living_cost_coverage": "A monthly lump-sum expense allowance for accommodation and living expenses. The monthly amounts are set annually and multiplied by the number of months your internship is active. Published city amounts: Antwerp 1,669.92; Brussels 1,669.92; Bruges 1,669.92; Luxembourg 1,669.92; Montreal 1,586.42; Montreal; Lilongwe 1,047.60; Midrand 1,202.34; Pretoria 1,202.34; Warsaw 1,392.20; Nairobi 1,720.02; Maputo 1,720.02; Madrid 1,836.91; Rome 1,853.61; Stockholm 1,753.42; Barcelona 1,903.70; Strasbourg 1,903.71; Bonn 1,970.51; The Hague 2,003.90; Washington D.C. 2,037.30; Paris 2,037.30; London 2,087.40; Vienna 2,137.50; New York 2,220.90; Copenhagen 2,304.49; Geneva 2,721.97.",
          "travel_coverage": "One-off payment of 200 EUR for travel expenses if the internship is within Europe (all Council of Europe member states, Belarus and Kosovo); one-off payment of 500 EUR if the internship is located outside Europe. No travel reimbursement if the internship is in Belgium.",
          "fully_funded": false,
          "tuition_rule": "Not applicable: the programme pays no tuition and confers no degree. The funded activity is an internship with a qualifying multilateral organisation, obtained either through a published vacancy or a spontaneous application.",
          "home_tuition_rule": null,
          "host_institution_fee": null,
          "tax_status": "Not published as a tax matter. The amounts page states the grant is not a salary but rather a lump-sum reimbursement of expenses actually borne, and that this is why a grant is not an obstacle to the Flemish Growth Package/child benefit.",
          "covered_expenses": [
            "One-off travel expenses of 200 EUR for an internship within Europe (all Council of Europe member states, Belarus and Kosovo)",
            "One-off travel expenses of 500 EUR for an internship outside Europe",
            "Monthly lump-sum accommodation and living-expense amount set annually by host city, multiplied by the number of active internship months"
          ],
          "not_covered_or_excluded": [
            "No travel reimbursement at all if the internship is in Belgium",
            "The travel element is a single capped payment (200 or 500 EUR); no onward travel, second journey or extended travel is named",
            "No tuition, enrolment or course fees — the programme funds an internship, not a course",
            "The grant is reduced by any remuneration or financial allowance you receive for the same internship from another Belgian or foreign government, or from the multilateral organisation itself",
            "The Flemish Growth Package/child benefit is preserved only if you receive no salary from the hosting organisation, so a paid placement removes that entitlement even though the grant itself is unaffected",
            "No health insurance, visa, relocation, dependants, per-diem or equipment provision is named in the published support list",
            "If you apply after the internship has started you are only paid for the remaining period counted from the first day after you submit, and that remaining period must be at least two months",
            "Applications submitted after the year's budget is exhausted are not processed and are not held until a new budget is available",
            "Ending the internship early can require repayment of part of the grant, the amount being determined by the number of days actually worked"
          ],
          "benefits": [
            "The grant is not a salary, so it is not an obstacle to the Growth Package/child benefit you may still be entitled to for 12 months after finishing your studies",
            "Payment split: 85% of the total grant after approval, 15% after the internship once the internship report and the supervisor's evaluation report are submitted",
            "Extension of the funded internship up to a total of six months, or nine months where the internship concerns a project funded by the Government of Flanders",
            "The internship can be taken up through a vacancy published on the programme's own page or through a spontaneous application to any organisation on the qualifying list",
            "Participation in Flemish foreign policy activity through Flanders' diplomatic representatives abroad"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Younger than 35 on the start date of the internship",
            "Secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders",
            "Internship secured with a multilateral organisation on the published qualifying list",
            "Internship of at least two and up to six months",
            "Internship at the headquarters or a field office of the organisation, within the jurisdiction of the Diplomatic Representations of Flanders"
          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "Under 35 at the internship start date",
            "Flemish secondary or higher education diploma",
            "Secured internship with a qualifying multilateral organisation"
          ],
          "ineligibility_conditions": [
            "35 years old or older on the start date of the internship",
            "No secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders",
            "No secured internship with an organisation on the published qualifying list",
            "Internship shorter than two months, including the remaining period if you apply after it has started",
            "Internship at an organisation that is not on the published qualifying list, or at a location outside the areas of jurisdiction of the Diplomatic Representations of Flanders",
            "Application submitted after the budget for the year is exhausted — not processed and not held for the following budget",
            "Receiving a salary from the hosting organisation, which forfeits the Growth Package/child benefit for the 12 months after your studies"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Nationality and official place of residence are irrelevant. The binding condition is holding a secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders.",
          "international_eligibility": "Open to applicants of any nationality resident anywhere in the world who hold a Flemish secondary or higher education diploma and have an internship at a qualifying multilateral organisation.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "A secondary education diploma obtained in Flanders is sufficient",
              "The Growth Package/child benefit interaction rule presupposes school leavers as well as graduates: entitlement runs for 12 months after finishing your studies if you are under 25 and not receiving a salary"
            ],
            "masters": [
              "A higher education diploma obtained in Flanders is sufficient",
              "The published list of recognised higher education institutions is linked from the terms and conditions page (in Dutch)"
            ],
            "phd": []
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "The host must be a multilateral organisation from the published qualifying list (for example the Benelux Union in Brussels, the Council of Europe in Strasbourg, the OECD in Paris, the UN family in Geneva and New York, the African Union in Addis Ababa, the NATO-adjacent OSCE and OPCW in Vienna and The Hague, the European institutions in Brussels, or the IMF/World Bank in Washington)",
            "Internships can only take place at the headquarters or at a field office of these organisations, within the areas of jurisdiction of the Diplomatic Representations of Flanders",
            "The internship supervisor at the organisation must complete the attestation regarding the internship offer and submit it to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "The internship supervisor must complete the evaluation form after the internship and submit it to the same address",
            "For the Growth Package/child benefit to be preserved, the hosting organisation must not pay you a salary"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Under 35 at the internship start date",
            "Secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders",
            "Secured internship of at least two months with a qualifying multilateral organisation",
            "Application submitted before the internship starts, or with at least two months remaining if it has already started",
            "Supervisor attestation regarding the internship offer submitted by the supervisor",
            "Personal evaluation form and supervisor evaluation form within two months after the internship",
            "Intake interview with the coordinator before the internship and a follow-up conversation afterwards",
            "No salary from the hosting organisation if the Growth Package/child benefit is to be preserved",
            "Notification if the internship ends earlier than expected"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Copy of your identity card",
            "Diploma obtained at a Flemish educational institution",
            "Letter of acceptance from the organisation, or another certificate proving acceptance for the internship",
            "Attestation regarding the internship offer, completed by the internship supervisor and submitted to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "Personal evaluation form (in Dutch), completed by the applicant",
            "Evaluation form, completed by the internship supervisor and submitted to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "Internship report, required before the second instalment is paid",
            "Extension certificate, if the internship is extended"
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "No file size limit, accepted file type, page limit, signature rule or translation/certification rule is published for the online application form",
            "The online application form and the personal evaluation form are published in Dutch",
            "The attestation regarding the internship offer and the evaluation form are completed and submitted by the internship supervisor, not by the applicant",
            "The personal evaluation form and the supervisor's evaluation form must be submitted at the latest two months after the end of the internship",
            "For an extension, a new application is submitted through the same online form with the 'internship extension' option, and the supervisor completes an extension certificate"
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Eligibility conditions as published: under 35 at the internship start date; secondary or higher education diploma obtained in Flanders; internship secured with a qualifying multilateral organisation",
            "Internship duration of at least two months and at most six months (nine months for a Flemish-government-funded project)",
            "Availability of budget for the year in question",
            "Reduction of the grant by any other remuneration or financial allowance received for the same internship"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "The programme publishes no jury, no ranking and no competitive scoring. It is a budget-limited reimbursement scheme: 'In principle, you can apply for a grant at any time of the year, but you can only get a grant if there is still budget available. If a budget is no longer available for the current year, it will be clearly announced on this website. If you submit an application when there is no more budget available, it will not be processed. The application is also not kept until a new budget is available.' The published procedure is: submit the application with the required documents; the supervisor submits the attestation; approval is given once all necessary documents are provided and the requirements are met, with an average administrative turnaround of three weeks; the coordinator contacts you for an intake interview; during the internship you stay in contact with the coordinator and provide visual material; afterwards you submit the personal evaluation form and the supervisor's evaluation form within two months and take part in a follow-up conversation.",
          "application_method": [
            "Online application form published on the Government of Flanders website (in Dutch)",
            "Supporting documents uploaded with the application form",
            "The internship supervisor submits the attestation regarding the internship offer and the evaluation form directly to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be"
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "Check the eligibility conditions: under 35 at the internship start date, Flemish secondary or higher education diploma, and a qualifying multilateral internship",
            "Secure the internship, either by responding to a vacancy published on the programme's internships page or by a spontaneous application to an organisation on the qualifying list",
            "Prepare a copy of your identity card, your diploma from the Flemish educational institution, and the letter of acceptance or other proof of acceptance",
            "Submit the online application form, no later than one day before the internship starts and at the earliest six months before it",
            "Ask your internship supervisor to complete the attestation regarding the internship offer and have them send it to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "Wait for approval (average administrative turnaround three weeks)",
            "Take part in the intake interview with the programme coordinator",
            "During the internship, stay in contact with the coordinator and provide visual material",
            "After the internship, submit the personal evaluation form and have your supervisor complete and submit the evaluation form, at the latest two months after the end",
            "Take part in the follow-up conversation with the coordinator, after which the second instalment of 15% is released",
            "To extend, submit a new application choosing the 'internship extension' option and have the supervisor submit the extension certificate"
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits the online application form themselves",
            "The internship supervisor submits the attestation regarding the internship offer directly to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "The internship supervisor submits the evaluation form directly to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "All questions and the extension certificate go to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be"
          ],
          "application_portal": "Online application form published on vlaanderen.be (Flanders Trainee Programme application and procedure page; form is in Dutch)",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "During the internship you stay in contact with the programme coordinator and provide visual material",
            "After the internship you submit the personal evaluation form, and your supervisor completes and submits the evaluation form, at the latest two months after the end",
            "You take part in a follow-up conversation with the coordinator",
            "You must inform the programme if you terminate the internship earlier than expected; you may have to repay a portion of the grant, determined by the number of days you actually worked",
            "Any extension requires a new application plus a supervisor extension certificate, capped at six months in total, or nine months for a project funded by the Government of Flanders",
            "The second instalment of 15% is only paid after the internship report and the supervisor's evaluation report are submitted"
