        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Check your age against the start date of the internship: you must be under 35 on that date, not on the application date",
            "Confirm your diploma was awarded by a Flemish educational institution; a Flemish diploma is the only nationality-neutral requirement",
            "Confirm your internship host is on the published list of qualifying multilateral organisations and that the location is a headquarters or field office within the jurisdiction of the Diplomatic Representations of Flanders",
            "Check the monthly amount for your host city before you commit, because the amount varies from 1,047.60 EUR (Lilongwe) to 2,721.97 EUR (Geneva)",
            "Work out the travel element: 200 EUR within Europe, 500 EUR outside Europe, nothing at all if the internship is in Belgium",
            "Have your identity card, Flemish diploma and letter of acceptance ready",
            "Get your internship supervisor to complete the attestation regarding the internship offer and send it to stages.dkbuza@vlaanderen.be",
            "Submit the online application form (Dutch) no later than one day before the internship starts",
            "If you have already started, submit immediately and check the remaining period is at least two months",
            "If the 2027 budget is your target, wait for applications to reopen in January 2027 and monitor the internships page for new vacancies from late 2026"
          ],
          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "Do not expect this to pay your way: it is a capped travel payment plus a city-based monthly lump sum, and it explicitly pays no tuition or course fees",
            "Do not apply while the budget is gone — an application submitted with no budget available is not processed and is not held over to the next year",
            "If you want the Flemish Growth Package/child benefit for the 12 months after your studies, do not accept a salary from the hosting organisation; the grant itself is fine but the salary kills the benefit",
            "If you already get paid or an allowance from the same organisation, another government, or another foreign government, expect the grant to be reduced by that amount — do not assume two pots of money stack",
            "Negotiate the unpaid or partly-paid placement deliberately: the monthly amount is fixed by city and does not scale with local cost differences beyond that matrix",
            "Do not skip the supervisor's attestation. Without it the application is not complete, and the supervisor, not you, has to send it",
            "Read the Dutch application form carefully if your Dutch is weak, and remember that the personal evaluation form is also only in Dutch"
