        "The applicant statement is mandatory and answers why you should be selected, how you will become an outstanding ambassador of CDU, your extracurricular activities with a focus on community engagement, work experience, creative arts and sport, and how you will use your CDU qualification to make a difference in your community.",
        "A declaration must be ticked confirming the information is true and correct, that you have read and understood the conditions of application, that the decision of the University selection panel is final, that you cannot hold more than one tuition fee scholarship from CDU at a time, that you do not hold another scholarship from an Australian or foreign sponsorship agency, and that you accept you may be asked to provide a student story or testimonial as a scholarship recipient.",
        "The form must be signed and dated.",
        "Ongoing eligibility: continue to be an international student liable for international student fees, pay your portion of tuition fees on or before the first day of teaching of each semester, maintain satisfactory academic progress each semester with a minimum GPA of 5.3 and no fail grade in any unit, and maintain a full-time enrolment of 40 credit points (0.5 EFTSL) each semester unless you have approval to reduce your study load or take a leave of absence for the semester."
      ],
      "english_requirement": "CDU requires all higher education applicants to satisfy the English Language Proficiency Requirements for their chosen course and to supply evidence of this at the time of application. CDU's published minimum English test scores are: IELTS Academic overall minimum 6.5 with no band below 6.0 for postgraduate and overall minimum 6.0 with no band below 6.0 for undergraduate; PTE Academic overall minimum 58 with no score below 50 for postgraduate and overall minimum 50 with no score below 50 for undergraduate; TOEFL overall minimum 79 with a minimum writing score of 21 for postgraduate and overall minimum 60 with a minimum writing score of 21 for undergraduate; Cambridge English Advanced overall minimum 176 with no skill below 169 for postgraduate and overall minimum 169 with no skill below 169 for undergraduate; CDU ELICOS EAP004 for postgraduate and EAP003 for undergraduate; and an approved English test completed within two years of commencement. IELTS One Skill Retake is accepted, allowing a single skill to be retaken within 60 days. Alternative evidence routes published on the same page include Year 12 in an approved English-speaking country, 0.5 FTE of higher education study in an approved country completed within the past five years where relevant, an enabling course, a TAFE qualification at Certificate III or higher, current AHPRA registration, two years of full-time equivalent employment in English-medium roles within the last five years in a recognised English-speaking country, or a primary language pathway declaration.",
