      "selection_notes": "CDU publishes the selection criteria as the overall score in your highest completed qualification plus a supporting statement. The application form adds that the decision of the University selection panel is final, and the declaration confirms the process is competitive. CDU publishes no interview requirement, no weighting for the two criteria, no offer round structure and no appeal process for VCIHAS; other CDU International College scholarships on the same page do publish an interview requirement, so confirm whether an interview applies to VCIHAS.",
      "notes": "This is not full funding: it covers 50% of the tuition fee only, and the recipient must pay their portion of tuition on or before the first day of teaching of each semester. The scholarship is neither transferable for cash nor refundable, and cannot be transferred to another person, semester, course or year. It is conditional rather than open-ended: it ends at the earliest of course completion, exhaustion of the maximum scholarship value, or loss of ongoing eligibility, and retaining it requires a minimum GPA of 5.3 with no fail grade in any unit and a full-time enrolment of 40 credit points (0.5 EFTSL) each semester unless a reduced load or leave of absence is approved. Only one CDU tuition fee scholarship may be held at a time, and holding another scholarship from an Australian or foreign sponsoring agency disqualifies the applicant. No deferral, return-home, clinical restriction, tax treatment or award renewal terms are published on the pages read. Official pages disagree on the statement length: the scholarship page says up to 600 words, the application form says 500 words or less.",
