      "notes": "This is not full funding and should not be budgeted as such: the published value is 20% off first-year tuition fees for one year only, and recipients pay the balance of all tuition fees by the prescribed date each session. ANU states recipients are responsible for the costs of books, study materials, accommodation and all other costs of study. The award can be offered only once at each level of study, with two published exceptions: progression from an undergraduate degree (AQF Level 7) to a one-year Honours program (AQF Level 8), and packaged offers such as a Graduate Certificate leading to a Master's degree. Eligibility is by residential status, not citizenship, and is restricted to China (including Taiwan, Hong Kong SAR and Macau SAR), Japan, Mongolia, the Republic of Korea and the Democratic People's Republic of Korea; residents of all other countries apply to the separate ANU International Achievement Award. Holding external sponsorship covering all or part of your ANU tuition fees disqualifies you. Deferral, renewal, return-home obligations, clinical restrictions and tax treatment are not published on the page read; the Conditions of Award (63/2026) PDF is the document that governs them and could not be read.",
