      "selection_notes": "Applicants are recruited and initially screened by the Japanese embassy or consulate general in their country, which sits its own qualifying examinations (Japanese and English for research students), conducts the interview and collects all required documents; MEXT then selects the scholarship students and allocates them to host graduate schools, subject to the host university's acceptance.",
      "notes": "No published deferral, renewal, return-home or clinical-restriction terms were readable on the official pages read. MEXT publishes rules on extending the scholarship period (applications for extension from newly admitted students in April 2026 and from early-completers are handled by notice), rules on combining the scholarship with other awards, and rules on part-time work by scholarship students, but these notices are in Japanese and were not readable in the English sources used for this record. Application is free of charge.",
