          "selection_notes": "Selection of applicants (host researcher) and candidate (invited overseas researcher) is done by the JSPS International Program Committee made up of Japan's frontline researchers. Selection is carried out through a document review in the first stage and a panel review in the second. Any reviewer with a potential conflict of interest is removed from the Review Committee for the relevant review, and all Members are obliged to comply with confidentiality and non-disclosure agreements. Document reviews are conducted by three examiners for each application, using a graduated scoring system on a scale 1 to 5 (5 superlative, 4 excellent, 3 good, 2 fair, 1 poor). Marks are made on a comprehensive basis taking into account research achievements, the research plan, estimated research capacity, and future potential of the research. The averaged score in the document review is used as the primary screening criterion in the panel review, through which a specified number of applicants are selected in each of the panel review sections.",
