      "application_period": "The 2027 Spring Semester international-track window (2026/08/18 - 2026/09/01) has closed. The next published window is Fall Admission (Early Track), Early December - Late December; the Fall 2027 Entry dates are published as TBA on the official timeline page.",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "KAIST's own scholarship for international graduate students, selected as part of the admission application rather than as a separate scholarship application. It covers full tuition fees plus national health insurance and a monthly stipend, and 94% of KAIST's international student body receive it. Two higher tiers are awarded automatically to those selected: the KAIST Global Presidential Scholarship (KRW 1,000,000 per month for 4 regular semesters) and the KAIST Prestige Scholarship for International Ph.D. Students (KRW 300,000 per month for 8 regular semesters). The published cost-of-study table shows the student still carries on-campus housing, food, books, travel and telecommunications costs.",
      "program_type": "University scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Non-Korean nationals applying to KAIST master's, Master's-Ph.D. integrated or Ph.D. programmes who meet KAIST's English proficiency requirement (or a published exemption) and can satisfy a doctoral or master's-level qualification by the start of the course.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to international applicants for KAIST graduate programmes who are citizens of countries other than Korea, hold a bachelor's degree (master's/Master's-Ph.D.) or a master's degree (Ph.D.) by the start of the course, and provide a qualifying English proficiency test score unless a published exemption applies.",
      "eligibility": [
