      ],
      "selection_notes": "Scholarship status is decided inside the admission process: applicants who select the KAIST scholarship as their financial resource in the application are automatically considered for the KAIST Scholarship and, where the degree programme matches, for the KGPS or the KPS. For the KGPS, no separate application is made and only highly competitive applicants will be recommended by the department head. For the KPS, applicants demonstrating outstanding academic and research achievements receive recommendations from the department head, with final selection by the college dean. KAIST states that 94 percent of its international students benefit from the scholarship and that the scholarship rate may vary by student.",
      "notes": "Not a standalone scholarship application: the award is attached to admission. The monthly stipend of the base KAIST Scholarship is stated to be dependent on research involvement, and no base stipend figure is published; KAIST also states the stipend amount may vary depending on individual colleges, with the College of Engineering publishing its own stipend terms separately. The KPS stipend for Master's-Ph.D. integrated entrants begins at the start of the Ph.D. programme, not on entry. The published Cost of Studying at KAIST figures are for the 2023 academic year. The Global Technology Innovation Program (GDI-GTIP Track) is excluded from KAIST Scholarship applications.",
