      ],
      "selection_notes": "Applications are initially scrutinised by the ICSSR Secretariat; an Expert Committee then reviews the applicant's research background, the quality of the paper to be presented and the academic credentials of the organising institution; recommendations go to the Research Committee/Council for final approval. The Council reserves the right to reject any application without assigning any reason and is not responsible for postal delays or loss.",
      "notes": "Not deferrable: the application will not be entertained or considered in any case after participation and presentation of the paper in the Conference. Not renewable in the sense that a scholar can avail of the award only twice in his/her lifetime, and a second application is considered only after a gap of three years. No must-return-home rule is published because this is a travel grant, not a degree award. Post-award: expenditure is reimbursed on submission of the original boarding pass, attendance certificate, statement of expenditure and a report on participation; ICSSR may ask for a copy of the tickets booked and the visa obtained before departure. Publication is expected in high valued journals/edited books/impactful reports with due acknowledgement of ICSSR, and the paper presentation should clearly display the ICSSR logo and its support. A second time application is not considered for poster presentations, session chairs, conveners, rapporteurs, or workshop/training/refresher/summer/winter course attendance.",
