      "description": "The ICSSR provides financial assistance to Indian social science scholars who need to travel abroad for data collection or to consult archival material in connection with their research. It is aimed at scholars who proposed fieldwork abroad in their original approved ICSSR fellowship or project proposal and have made substantial progress, or at independent scholars for whom data collection abroad is academically justified and the research is at an advance stage. The total expenditure on the foreign visit, including economy class airfare, visa fee, travel insurance, local conveyance and maintenance, is supported within the prescribed norms of Government notifications.",
      "program_type": "Government research fieldwork grant",
      "best_fit": "Indian social science faculty, Ph.D holders and PDF scholars at an advanced stage of research who need a short (up to two-week) funded research visit abroad to collect data or consult archival material.",
