      "selection_notes": "All eligible applications are comparatively evaluated by the Program Implementation Unit hired by the African Development Bank, and the final selection is approved by the JADS Secretariat. Evaluation focuses on educational and professional excellence, commitment to home country development priorities, the quality of the statement of purpose, financial status and geographic diversity of awardees. The Bank's management decision and approval of the finalist also takes into consideration geographical diversity, gender balance, equity and inclusiveness (unusual circumstances or hardships when assessing employment experience), financial needs (applicants are financially constrained), and special consideration for applicants with special needs.",
      "notes": "There is no separate application to the African Development Bank - \"Only candidates who have been offered admission and endorsed by the university will be considered for the JADS Program\", and a university admission offer alone is not a scholarship award. The scholarship \"may only supplement, and does not duplicate, any other source of financial support/fellowship you might have\"; finalists and awardees must inform the JADS Secretariat of other funding, and \"The JADS stipend may be withdrawn completely or partially if during the scholarship period the program has evidence of additional sources of support.\" Deferral and renewal are not addressed on the AfDB pages. Scholars \"are expected to return to their home countries and contribute to national and continental socio-economic development, using the newly acquired knowledge and skills.\" No clinical or field-of-practice restriction is published, but the approved master's courses are limited to energy, agriculture, health, environmental sustainability, engineering and related areas. \"The scholarship only covers the duration of the graduate program or two years, whichever is less.\"",
