      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Mandela Washington Fellowship for Young African Leaders is the flagship programme of the U.S. Government's Young African Leaders Initiative (YALI) and the exchange component of that initiative. It brings up to 550 young African leaders to the United States in the summer of 2027 for a six-week executive-style institute at a U.S. college or university, placed in groups of approximately 25, with an academic track of Business and Trade, Emerging Technologies, or Governance and Security. The 2027 instructions state that \"If you are selected for the Fellowship, the U.S. Government will cover all program costs\", listing J-1 visa support, round-trip travel from the Fellow's home city to the United States plus required domestic U.S. travel, the six-week institute, a limited accident and sickness benefit plan, housing and meals, and the optional four-week Professional Development Experience for up to 50 Fellows. It is not a degree programme and no tuition is charged or funded, and the U.S. Government does not pay for a Fellow's salary while away from work or for personal purchases. The programme is fully cost-covered for the six-week (or ten-week with PDE) stay, with no application fee.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship (U.S. Department of State educational and cultural exchange programme, administered by IREX)",
      "best_fit": "Citizens and permanent residents of any of the 49 listed Sub-Saharan African countries, aged 25 to 35 on the application deadline of 13 October 2026 (exceptional applicants aged 21-24 may be considered), proficient in reading, writing and speaking English, with a proven record of accomplishment in business and trade, emerging technologies, governance and/or security, and with a commitment to return to Sub-Saharan Africa. Applicants must not be U.S. citizens or permanent residents, must be eligible for a U.S. J-1 visa, must not be U.S. Government employees or their immediate family, and must not be alumni or prior participants of the Fellowship.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Must be aged 25-35 on 13 October 2026 (exceptional 21-24 applicants may be considered), a citizen and permanent resident of one of 49 listed Sub-Saharan African countries, proficient in English, J-1 visa eligible, not a U.S. citizen or permanent resident, not a U.S. Government employee or immediate family member, and not a previous Mandela Washington Fellow or participant.",
      "eligibility": [
