    {
      "name": "African Institute for Mathematical Sciences (AIMS) Structured Master's Scholarship - January 2027 intake (South African applicants)",
      "country": "South Africa",
      "degree_levels": "Master's",
      "funding_type": "Fully Funded",
      "official_source": "African Institute for Mathematical Sciences (AIMS), Muizenberg, Cape Town",
      "official_source_url": "https://aims.ac.za/academics/prospective_students/",
      "catalogue_url": null,
      "official_updates_url": "https://aims.ac.za/",
      "region": "South Africa (AIMS, 6 Melrose Road, Muizenberg, Cape Town); applicants must be citizens of any African country and resident in Africa, and this January intake is open to South African applicants only",
      "duration": "Structured Master's programme within AIMS's academic year, which \"kicks off in September and runs through until the end of June\"; the January intake begins in January and AIMS publishes no separate end date or programme length for it on this page",
      "deadline": "\"Applications are open from January to March.\" and \"For our Mathematical Sciences stream, we have a September intake, open January to March and a January intake (South African applicants) open August to October of the preceding year.\" No day-level closing date is published, so the January 2027 intake window is stated only as closing in October 2026, and no day has been inferred.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": null,
      "application_period": "Two published windows. September intake (African applicants): applications open January to March. January intake (South African applicants): applications open August to October of the preceding year. As at 2026-10-01 the only window still running is the January 2027 intake for South African applicants, open August to October 2026. The AI for Science stream is not part of this window because AIMS states: \"For the AI for Science stream we only have the September intake with applications open from January to March.\"",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The AIMS Structured Master's Scholarship funds a full postgraduate master's programme at the African Institute for Mathematical Sciences in Muizenberg, Cape Town. AIMS publishes the covered items as a complete package: flights to and from South Africa, airport transfers, medical insurance, tuition and research fees, a monthly stipend of R2,200, on-site accommodation at AIMS, and three meals a day at the AIMS canteen - so tuition, living costs, travel and health cover are all established by the institute. AIMS handles the money itself: \"the scholarship funds are managed by AIMS and are not paid into students' bank accounts\", with only the stipend paid directly into a South African bank account. There are two intakes, and on 2026-10-01 the live one is the January intake, which AIMS restricts to South African applicants with an application window of August to October of the preceding year; the Africa-wide September intake window (January to March) is closed. The AI for Science stream has only the September intake and is therefore also closed.",
      "program_type": "Institute scholarship (fully funded postgraduate award from the African Institute for Mathematical Sciences)",
      "best_fit": "Applicants who are citizens of any African country and resident in Africa at the time of application, hold a four-year undergraduate degree or a three-year undergraduate degree plus an honours year (or the French LMD equivalent of an M1 year) in physics, mathematics, statistics, computer science, engineering or another discipline with a strong computational and mathematical component, and have never previously held a scholarship to study at an AIMS centre. For the intake that is open on 2026-10-01, applicants must additionally be South African, and the degree must be completed by December.",
