      "selection_notes": "\"Shortlisted candidates will be invited for an online interview before final selections are made.\" AIMS publishes no scoring criteria, no weighting, no shortlist size and no results date, so selection beyond the interview stage is not documented on its public pages.",
      "notes": "Money is handled by the institute rather than by the student: \"the scholarship funds are managed by AIMS and are not paid into students' bank accounts. Students receive stipends, paid directly into their South African bank accounts. AIMS processes and covers all other expenses directly.\" Applicants are barred from applying if they have previously held a scholarship to study at an AIMS centre. The Africa-wide September intake is closed for the year, so the live window in October is the South African applicant intake only, and the AI for Science stream has no January intake. AIMS publishes no deferral rule, no renewal rule, no return-home obligation and no disciplinary or clinical restriction, so those fields are left null rather than assumed. AIMS does publish a residency exception: \"The residency requirement is not applicable to students who are displaced by war.\"",
