          "source_conflict_rule": "AIMS presents two streams and three windows on a single page. Where the general statement \"Applications are open from January to March\" could be read as covering all intakes, the stream-specific sentence is treated as authoritative: it names the Mathematical Sciences stream's January intake and separately restricts the AI for Science stream to the September intake. The homepage claim of \"full scholarships\" is read together with the itemised seven-item package on the prospective students page rather than on its own.",
          "source_freshness_rule": "The prospective students page carries no visible last-updated stamp, so the intake windows and the R2,200 stipend are treated as current-as-at-read but unversioned. Because the window is expressed in months only and the whole package is small enough to change between cohorts, any applicant relying on this record should re-read the prospective students page and the live portal in the same week they apply, and must not assume next year's window or amount is unchanged.",
