      "description": "The University of Glasgow Sanctuary Scholarship supports applicants with refugee or asylum seeker status who are living in the UK and hold an offer to study at the University in the 2027/28 academic year, covering undergraduate and postgraduate taught entry in September 2027/28. It provides a full tuition fee waiver for applicants who cannot access mainstream funding through Student Awards Agency Scotland or Student Finance, together with a £5,000 per year stipend towards study costs. Six scholarships are available, and applying also puts a candidate forward for a small number of donor-funded awards that cover the £5,000 stipend only.",
