      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Ernst Mach Grant – worldwide finances short research stays in Austria for young researchers from all disciplines and all countries except Austria. The published grant benefit is a supplementary monthly grant of EUR 1,300, together with assistance in arranging accommodation and health insurance, but scholarship holders pay the costs of accommodation and insurance themselves and must show own funds. Tuition fees at Austrian public universities and universities of applied sciences do not have to be paid by grant holders, and may be waived upon request to the rectorate, but this does not apply to private universities and private colleges. Holders from listed non-European developing countries also receive a travel costs subsidy of up to EUR 1,200 upon submission of original travel invoices.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Postgraduates enrolled in a doctoral/PhD programme outside Austria, postgraduates and postdocs who completed their studies at a university outside Austria after 30 September 2025 and want to pursue research in Austria with a view to an academic career, and postdocs working as researchers at a university outside Austria, all aged 35 or under at the start of the stay.",
      "funding_amount": 1300,
      "funding_currency": "EUR",
      "funding_period": "per month",
      "eligibility_summary": "Young researchers from countries other than Austria, aged 35 or under at the start of the stay, who are pursuing a PhD outside Austria or who completed their studies abroad after 30 September 2025, and who have a written supervision confirmation from an Austrian university lecturer.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Eligible for application are: a. Postgraduates pursuing a doctoral/PhD programme outside of Austria; b. Postgraduates and postdocs wishing to pursue research in Austria with a view to an academic career and who completed their studies (at a university outside of Austria) after 30 September 2025; c. Postdocs who are working as researchers at a university outside of Austria",
        "Applicants must not have lived/studied/pursued research/pursued academic work in Austria in the last six months before taking up the grant",
        "Applicants who have completed their academic education mainly in Austria (does not apply to applications by Postdocs) or who are already permanently residing in Austria are not eligible to apply",
        "Maximum age: 35 years (born on or after 01 October 1991)",
        "Country of origin: all except Austria",
        "Language skills: very good knowledge of English and/or German",
        "Consent of a lecturer at the Austrian target university to supervise the applicant academically is a required document",
        "The scholarship will only be granted for projects that can be completed within the scholarship period (max. 9 months)"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Monthly grant rate: 1,300 Euro",
        "Assistance in arranging accommodation and health insurance (scholarship holders have to pay the costs for accommodation and insurance themselves)",
        "Grant holders do not have to pay tuition fees in Austria; tuition fees may be waived upon request to the Rectorate of the public university or university college of teacher education for the semesters in which studies or research can be shown to have been completed elsewhere, i.e. as part of transnational EU, state or university mobility programmes; any tuition fees at universities of applied sciences may be waived by the rectorate upon application",
        "Scholarship holders with citizenship and travel from non-European developing countries (Least Developed Countries, Low Income Countries and Lower Middle Income Countries and Territories according to the DAC list, plus Gabon, Malaysia, Namibia, South Africa, Thailand) or for their return will also receive a travel costs subsidy of up to 1,200 Euro upon submission of original travel invoices"
