        "Await the expert evaluation; results are expected at the beginning of July 2027"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "The selection follows a multistage process: 1. Examination of the formal requirements; 2. Examination of the application's general plausibility; 3. Assessment and evaluation of the application by experts; 4. Final decision by the BMFWF. Incomplete applications and applications not complying with the application criteria will not be accepted for the further selection process. All formally valid applications are then evaluated by experts from the respective field and the selection committee awards the best applicants. The selection is competitive, i.e. there is no legal claim to a grant even if all application requirements are fulfilled; the number of grants awarded during one call depends on the quota and/or the available budget.",
      "notes": "Grant period is 1 to 9 months and must be consumed by the end of 2028. Extensions are not possible for this grant. The earliest possible start is September 2027 (the Austrian academic year 2027/28). Stay dates must consist of full months only, starting on the first of a month and ending on the last; short-term grants of 1 month should be consumed in February or September. Applicants must have interrupted any stay in Austria for at least six months before taking up the grant. Gainful employment is not allowed, with a marginal employment exemption of EUR 551.10 per month in 2026. A final report is obligatory at the end of the stay. The grant contract (Letter of Award and Letter of Acceptance) defines start and end date, grant amount, payment modalities, compulsory attendance at the guest institution, performance report and final report, data protection and repayment obligations. The grant cannot be used to enrol in a Master or PhD programme in Austria. Without written proof of accommodation in Austria, a residence permit is not granted. Applicants from non-EU/EEA countries planning a stay of more than 6 months whose accommodation costs exceed EUR 386.43/month may need to prove additional funds to the Austrian residence authority.",
      "image_url": "https://www.oead.at/fileadmin/Dokumente/oead.at/00_site_config/OeAD_logo.png",
      "image_source_url": "https://oead.at/en/study-research-teaching/overview-grants-and-scholarships/ernst-mach-grant",
      "image_source_type": "official_government",
      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
      "image_alt_text": "OeAD, Austria's Agency for Education and Internationalisation",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Ernst Mach Grant programme is named after the Austrian physicist and philosopher Ernst Mach (1838-1916) and is financed by the Austrian Federal Ministry of Women, Science and Research (BMFWF). The Ernst Mach Grant – worldwide is a supplementary grant for young researchers from all countries except Austria who wish to pursue a research project in Austria for 1 to 9 months. The published grant benefit is a monthly grant rate of EUR 1,300 plus assistance in arranging accommodation and health insurance, with own funds required.",
          "purpose": [
            "To promote research cooperation",
            "To promote young academics in the early stages of their scientific career",
            "To establish an effective network of researchers with relations to Austria"
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [],
          "degree_levels": [
