            "PhD students",
            "PhD holders, post docs"
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Research stay in Austria",
            "Visiting scholar stay (not a degree programme)"
          ],
          "degree_award": "Short-term award – not a full or partial degree. The Ernst Mach grant is not intended to finance a complete or parts of a regular PhD, Master or study programme in Austria",
          "duration": "1 to 9 months",
          "application_cycle": "Annual cycle for the Austrian academic year 2027/28; online application possible from September to 1 December 2026, 23:59 CET; expert evaluation after the deadline; results expected at the beginning of July 2027; grant must be consumed by the end of 2028",
          "deadline_central": "2026-12-01",
          "deadline_central_display": "01.12.2026 (December 1st, 2026, 23:59 CET)",
          "deadline_institutional": "None published – a single central OeAD deadline applies",
          "deadline_note": "The grants.at entry gives the closing date as 01.12.2026 and the OeAD FAQ states the application deadline as December 1st, 2026, 23:59 (CET) for all applications for stays during the academic year 2027/28. Both are consistent.",
          "status": "OPEN",
          "funding_type": "Partial Funding",
          "funding_label": "Supplementary grant, own funds are required – monthly grant rate EUR 1,300 plus assistance in arranging accommodation and health insurance",
          "funding_amount": 1300,
          "funding_currency": "EUR",
          "funding_period": "per month",
          "tuition_coverage": "Grant holders do not have to pay tuition fees in Austria. Tuition fees may be waived upon request to the Rectorate of the public university or university college of teacher education for the semesters in which studies or research can be shown to have been completed elsewhere, i.e. as part of transnational EU, state or university mobility programmes. Any tuition fees at universities of applied sciences may be waived by the rectorate upon application. This does not apply to tuition fees at private universities and private colleges.",
          "living_cost_coverage": "Only a supplementary monthly grant rate of EUR 1,300. The grant benefit is explicitly labelled 'Supplementary grant, own funds are required'; scholarship holders have to pay the costs for accommodation and insurance themselves.",
          "travel_coverage": "Scholarship holders with citizenship and travel from non-European developing countries (Least Developed Countries, Low Income Countries and Lower Middle Income Countries and Territories according to the DAC list, plus Gabon, Malaysia, Namibia, South Africa, Thailand) or for their return also receive a travel costs subsidy of up to EUR 1,200 upon submission of original travel invoices.",
          "fully_funded": false,
          "tuition_rule": "Grant holders do not have to pay tuition fees in Austria; tuition fees may be waived upon request to the Rectorate of the public university or university college of teacher education for semesters in which studies or research can be shown to have been completed elsewhere (transnational EU, state or university mobility programmes). Tuition fees at universities of applied sciences may be waived by the rectorate upon application. No waiver at private universities or private colleges.",
          "home_tuition_rule": null,
          "host_institution_fee": "Scholarship holders pay accommodation and health insurance costs themselves. Health insurance costs are estimated at the moment at EUR 55 to EUR 200 per month depending on age, scholarship category and state of health.",
          "tax_status": null,
          "covered_expenses": [
            "Monthly grant rate of EUR 1,300",
            "Assistance in arranging accommodation and health insurance (advice/arranging only, not payment)",
