          "host_requirements": [
            "Consent of a lecturer at the Austrian target university to supervise the applicant academically (must use the OeAD template, including date, signature and stamp)",
            "The Austrian academic supervisor has to confirm that the project can be done in English",
            "All Austrian universities are eligible to host grant awardees; the supervisor must not also write a letter of recommendation",
            "If the Austrian host is a research institute that is not technically a university, eligibility is assessed individually by the OeAD and the supervision confirmation must come from a supervisor who works at the institute and teaches at a university",
            "Without written proof of accommodation in Austria, a residence permit is not granted",
            "Grant holders must be continuously present at their place of study in Austria and must observe the current conditions of the host institution regarding attendance/participation",
            "Applicants who seek admission to a university in Austria have to contact the institution of their choice directly; the application for a scholarship does not yet require admission to a University of the Arts"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Submit everything through the online application at www.scholarships.at",
            "Upload two letters of recommendation by university lecturers and the consent of an Austrian lecturer to supervise",
            "Upload passport scan, graduation certificate scan and the level-specific confirmation",
            "Fill in all sections of the online application thoroughly and observe the minimum number of words – an upload of a research proposal is not necessary",
            "Declare any use of generative AI in the application, documenting which AI tools were used and to what extent",
            "Abide by the no-gainful-employment rule, with the marginal employment exemption of EUR 551.10 per month in 2026",
            "Consume the grant by the end of 2028",
            "Submit a final report at the end of the scholarship stay"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Two letters of recommendation by university lecturers (no specific form required; must contain the letterhead, date and signature of the person recommending the applicant and the stamp of the university/department, and must not be older than six months at the time of application)",
            "Consent of a lecturer at the Austrian target university to supervise the applicant academically (OeAD template required, including date, signature and stamp)",
            "Scanned copy of your passport (page with the name and photo)",
            "Scanned copy of your university graduation certificate of your diploma, master, PhD or doctoral studies",
            "Only for PhD-students: confirmation that proves your participation in a PhD-programme at your home university",
            "Only for postdocs: confirmation that proves your employment at your home university"
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "Letters of recommendation can be freely worded but must contain a letterhead, date and signature of the person recommending the applicant and the stamp of the university or department",
            "For the supervisor's confirmation letter, the OeAD template must be used, including date, signature and stamp",
            "All letters must be no older than six months at the time of application",
            "Documents submitted after the deadline cannot be accepted",
            "A valid, biometric passport must be uploaded; an identity card is only acceptable for applications from the EU",
            "Only original signatures or certified digital signatures are accepted; a non-certified digital signature requires proof such as an institution stamp on the document, and where no university stamp is available the signature must be a genuine wet-ink signature, not copied or inserted digitally, with genuine (not copied) letterhead and a date included",
            "If it cannot be verified that a document is official, the application is considered formally invalid",
            "If documents are in English, a translation into German is not necessary; if they are neither in English nor German, upload a copy of the original plus an English or German translation",
            "Officially certified translations are not required; a rough English or German translation is sufficient",
            "When providing a translation, always upload the copy of the original as well – this applies to diplomas and to confirmations of employment or enrolment at a university",
            "Normally letters of recommendation are uploaded by the applicant into the online application account; if professors do not hand out signed letters, ask them to send scanned attachments to the OeAD by e-mail, and ensure they arrive before the deadline",
            "No separate upload of a research proposal is required; the research activities are described in the online application sections",
            "File size limits and accepted file types are not published on the pages read"
