      "selection_notes": "Assessment is carried out by an academic committee appointed by FCT and FLAD. Criterion A: candidate's curriculum, considering academic grades, track record and scientific achievements including peer-reviewed publications, scholarships, prizes, conferences and project participation (40%). Criterion B: scientific quality, innovative character of the work plan and feasibility of the research activities to be developed (30%). Criterion C: motivation letter explaining the relevance of the stay and the work to be developed for the scientific ambition of the doctoral work plan, and the expected impact of the stay on the candidate's career (30%). Selection is based on the analysis of these criteria, producing a positive or negative opinion, with final classification CF = 0.4 A + 0.3 B + 0.3 C.",
      "notes": "Applications are open on a rolling basis and are assessed in quarterly windows, so an application can be submitted at any time before closing; the call closes early if the annual quota is reached. Selected candidates must finance their own travel, accommodation and health insurance. Arrival at UC Berkeley cannot occur earlier than six months after selection for the programme. The call is governed by the published Expression of Interest Call (Chamada de Manifestação de Interesse) and the accompanying documents (Memorandum of Understanding Portugal_Berkeley_Program, FCT-CPS-Berkeley Protocol, model letter, Research Scholarships Regulation, Table of Scholarship-related Subsidies (2025), and the assessors' college).",
