      "application_period": "The 11th edition ran 20 April 2026 to 11 May 2026 at 6:00pm Italian time and is closed, with 1634 applications received, 982 eligible and 211 scholarships awarded. The official site carries the banner 'NEW APPLICATION OPENS 2027!' / 'IL NUOVO BANDO APRE NEL 2027!', so the next edition is announced but no opening date, closing date or application window has been published.",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "Invest Your Talent in Italy is a MAECI scholarship programme run with the ICE Agency and Uni-Italia that pays a nine-month scholarship to foreign students from 22 partner countries to attend a Master's or Postgraduate course at a participating Italian university, combined with a compulsory internship at an Italian company or professional association. Courses are taught entirely in English, and the programme includes study of Italian language and culture plus a mandatory gender-equality and anti-gender-violence seminar or module. The winner receives an annual scholarship of EUR 10,800, paid quarterly into an Italian bank account in the holder's name, and is exempt from enrolment fees and university contributions, but must still pay the regional right-to-education tax, stamp duty, accident and civil liability insurance and health insurance. The scholarship explicitly does not cover travel expenses and does not include accommodation, and the recipient must independently arrange health insurance.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Students aged 25 or under (born on or after 1 January 2000) who hold a qualification valid for enrolment in a participating Italian Master's or Postgraduate course, permanently resident in one of the 22 listed partner countries, and not already studying at or graduated from an Italian university.",
