        "Course listings are published on the basis of a written undertaking by the relevant Rector, subject to withdrawal within 60 days if the university's governing bodies do not ratify participation"
      ],
      "english_requirement": "Courses are taught entirely in English. Applicants must attach certification of English language proficiency from level B2 of the Common European Framework of Reference (Cambridge, IELTS, TOEFL iBT, ISE Digital – Trinity College, ISE Paper – Trinity College, PTE, Linguaskill, ESOL, TOEIC covering listening, reading, speaking, writing). Candidates who obtained a university degree at the end of a degree course taught in English may submit a university certificate attesting that English was the language of instruction, accepted as proof of level C1. A separate requirement exists for Italian: certification issued by the institution where the training was undertaken, or a declaration of commitment to attend a classroom or self-study Italian course before departure; Italian certification is not mandatory but contributes to the evaluation score.",
      "application_method": [
        "Apply for pre-admission to a chosen IYT course directly with that university, following the university's own procedures, within the deadlines set by the Technical Committee",
        "Register on the IYT portal (My-App) using name and surname exactly as printed on the passport",
        "Upload the required documents: final transcript with CGPA (or the dated and signed university statement if the certificate is pending), English proficiency certification from B2, Italian certification or commitment declaration, a video of no longer than 59 seconds, a one-page CV, and a valid passport",
        "Submit the application online during the published call window",
        "Await the Technical Committee's comparative evaluation; successful candidates are informed by email to the registration address"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Examination and evaluation of applications is carried out by the Technical Committee of the IYT Program (MAECI, ICE and Uni-Italia), which may use an ad hoc commission. Scholarships are allocated in quotas defined for each country and awarded on the basis of a comparative evaluation of the applications against the requirements in Articles 3 and 5 of the call. The Design Scholarship quota is allocated using specially drawn-up rankings that take into account the order of preference for courses given by the student, as is the Borse Ateneo quota.",
      "notes": "Renewable: IYT scholarship holders may apply to continue the second year of the Master's by uploading a university certificate of exams taken (CFU), a certificate of attendance for an Italian language course (and, for the 11th edition holders, an internship project) by 20 July 2027; renewal and fee exemption for the second year are conditional on achieving 30 credits by 20 July 2027 and verified regular attendance of the university's Italian language course. All scholarship recipients must complete the paperwork for the start of their internship by 20 January 2027. Incompatible: the IYT scholarship cannot be combined with any other scholarship or financial benefit from the Italian Government or any public institution (e.g. Erasmus+), including scholarships offered by Italian regions under regional education programmes. Must fund separately: the scholarship does not cover travel expenses and does not include accommodation, and the recipient must independently arrange health insurance covering illness and accidents in Italy. Not covered even after fee waiver: regional tax for the Right to Education, stamp duty, accident and/or civil liability insurance costs, and health insurance. Restrictions on mobility: the scholarship only covers attendance at courses in Italy. Award is conditional on the positive outcome of the Court of Auditors legality review.",
