      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "RESTART is an FCT funding instrument that competitively finances individual R&D projects in all scientific domains for researchers who have recently taken a parental leave, including adoption leave. The award is a project grant of up to EUR 50,000 per project for a maximum of 18 months, drawn from a total budget allocation of EUR 1.6 million, and it is held by the beneficiary R&D unit rather than paid as a personal living stipend. Candidates must hold a doctorate, be an integrated doctoral member of an R&D unit or hold a contract with a State laboratory, and have taken a parental leave of at least 120 days (or at least 72 days in a shared leave, whether exclusive or shared) between 3 June 2025 and 1 October 2026 inclusive.",
      "program_type": "Research grant",
      "best_fit": "Doctorate-holding researchers, including foreign and stateless researchers, based at a Portuguese FCT-funded R&D unit or State laboratory, who have taken a qualifying parental or adoption leave between 3 June 2025 and 1 October 2026 and can obtain a commitment from their host institution.",
