      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Fundação para a Ciência e a Tecnologia (FCT), alongside its commitment to promoting the advancement of scientific and technological knowledge, aims to promote gender equality in R&D activities and careers, inseparable from equality of opportunity for the whole national scientific community. With this objective FCT launches the 4th edition of the RESTART programme. RESTART is intended to promote gender equality and opportunity through the competitive funding of individual R&D projects in all scientific domains, when carried out by researchers who have recently taken a parental leave, including for adoption. Aligned with public policies in this area, RESTART also covers, with specific eligibility conditions, cases of shared parental leaves. By empowering a competitive return to research activity in new circumstances, RESTART will support researchers in pursuing and developing an original and innovative research idea, with the possibility of associating other human and/or material resources, according to the funding made available and the planned execution time. This funding instrument is aligned with the concerns and recommendations of various international bodies, namely the Council of the European Union and the OECD.",
          "purpose": [
            "Promote gender equality and equality of opportunity in R&D activities and careers",
            "Competitively fund individual R&D projects in all scientific domains",
            "Enable researchers who have recently taken a parental leave, including for adoption, to return competitively to research activity",
            "Support the development of an original and innovative research idea, optionally with associated human and/or material resources",
            "Cover shared parental leave cases with specific eligibility conditions, favouring equality in care provision and the sharing of family responsibilities and leave durations",
            "Better reconcile professional and family life for those working in R&D"
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [
            "Gender equality is the programme's stated policy objective (promover a igualdade de género nas atividades e carreiras de I&D) rather than a formal SDG requirement attached to the award",
            "The instrument is aligned with concerns and recommendations of the Council of the European Union and the Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development that promote better reconciliation of professional and family life for those engaged in R&D"
          ],
          "degree_levels": [
            "PhD"
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Individual research project",
            "Competitive research grant"
          ],
          "degree_award": "Not a degree award. RESTART funds an individual R&D project of up to 18 months; no degree, certificate or qualification is awarded.",
          "duration": "Maximum of 18 months of project development.",
