      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "A*STAR Graduate Scholarship (AGS) funds up to four years of PhD or EngD study at an autonomous university in Singapore, jointly supervised by an A*STAR researcher and a university faculty member, with research conducted at an A*STAR Research Institute. Support published for up to 4 years comprises full tuition fees, a monthly sustenance allowance inclusive of CPF contribution where applicable, book, computer, conference and thesis allowances, and support for up to 12 months of overseas attachment. Monthly allowance is a published matrix by track and residency status: AGS (STEM) $4,500 for Singapore Citizens, $4,100 for Singapore Permanent Residents and $3,600 for International Students; AGS (Specialised Tracks: Semiconductor, Quantum, Computing) $6,200, $5,600 and $5,000 respectively.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Final-semester undergraduates and Master's students at, or on track to graduate from, a Singapore autonomous university, and mid-PhD students already enrolled in a Singapore autonomous university, who want to do a research-intensive PhD at an A*STAR Research Institute. International students without Singapore Permanent Residence should be comfortable with a 3-year service commitment in a Singapore-based company.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants of all nationalities may apply, but international students must have completed or be on track to obtain a Bachelor's or Master's degree in a Singapore autonomous university, hold at least a Second-Class (Upper) Honours degree or equivalent, be in the last semester of final studies (full-term) or minimally one semester into a Singapore AU programme (mid-term), and satisfy PhD admission criteria at an autonomous university.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Study at an autonomous university in Singapore",
        "Open to applicants of all nationalities. International Students applying must have completed or on track to obtain a Bachelor's or Master's degree in a Singapore Autonomous University (AU)",
        "Obtained or on track to obtain at least a Second-Class (Upper) Honours degree or equivalent in a relevant discipline",
        "Be in the last semester of their final studies to apply",
        "Satisfy the criteria for and gain admission to a PhD programme in an autonomous university",
        "Mid-Term AGS applicants: open to applicants of all nationalities; International Students applying must have completed or on track to obtain a Bachelor's or Master's degree in a Singapore Autonomous University (AU)",
        "Mid-Term AGS applicants: obtained or on track to obtain at least a Second-Class (Upper) Honours degree or equivalent in a relevant discipline",
        "Mid-Term AGS applicants: enrolled in a Singapore autonomous university and minimally completed at least 1 semester at the point of scholarship application",
        "Mid-Term AGS applicants: on track to attain excellent academic standing for current degree",
        "Mid-Term AGS applicants: good research potential and/or achievements",
        "Mid-Term AGS applicants: current university supervisor to be at least 1 out of the 2 academic referees",
        "The above eligibility criteria are not exhaustive. A*STAR may include additional selection criteria based on prevailing scholarship policies. These policies may be amended from time to time without notice."
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Full tuition fees",
        "Monthly sustenance allowance, inclusive of CPF contribution (where applicable)",
        "Book allowance",
        "Computer allowance",
        "Conference allowance",
        "Thesis allowance",
        "Support for up to 12 months of overseas attachment"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Specialised tracks in Semiconductor, Quantum and Computing offer a higher stipend than the AGS (STEM) track",
        "Bond-free scholarship for Singapore citizens and Singapore Permanent Residents",
        "12-month overseas attachment opportunity (AGS scholars may be funded to conduct research at an overseas university/lab for a minimum period of 3 months and up to one year max, midway through the PhD, subject to supervisor endorsement and existing overseas collaborations)",
        "AGS scholars can apply for the A*STAR International Fellowship (AIF), an overseas postdoctoral attachment of up to 2 years after PhD completion, fully funded by A*STAR; the AIF can be applied for within 4 years after completion of the PhD",
        "Participation in Vista, A*STAR Graduate Academy's signature developmental programme series for scholars"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Before applying, identify and engage both an A*STAR researcher and a university faculty member who are willing to collaborate on the project and co-supervise the PhD",
        "In consultation with both supervisors, develop a research proposal that aligns with your research interests and contributes to Singapore's Research, Innovation and Enterprise (RIE) ecosystem",
        "Obtain endorsement from the A*STAR supervisor",
        "Applicants need to apply separately to obtain admission to the intended partner university; the AGS award is conditional upon awardees obtaining confirmation of placement at one of the partner universities",
        "AGS applicants should apply for university admission concurrently with the scholarship application",
        "Scholars are required to satisfy the coursework requirements specified by the University conferring the PhD degree; graduation requirements shall be in accordance with the prevailing rules for the PhD degree applicable at the university",
        "Please have your CV ready before creating your account to apply for the scholarship"
      ],
      "english_requirement": null,
      "application_method": [
        "Have your CV ready before creating your account to apply for the scholarship",
        "Identify a research project and both supervisors (an A*STAR researcher and a university faculty member)",
        "Develop the research proposal in consultation with both supervisors",
        "Apply for admission to the intended partner university concurrently with the scholarship application",
        "Obtain endorsement from the A*STAR supervisor",
        "Submit the online scholarship application with all supporting documents",
        "Nominate at least 2 academic referees who will receive an auto-generated email with a link to complete an online referee report",
        "Attend at least 2 rounds of interviews",
        "Successful candidates are notified via email"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Referees can be academic referees from universities or supervisors/PIs whom you have worked with. There will be at least 2 rounds of interviews involving the senior management of the Biomedical Research Council or Science & Engineering Research Council, and researchers from A*STAR's Research Entities. The nomination of supervisor(s) has to be approved by A*STAR; in most cases the main and co-supervisors should hold at least the designation of Principal Investigator or Principal Scientist at an A*STAR RI. Final approval of the PhD supervisor(s), research project and university for successful applicants is subject to A*STAR's approval. A*STAR makes a holistic assessment of each application and takes into consideration factors such as achievements in science/maths related competitions and CCAs; prior research experience helps but is not mandatory. The application process typically takes about 5 months from submission of a complete application to notification of results.",
      "notes": "Bond-free for Singapore citizens and Singapore Permanent Residents. Foreigners who are non-SPRs must serve a 3-year service commitment in Singapore-based companies, without commitment to any specific organisation; Singapore-based companies refer to local companies and international companies that have a base in Singapore and which is registered with the Accounting & Corporate Regulatory Authority (ACRA). The area of work should preferably be in Biomedical Sciences, Physical Sciences, Engineering or Computing and Information Sciences. Not deferrable within the 4-year funding period without approval: if you need more time to complete your PhD you will have to seek approval from A*STAR's management for your PhD extension. A*STAR does not pay for consumables or research fees; fees involved in the lab should be borne by the university. All scholars need to seek A*STAR's written permission before changing your course of study/research project. Mid-term applicants receive the same terms of support as full-term AGS awardees from the point of the award, with retrospective payment for all tuition fees and/or any compulsory fees from Year 1 of study onward. All rates/allowances are subject to adjustments by A*STAR from time to time. A pre-application Master's degree is not required.",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "Whether you're looking to explore broad scientific fields or dive deep into a specialised area, AGS offers full funding, access to world-class research labs, and the chance to take on a 12-month overseas attachment during your PhD. Begin your research journey at an A*STAR Research Institute, and shape the future of science, technology, and innovation.",
          "purpose": [
            "A*STAR Graduate Scholarship (STEM): enabling aspiring researchers to pursue PhD studies in biomedical sciences, chemistry, physics, engineering, and related fields. Scholars gain research experience at A*STAR and contribute to impactful work.",
            "A*STAR Graduate Scholarship (Semiconductor): supporting students in chip design, materials science, and semiconductor technologies. Scholars gain hands-on experience and help Singapore grow as a global hub for semiconductor talent and innovation.",
            "A*STAR Graduate Scholarship (Quantum): advancing talents in quantum computing, communications, and sensing. Scholars drive cutting-edge research and discoveries that strengthen Singapore's position in quantum technologies.",
            "A*STAR Graduate Scholarship (Computing): nurturing leaders in AI, cybersecurity, software engineering, and data science. Scholars tackle real-world digital challenges and build expertise to power Singapore's growth as a tech-driven nation.",
            "AGS is a collaboration between A*STAR and local Autonomous Universities (AUs). Scholars will be jointly supervised by both the A*STAR and University supervisors.",
            "The research proposal should align with your research interests and contribute to Singapore's Research, Innovation and Enterprise (RIE) ecosystem."
          ],
