      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The National Science Scholarship (PhD) funds up to five years of PhD study at a top overseas institution for applicants who will serve a bond in Singapore's research ecosystem. Published support for up to 5 years comprises full tuition fees, a monthly sustenance allowance inclusive of CPF contribution where applicable, a monthly overseas living allowance, annual return airfare, conference, thesis, computer and settling-in allowances, and language programme fees where the scholar studies in a non-anglophone country. Successful candidates must complete a compulsory one-year research attachment at an A*STAR research institute before commencing PhD studies, and must convert to Singapore citizenship no later than the third year of the PhD if they are not already citizens.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Singapore citizens, Singapore permanent residents, and foreign nationals who intend to take up Singapore citizenship and are in the last semester of an undergraduate degree in a relevant discipline, seeking to do a research PhD at a leading overseas university with the intention of returning to contribute to Singapore's R&D sector.",
