      "selection_notes": "2 academic referee reports are required and must be submitted within 7 working days of submission of the online application; referees will receive an auto-generated email with a link to complete an online referee report, so applicants are advised to give referees a heads-up before applying. Referees can be academic referees from universities or supervisors/PIs whom you have worked with. For shortlisted candidates, there will be 2 rounds of interviews: the first round with a panel of A*STAR scientists and the final round with the senior management of A*STAR. The scholarship application process typically takes about five months from the submission of a complete application to the notification of results. As these are national scholarships, all applications will be treated equitably and reviewed holistically such as on academic track record, publications and research exposure/experience.",
      "notes": "Bond period: 4 years. Upon completion of the PhD programme, NSS (PhD) scholars will return to Singapore and contribute to A*STAR's research institutes and/or relevant organisations for 4 years. Scholars who complete their PhD in a non-anglophone country would serve a 3-year service commitment instead. Non-Singaporeans must take up Singapore citizenship no later than the third year of the PhD. A*STAR does not pay for consumables or research fees; fees involved in the lab should be borne by the university. If you need more time to complete your PhD beyond the funding period, you will have to seek approval from A*STAR's management for your PhD extension. All scholars need to seek A*STAR's written permission before changing your course of study/research project. Applicants with prior research experience at A*STAR (beyond their undergraduate Final Year Project) may request a waiver of the compulsory research attachment year, subject to approval; however, scholars are strongly encouraged to complete the attachment. Mid-term awardees receive the same terms of support as full-term NSS (PhD) awardees from the point of the award, with retrospective payment for all tuition fees and/or any compulsory fees from Year 1 of study onwards. All rates/allowances vary according to country and university, and are subject to adjustments made by A*STAR. If you are currently holding a scholarship for your undergraduate studies from another government ministry/agency, the page advises clarifying the policy and guidelines from your sponsoring organisation before applying to A*STAR.",
