      "description": "The Nanyang President's Graduate Scholarship is NTU President's premier PhD scholarship, tenable for up to 4 years for a full-time PhD at NTU with no bond attached. It pays the annual tuition fee plus a monthly stipend published by citizenship status - S$5,300 for Singapore Citizens, S$4,800 for Singapore Permanent Residents and S$4,300 for International Students - with CPF contributions on top for citizens, and with overseas conference, book, IT and thesis allowances. International students must perform teaching or laboratory supervision duties to satisfy the Graduate Assistantship Programme requirement. There is no separate scholarship application: candidates are considered through the normal NTU research degree application by indicating interest in the 'NTU Scholarship'.",
