            "Part-time (PhD only, under a continuing pilot scheme)"
          ],
          "degree_award": "Full postgraduate degree at the University of Cambridge (PhD, MLitt or a one-year postgraduate course). Not a short-term award.",
          "duration": "PhD: maintenance awarded for up to 4 years. MLitt and one-year postgraduate courses: 12 months, with maintenance paid pro rata for shorter courses.",
          "application_cycle": "Annual. Two selection rounds each year, both opening on 11 September 2026 for entry in the academic year 2027/8: an October round for US citizens resident in the USA, and an international round aligned with the University of Cambridge postgraduate funding competition.",
          "deadline_central": "2026-10-14",
          "deadline_central_display": "Wednesday 14th October 2026 (US citizens resident in the USA; full application must be submitted by 11:59pm UK time)",
          "deadline_institutional": "All other eligible applicants: dependent on the course - either Tuesday 8th December 2026 or Wednesday 6th January 2027, as published in the Course Funding Deadline column of the University of Cambridge Course Directory. Full application must be submitted by 11:59pm UK time.",
          "deadline_note": "Two separate published deadlines exist for this open cycle. The record's deadline_date 2026-10-14 is the earlier, October round, which is restricted to US citizens who are currently resident in the United States. Applicants from every other eligible country must use their own course's Course Funding Deadline, which is either 2026-12-08 or 2027-01-06. Applicants who are US citizens but studying or working overseas at the time of application must apply in the later round. US citizens resident in the USA are not eligible for the later round.",
          "status": "OPEN",
          "funding_type": "Fully Funded",
