          "funding_period": null,
          "tuition_coverage": "The University Composition Fee at the appropriate rate. The fee varies by type of student; applicants should see the Graduate Studies prospectus for exact amounts. Where a student has already secured a fee award from public authorities (such as UKRI) they should accept that award, and the Trust will not pay their fee or may share their fee and maintenance costs.",
          "living_cost_coverage": "A maintenance allowance for a single student of £23,152 for 12 months at the 2026-27 rate, paid pro rata for courses shorter than 12 months. For PhD scholars the award is for up to 4 years.",
          "travel_coverage": "One economy single airfare at both the beginning and end of the course. The Trust does not fund other fieldwork costs.",
          "fully_funded": true,
          "tuition_rule": "The Gates Cambridge Trust pays the University Composition Fee directly as part of the scholarship for the whole of the eligible course. The Trust may reduce or decline the maintenance allowance if the scholar already holds a salary or another substantial scholarship. If the scholar has been successful in gaining a fee award from public authorities such as UKRI, the scholar should accept that award instead, and the Trust will not pay the fee or may share fee and maintenance costs.",
          "home_tuition_rule": "Not published. The Gates Cambridge pages do not state whether tuition at a home-country institution continues during the award. Because the award is for study at the University of Cambridge, no home-country tuition rule is addressed on any official page read.",
          "host_institution_fee": "No separate host fee is published. The relevant published charges are the University Composition Fee (covered by the Trust) and any college-related costs, which are not itemised on the Gates Cambridge pages read.",
          "tax_status": null,
          "covered_expenses": [
