              "Approximately two-thirds of the annual awards are offered to PhD students",
              "The maintenance award runs for up to 4 years",
              "PhD applicants must submit a research proposal as part of the application for funding",
              "Fieldwork may be undertaken while keeping up to the normal maintenance allowance; other fieldwork costs are not funded"
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "The applicant must secure an admission offer and a College place at the University of Cambridge through the standard postgraduate admissions process.",
            "The applicant's academic department at Cambridge must nominate them; a relatively small number of applicants are nominated and invited to interview.",
            "The department or course must publish a Course Funding Deadline in the University Course Directory, which sets the applicant's application deadline.",
            "Core course costs such as bench fees and scientific equipment are expected to be covered by the Cambridge academic department rather than by the Trust."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Complete the admission to a course and a College place section of the Graduate Application Portal",
            "Complete the funding section including the Gates Cambridge sub-section",
            "Answer the four Gates Cambridge selection questions within the published character limits",
            "Submit a research proposal (PhD applicants only)",
            "Provide two academic references for admission",
