          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "Documents should be in PDF format",
            "Documents must be under 2MB",
            "Documents must not be encrypted ('If you are having difficulty uploading a document it may be encrypted or too large')",
            "Upload scanned originals to the Applicant Portal; you will not be able to submit an application without the required documents",
            "If your documents are not in English, you must upload a full translation of each document prepared by a registered translator - 'Do not translate the documents yourself'",
            "Cambridge cannot accept any documents that have been written on or defaced in any way",
            "Do not send hard copies of documents, as these cannot be processed and will be disposed of",
            "No hard-copy route exists; everything is uploaded via the Applicant Portal by the relevant application deadline",
            "References are excluded from the applicant upload: referees must upload their reference via the Referee Portal",
            "Applying for more than one course requires separate uploads for each course, and a referee nominated for multiple applications must submit a separate reference for each course",
            "Gates Cambridge selection questions carry hard character limits: approx. 200 words / up to 1,400 characters for academic excellence and for reasons for the course; approx. 300 words / up to 2,100 characters for commitment to improving the lives of others and for capacity for leadership",
            "The Gates Cambridge reference may be pasted or typed up to 4,000 characters or uploaded as a separate letter",
            "If applying for a second Cambridge degree of the same type, a Declaration form must be completed and submitted",
            "If an offer is made, original documents must be sent so Cambridge can verify their authenticity; a secure electronic document transfer service such as Parchment Digitary or Qualification Check may be used (Qualification Check charges a fee, removable if an application fee waiver was granted)"
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "outstanding intellectual ability",
            "reasons for choice of course",
            "a commitment to improving the lives of others",
            "leadership potential"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Gates Cambridge uses a two-stage selection process to ensure Scholars meet all criteria to the highest level. Stage 1, departmental nomination: academic departments nominate a small number of eligible applicants who meet all four criteria to a very high level; only those nominated are invited to interview. Stage 2, interview: a 25-30 minute interview, in person or virtually (in-person attendance encouraged where possible), with one of four subject-based panels - Arts, Biological Sciences, Physical Sciences and Social Sciences - each made up of experienced academics and practitioners and possibly Gates Cambridge alumni and a Trust representative. Interview sections: (1) welcome and introduction; (2) Gates Cambridge - what you know about the Scholarships, your motivation, why you could be a Scholar, your thoughts on the opportunities and responsibilities; (3) academic and career plans - your academic work to date, your proposed degree, your career plans, and possibly probing intellectual or ethical questions with no 'right' answers; (4) final thoughts and questions, optional. Scholars are then selected after interview. Gates Cambridge states it is not able to provide feedback to unsuccessful applicants. The four selection questions and the Gates Cambridge reference are used to distinguish between candidates nominated by academic departments.",
          "application_method": [
            "Combined online application: admission and funding are submitted through the University of Cambridge Graduate Application Portal (Applicant Portal at apply.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk).",
            "Complete the admission section (specific graduate course and College place, usual details about yourself, academic background, plans and suitability).",
            "Complete the funding section and the Gates Cambridge sub-section, answering the four selection questions.",
            "Upload documents via the Applicant Portal; referees upload references via the Referee Portal.",
            "Gates Cambridge has access to the full application for admission and funding when reviewing applications."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "Check the University of Cambridge Course Directory and note the Course Funding Deadline for your course (8 December 2026 or 6 January 2027 for the international round).",
            "Confirm you are an eligible applicant: non-UK citizen applying to a Cambridge PhD (full-time or part-time), MLitt (full-time) or one-year full-time postgraduate course, and not applying for an excluded course.",
            "If you are a US citizen currently resident in the USA, you must apply in the October round with a deadline of 14 October 2026.",
            "Contact prospective supervisors; for PhD applications, agree and develop the research proposal.",
            "Prepare supporting documents before starting: transcripts and certificates for each degree, CV, personal statement, research proposal (PhD), and any written work or GRE score the course requires.",
            "Register on the Applicant Portal and start the application.",
            "Complete the admission section: choose the course and a College, and give academic background, plans and suitability.",
            "Complete the funding section and answer the four Gates Cambridge selection questions within the character limits.",
            "Upload scanned original documents as PDFs under 2MB and unencrypted; upload a registered-translator translation for any document not in English.",
            "Nominate two academic referees and a third Gates Cambridge referee; brief the Gates Cambridge referee on the four selection criteria and the competitive nature of the programme so the reference addresses the scholarship rather than repeating a standard academic reference.",
            "Submit the application before the deadline; you may submit before references are uploaded, but both academic referees and the Gates Cambridge referee must have submitted their references by the specified deadline.",
            "Track departmental ranking (late October to November 2026 for the US round; December to February for the international round) and await the outcome notification.",
            "If departmentally nominated, attend the 25-30 minute panel interview in late January 2027 (US round: 22-23 January 2027) or 22-23 March 2027 (international round).",
            "If offered a scholarship, accept within 72 hours of the offer."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits their own application online through the University of Cambridge Applicant Portal; there is no nominating institution in the application step.",
            "Referees submit their references themselves through the Referee Portal.",
            "Gates Cambridge and the Cambridge academic department then act on the submitted application; departmental nomination follows."
          ],
          "application_portal": "https://apply.postgraduate.study.cam.ac.uk/applicant/login (University of Cambridge Applicant Portal, referred to by Gates Cambridge as the Graduate Application Portal)",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Scholars must tell the Trust ASAP if they are awarded any other funding towards their degree at Cambridge, and the Trust reserves the right to reduce or not pay the standard maintenance allowance where a salary or another substantial scholarship is held",
            "Where a scholar has secured a fee award from public authorities such as UKRI they must accept that award; the Trust will not pay their fee or may share fee and maintenance costs",
            "Core course costs such as bench fees and scientific equipment are expected to be covered by the Cambridge academic department, not by the Trust",
            "Discretionary funding (academic development, dependent children, fieldwork, maternity/paternity, hardship) is applied for separately and is awarded at the Trust's discretion",
            "Scholars must not apply for Gates Cambridge funding to complete the remainder of a course they have already started",
            "Where a scholar receives a salary or substantial other scholarship, the Trust may reduce or decline the maintenance allowance",
