      "description": "The UJMT LAUNCH programme is a 12-month, full-time mentored global health research training fellowship funded by the NIH Fogarty International Center and delivered by a consortium of UNC Chapel Hill, Johns Hopkins, Morehouse School of Medicine and Tulane. It places trainees at core research sites in Africa, Asia and the Americas with at least one U.S. and one international mentor. Two award types exist: a Full award (monthly stipend, research funds, health insurance plus emergency medical and evacuation insurance, and travel funds) and a Travel and Research award (the same package without the monthly stipend). Research support is capped at up to USD 10,000 for postdoctoral and up to USD 7,000 for U.S. doctoral trainees. No stipend figure is published.",
