          "selection_criteria": [
            "Targeted funding is expected for proposals on HIV, mental health and neurological disorders",
            "Programme support for projects across a wide range of research topics",
            "Mentor review of application materials prior to submission",
            "At least two mentors, including one U.S. and one international member providing on-site supervision"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "The UJMT pages publish priorities rather than a scoring rubric. Targeted funding is expected for proposals on HIV, mental health and neurological disorders, although the programme supports projects across a wide range of research topics. Among eligible U.S. candidates from any institution, applicants from the four consortium universities may be given priority. Among doctoral applicants, those in later stages of training - for example following comprehensive examinations or after clinical rotations - will be given priority. The application guidance requires all materials to be reviewed by mentors before submission and requires at least two mentors. A recorded application information webinar is published for applicants. No interview process, review panel composition, award announcement date or successful-applicant profile is published on the pages read.",
          "application_method": [
            "Online application through the UJMT application portal, with a Start Application link published on the programme page.",
            "Letters of recommendation are emailed directly by the mentors to FGHFP@med.unc.edu rather than uploaded.",
            "Programme questions are directed to the named contact at UNC."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "Watch the published recorded application information webinar if you want the applicants' own walkthrough.",
            "Confirm your eligibility: U.S. citizen or permanent resident, or a citizen of a country with UJMT-affiliated research institutions; and for postdoctoral applicants, completion of an MD, PhD, DrPH, DVM, PharmD or equivalent by July of the academic year.",
            "Confirm you can defer your studies for the full 12 months if you are a doctoral applicant, and that you are in a later stage of training if you want priority.",
            "Choose the award type you are seeking - the Full award with the monthly stipend, or the Travel and research award without it.",
            "Secure at least two mentors, including at least one U.S. mentor and one international mentor who is living and working full-time at your chosen site.",
            "Review the proposed research design extensively with your U.S. mentor and your international site mentor.",
            "Draft the research proposal to the published structure: Specific Aims; Research Plan with Significance, Innovation and Approach; timeline for the proposed scope of work; Human Subjects describing the IRB process and approval timeline; with references outside the two-page limit.",
            "Draft the one-page budget and justification within the caps (up to USD 10,000 postdoctoral, up to USD 7,000 U.S. doctoral), and the one-page statement of career goals.",
            "Draft the one-page plan for mentorship, specifying areas of mentorship and the frequency of meetings or calls with the mentorship committee.",
            "Complete and format the NIH Biosketches for yourself and for both primary mentors.",
            "If you are an international postdoctoral applicant, draft the Short-Term U.S.-based Training Attachment with up to three key learning objectives, courses with dates at your U.S. host's home institution, other workshops and conferences, and the relevance to your research project.",
            "If you are jointly supported by another programme or grant, obtain a letter from that programme's PI or director stating the amount and duration of the support.",
            "Have a mentor or mentors review all application materials before submission.",
            "Format everything single-spaced with 0.5\" margins in Arial 11-point font.",
            "Submit the application online by the October 1 due date and ensure your mentors email their letters directly to FGHFP@med.unc.edu by that date."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
