      "description": "The Whitley Awards recognise grassroots conservation leaders who are already delivering measurable, science-based conservation impact and give each awardee GBP 50,000 of project funding over one year to scale that work up. Applicants must be nationals of the country where they work, embedded in local communities, and backed by an experienced team or organisation, and the project must deliver practical, measurable conservation action for threatened ecosystems and biodiversity at the landscape or seascape level with tangible benefits for Indigenous peoples and local communities. Applications are made directly through WFN's online portal, with no invitation or nomination needed, and include a logical framework/timeline on the current-year Word template, a budget on the current-year Excel template, and three referees who must submit their references by the deadline. Winners also receive international recognition, media and communications support, peer training and collaboration opportunities, and eligibility for future Continuation Funding and the Whitley Gold Award.",
