    {
      "name": "Mandela Rhodes Scholarship (Class of 2028)",
      "country": "South Africa",
      "degree_levels": "Master's, Honours (postgraduate)",
      "funding_type": "Fully Funded",
      "official_source": "The Mandela Rhodes Foundation",
      "official_source_url": "https://www.mandelarhodes.org/scholarship/apply/",
      "catalogue_url": "https://www.mandelarhodes.org/scholarship/apply/",
      "official_updates_url": "https://www.mandelarhodes.org/news-impact/categories/news/",
      "region": "South Africa (study must be in South Africa) - for citizens of any African country",
      "duration": "Maximum two years of funding; one year for an Honours degree, one or two years for a Masters",
      "deadline": "Applications for 2028 will open 9 March 2027. Applications close by the end of Wednesday, 14 April 2027 23:59 GMT+2.",
      "deadline_date": "2027-04-14",
      "deadline_precision": "day",
      "application_period": "The applications timeline runs from March to November of each year for the following year's intake. For the Class of 2028: applications open Tuesday 9 March 2027 and close 14 April 2027 23:59 GMT+2.",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The Mandela Rhodes Scholarship funds a one-year Honours degree or a two-year Masters degree in any field at a recognised South African institution of higher education, and pairs it with a compulsory Leadership Development Programme of residential workshops and regional pods. The Foundation states it offers comprehensive funding for the core costs of study: tuition and registration fees, a study materials allowance, research and conferencing grants on request, a medical aid allowance, accommodation and meal allowances, a personal allowance, and economy-class flights between the scholar's home country and their South African institution at the start and end of the degree. The Foundation does not pay university application fees, SAQA accreditation of existing degrees, or visa application costs. Specific allowance amounts are set by the Foundation and no figures are published.",
      "program_type": "Foundation postgraduate scholarship with leadership development programme",
      "best_fit": "African citizens aged 19 to 29 in the year of applying, with an undergraduate degree above 70% or an upper-second class Honours, who intend to study an Honours or Masters degree in South Africa and can commit to the compulsory leadership programme.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Citizen of an African country, aged 19 to 29 in the year of applying, with an undergraduate degree completed by 1 January 2028 with above 70% or upper-second class results, and able to study at postgraduate level in English.",
      "eligibility": [
        "I can study at a postgraduate level in English",
        "I am a citizen of an African country",
        "I am between the ages of 19 and 29 in the year of applying",
        "By 1 Jan 2028, I will have an undergraduate degree with excellent academic results (above 70% or upper-second class Honours)",
        "I aspire to be an ethical leader and I am committed to using my talents to advance equality, freedom and human dignity in Africa",
        "I admire Nelson Mandela's ability to bridge divides and bring people together around our common humanity",
        "I am prepared to reflect deeply on my own leadership and undergo a process of personal change and growth"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Tuition and registration fees as set by the scholar's university or institution",
        "A study materials allowance as set by the MRF",
        "Accommodation and meal allowances as set by the MRF",
        "A medical aid allowance as set by the MRF",
        "A personal allowance as set by the MRF",
        "Research and conferencing grants, which can be made available on request",
        "Economy-class flights for international scholars from their home countries to their institutions at the start and end of their studies"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Participation in the Leadership Development Programme of week-long residential workshops and regional pods",
        "Optional participation in the Mentoring Programme"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Apply online through the Foundation's applications platform",
        "Three letters of recommendation, in English, submitted by the referees directly through the application platform",
        "Upload certificates of completion for your degrees",
        "Upload transcripts of your academic results, in English",
        "Upload scans of your ID and passport documents",
        "Write two short essays: one on your personal journey, and one on a specific question relating to the Foundation's principles",
        "State your proposed course of study; proof of having applied to a university is not required"
      ],
      "english_requirement": "You must be able to do written and verbal academic work, in English, at a postgraduate level. English is the main medium of tuition at South African universities. The Foundation states its own test as a self-check and does not publish a required IELTS or TOEFL score on this page.",
      "application_method": [
        "Register on the Foundation's applications platform after applications open on 9 March 2027",
        "Add three recommenders on the platform before the close",
        "Upload certificates, transcripts, ID and passport scans and both essays",
        "Have the three recommenders sign in to the platform and upload their English letters",
        "Submit the complete application before 14 April 2027 23:59 GMT+2"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "The Foundation looks for young leaders who aspire to leadership, reconciliation, education and entrepreneurship, and who demonstrate the combination of intellect and character. Applicants are screened in rounds: a notification by mid-July indicates whether the applicant reached Round Two, by end of July for Round Three, and by end of August whether they are invited to a Final Round interview. Final Round interviews are conducted in South Africa in October, and final-round applicants based outside South Africa are flown in for an in-person interview with the selection committee. Selected scholars are notified by the end of October.",
      "notes": "The scholarship cannot be deferred: you must accept it for the year it is offered. Attendance at the residential workshops and regional pods is mandatory and a condition of the scholarship, and the Foundation will not accept travel outside South Africa, even for research purposes, as a reason for absence. You may not hold other scholarships or funded opportunities and may not do paid work for more than 12 hours a week. The award is conditional on you being offered a place at a South African institution, and the Foundation does not apply to universities for you. If you are not accepted by a South African institution in time, you cannot accept the scholarship. The Foundation does not pay visa application costs, and states that a delayed visa may mean you cannot start on time and could lose the scholarship. Applicants from outside South Africa may need SAQA verification, which the Foundation states can take 4-8 weeks and is not covered by the award. Any amount you owe prior to becoming a Scholar is your sole responsibility. The Foundation does not fund MBAs, block courses, or courses delivered predominantly online, and distance learning is not allowed.",
      "image_url": "https://www.mandelarhodes.org/uploads/190eb61b-acd4-4d81-946b-6af253c887b6.png",
