          "selection_criteria": [
            "Leadership: 'Do you aspire to be a visionary leader who has moral authority?' and to pursue the advancement of equality and freedom, human rights and human dignity, and to guide and inspire others",
            "Reconciliation: belief that reconciliation combined with reparation is the key to harnessing an imperfect past to develop a more just world, starting by looking at one's own internal landscape",
            "Education: excellent academic results, belief that education should make a difference for others, and agreement that intellectual excellence must be accompanied by character and a rounded personality",
            "Entrepreneurship: the wish to see Africa take its rightful place as an equal and competitive presence in the global world, with demonstrated individual effort, innovation and creativity",
            "Academically strong: marks should be above 70% or an upper second",
            "Demonstrated leadership on campus or in the community",
            "Readiness for the personal, internal work of leadership: self-awareness, openness to learning from the diversity and differences in the cohort, and a willingness to explore complexity",
            "The combination of intellect and character"
          ],
          "application_method": [
            "Register on the applications platform when applications open on 9 March 2027",
            "Add three recommenders on the platform",
            "Upload degree certificates, transcripts, ID and passport scans, and both essays",
            "Have the three recommenders log on to the platform and upload their English letters",
            "Submit the completed application before 14 April 2027 23:59 GMT+2"
          ],
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "The Scholarship must be accepted for the year it is offered and cannot be deferred",
            "Must have secured admission to the university of choice by January of the year in residence",
            "Must attend and participate in all activities of the Leadership Development Programme, including the residential workshops and regional pods; attendance is a condition of the Scholarship unless there are exceptional circumstances agreed to by the Foundation. There are three workshops in the first year in residence and two in the second year on a two-year programme, and dates are given well in advance",
            "Scholars completing a two-year Master's programme are required to fully participate in the Second Year Programme activities during their second year in residence",
            "Travel outside South Africa, even for research purposes, will not be accepted as a reason for absence",
            "Full-time study only; may not be held simultaneously with paying work exceeding a maximum of 12 hours per week. In such cases the Foundation must be kept fully informed on the nature and terms of the additional work and must give its consent",
            "May not hold other scholarships and funded opportunities. If offered any additional funding, communicate directly with the Foundation",
            "Must uphold the values, principles and standards of the Foundation and maintain evidence-based, high standards of work and conduct as determined by the Trustees and/or the Foundation; failing this the MRF may cease payments to and participation in the Programme by the Scholar",
            "Must be younger than 30 years of age at the time of taking up the Scholarship",
            "Must adhere to the principles and goals of the Scholarships Programme",
            "Completing feedback forms and reflections timeously is a requirement",
            "Must not change institution of study from the one indicated on the application unless in exceptional circumstances explicitly approved by the MRF",
            "Should the Scholar fail to comply with the requirements for continued study in the course for which they are registered, financial support from the MRF ceases",
            "Must undertake to reply timeously and comprehensively each year, during residence and thereafter, to a written electronic request from the MRF for an update of personal details",
            "May be offered access to a Mentoring Programme, which is optional",
            "Where specific donors underwrite a Mandela Rhodes Scholarship, reasonable requests from the donor made in good time should be acceded to where possible, and if declined the Scholar must supply reasons on time"
