          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "The Mandela Rhodes Foundation. Contact page: https://www.mandelarhodes.org/contact/. Application platform: accessed through https://www.mandelarhodes.org/scholarship/apply/. Tips and alerts signup: http://eepurl.com/ikEc1v. Terms and conditions of the Scholarship: https://www.mandelarhodes.org/uploads/41e8a286-4dea-4e11-a2ec-108530a9d189.pdf",
            "email": "Ernst@mrf.org.za — the address the Foundation's published Terms and Conditions (clause 2, 'Other Scholarships may not be held in conjunction with a Mandela Rhodes Scholarship. If offered any additional funding please communicate directly with Ernst (Ernst@mrf.org.za)') give for reporting additional funding. No general admissions contact email or postal address is published on the pages read."
          },
          "citizenship_residency": "Citizens of an African country, no matter where they are currently living or studying. Study must be in South Africa, at a South African institution of higher education; study in the applicant's home country and distance learning are not allowed.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
          "purpose": [
            "Combine financial support with a compulsory leadership development programme that 'will challenge you, grow you, and connect you to young African changemakers' (Explore & apply page).",
            "Equip young African leaders with the competence and courage to transform the continent into a place where everyone has equal opportunity to thrive, keeping Nelson Mandela's legacy alive (Explore & apply page).",
            "Build a pipeline of ethical African leaders by selecting scholars who aspire to leadership, reconciliation, education and entrepreneurship and who demonstrate the potential to live them out (How are Mandela Rhodes Scholars selected).",
            "The programme is built on the Foundation's founding principles of reconciliation, education, entrepreneurship and leadership, and on 'a belief that leadership begins with inner transformation' (Explore & apply page).",
            "Produce scholars who use their talents to advance equality, freedom and human dignity in Africa, and who reflect deeply on their own leadership and undergo a process of personal change and growth (eligibility character statements)."
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [
            "No SDG, development goal or impact-reporting requirement is published. The Foundation publishes four founding principles (reconciliation, education, entrepreneurship, leadership) and states that its programme is delivered through workshops, regional pods and an optional Mentoring Programme, but it does not frame any part of the scholarship against the UN Sustainable Development Goals or Agenda 2063.",
            "The Foundation does ask scholars, after the scholarship, to reply to written requests for updates of personal details so that the MRF can report on its impact — but this is an alumni reporting duty, not an SDG alignment requirement."
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Postgraduate degree study: a one-year Honours degree or a one-to-two-year Master's degree, or their academic equivalents",
            "Full-time study only; distance learning is not allowed",
            "Paired with a compulsory Leadership Development Programme of residential workshops and regional pods, with in-person and online gatherings"
          ],
          "degree_award": "A full accredited postgraduate degree, not a short-term award. The Scholarship funds a one-year Honours degree or an up-to-two-year Master's degree (or academic equivalents) at a South African-located tertiary institution registered with the South African Council of Higher Education and approved by the MRF. The degree itself is awarded by the university, not by the Foundation.",
          "tuition_rule": "The MRF pays tuition and registration fees as set by the Scholar's university or institution, and pays them directly to the tertiary institution rather than to the Scholar (Explore & apply FAQ 'How do the finances work'; Terms and Conditions clause 3). Payment is conditional: allowances and fees are released twice a year against proof of registration and a progress report from the institution no later than two weeks after the start of the second semester. If a Scholar receives a rebate from the institution, the MRF will not refund the amount of the rebate (Terms and Conditions clause 4). A Scholar who fails to comply with the requirements for continued study in the registered course loses MRF financial support (clause 7).",
          "home_tuition_rule": "Not applicable as a funding rule: the Scholarship cannot be used to study in the applicant's home country. The Foundation states that the scholarship is for study in South Africa, at a South African institution of higher education, and that distance learning is not allowed, because the Scholar must be at a South African institution in order to participate in the Leadership Development Programme.",
          "host_institution_fee": "Tuition and registration fees are paid by the MRF directly to the tertiary institution, as set by that institution. University application fees are not paid by the MRF. A Scholar may not change their institution of study from the one indicated on their application unless in exceptional circumstances explicitly approved by the MRF (Terms and Conditions clause 5).",
          "tax_status": null,
          "covered_expenses": [
            "Tuition and registration fees as set by the university or institution (paid directly to the institution)",
            "Study materials allowance as set by the MRF",
            "Accommodation and meal allowances as set by the MRF",
            "Medical aid allowance as set by the MRF",
            "Personal allowance as set by the MRF",
            "Research and conferencing grants, which can be made available on request",
            "Economy-class travel allowance for international Scholars only, from the Scholar's home to their institution at the beginning and end of their degree"
