          "official_fields_confirmed": [
            "The Class of 2028 opens 9 March 2027 and closes 14 April 2027 23:59 GMT+2, with no late or incomplete applications accepted (Explore & apply page)",
            "Full funding scope: tuition and registration fees, study materials, accommodation and meal, medical aid, personal allowances, research and conferencing grants on request, and economy-class travel for international Scholars at the start and end of the degree (Explore & apply FAQ; Terms and Conditions clause 3)",
            "Explicit not-covered list: university application fees, SAQA accreditation of existing degrees, and visa application support (Explore & apply FAQ 'What costs are not covered?')",
            "Payment mechanics: allowances paid twice a year against proof of registration and a progress report no later than two weeks after the start of the second semester; tuition and registration fees paid directly to the institution (FAQ and clause 3)",
            "Rebate principle: the MRF does not refund an institutional rebate received by the Scholar (clause 4)",
            "Degree scope: one-year Honours or up-to-two-year Master's degree or academic equivalents, at a South African institution registered with the CHE and approved by the MRF (clause 1)",
            "Not funded: undergraduate study, MBAs, block courses, courses delivered predominantly online, distance learning, and study outside South Africa (Explore & apply FAQs)",
            "Tenure cap of a strict maximum of two years with no exceptions; one year for Honours, one or two for Masters (FAQ; clause 1)",
            "Conditions of tenure including no deferral, compulsory workshop and pod attendance, full-time study only, the 12-hour paid work limit, the prohibition on holding other scholarships, and the Foundation's right to cease payments (Explore & apply page; clause 2)",
            "Two-year Masters Scholars must fully participate in Second Year Programme activities (clause 1)",
            "Institutional change requires exceptional circumstances and explicit MRF approval (clause 5)",
            "Loss of funding if a Scholar fails to comply with the requirements for continued study in the registered course (clause 7)",
            "Annual personal-update undertaking during residence and thereafter (clause 8)",
            "No responsibility for bodily injury, sickness, accident or death; Scholars must insure themselves (clause 9)",
            "Selection round-by-round notifications, October in-person interviews in South Africa, and end-of-October selection notification (Explore & apply Step 1)",
