            "No file size limit, no accepted file-type list, no translation rule and no document-expiry rule are published for any document on the pages read. The only format rules published are that the ID must be valid, clear and accessible, must display the headshot, full name and date of birth, must match TEFConnect exactly, and that documents submitted in the wrong format are rejected with feedback rather than accepted"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "The process runs in six phases after application. Applications are immediately and automatically reviewed when the window closes and applicants are notified via TEFConnect and email of their category. Independent third-party experts review applications deemed eligible, assessing the business idea for feasibility, scalability, market potential and financial viability. Shortlisted applicants undergo LSEG World-Check screening, a global risk-intelligence database, to ensure compliance with global financial and business regulations, then a Physical Verification Exercise by authorised enumerators to confirm identity and the legitimacy of the business documents provided, conducted by physical visit or virtually. Only applicants who pass application review, global compliance and physical verification are considered for the cohort. Successful applicants are notified of participation confirmation on 22 March each year. In the investment readiness phase, an independent audit consulting firm reviews the business plan, financial projection and pitch video, indicates areas of improvement, and ranks participants on investment readiness. In the seed capital phase the TEF Audit and Finance team reviews the disbursement documents.",
          "application_steps": [
            "The application portal opens on 1 January and closes at midnight on 1 March each year on the TEFConnect digital platform.",
            "Register on TEFConnect and complete the programme's application form with valid and accurate responses, across four sections: personal information; business idea and experience information; business assessment test; declaration.",
            "Complete all mandatory fields in the online application form.",
            "Attach the requested documents: a valid government-issued ID displaying date of birth and photo, and a high-resolution headshot. Ensure the name and personal details on TEFConnect exactly match the government-issued ID.",
            "Submit the form.",
            "Receive a notification on screen and by email confirming eligibility status and next steps.",
            "Applicants classified ineligible may reapply the following year; there is no appeal route in the published process.",
            "If confirmed as a participant, attend the onboarding session, physical or virtual, and then complete 100% of all training modules on TEFConnect, participate in coaching sessions and engage with the assigned mentor.",
            "Submit a business plan, financial projection and a 2-3 minute pitch video using the templates supplied, for independent audit review and investment-readiness ranking.",
            "Open a business account at one of the partner banks the Foundation lists, so fund tracking and disbursement are easier.",
            "Submit the seed capital documents: government-issued ID, Business Registration Certificate, evidence of tax registration in the business name, a bank reference letter, a Partner Consent form if a co-owner, and a medical report from a reputable hospital if living with a disability.",
            "Sign the TEF Entrepreneurship Programme seed capital undertaking so that payment can be processed into the business account.",
            "Receive the acknowledgement form, the Certificate of Completion and Achievement, and onboarding into the TEF Alumni network."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits their own application directly. There is no institutional nomination, university submission, referee-mediated submission or intermediary: registration and submission are on the applicant's TEFConnect account.",
            "Physical verification may involve an authorised enumerator visiting the applicant, or being conducted virtually, so the applicant must be reachable at the address and number given on the application.",
            "The seed capital is paid into the business account the participant provides, so the participant must personally control and open that account."
          ],
          "application_portal": "www.TEFConnect.com - the TEFConnect digital platform. The Foundation states the application portal for the flagship programme opens on 1 January and closes at midnight on 1 March on this platform.",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "deferrable": null,
          "renewable": null,
          "return_home_required": null,
          "clinical_restriction": null,
          "arrival_rules": [],
          "timeline_rules": [
            "The application window opens on 1 January and closes at midnight on 1 March every year.",
            "Applications are reviewed immediately and automatically after the window closes; applicants are notified via TEFConnect and email of their category.",
            "Participation confirmation for shortlisted applicants is issued on 22 March each year.",
            "Shortlisted participants are invited to an onboarding session, physical or virtual, after which they are referred to as TEF Entrepreneurship Programme Participants.",
            "The Training Phase follows onboarding and requires 100% completion of all modules on TEFConnect before progression.",
            "The Investment Readiness Phase requires submission of the business plan, financial projection and pitch video, followed by independent audit review and ranking.",
            "The Seed Capital Phase follows successful investment-readiness ranking, with document submission, Audit and Finance endorsement, signature of the seed capital undertaking, and disbursement.",
            "No fixed dates are published for the training, investment readiness and seed capital phases; they are cohort-relative and announced at onboarding."
          ],
          "official_application_route": [
            "Register and apply on the TEFConnect digital platform at www.TEFConnect.com between 1 January and midnight on 1 March in the year of application.",
            "Complete all four sections of the application form, upload the government-issued ID and high-resolution headshot, and submit.",
            "Complete any required physical or virtual verification with TEF's authorised enumerators.",
            "On confirmation, attend onboarding and complete the training, investment readiness and seed capital document requirements directly, without institutional intermediation.",
            "The Foundation does not accept applications by email, post or through a university; TEFConnect is the only published application route."
          ],
          "program_type": "Philanthropic entrepreneurship and seed capital programme",
          "region": "Africa-wide; applicants must reside in Africa and establish their business in Africa"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Register on TEFConnect before 1 January so your account exists when the window opens",
            "Confirm you are 18 or older, live in Africa, and will build the business in Africa",
            "Check you have never received a TEF programme award and have not already applied in the same window of the same year",
            "Prepare a government-issued ID showing your date of birth and photo, and make sure your TEFConnect name and personal details match it exactly",
            "Take a high-resolution headshot",
            "Practise the business assessment test, because a minimum score is the first gate and a fail means waiting a full year",
            "Have a business idea or a business registered no more than five years ago, with a clear value proposition and market opportunity"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Failing to reach the minimum score in the business assessment test; the Foundation notifies you as ineligible and only invites reapplication the following year",
            "Name or personal details on TEFConnect that do not match the government-issued ID exactly",
            "An unclear, inaccessible or invalid government-issued ID, or a low-resolution headshot",
            "An ID that does not show the date of birth or photo",
            "Business older than five years with no qualifying new idea",
            "Previous benefit from any TEF programme, or a prior application in the same application window",
            "Failing the LSEG World-Check compliance screening or the physical verification exercise",
            "A business plan, financial projection or pitch video that the independent audit firm does not rate as investment ready",
            "Seed capital documents that are not endorsed by the TEF Audit and Finance team, which requires resubmission in the correct format",
            "Seed capital documents found inauthentic or discrepant, which lead to immediate disqualification"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Your own living expenses for the whole cycle: the award is USD 5,000 of business seed capital and no living cost support is published",
            "Any tuition or training fees if you want formal business education alongside the programme",
            "Business registration and tax registration costs, if not already completed before applying",
            "Costs of setting up or running the business beyond the USD 5,000 seed capital",
            "Costs associated with world-check and physical verification, if any are charged to the applicant"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Government-issued ID: National Driver's Licence, International Passport, or Permanent Voter's Card, the last applying to Nigerian participants only",
            "The ID must clearly display your headshot and full name, and both must match your TEFConnect registration",
            "Business Registration Certificate must clearly capture the name of the business",
            "Tax registration evidence must be in the business name, not your personal name",
            "Bank reference letter must clearly capture your name as registered on TEFConnect and on your ID, the business name, and the business bank details",
            "Partner Consent form is only required if you are a co-owner of the business",
            "Medical report from a reputable hospital is only required if you live with a disability",
            "Pitch video must be 2-3 minutes long; business plan and financial projection should use the Foundation's expert-developed templates",
            "Resubmission is allowed if the TEF Audit and Finance team does not endorse documents, but plan for the extra review round"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "1 January each year",
              "message": "The portal opens. Be registered and ready, because the window is only two months long."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "midnight 1 March each year",
              "message": "The window closes and applications are immediately reviewed. There is no grace period."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "22 March each year",
