            },
            {
              "trigger": "After selection, before seed capital",
              "message": "Gather your business registration certificate, tax registration evidence and bank reference letter early, and open a business account with a TEF partner bank."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Create your TEFConnect account",
            "On 1 January, log in and start the application form",
            "Complete personal information",
            "Complete business idea and experience information",
            "Sit the business assessment test",
            "Read and accept the declaration, then submit",
            "Confirm the eligibility notification on screen and by email",
            "Save screenshots or exports of your submitted form for your records",
            "Respond promptly to world-check and physical verification requests if shortlisted"
          ],
          "referee_tracking": [],
          "post_award_requirements": [
            "Achieve 100% completion of all TEFConnect training modules",
            "Attend coaching sessions and engage with your assigned mentor as required each month",
            "Submit the business plan, financial projection and 2-3 minute pitch video for the investment readiness review",
            "Submit the full seed capital document set for review by the TEF Audit and Finance team",
            "Open a business account, ideally with a TEF partner bank",
            "Sign the TEF Entrepreneurship Programme seed capital undertaking so payment can be processed"
          ],
          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "Treat 1 March midnight as a hard stop. The window closes automatically and late applications are not accepted, so build your application to be submitted and confirmed weeks earlier.",
            "Do not apply if you have ever received anything from a previous Tony Elumelu Foundation programme, or if you already applied in the same window this year. Both are stated disqualifiers, and a first-time application that is wrong costs you a full year.",
            "Make your TEFConnect name and personal details character-for-character identical to your government-issued ID. The Foundation states this exact-match requirement and it also has to hold at the seed capital stage, where your bank reference letter, business name and ID must all agree.",
            "The business assessment test is pass/fail. Applicants who miss the minimum score are classed ineligible with no appeal. Practise before you sit it inside the form, and leave time inside the window to retake it.",
            "Take the shortlist criteria seriously rather than writing a generic business plan: feasibility, market opportunity, financial understanding, scalability and leadership are each separately scored, with market research and financial projections explicitly expected.",
            "Prepare the seed capital documents before onboarding, not after. Business registration, tax registration in the business name, a bank reference letter and the co-owner consent form can each take weeks in some jurisdictions, and every one of them gates the $5,000.",
            "Open the business account at one of the Foundation's partner banks. The Foundation says this makes fund tracking and disbursement easier, and the money is paid into that account, not to you personally.",
            "Complete 100% of the training modules. Partial completion does not progress you to seed capital, whatever else you have done.",
            "If you are a co-owner, the Partner Consent form is mandatory. If you live with a disability, get the medical report from a reputable hospital ready. Both are conditional documents that applicants often leave out.",
            "Budget the $5,000 as capital for the business, not as income for yourself. It is non-refundable and there is no published second tranche, so it does not replace a business plan with real unit economics.",
            "Expect physical or virtual verification by an enumerator after the window closes. Keep your phone reachable and your premises accessible, because this sits between you and the shortlist."
          ],
          "questions_to_ask_host": [
            "What is the exact minimum score in the business assessment test that separates eligible from ineligible applicants? The process is described as pass/fail but the threshold is not published.",
            "What is the current $5,000 disbursement schedule, and is any second tranche or scale-up round planned for this cohort?",
            "Which banks are on the partner list for this cohort, and does the choice affect how quickly funds are traced?",
            "What file format and maximum file size does TEFConnect accept for the ID and headshot upload?",
            "What are the exact business plan, financial projection and pitch video templates and page or slide limits?",
            "What is the assessment weighting across feasibility, market opportunity, financial understanding, scalability and leadership?",
            "How many participants are in a cohort, and how many reach seed capital?",
            "How long does the physical verification step take after the window closes, and in which countries is it conducted by physical visit rather than virtually?",
            "Does the seed capital undertaking contain any repayment, reporting or clawback clause? The page states the amount is non-refundable but does not publish the undertaking itself.",
            "Is there any tax obligation on the $5,000 in my country, and does the Foundation issue any documentation for tax purposes?",
            "What ongoing support or alumni obligations follow after the Certificate of Completion and Achievement is issued?",
            "Are the BeGreen Africa or Women Entrepreneurship for Africa tracks open to this cohort's alumni, and on what separate terms?"
          ]
