            "Due diligence detail: independent third-party expert review, LSEG World-Check screening, and Physical Verification by authorised enumerators by visit or virtually",
            "Participation confirmation date of 22 March each year and the onboarding session (physical or virtual)",
            "Training phase requirements: 100% completion of all modules, coaching sessions, mentor engagement, and any additional stated activities",
            "Mentor allocation rules: maximum three mentees per mentor and a minimum of two hours of mentoring per mentee every month, pairing based on shared language, interests and industry",
            "Investment readiness requirements: business plan, financial projection and a 2-3 minute pitch video using supplied templates, reviewed and ranked by an independent audit consulting firm",
            "Full seed capital document list including the ID options (National Driver's Licence, International Passport, Permanent Voter's Card for Nigerian participants only), Business Registration Certificate, tax registration evidence in the business name, bank reference letter with matching name details, Partner Consent form for co-owners and a hospital medical report for participants living with disabilities",
            "$5,000 non-refundable seed capital, the requirement to sign the seed capital undertaking, and immediate disqualification for inauthentic or discrepant documents or documents matching past beneficiaries",
            "Certificate of Completion and Achievement and onboarding into the TEF Alumni network, with the published alumni naming conventions",
            "Five shortlist criteria with their published sub-criteria: feasibility, market opportunity, financial understanding, scalability, leadership and entrepreneurial skills",
            "Official contact telephone +234-1-2774641-5 and enquiries@tonyelumelufoundation.org"
          ],
          "institution_check_required": [
            "home_tuition_rule left null: no academic study is funded, so no official page states anything about home-country tuition",
            "host_institution_fee left null: this is not a placement at a host institution, and no official page states any fee payable to any institution",
            "tax_status recorded as published text rather than a figure: the Foundation requires evidence of tax registration in the business name but publishes no tax treatment for the $5,000 disbursement. Confirm the local tax position with the Foundation or a local adviser",
            "deferrable left null: the published process contains no start-date deferral or waitlist mechanism",
            "renewable left null: no official page describes a second tranche, follow-on round or renewal of the seed capital for this programme",
            "return_home_required left null: no official page states a return-home condition, though eligibility does require African residence and establishing the business in Africa",
            "clinical_restriction left null: no clinical restriction is published. The only health-related rule is the conditional medical report required from participants living with disabilities",
            "arrival_rules left empty: no official page describes an arrival date or physical relocation requirement, because the programme is delivered on TEFConnect with physical or virtual onboarding",
            "No file size limit, accepted file-type list, translation rule or document-expiry rule is published for any of the eight required documents",
            "The minimum passing score for the business assessment test is not published; the pass/fail rule is published but the threshold is not",
            "The seed capital undertaking itself is not published as a document on the page, so its repayment, reporting or clawback terms are unconfirmed",
            "No phase-by-phase calendar is published for training, investment readiness or seed capital; only the 1 January to 1 March window and the 22 March confirmation date are fixed",
            "The page carries a 2025 cohort press-release link and a TEF2025 FAQs link; neither was used as a source for the 2027 cycle, and the current programme page's 1 January to 1 March window is the governing statement"
          ],
          "unverified_or_removed_claims": [
