            "Rejected any tuition, living-cost or travel coverage: the programme funds business capital and training, not study or relocation, so tuition_coverage, living_cost_coverage and travel_coverage remain false",
            "Rejected describing the $5,000 as a grant that could be spent freely: it is explicitly non-refundable capital disbursed into a business account against signed documentation, and no personal-use rule is published either way",
            "Rejected any statement about post-award reporting or alumni obligations: the page describes onboarding into the alumni network but publishes no continuing duty, so post_award_requirements is limited to what is written",
            "Demoted the past-cohort press release and TEF2025 FAQ links as sources, because the governing programme page sets the current window"
          ],
          "source_conflict_rule": "The TEF Entrepreneurship Programme page on the Foundation's own site governs the eligibility criteria, the six-phase process, the shortlist criteria, the document list and the programme timeline. Where a press release, an FAQ page or a TEFConnect system message differs from that page, the programme page is recorded and the discrepancy is noted rather than resolved in favour of the more favourable statement.",
          "source_freshness_rule": "The cycle is annual and calendar-driven, with the window fixed at 1 January to 1 March. Anything describing a cohort year older than the current one is stale, and because the window opens on 1 January, a record written early in the year must be re-checked once the window opens for the following cohort.",
