      "description": "The Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program enables highly talented, service-oriented young people to pursue higher education and is delivered through partner universities and non-governmental organisations rather than through a single central application. Financial support includes tuition fees, accommodation, books and other academic materials, mentoring, counselling, leadership development, and a return air ticket to the Scholar's country of origin if necessary, alongside psychosocial and academic support. Scholarships are available at secondary, undergraduate and master's levels, but are not currently available to PhD candidates. Admission to a partner institution does not guarantee selection for the scholarship.",
