      ],
      "selection_notes": "The application process and decision-making are managed individually by each partner university and non-governmental organisation, not by the Mastercard Foundation. Admission to a partner university does not guarantee selection for the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program, which the Foundation states is highly competitive. There is no limit to the number of partner universities an applicant may apply to, but each application is a substantial submission and may carry a fee.",
      "notes": "There is no central application, no central deadline and no central eligibility test, so a record of this scholarship cannot tell you whether a specific window is open. You must check each partner institution's own programme page for its deadline. Many partners require an admission application fee that the Foundation states will be reimbursed if you are selected, so do not let the fee stop you applying. The Foundation warns publicly that there are Facebook posts and groups advertising recruitment for this programme and requesting an application fee, and states that these groups are not associated with the Mastercard Foundation; the Foundation does not solicit funding or request payments from individuals. Report suspected fraud to local law enforcement and to ethics@mastercardfdn.org. PhD and doctoral candidates are not currently eligible. The Foundation does not provide financial support to candidates who are not awarded a scholarship through this programme. The Foundation is not currently accepting unsolicited partnership proposals.",
