            "Gaining admission to a partner institution does not guarantee selection for the Programme; the partner manages both the application and the decision-making.",
            "Partner institutions serve young people from underrepresented backgrounds, and the Foundation publishes an inclusive approach covering women and marginalized groups and a disability inclusion focus area."
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "No central document list, file format, size limit, translation rule, signature rule or date rule is published by the Mastercard Foundation for this programme. Every partner institution sets its own application guidelines.",
            "The only format-related statements on the Foundation's pages are procedural: read the partner's application guidelines, and contact the institution of your choice for more information.",
            "Where an institution requires TOEFL and/or SAT scores for international candidates, the Foundation publishes guidance on how to seek help: applicants confident they can meet the requirements should ask their counsellor or principal for a letter of support or similar documentation expressing confidence in their academic achievements, and share those letters together with their story with the admissions office at the university to which they are applying.",
            "The Foundation publishes the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program Handbook in English and French, which covers programme supports, values and expectations, leadership development, councils and community initiatives, the Baobab platform and Baobab Summit, well-being and safeguarding, transition support, and joining the Alumni community."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "The Foundation publishes no central selection method. Each partner university or NGO runs its own application process and makes its own decision, and the Foundation states repeatedly that the process and decision-making are managed by the partner. Applicants are advised to research the partner's guidelines or contact the institution directly to learn the status of their application. The Foundation warns that the Programme is highly competitive and that admission to a partner institution does not guarantee selection. The Foundation's own award decisions are made through the partner, not through a central Foundation panel described on the page.",
          "application_steps": [
            "Research and choose a Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program-affiliated partner institution from the Foundation's published list of institutions. The Foundation states: 'Find an institution that will help you achieve your academic goals.'",
            "Read the chosen institution's application guidelines, or contact the institution directly, to learn its own programme options, deadline, admission fee and document requirements.",
            "Check whether the partner requires TOEFL and/or SAT scores for international candidates. If it does, either budget for and sit the tests, seek a counsellor or principal support letter as the Foundation describes, look for Education USA support, or choose an Africa-based partner university that does not require SAT or TOEFL.",
            "Pay the partner's admission or application fee if it charges one. The Foundation states such fees will be reimbursed if the candidate is selected for the Programme.",
            "Submit the application directly to the partner institution through that institution's own application process.",
            "Apply to as many partner universities as you wish; there is no limit, though each requires a full application package and possibly a fee.",
            "Await the partner's admission decision and its decision on selection for the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program. Admission alone does not guarantee the scholarship.",
            "If shortlisted for an interview, check whether interview travel is covered, noting that the published support list includes a return air ticket to the Scholar's country of origin if necessary but does not state whether interview travel is included.",
            "Once a Scholar, engage with the wraparound support at the institution: academic, financial and psychosocial support, mentoring, counselling and leadership development, and the Scholars' councils and community initiatives.",
            "Use the transition support at the end of the programme for employment, entrepreneurship or further study, and join the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program Alumni Network and the Baobab platform."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant applies directly, without any central Foundation application: 'If you are interested in becoming a Mastercard Foundation Scholar, please apply directly through the Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program-affiliated institution you wish to attend.'",
            "The applicant submits to the partner institution's own admissions process, and the partner institution manages both the application and the decision-making.",
            "The Mastercard Foundation itself does not accept applications, does not set a central deadline and does not publish a central application portal. The only route is the partner institution's own process.",
            "The Foundation explicitly warns against fraudulent recruitment: it is aware of Facebook posts advertising recruitment for the Programme and requesting an application fee, states those groups are not associated with the Mastercard Foundation, and asks the public to report suspected fraud to local law enforcement and inform the Foundation at ethics@mastercardfdn.org."
          ],
          "application_portal": "No central Mastercard Foundation application portal exists. Applications are submitted through the chosen partner institution's own admissions portal. The Foundation's published list of affiliated institutions is at https://mastercardfdn.org/en/what-we-do/our-programs/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program/where-to-apply/.",
