            "Rejected any central eligibility criteria or scoring rubric: none is published, so general_eligibility records only the published route requirement and ineligibility_conditions records only the explicit disqualifiers (PhD exclusion, non-partner exclusion, no support for unawarded candidates, fraud exclusion)",
            "Rejected treating TOEFL/SAT as a funded cost: the Foundation explicitly states it cannot influence those admission requirements and funds neither test",
            "Rejected any claim that interview travel or relocation costs are covered: only a return air ticket to the country of origin 'if necessary' is published",
            "Demoted partner institutions named in news items as a partner list, because the authoritative list is the Where to Apply page, which did not render"
          ],
          "source_conflict_rule": "The Mastercard Foundation programme page and its FAQ govern what the Foundation itself states: scope, levels, coverage, partner-delivered administration and exclusions. Where the Foundation's programme page and an individual partner institution's guidelines differ, the partner governs its own admissions process, deadline, fees and document requirements, and the partner's page is the one the applicant must follow. Where a partner page and the Foundation's Where to Apply page differ on partner status, the partner's own current listing is treated as current and the discrepancy is recorded rather than resolved in the applicant's favour.",
          "source_freshness_rule": "The programme is continuous and the partner network changes during the year, so a partner list read earlier in the year is stale. Any partner institution, deadline or fee older than the current academic cycle must be re-verified directly with the partner, because the Foundation publishes no version date for the institution list and its news items show new partnerships being added during 2025 and 2026.",
          "source_citations": [
            "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/what-we-do/our-programs/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program/",
            "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/what-we-do/our-programs/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program/where-to-apply/",
            "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program-handbook/",
            "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/frequently-asked-questions/"
          ],
          "researched_by": "deep_01",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
          "data_quality": {
            "source_level": "Official provider pages (Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program page, Where to Apply page, Scholars Program Handbook page and the site's FAQ block, all on mastercardfdn.org)",
            "coverage": "Medium. High for what the Foundation itself publishes: the programme description, the levels funded and the PhD exclusion, the non-exhaustive coverage list, partner-delivered administration, the absence of a central deadline or portal, the fee reimbursement rule, the English-test barrier and its three workarounds, the fraud warning and the reporting address. Low for anything an applicant must budget or plan against: there is no amount, no currency, no disbursement schedule, no central deadline, no central document list, no central eligibility criteria and no selection rubric, because the Foundation delegates all of that to partner institutions. The partner institution list on the Where to Apply page did not render, so the authoritative partner list could not be read.",
            "pages_read": [
              "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/what-we-do/our-programs/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program/",
              "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/what-we-do/our-programs/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program/where-to-apply/",
              "https://mastercardfdn.org/en/mastercard-foundation-scholars-program-handbook/"
            ],
            "pages_unreadable": [
              "Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program institution list on the Where to Apply page - the embedded list returned 'Error loading data. Please try again.' instead of rendering partner institutions, so no authoritative partner enumeration was possible",
              "Mastercard Foundation Scholars Program Handbook PDF (https://cdn.buttercms.com/GCH7h554SbeWtA9pYxCm, English) - identified on the Handbook page but not downloaded or read; only the page's chapter summary was used"
            ]
          }
        }
