          "selection_notes": "The selection procedure comprises two rounds: a desk-review of applications, followed by an online interview of the shortlisted applicants by a selection committee. Shortlisted candidates are announced by the last week of February 2027 and are then invited for a final interview within a fortnight. Final fellows are announced by the last week of March, and fellows are expected to begin work from 1st May 2027. The Foundation states it is unable to respond to individual queries regarding the status of an application. Beyond the two-stage structure and the alignment-to-vision test, no scoring rubric or weighting is published.",
          "application_steps": [
            "Click 'Apply Now' on the fellowship page, which leads to the detailed application instructions and the application form, and then to the Foundation's Online Application System (OAS).",
            "Enter your name, address, latest contact information and other details correctly.",
            "Enter your Date of Birth, scrolling through the calendar or entering it manually, matching the proof of age and citizenship you will upload.",
            "Describe the fellowship activity in a few lines in the 'Topic of your project' field, ensuring it correctly represents the nature of the project.",
            "Download the Statement of purpose and work plan format published by the Foundation, fill it in, and upload it as a PDF only.",
            "Keep the Statement of purpose within 1000 words: outline your personal and professional trajectory very briefly, plus your motivation to take up the project and how it contributes to social change.",
            "Keep the work plan within 1000 words and include a title, a concise description of the work or research to be undertaken during the Fellowship, the expected outcomes, and in detail the manner in which the project will be undertaken with a clear two-year timeline.",
            "Enter your mentor's email address in the Mentor Endorsement field, checking the field carefully because its default subtext refers to a reference rather than a mentor, then submit so that the mentor receives a link and the upload format by email.",
            "Ensure the mentor's Letter of Endorsement contains all five required elements, including the mentor's work experience, contact details, endorsement of the work plan, agreement to supervise and to review quarterly and annual progress reports, and willingness to hold periodic meetings with the Foundation.",
            "Enter your referee's email address in the Referee field and submit so that the referee receives a link and the upload format by email.",
            "Ensure the referee's Letter of Recommendation contains the nature of the engagement and the capacity in which they have engaged with you, and their reason for recommending you and your work plan. The referee must have supervised your work for at least six months and must not be your mentor.",
            "Verify that neither your mentor nor your referee is a current Inlaks Fellow or is currently supported by Inlaks under any other opportunity.",
            "Have both letters uploaded. The Foundation states you can request that your mentor and referee upload their letters even before you make your final submission, and recommends uploading the supporting letters a few days before the deadline.",
            "Submit the complete application by 15 November 2026, 11:59pm IST.",
            "If shortlisted, expect an announcement by the last week of February 2027 and an online interview with a selection committee within a fortnight of that announcement."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits their own application directly on the Foundation's Online Application System (OAS), reached from the 'Apply Now' button on the fellowship page. There is no institutional nomination, university submission or intermediary.",
            "The mentor and the referee each upload their own letters onto the portal themselves, after the applicant enters their email addresses and submits. The applicant does not upload the letters on their behalf, and the Foundation states explicitly that both letters must also be submitted by the 15 November 2026, 11:59pm deadline.",
            "No paper, postal or email application route is published. The Foundation directs all questions to fellowships@inlaksfoundation.org but publishes that address as an enquiry channel, not as a submission channel."
          ],
          "application_portal": "The Inlaks Shivdasani Foundation Online Application System (OAS), reached from the 'Apply Now' button at https://inlaksfoundation.submittable.com/submit/640c6504-aa08-4f03-9f0b-c5a25eb444e8/the-inlaks-fellowship-for-social-engagement-2027. The Foundation states it uses Submittable to accept and review submissions.",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "deferrable": null,
          "renewable": null,
          "return_home_required": null,
          "clinical_restriction": null,
          "arrival_rules": [
            "Fellows are expected to begin work from 1st May 2027, following the announcement of final fellows by the last week of March 2027.",
            "No arrival date, relocation support, visa arrangement or relocation timetable is published on the fellowship page or the application instructions.",
            "Because the stipend varies by geographical category of the Fellow's place of living and working, the city or location of work directly affects the amount; the Foundation publishes the HRA category definitions via a link to a Government of India pay document."
          ],
          "timeline_rules": [
            "Applications for the 2027 fellowship can be submitted latest by 15th November 2026 by 11.59 PM IST.",
            "The Foundation states: 'Please do not wait till the end to apply and it is recommended that your supporting letters be uploaded a few days before the deadline.'",
            "Both the Mentor Endorsement letter and the Recommendation letter must be submitted by 15th November 2026, 11:59pm. Requests to the mentor and referee can be sent before the applicant's own final submission.",
            "Shortlisted candidates will be announced by the last week of February 2027.",
            "Shortlisted candidates are invited for a final interview by a selection committee within a fortnight of the shortlist announcement.",
            "Final fellows will be announced by the last week of March.",
            "Fellows are expected to begin work from 1st May 2027.",
            "The Fellowship then runs for two years, with a probation period of the first six months and quarterly and annual reviews of the Fellow's work throughout.",
            "Fellows must attend three Foundation-hosted workshops at regular intervals during the Fellowship; specific dates are not published."
          ],
          "official_application_route": [
            "Click 'Apply Now' on the fellowship page to reach the detailed application instructions and the application form, then the Online Application System (OAS).",
            "Complete all OAS questions, including name and contact details, date of birth matching the uploaded proof of age and citizenship, and the topic of the project.",
            "Download the Foundation's Statement of purpose and work plan format, complete it within the two 1000-word limits, and upload it as a PDF only.",
            "Enter the mentor's email address so the mentor receives a link and the upload format, and have the mentor upload a Letter of Endorsement meeting all five stated requirements.",
            "Enter the referee's email address so the referee receives a link and the upload format, and have the referee upload a Letter of Recommendation meeting the two stated requirements, from someone who has supervised the applicant for at least six months and who is not the mentor.",
