      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
      "image_alt_text": "RISE Germany, German Academic Exchange Service",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "RISE Germany offers undergraduate students from North American, British and Irish universities the opportunity to complete a summer research internship at top German universities and research institutions. RISE Germany is funded by the German Federal Foreign Office. Students are matched with a host university or institute according to their area of interest. DAAD provides students a monthly stipend for three months to help cover living expenses, and host institutions provide housing assistance and match students with mentors.",
          "degree_levels": [
            "Undergraduate"
          ],
          "duration": "3 months (min. 10 weeks)",
          "application_cycle": "Annual cycle: applications October 15 - November 30, 2026 for internships in the following summer",
          "deadline_central": "2026-11-30",
          "deadline_central_display": "Applications: October 15 - November 30, 2026 (11:59 pm CET - Central European Time); Letters of reference: October 15 - December 15, 2026",
          "deadline_institutional": "Letters of reference: October 15 - December 15, 2026",
          "status": "UPCOMING",
          "funding_label": "Monthly stipend",
          "funding_amount": 992,
          "funding_currency": "EUR",
          "funding_period": "per month",
          "tuition_coverage": false,
          "living_cost_coverage": true,
          "travel_coverage": true,
          "fully_funded": false,
          "eligibility": [
            "Undergraduate students majoring in the fields of science and engineering as well as in computer science",
            "Applicants must have completed at least two years of undergraduate study",
            "Seniors or forth year students must prove that they will still be fully enrolled upon their return to their home university in North America, the UK or Ireland",
            "For most positions knowledge of German is not required"
          ],
          "coverage": [
            "monthly rate of 992 Euros",
            "health-, accident- and private liability insurance",
            "a lump sum towards international travel costs",
            "a lump sum of 160 Euros for travel within Germany",
            "a three day meeting of all RISE scholars in July"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "The application is completely online at www.daad.de/rise-germany",
            "Register in the RISE internship database and search the internship offers"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Motivation letters",
            "Curriculum vitae (CV)",
            "List of courses",
            "Transcript",
            "Certificate of enrollment",
            "Letter of reference"
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Academic performance, indicated by grade point average: undergraduates are ranked in order of academic performance as indicated by their GPA",
            "The internship providers' ranking of applicants, which is the starting basis for all further decisions taken by DAAD",
            "Project demand, indicated by the number of applications each project has attracted; projects are ranked in order of demand",
            "Motivation letters, which are written per project and explain how past experience has prepared the applicant for the position",
            "Letter of recommendation quality",
            "Practical experience",
            "The combination of all of the above: 'There is no single determinant for being awarded a RISE Germany scholarship in this highly competitive program but a combination of various factors.'",
            "Providers have the option to exclude undergraduates they consider unsuited, which the FAQ says rarely happens",
            "The published degree-of-approval scale in the reference guideline (emphatic approval, approval, conditional approval) and the ranking statement (top 5%, 10%, 20%, 30%, or no assessment possible)"
          ],
          "application_method": [
            "Register for the RISE internship database",
            "Search more than 450 internship offers",
            "Submit the online application with the required documents",
            "Submit a letter of reference in the reference window"
          ],
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "The intern must retain undergraduate student status at their home university throughout the internship and afterwards, which is a condition of the German labour law basis for the internship",
            "The intern must study in biology, chemistry, computer science, physics, earth sciences or engineering, or a closely related field",
            "The intern must be matched to a project from the RISE internship database and cannot substitute an independently arranged internship",
            "The intern must attend the RISE Germany meeting in Heidelberg in July 2027, to which all RISE interns are invited",
            "For US, British and Irish students, the monthly scholarship is paid at 992 Euros for a full month and is calculated on a daily basis if the student stays less than 23 days in a month, so a shortened month reduces the payment",
            "Virtual internships carry different scholarship rates from in-person internships",
            "The intern must open a European bank account using the IBAN system to receive the monthly stipend and the DAAD travel stipends",
            "The intern is responsible for visa and residence permit requirements where applicable, and must be able to re-enter their home country after the internship",
            "Where the project description notes a German language requirement, the intern must meet it; otherwise German is not required and the working language is English"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "Daniela Wiesen, Scholarship Programs, North America, RISE, DAAD – German Academic Exchange Service, Kennedyallee 50, 53175 Bonn, GERMANY. Phone +49 (228) 882-425. RISE contact page: https://www.daad.de/rise/en/contact/. Programme page: https://www.daad.de/rise/en/rise-germany/.",
            "email": "rise-germany@daad.de"
          },
          "citizenship_residency": "Students enrolled at universities in North America, the United Kingdom and Ireland",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
          "purpose": [
            "RISE stands for Research Internships in Science and Engineering. RISE Germany 'offers undergraduate students from North American, British and Irish universities the opportunity to complete a summer research internship at top German universities and research institutions'.",
            "Match students with a host university or institute according to their area of interest, in biology, chemistry, physics, earth sciences, engineering, or a closely related field.",
            "Support students with a monthly stipend for three months to help cover living expenses, and have host universities, universities of applied sciences and institutes provide housing assistance and match students with Ph.D. student mentors or researchers.",
            "Keep the programme accessible by not requiring German: German language is not required and the working language will be in English.",
            "RISE Germany is funded by the German Federal Foreign Office."
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [
            "No SDG, development-goal or impact-alignment requirement is published for applicants. The programme is a research internship in the sciences and engineering, and neither the RISE Germany overview page, the What applicants need to know page, nor the FAQ states any requirement to align the project with a named Sustainable Development Goal.",
            "The programme's stated sponsor is the German Federal Foreign Office, but the pages read publish no development-policy objective that an applicant must satisfy."
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Summer research internship in science or engineering at a German university, university of applied sciences or research institute",
            "Full-time research placement, either in person or virtual where the individual project description explicitly offers a virtual option",
            "Structured research project matched to the applicant's field of interest, with doctoral-student or researcher supervision at universities of applied sciences"
          ],
          "degree_award": "No degree, certificate or academic credit is awarded. RISE Germany is a research internship placement for three months with a scholarship; the intern remains an undergraduate at their home university throughout and must retain undergraduate status after the internship.",
          "tuition_rule": "Not applicable. The intern pays no tuition because they remain enrolled at their home university: eligibility requires that the applicant 'prove that you will maintain undergraduate status after the internship has taken place', and the FAQ states that graduates before the internship are ineligible because of German labour law and that DAAD cannot obtain a work permit waiver for non-undergraduates. The internship itself is not a course at a German institution and no tuition waiver or host fee is published.",
          "home_tuition_rule": "The intern must remain enrolled in their home university bachelor's programme throughout: they must currently be enrolled in a bachelor's degree programme at a US, Canadian, British or Irish university by the application deadline, must have completed at least two years by the time of the placement, and must maintain undergraduate status after the internship has taken place. The certificate of enrollment must show an expected graduation date after the internship so that the German Federal Employment Agency can be assured of continuing academic study in fall 2027.",
          "host_institution_fee": null,
          "tax_status": null,
          "covered_expenses": [
            "For US, British and Irish students: a monthly scholarship of 992 Euros for a full month, calculated on a daily basis if the student stays less than 23 days in a month",
            "For US, British and Irish students: health insurance, accident insurance and personal liability insurance",
            "For US, British and Irish students: an international travel subsidy and a 160 Euros travel stipend for the RISE meeting",
            "For Canadian students: a combined Mitacs and DAAD scholarship of 7,000 CAD provided directly by Mitacs to support travel costs and living expenses, for 100 applicants",
            "For Canadian students: health, accident and liability insurance provided by DAAD",
            "Housing assistance from the host university, university of applied sciences or institute, and matching with a Ph.D. student mentor or researcher (only UAS)",
            "Invitation to the RISE Germany meeting in Heidelberg in July 2027 for all RISE interns"
          ],
          "not_covered_or_excluded": [
            "Housing costs. The host provides housing assistance and the intern's supervisor helps find reasonably priced housing, but no official page states that DAAD pays rent; the intern must find and pay for their own accommodation, anywhere from a student dormitory room to a shared apartment.",
            "Visa and residence permit costs. European citizens need no visa, and US, Canadian and British citizens staying 90 days or less need none, but students staying longer than 90 days must apply for a visa themselves, and non-citizens are strongly advised to check with the German Federal Foreign Office. No page states that DAAD funds visa costs.",
            "Living costs beyond the stipend: the stipend is stated as help to cover living expenses, with no published statement that it covers them in full.",
            "Tuition or fees at any German institution",
            "Recommendation letters from companies: 'We do not accept recommendation letters from companies.'",
            "Research internships arranged independently rather than through the RISE database: 'We are not able to support personal or institutional contacts that already exist and are not open to the general public.'",
            "Applicants graduating in spring or summer 2027, who are ineligible for RISE Germany 2027 and directed to RISE Professional",
            "A parallel RISE Germany and RISE Professional application in the same cycle",
            "Repeating the same internship twice: if planning RISE Germany for a second time, the applicant must choose another internship offer, city or provider",
            "Any cost of withdrawing from or changing an application after submission; withdrawals cause considerable inconvenience for DAAD and the provider"
          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "Currently enrolled in a bachelor's degree programme at a university or college in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom or Ireland, in biology, chemistry, computer science, physics, earth sciences or engineering, or a closely related field",
            "An undergraduate who will have completed at least two years of a degree programme by the time of the internship placement",
            "Able to prove that undergraduate status will be maintained after the internship has taken place",
            "International students must prove that they study at a university or college located in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom or Ireland for more than 12 months by the application deadline",
            "German citizenship holders are only eligible if they can prove they have been living outside of Germany for six years or more, with the relevant information added to the CV",
            "Canadian students may apply through the Mitacs Globalink Research Internship route as well as the RISE Germany route",
            "No German language ability is required unless otherwise noted in the individual project description; the working language is English"
          ],
          "ineligibility_conditions": [
            "Freshmen: applicants are required to have completed at least two years of an undergraduate degree programme by the time of the internship",
            "Anyone enrolled at a community college: 'You have to be enrolled at a university/college in a bachelor's degree program.'",
            "Anyone who will finish their undergraduate degree before the internship begins, including those graduating in spring or summer 2027. This is due to German labour law: DAAD cannot obtain a work permit waiver for a non-undergraduate. Students who will graduate in winter 2027 or later are eligible.",
            "Anyone not enrolled at a university or college in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom or Ireland",
            "International students who cannot prove more than 12 months of study at a US, Canadian, British or Irish institution by the application deadline",
            "German citizenship holders who cannot prove six years or more of living outside Germany",
            "Pre-med students who have already obtained their first B.A. degree",
            "Applicants whose major is outside the natural sciences and who have already completed a first B.A. degree",
            "Anyone applying in parallel to RISE Germany and RISE Professional in the same cycle: you must choose one",
            "Anyone proposing to repeat the same internship twice; a second RISE Germany requires a different internship offer, city or provider",
            "Anyone seeking to use the programme for an independently arranged internship: 'We are not able to support personal or institutional contacts that already exist and are not open to the general public.'",
            "Incomplete applications: if everything has not been received online by November 30, 2026, the application cannot be considered",
            "Recommendation letters from companies, and letters based on a research internship that was not held in a university setting or did not last at least two months"
          ],
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "The only funded level. Applicants must currently be enrolled in a bachelor's degree programme at a US, Canadian, British or Irish university or college, must have completed at least two years by the time of the placement, and must retain undergraduate status after the internship.",
              "Field of study must be biology, chemistry, computer science, physics, earth sciences or engineering, or a closely related field.",
              "The FAQ notes that experience shows internship providers tend to prefer applicants who have already completed their third year of study and gained practical experience, but that the Foundation also welcomes students who have just finished their second year and stand out through excellent recommendation letters and high academic grades.",
              "Recent graduates and Master's and PhD students are directed to RISE Professional instead."
            ],
            "masters": [
              "Not eligible for RISE Germany. The FAQ states: 'We encourage all recent graduates, Master's and PhD students to apply for our RISE Professional program.'"
            ],
            "phd": [
              "Not eligible for RISE Germany. PhD students are directed to RISE Professional."
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "Students are matched with a host university or institute according to their area of interest, at top German universities and research institutions, and the intern cannot choose their own provider outside the RISE database.",
            "Host universities, universities of applied sciences (UAS) and institutes provide housing assistance and match students with Ph.D. student mentors or researchers; the mentoring element is stated for UAS only.",
            "The intern's supervisor helps them find reasonably priced housing for the duration of the internship.",
            "The internship must be a project that was submitted to the RISE internship database and is open to general application; personally or institutionally arranged internships are not supported.",
            "Virtual internships are possible only where the individual project description explicitly offers that option, and virtual internships carry different scholarship rates.",
            "German language is not required unless otherwise noted in the individual project description; the working language is English.",
            "The intern may be required to obtain a visa or residence permit and, for some nationalities, must be able to re-enter their home country after the internship. For internships in Germany under the Federal Employment Agency's rules, the intern needs the certificate of enrollment showing an expected graduation date so continuing study in fall 2027 can be confirmed."
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "The application process is completely online in the RISE Germany internship database. Applicants must first register for a DAAD ID in order to get access to the database.",
            "Motivation letters: one motivation letter per project applied to. Design and formatting are up to the applicant; DAAD publishes no word or page limit. The salutary address may address the internship provider directly.",
            "Curriculum vitae: should include education, work or volunteer experience, details of interest or previous experience in the field, and may mention involvement in political, cultural and social commitment and special life circumstances. German citizenship holders must add the relevant information about years living outside Germany.",
            "List of courses: a document the applicant writes or produces themselves, no longer than one page, listing courses completed by the time the internship begins. Applicants are told not to copy the entire course catalogue and descriptions.",
            "Transcript: either a digital transcript with university name or logo, student's name and print date, or a copy of a certified hard copy. DAAD states it does not matter if the transcript bears an 'issued to student' stamp.",
            "Certificate of enrollment: some universities do not complete third-party verification forms, in which case DAAD accepts the university's own official enrollment form as long as it shows a prospective, anticipated or expected graduation date. The certificate must show the stamp of the university or college and the signature of an authorized person. DAAD publishes a sample certificate of enrollment for the German Federal Employment Agency at https://www.daad.de/rise/files/2025/11/NEW_CoE_GermanWorkAgency_2025.pdf",
            "The certificate of enrollment is used by the German Federal Employment Agency to decide on approval of the internship, so the expected date of graduation is required to prove ongoing student status. DAAD advises explaining to the Office of Student Services or Registrar that the date is not permanent or binding and is meant to demonstrate current second- or third-year undergraduate status with expected graduation only after the internship.",
            "Letter of reference: must be submitted on the official letterhead of the referee's university and bear the referee's signature. The referee must hold a PhD degree at least. DAAD publishes guidance on what the letter should contain: since when and in what capacity the referee has known the applicant; a ranking statement (among the best 5%, 10%, 20%, 30%, or no assessment possible); how the applicant stands out academically and personally and an assessment of potential; the significance of the scholarship to the applicant's academic and professional career; additional information relevant to the award decision; and a degree of approval (emphatic approval, approval, or conditional approval).",
            "Letter of reference must be uploaded online by the professor. After the applicant logs in and saves the application for the first time, a field named 'Letter of Reference – Please create a link for your professor' appears; entering the professor's name and email creates a web link assigned to that professor, who receives an email and submits the letter online.",
            "The complete required set is described by DAAD as: working PDF documents, transcript, official certificate of enrollment, and a reference letter including an official letterhead and the referee's signature. If anything has not been received online by November 30, 2026, the application cannot be considered.",
            "No file size limit, accepted file-type list beyond the working PDF requirement, translation rule or document-expiry rule is published for the other documents."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "The placement process is formalized because RISE receives a large number of applications from undergraduates and a large number of project offers. First the internship providers send their ranking of applicants. DAAD then ranks undergraduates by academic performance as indicated by GPA, and ranks projects by demand as indicated by the number of applications attracted. The two rankings are matched: the top 30 projects are assigned one of the three applicants they gave highest priority who are still available; the 30 top students by academic performance are assigned one of the three projects they applied for that are still available; and the process continues in this alternating manner until all scholarships are awarded. Once a pair has been matched it is removed from the process. DAAD states the system is not absolute and it always tries to make matches that please both undergraduates and providers, and that it believes the design achieves fairness and transparency. Internship providers are encouraged to contact applicants by phone or email. All providers submit their preference list by the end of January, and DAAD notifies outcomes beginning in March. No individual feedback is provided on an application, by email or by phone.",
          "application_steps": [
            "Register for a DAAD ID to gain access to the RISE Germany internship database at https://www.daad.de/rise/en/rise-germany/find-an-internship/application-portal/. The application process is completely online.",
            "Confirm eligibility against the published requirements, including enrolment in a bachelor's programme in the US, Canada, the UK or Ireland, at least two years completed by the time of the placement, and continued undergraduate status afterwards.",
            "Search the internship database. Do not restrict the search to a single field of study, because many projects treat aspects of more than one field and providers must choose a field when submitting offers.",
            "Choose projects carefully and make sure they are in line with your academic field of interest, since withdrawals cause considerable inconvenience for DAAD and the provider.",
            "Read each project description carefully, including whether German is required, whether the project offers a virtual option, and any other project-specific note.",
            "Write one motivation letter per project you apply to, explaining how your past experience has prepared you for the position and optionally your future plans.",
            "Prepare your CV covering education, work or volunteer experience, interest or previous experience in the field, and involvement in political, cultural and social commitment; add special life circumstances if you wish, and for German citizens the information proving six years or more outside Germany.",
            "Produce your own list of courses, no longer than one page, listing the courses you will have completed by the time the internship begins.",
            "Obtain your transcript as either a digital transcript with university name or logo, student's name and print date, or a copy of a certified hard copy.",
            "Obtain an official certificate of enrollment showing a prospective, anticipated or expected graduation date, with the stamp of the university or college and the signature of an authorized person. Use the Office of Student Services or Registrar, and explain that the date is not permanent or binding.",
            "Save your application for the first time so that the 'Letter of Reference – Please create a link for your professor' field appears.",
            "Enter your professor's name and email address in that field. A web link is created and assigned to the professor, who receives an email and submits the letter of reference online, on the official university letterhead, with the referee's signature. The referee must hold a PhD degree at least.",
            "Submit the complete application online by November 30, 2026, 11:59 pm CET. DAAD sends a confirmation email once it receives your complete application.",
            "Ensure the letter of reference reaches DAAD by December 15, 2026, 11:59 pm CET.",
            "Await the placement. Providers submit their preference lists by the end of January, and DAAD notifies applicants of the outcome beginning in March, with positions announced around February/March 2027.",
            "Confirm the start date with your internship provider. Start dates in the offers are meant as a timeframe and are somewhat flexible, determined between you and the provider.",
            "Arrange a European bank account using the IBAN system to receive the monthly stipend and DAAD travel stipends; DAAD recommends an online account and setting it up as soon as you arrive.",
            "Arrange housing with your supervisor's help once you know your city."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits directly, online, in the RISE Germany internship database. There is no institutional nomination: RISE Germany 'is a program that offers every applicant the possibility to apply for any internship in the program' and explicitly does not support personal or institutional contacts.",
            "The academic referee submits the letter of reference directly and online, through a link generated by the applicant and emailed to the professor.",
            "The applicant applies to individual internship projects within the database, writing a separate motivation letter for each project applied to.",
            "For Canadian students, a parallel route exists through the Mitacs Globalink Research Internship programme, which offers up to 100 positions for successful matched candidates in RISE Germany."
          ],
          "application_portal": "The RISE Germany internship database at https://www.daad.de/rise/en/rise-germany/find-an-internship/application-portal/, which requires a DAAD ID registration. Canadian students may also apply through the Mitacs Globalink Research Internship programme at https://www.mitacs.ca/en/programs/globalink/rise-globalink-research-internship.",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "deferrable": null,
          "renewable": false,
          "return_home_required": null,
          "clinical_restriction": null,
          "arrival_rules": [
            "The internship can start between May 15 and July 15, 2027, for a duration of three months, with a minimum stay of ten weeks and a maximum stay of 90 days.",
            "Start dates in the internship offers are meant as a timeframe and are somewhat flexible; they are determined between the intern and the internship provider, and the FAQ advises getting in touch with the provider if there are questions about dates.",
            "The intern needs a European bank account using the IBAN system to receive the monthly stipend and the travel stipends, and DAAD recommends opening an online account as soon as they arrive in Germany.",
            "Housing is arranged by the intern with the supervisor's help after arrival; no arrival date, arrival grant or relocation support beyond the published international travel subsidy is published.",
            "Visa and residence permit: European citizens do not need a visa; US, Canadian and British citizens staying 90 days or less do not need one either, but students staying longer than 90 days must apply for a visa. Students without those citizenships are strongly advised to check with the German Federal Foreign Office or their embassy."
          ],
          "timeline_rules": [
            "Applications: October 15 to November 30, 2026, 11:59 pm CET. All applications must be submitted online by November 30, 2026; if everything has not been received online by that date the application cannot be considered.",
            "Letters of reference: October 15 to December 15, 2026, 11:59 pm CET. This is a separate, later deadline from the application deadline.",
            "All internship providers submit their list of preferences by the end of January.",
            "Ranking by providers: January 14 to January 25, 2027.",
            "DAAD begins the placement process and notifies applicants of the outcome beginning of March.",
            "Announcement of RISE internship positions: around February/March 2027.",
            "Internship start window: May 15 to July 15, 2027, for three months, minimum ten weeks and maximum 90 days.",
            "RISE Germany meeting in Heidelberg in July 2027, to which all RISE interns are invited.",
            "The scholarship for a full month is 992 Euros; if the student stays less than 23 days in a month the amount is calculated on a daily basis.",
            "An applicant who is still an undergraduate the following summer may apply again, but must choose a different internship offer, city or provider, and cannot do the same internship twice."
          ],
          "official_application_route": [
            "Register for a DAAD ID, then apply through the RISE Germany internship database at https://www.daad.de/rise/en/rise-germany/find-an-internship/application-portal/, which DAAD states is where 'the application process is completely online'.",
            "Choose internship projects within the database and submit a separate motivation letter for each project applied to.",
            "Upload the CV, the self-produced list of courses, the transcript, the official certificate of enrollment and the other working PDF documents.",
            "Enter the academic professor's name and email in the 'Letter of Reference – Please create a link for your professor' field so that a link is generated and the professor can upload the letter online by December 15, 2026.",
            "Canadian students may additionally use the Mitacs Globalink Research Internship route, where up to 100 positions are offered for successful matched candidates in RISE Germany, with 7,000 CAD provided directly by Mitacs.",
            "DAAD confirms receipt by email once the complete application is received, then runs the ranking and placement process and notifies outcomes beginning in March.",
            "RISE Germany does not accept applications by post, email or through a home university, and does not support independently arranged internships."
          ],
          "program_type": "Government-funded international research internship scholarship",
          "region": "Germany (host country); applicants must be enrolled at a university or college in the United States, Canada, the United Kingdom or Ireland"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are enrolled at a university in North America, the UK or Ireland in a science, engineering or computer science major",
            "Confirm you will have completed at least two years of undergraduate study before the internship",
            "If you are a senior or fourth-year student, be ready to prove you will still be fully enrolled when you return home",
            "Register in the RISE internship database as soon as the window opens on October 15, 2026",
