          "cycle_verified": "RISE Germany 2027 (summer 2027 internship): applications 15 October to 30 November 2026, letters of reference to 15 December 2026, provider ranking 14 to 25 January 2027, positions announced around February/March 2027, internships starting between 15 May and 15 July 2027. As at 2026-10-01 the application window had not yet opened, so the record is correctly marked upcoming.",
          "verification_confidence": 0.96,
          "official_fields_confirmed": [
            "Programme name, expansion of the RISE acronym, purpose, funder (German Federal Foreign Office), the four eligible home countries, and the statement that German is not required and the working language is English (RISE Germany overview page)",
            "Full application deadlines: applications 15 October to 30 November 2026 at 11:59 pm CET; letters of reference to 15 December 2026; ranking by providers 14 to 25 January 2027; announcement of positions around February/March 2027 (RISE Germany overview page)",
            "Eligibility: currently enrolled in a bachelor's programme at a US, Canadian, British or Irish university or college in biology, chemistry, computer science, physics, earth sciences or engineering or a closely related field; at least two years completed by the time of the placement; continued undergraduate status after the internship (What applicants need to know)",
            "International students must prove more than 12 months of study at an institution in those four countries by the application deadline",
            "German citizenship holders eligible only if they can prove six years or more living outside Germany, with the information added to the CV",
