            "Complete document list with rules: one motivation letter per project with no word or page limit; CV contents; self-produced list of courses no longer than one page; transcript as digital transcript with university name or logo, student's name and print date, or a copy of a certified hard copy where an 'issued to student' stamp does not matter; official certificate of enrollment showing a prospective, anticipated or expected graduation date with the university stamp and an authorized signature, accepted as the university's own form where third-party verification is unavailable",
            "Letter of reference rules: PhD-holding academic referee, official university letterhead, referee's signature, submitted online by the professor via a link generated in the 'Letter of Reference – Please create a link for your professor' field, and the six published content guidelines including the 5/10/20/30% ranking statement and the emphatic/approval/conditional approval scale",
            "Exclusion of company recommendation letters, and the rule that a research-internship supervisor's letter counts only if the internship was in a university setting and lasted at least two months",
            "The statement that if everything has not been received online by 30 November 2026 the application cannot be considered, and the list of documents DAAD calls working PDF documents plus transcript, official certificate of enrollment and reference letter with letterhead and signature",
            "FAQ exclusions: freshmen, community college students, those graduating before or during the internship with winter 2027 or later stated as the eligible boundary, the parallel RISE Germany and RISE Professional prohibition, the same-internship-twice prohibition, pre-med students who already hold a first B.A. degree, and the refusal to support independently arranged internships",
            "The full formalized placement algorithm: providers rank first; undergraduates ranked by GPA; projects ranked by number of applications; top 30 projects receive one of their top three available applicants; top 30 students receive one of their three available projects; alternating until all scholarships awarded, with matched pairs removed",
            "No individual feedback is provided on an application, by email or by phone",
            "Visa rules: no visa for European citizens or for US, Canadian and British citizens staying 90 days or less; a visa is required for stays beyond 90 days; other nationals advised to check with the German Federal Foreign Office",
            "European IBAN bank account required to receive the monthly stipend and DAAD travel stipends, with a recommendation to use an online account and set it up on arrival",
            "Housing is not funded: the supervisor helps find reasonably priced housing, and the FAQ warns that depending on the city it is not always easy, especially in Munich and Berlin, and warns of fake advertisers and rental scammers",
            "Provider contact block: Daniela Wiesen, Scholarship Programs, North America, RISE, DAAD, Kennedyallee 50, 53175 Bonn, phone +49 (228) 882-425, email rise-germany@daad.de",
            "Virtual internships are available only where the project description explicitly offers them, and carry different scholarship rates",
            "The published reference-guideline content list including the degree of approval scale",
