            "Rejected any return-home bond or obligation: none is published, and only a visa re-entry caveat for international students appears"
          ],
          "source_conflict_rule": "DAAD's own RISE Germany pages govern every term of the award: the overview page for the programme identity, funder and headline dates; 'What applicants need to know' for requirements, the scholarship package and the document rules; and the FAQ for exclusions, the placement algorithm and the in-Germany questions. Where the overview page and the FAQ state dates at slightly different precision, both are recorded and the more specific operational page governs the operational question. Mitacs, as a named co-funder for the Canadian route, governs the CAD component only; DAAD governs the insurance and the placement process.",
          "source_freshness_rule": "The cycle is annual and every date in the programme shifts each year, so a page read for one summer is stale for the next. Because the application window opens on 15 October and closes on 30 November, a record verified before the window opens must be re-read once the window is live and again after the 15 December reference deadline, and the internship project descriptions must be re-read each cycle because they are rewritten annually and carry project-specific language and scholarship conditions.",
          "source_citations": [
