          ],
          "degree_award": "A full degree at a German higher education institution, not a short-term award. The Grundförderung covers Bachelor's, Master's and Diplom degree programmes and programmes leading to the Staatsexamen. No degree is awarded by the Foundation itself.",
          "tuition_rule": "The Foundation states that its financial support amounts to 992 Euro per month and that the cost of health insurance is covered, but it publishes no tuition-waiver rule. The applicant's tuition and semester contribution fees at the German institution are not listed as covered by the Foundation, and no official page states that the Foundation pays them. Where the Foundation's stipend is described, it is described as support for living during the study, not as a fee waiver.",
          "home_tuition_rule": "Not applicable as a published rule. The programme requires the applicant to be already studying at a German institution, and the Foundation explicitly does not fund study abroad programmes outside the EU or short-term stays abroad.",
          "host_institution_fee": null,
          "tax_status": null,
          "covered_expenses": [
            "A monthly stipend of 992 Euro",
            "The costs of health insurance: 'Die Kosten für die Krankenversicherung werden übernommen.' The Foundation's English page states this as refund of health care costs.",
            "An additional 255 Euro per month for scholarship holders with children (stated on the German Grundförderung page)"
          ],
          "not_covered_or_excluded": [
            "Tuition and semester contribution fees at the German institution: no official page states that these are paid",
            "Short-term courses of study of less than three semesters, for example a two-semester Master's programme",
            "Short-term stays abroad and study abroad programmes outside the EU",
            "Research visits, postdoctoral projects, trainee programmes and project proposals",
            "University preparatory courses",
            "Medical studies up to and including the preliminary medical examination (Physikum)",
            "Doctoral degrees and further education or training in the medical field; final stages of a degree course or of a doctoral degree",
            "Training to become a physiotherapist, and further training to become a psychological psychotherapist",
            "Extra-occupational or part-time courses of study",
            "Language courses, unless the applicant already holds an FES scholarship",
            "Second degrees, unless the applicant already holds an FES scholarship",
            "Travel costs generally: the only published travel reimbursement is for applicants who are invited to a selection interview and have incurred travel costs, for which the Foundation publishes a travel-cost reimbursement form for the Grundförderung"
          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "The applicant must be a foreign national (Ausländer:in)",
            "The applicant must already be enrolled at a German public or state-recognised university, higher education institution or university of applied sciences at the time of application",
            "The applicant must have very good German language skills, and must prove sufficient German with the application",
            "The applicant must have above-average grades in their studies (überdurchschnittliche Noten im Studium)",
            "The applicant must already have first graded performance records (erste benotete Leistungsnachweise) as a prerequisite for applying",
            "The applicant must be socially or politically engaged (gesellschaftspolitisch engagiert)",
            "The applicant must identify with the values of social democracy",
            "The application must be submitted in German",
            "The applicant must answer three questions with a clear yes: do you identify with the fundamental values of social democracy; is it self-evident to you to volunteer for society; do you have good grades in school, in your studies or in your degree"
          ],
          "ineligibility_conditions": [
            "Not already studying in Germany at the time of application. The Foundation states 'You are already studying in Germany at the time of your application' as a requirement for foreign students, and that living in Germany and studying at a German university is essential.",
            "Without proof of sufficient German language skills. The Foundation states 'German language skills are absolutely necessary and must be proven', and that even if you study in English you must prove sufficient German with your application.",
            "Applications not submitted in German: 'Applications have to be submitted in German.'",
            "Applications without first graded performance records: 'Bachelor's students must submit their first graded performance records.'",
            "Students enrolled at an institution that is not a state or state-recognised university, higher education institution or university of applied sciences",
            "Applicants in fields or at stages the Foundation does not fund: short-term courses of under three semesters, medical studies up to and including the Physikum, doctoral and postdoctoral study, final stages of a degree or doctorate, physiotherapy and psychological psychotherapy training, research visits, trainee programmes, university preparatory courses, extra-occupational or part-time study, study abroad outside the EU, and short-term stays abroad",
            "Applicants already holding an FES scholarship who wish to add funding for a language course or a second degree",
            "Applicants missing the stage-specific application window: Master's before or at the start of the first semester of the Master's programme; Bachelor, Diplom, Magister and Staatsexamen after the first semester and up to three semesters before the end of the standard period of study; medicine after the fourth semester or after the Physikum and to the end of the sixth semester"
          ],
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "Bachelor's, Diplom, Magister and Staatsexamen programmes are included in the Grundförderung.",
              "Application window: after the first semester and up to three semesters before the end of the standard period of study. The Foundation's English page states this as until three semesters before finishing the standard period of study, giving the examples 'if 6 semesters by the end of 3rd semester; if 7 semesters by the end of 4th semester'.",
              "Bachelor's students must submit their first graded performance records before applying.",
              "Medicine has its own window: after the fourth semester or after the Physikum, to the end of the sixth semester. The Foundation does not fund medical studies up to and including the Physikum.",
              "Second degrees are not funded unless the applicant already holds an FES scholarship."
            ],
            "masters": [
              "Master's and postgraduate programmes are included in the Grundförderung.",
              "Application window: before or at the start of the first higher education semester of the Master's programme, stated as by 30 November for a winter semester start and by 31 May for a summer semester start. The Foundation's English page states the same window as by the end of the first semester.",
              "A short-term course of study of less than three semesters, for example a two-semester Master's programme, is not funded. An applicant who does not qualify for a Master's programme is pointed to the Bachelor/Diplom/Magister/Staatsexamen route.",
              "The German page states that graduates and postgraduates are directed to the separate Promotionsförderung für Ausländer:innen doctoral programme instead."
            ],
            "phd": [
              "Not funded under the Grundförderung. Doctoral study is handled by a separate programme, Promotionsförderung für Ausländer:innen, which funds foreign doctoral candidates admitted to a state or state-recognised German university and funds all dissertation projects except medicine.",
              "The Foundation explicitly does not fund doctoral degrees, postdoctoral projects, or the final stages of a doctoral degree."
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "The applicant must already be enrolled at a German public or state-recognised university, higher education institution or university of applied sciences (an einer deutschen, staatlichen oder staatlich anerkannten Hochschule oder Fachhochschule).",
            "Enrolment must be confirmed by an Immatrikulationsbescheinigung, and university entrance qualification and certificates are among the documents requested at the second stage.",
            "The applicant's study must be a full-time degree programme; extra-occupational and part-time courses of study are not funded.",
            "Scholarship holders with children receive an additional monthly amount, which requires a declared family situation.",
            "The Foundation's English page notes particular importance for students at universities of applied sciences, so those institutions are an accepted host type rather than a second-tier route."
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "The application is made in the online application form, using the form published for the Grundförderung für Ausländer:innen at https://www.fes.de/oas/portal/pls/portal/bewsti2014.bewmaske?pFprog=2&pkn=A. The online form is required as the first step and is checked by FES staff against the formal and substantive criteria.",
            "The first-step online form requires general personal information, information on professional and family background, the applicant's motivation to become an FES scholarship holder, and information on socio-political engagement.",
            "Applications must be submitted in German.",
            "Second-stage documents requested by email: a detailed CV covering previous education and socio-political engagement; certificates, university entrance qualification, enrolment certificate (Immatrikulationsbescheinigung) and other evidence; a detailed letter of motivation; and two references (Gutachten) from university lecturers, or from teachers for first-year students.",
            "For the Grundförderung, the Foundation publishes a dedicated document and reference checklist as a downloadable file at https://www.fes.de/index.php?eID=dumpFile&t=f&f=160624, which is the governing list of required documents and guidance for this programme specifically.",
            "Applicants have three weeks to assemble the documents and up to six weeks for the references, and the Foundation sends a receipt confirmation on receipt.",
            "If an applicant is invited to a selection interview and has incurred travel costs, those costs can be reimbursed by submitting the Foundation's travel-cost reimbursement form for the Grundförderung (Fahrtkostenerstattung_BMFTR_Grundförderung), published at https://www.fes.de/index.php?eID=dumpFile&t=f&f=165947.",
            "Applicants can log back in at any time before submitting to continue an unfinished online application, and can upload further documents through the same login once they advance a stage.",
            "The Foundation informs every applicant by email about the result of each stage, and the final decision is communicated at the latest one week after the selection committee's meeting.",
            "No file size limit, accepted file-type list, translation rule, certification rule or document-expiry rule is published on the pages read. The documents checklist PDF and the reference-writing guidance are published as separate files and were not downloaded."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "The procedure has five published steps. Step 1: complete the online application form; FES staff check it against formal and substantive criteria, and within two to four weeks of receipt the applicant receives either a rejection or a request to submit documents and references. Step 2: submit documents and references; the file is reviewed and the applicant receives either a rejection or notification that the application has been passed to a Vertrauensdozentin or Vertrauensdozent. Step 3: the first selection interview, a subject-related discussion with a Vertrauensdozentin or Vertrauensdozent, from which a Gutachten is produced and attached to the file; the applicant then receives either a rejection or notification that the file has gone to a member of the selection committee. Step 4: the second selection interview with a person from the selection committee, producing a further Gutachten attached to the file and tabled at the committee's meeting. Step 5: decision by the selection committee, which meets eight to ten times a year; once both Gutachten are available the application is presented in detail to the committee at the relevant meeting and the members decide on admission to the funding programme. The Foundation informs the applicant of the final decision at the latest one week after the meeting, whether that is an offer or a rejection, and states that the whole process from application to decision can take three to seven months.",
          "application_steps": [
            "Apply early. The Foundation states the best time to apply is as early as possible, because it wants scholarship holders to benefit from the scholarship for as long as possible, and the deadlines are listed per programme.",
            "Check your degree-stage window. Master's: before or at the start of the first semester of the Master's programme (winter semester by 30 November, summer semester by 31 May). Bachelor, Diplom, Magister, Staatsexamen: after the first semester and up to three semesters before the end of the standard period of study. Medicine: after the fourth semester or after the Physikum, to the end of the sixth semester.",
            "Complete the online application form for the Grundförderung für Ausländer:innen at https://www.fes.de/oas/portal/pls/portal/bewsti2014.bewmaske?pFprog=2&pkn=A, in German, covering general personal information, professional and family background, your motivation to become an FES scholarship holder, and your socio-political engagement.",
            "Submit the form. FES staff check it against the formal and substantive criteria.",
            "Wait two to four weeks. You will receive either a rejection or an email requesting your documents and references.",
            "If invited, submit within the stated windows: three weeks for the documents and up to six weeks for the references. Documents: a detailed CV covering your previous education and socio-political engagement; certificates, university entrance qualification, enrolment certificate and other evidence; and a detailed letter of motivation. References: two Gutachten from university lecturers.",
            "Consult the Foundation's published Grundförderung document and reference checklist at https://www.fes.de/index.php?eID=dumpFile&t=f&f=160624 for the full required list for this programme.",
            "Use your FES login at https://www.fes.de/oas/portal/pls/portal/bewsti2014.login to upload further documents when you advance to the next stage. FES confirms receipt of the documents.",
            "If the file passes, attend the first selection interview, a subject-related discussion with a Vertrauensdozentin or Vertrauensdozent. A Gutachten is produced and attached to your file.",
            "If you advance, attend the second selection interview with a member of the selection committee. A second Gutachten is produced.",
            "If you have travelled for an interview, submit the Foundation's travel-cost reimbursement form for the Grundförderung to claim reimbursement of your travel costs.",
            "Await the decision. The selection committee meets eight to ten times a year and you will be informed by email at the latest one week after the meeting, whether the outcome is an offer or a rejection. The full process from application to decision can take three to seven months."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits directly. The online application form, the documents and the references are all submitted by the applicant to the Foundation, with no institutional nomination and no employer or university acting as an intermediary.",
            "Applications may be submitted formally from Germany or from abroad: 'Bewerbungen sind formell sowohl aus Deutschland als auch aus dem Ausland möglich.'",
            "The two Gutachten must be written by university lecturers, or by teachers for first-year students, and submitted by the applicant with the document package within the stated six-week window. The Foundation publishes guidance on preparing the references separately.",
            "After the first stage, further documents are uploaded by the applicant through the Foundation's own application login.",
            "The Foundation's contact addresses for Auslandsförderung are published for questions, not as a submission channel; submission is through the online system."
          ],
          "application_portal": "The Foundation's online application system at https://www.fes.de/oas/portal/pls/portal/bewsti2014.bewmaske?pFprog=2&pkn=A (the Grundförderung für Ausländer:innen form), with applicant login at https://www.fes.de/oas/portal/pls/portal/bewsti2014.login.",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "deferrable": null,
          "renewable": null,
          "return_home_required": null,
          "clinical_restriction": true,
          "arrival_rules": [
            "The applicant must already be living in Germany and studying at a German university at the time of application, and applications may formally be submitted from Germany or from abroad. Consequently there is no arrival provision: the applicant is already in Germany when applying.",
            "No arrival date, latest-arrival rule, visa support arrangement or relocation funding is published. Study abroad programmes outside the EU and short-term stays abroad are not funded.",
            "Enrolment must be confirmed by an Immatrikulationsbescheinigung, and the Foundation's stage-two document request includes the enrolment certificate."
          ],
          "timeline_rules": [
            "The best time to apply is as early as possible, because the Foundation wants scholarship holders to benefit for as long as possible.",
            "Application windows by degree stage: Master's, before or at the start of the first semester of the Master's programme (winter semester by 30 November, summer semester by 31 May); Bachelor, Diplom, Magister and Staatsexamen, after the first semester and up to three semesters before the end of the standard period of study (English page: until three semesters before finishing the standard period of study, so by the end of the 3rd semester on a six-semester programme or the end of the 4th semester on a seven-semester programme); medicine, after the fourth semester or after the Physikum to the end of the sixth semester. The Foundation's English page also states diploma, magister and state examination by the end of the 6th semester.",
            "There is no single annual closing date: applications are accepted on a rolling basis within the stage-specific windows, which is why the record's deadline_date is only meaningful as the 30 November master's-stage date.",
            "Step 1 to first outcome: within two to four weeks of receiving the online application, the applicant receives either a rejection or a request to submit documents and references.",
            "Step 2: three weeks to assemble the documents and up to six weeks for the references, with a receipt confirmation on arrival.",
            "The selection committee meets eight to ten times a year, and the applicant is informed of the final decision at the latest one week after the meeting.",
            "Total elapsed time from application to decision: three to seven months.",
            "The Foundation informs all applicants by email about the result of each individual stage.",
            "Applicants who have not yet submitted their online application can log in at any time and continue editing it."
          ],
          "official_application_route": [
            "Complete the online application form published for the Grundförderung für Ausländer:innen at https://www.fes.de/oas/portal/pls/portal/bewsti2014.bewmaske?pFprog=2&pkn=A, in German.",
            "The form is checked by FES staff against the formal and substantive criteria, and a decision or a document request follows within two to four weeks.",
            "On invitation, submit the document package and two academic references through the Foundation's application login within three weeks for documents and up to six weeks for references, using the Grundförderung checklist at https://www.fes.de/index.php?eID=dumpFile&t=f&f=160624 as the governing list.",
            "Attend the first selection interview with a Vertrauensdozentin or Vertrauensdozent if invited.",
            "Attend the second selection interview with a member of the selection committee if shortlisted.",
            "Submit the Foundation's travel-cost reimbursement form for the Grundförderung if you have incurred interview travel costs.",
            "The decision is communicated by email at the latest one week after the selection committee's meeting. The Foundation does not publish a postal submission route for the Grundförderung; the online system is the route."
          ],
          "program_type": "Political foundation scholarship for international students in Germany",
          "region": "Germany — study must take place at a German public or state-recognised university, higher education institution or university of applied sciences; applicants may apply from Germany or from abroad"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are, or will be, enrolled at a German public or state-recognised university in a Bachelor's, Master's, Diplom or Staatsexamen programme",
            "Have your first graded transcript (erste benotete Leistungsnachweise) ready",
            "Prepare proof of very good German; B2 is accepted even without a certificate",
            "Collect evidence of social-political engagement, including engagement in your country of origin",
            "Have an expert opinion (Gutachten) ready - the application requires documents plus an assessment",
            "Apply as early as possible because the foundation aims for long funding periods"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Insufficient German - the foundation requires very good German even for English-taught programmes",
            "Grades that are not above average for the degree programme at that university",
            "Missing first graded transcripts at the time of application",
            "Application not submitted in German",
            "Missing expert opinion (Gutachten) or incomplete document upload",
