            "Grant-in-Aid for Scientific Research (Grant-in-Aid for JSPS Research Fellow) for cooperative research-related expenses, applied for by the host researcher through the host institution"
          ],
          "not_covered_or_excluded": [
            "Outbound airfare and the settling-in allowance are not paid to a candidate who has been living in Japan with a mailing address before the fellowship start date",
            "The Grant-in-Aid for Scientific Research (Grant-in-Aid for JSPS Research Fellow) is applied for by the host researcher through the host institution, so it is not a personal entitlement of the fellow",
            "The published provisions contain no tuition waiver, because the programme is a research appointment rather than a degree programme",
            "The published provisions contain no mention of any allowance for family members or dependants of the fellow",
            "The published provisions contain no arrangement for visiting the host institution at another research institution, including one overseas, other than the statement that fellows may spend part of the tenure there when recognised as necessary to advance their research"
          ],
          "benefits": [
            "Settling-in allowance and outbound airfare are not paid to a candidate who has been living in Japan with a mailing address before the fellowship start date",
            "Fellows may spend part of the tenure at another research institution, including one located overseas, when recognised as necessary to advance their research",
            "From the FY2024 application, JSPS sends the award letter and related documents for successful candidates to the host institutions"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Be a citizen of a country that has diplomatic relations with Japan (JSPS treats Taiwanese and Palestinian researchers in this manner)",
            "As of April 1 of the fiscal year, have obtained a doctoral degree within six years of the date the fellowship goes into effect, or who are expected to receive a Ph.D. by the start date of the fellowship period",
            "Previously awarded and started fellows under the JSPS Postdoctoral Fellowship Program for Research in Japan (Standard, Pathway to University positions in Japan) are not eligible",
            "Japanese citizens and permanent residents of Japan are not eligible",
            "Candidates must submit an original doctoral degree certificate or diploma before the fellowship starting date"
          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "Be a citizen of a country that has diplomatic relations with Japan (JSPS treats Taiwanese and Palestinian researchers in this manner)",
            "As of April 1 of the fiscal year, hold a doctoral degree obtained on or after April 2 of the year six years before the fiscal year, or be expected to receive a Ph.D. by the start date of the fellowship period",
            "Whether or not the candidate is employed in a full-time position is not considered",
            "Time taken for maternity and/or parental leave is subtracted from the six-year limit, counting every four weeks of leave as one month",
            "The field of research may be in any field of the humanities, social sciences and natural sciences",
            "The host researcher must be a full-time researcher at a KAKENHI-eligible institution, eligible to apply for a KAKENHI grant, and may submit up to three applications"
          ],
          "ineligibility_conditions": [
            "Those who have previously been awarded and started a fellowship under the JSPS Postdoctoral Fellowship Program for Research in Japan (Standard, and Pathway to University positions in Japan) are not eligible",
            "Japanese citizens are not eligible",
            "Foreigners with permanent residence status in Japan are not eligible",
            "A candidate who cannot produce an original copy of the doctoral degree certificate or diploma before the fellowship starting date cannot take up the award, even if selected"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Citizens of countries with diplomatic relations with Japan, including Taiwan and Palestine; permanent residents of Japan and Japanese citizens are not eligible.",
          "international_eligibility": "Open to nationals of any country that has diplomatic relations with Japan, with Taiwan and Palestine treated by JSPS in the same way. A candidate who is already living in Japan with a mailing address remains eligible but is not paid the outbound airfare or the settling-in allowance.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [],
            "masters": [],
