          "host_requirements": [
            "Applications must be submitted to JSPS by a host researcher in Japan via the head of their university or institution",
            "The host researcher must be a full-time researcher at a KAKENHI-eligible institution and must be eligible to apply for a KAKENHI grant",
            "Each host researcher may submit up to three applications",
            "The host researcher chooses the screening category from the FY2027 Review Section Table, and reviews are grouped into Review Section Sets with assigned reviewers",
            "Depending on the institution, the host may set its own deadline more than one month before the JSPS application deadline",
            "The institution's application must be sent (transmitted) to the president of JSPS by the application deadline for the programme",
            "Before sending, the host institution must verify that the application has been approved by the head of the institution and that the below-stated requirements will be carried out if the application is approved",
            "When submitting, the institution must first check the \"List of Applications\" on the JSPS Electronic Application System to verify that the registered information is correct",
            "The published selection policy requires the applicant's institution to establish a suitable place for the candidate to work and stay",
            "From the FY2024 application, JSPS sends the award letter and related documents for successful candidates to host institutions rather than to the candidates directly"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Applications must be submitted to JSPS by a host researcher in Japan via the head of their university or institution",
            "Use the JSPS Electronic Application System, available approximately two months before the application period",
            "Host institution must verify approval by the head of the institution and the stated requirements",
            "Each host researcher may submit up to three applications"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "FORM1 (Reference) for the JSPS Electronic Application System, completed by the host researcher",
            "FORM2 completed by the foreign candidate",
            "One-page letter of recommendation from the candidate's recommender, written in English or Japanese",
            "An original copy of the doctoral degree certificate or diploma, submitted after selection and before the fellowship starting date"
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "Applications are made only on the JSPS Electronic Application System, which becomes available approximately two months before the JSPS application period",
            "FORM2 uses the FY2027 template; the page states the data was replaced as of June 8, 2026 with no change to content, only the default character width of text fields, and that using the data prior to replacement will not affect the evaluation",
            "The Letter of Recommendation must be within one page and must be written in English or in Japanese, using the official sample format supplied on the Application Guidelines page",
            "FORM1 is entered on the JSPS Electronic Application System by the host researcher, not on a separate file",
            "The host institution must check the \"List of Applications\" on the JSPS Electronic Application System before transmitting, to verify the registered information is correct",
            "No file size limit, accepted file type or certified translation rule is published on the official guidance pages read"
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Selection of applicants (host researcher) and candidates (invited overseas researchers) is done by the JSPS International Program Committee, made up of Japan's frontline researchers",
            "Two-stage selection: a document review in the first stage and a panel review in the second",
            "Document review is conducted by six examiners per application, with experts in the subject field assigned according to the contents of the application",
            "Graduated scoring system on a scale of 1 to 5: 5 superlative, 4 excellent, 3 good, 2 fair, 1 poor",
            "Marks are made on a comprehensive basis, taking into account research achievements, the research plan, estimated research capacity, future potential of the research, and establishment of new research networks",
            "The averaged score in the document review is used as the primary screening criterion in the panel review",
            "Panel review selects a specified number of applicants in each panel review section",
            "The host researcher selects the screening category from the Review Section Table; Review Section Sets pair each review section with the reviewers who screen it, and reviewers are selected in a balanced manner for a diverse range of perspectives",
            "Published selection policy: the collaboration must contribute to advancing science in Japan and other countries",
            "Published selection policy: the collaboration must be expected to advance the subject research",
            "Published selection policy: the applicant and candidate must have established contact in advance and created a concrete research plan",
            "Published selection policy: the applicant's institution must establish a suitable place for the candidate to work and stay",
            "Published selection policy: as much as possible, unbalance should be avoided in the selectees' nationalities, host institutions and areas of specialization, and care should be taken to allow people from a wide diversity of countries to come to Japan",
            "Published selection policy: not only the score of the document review but also the examiners' reasons and comments are to be given adequate consideration",
            "Published selection policy: two selection judgements are made, Selected and Not-selected",
            "Integrity rules: any reviewer with a potential conflict of interest is removed from the Review Committee for the relevant review, and all Review Committee members are obliged to comply with a confidentiality and non-disclosure agreement"
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Published FY2026 outcomes by review section. 1st recruitment: Humanities 125 applied / 10 selected; Social sciences 114 / 9; Mathematical and physical sciences 305 / 24; Chemistry 177 / 14; Engineering sciences 510 / 39; Informatics 76 / 6; Biological sciences 96 / 7; Agriculture/Environmental sciences 292 / 23; Medicine dentistry and pharmacy 173 / 13; total 1,868 applied / 145 selected, selection ratio 7.8%. 2nd recruitment: Humanities 136 / 8; Social sciences 128 / 7; Mathematical and physical sciences 361 / 20; Chemistry 242 / 14; Engineering sciences 623 / 35; Informatics 80 / 4; Biological sciences 124 / 7; Agriculture/Environmental sciences 349 / 19; Medicine dentistry and pharmacy 188 / 11; total 2,231 applied / 125 selected, selection ratio 5.6%.",
          "application_method": [
