          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "Do not try to apply on your own. There is no candidate-facing portal: the host researcher enters the application and the head of the host institution transmits it to JSPS. Start the host relationship first, and note that this programme publishes three rounds a year, so a missed host deadline only costs you one round, not a whole year.",
            "Check the country rule carefully before anything else. Citizenship alone is not the only route: three or more continuous years of research at an institution in an eligible country also qualifies, but Japanese resident-card holders with a Japanese mailing address at the JSPS deadline are excluded outright.",
