      "image_alt_text": "POSCO TJ Park Foundation",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The POSCO Global Scholarship in Korea, also called the Global Future Leaders Scholarship Program, funds international students admitted to a master's or doctoral programme at a designated Korean graduate school and recommended by that institution. Published benefits are full tuition, living expenses, a settlement fee, insurance premium, and Korean language and cultural support.",
          "purpose": [
            "An inbound scholarship supporting global talents to complete Master's and doctoral programs in Korea, published as 'For Next Generation Global Leaders'",
            "The programme empowers promising global leaders by offering full tuition and living expenses as they pursue Master's or doctoral degrees at top Korean universities",
            "Unlike traditional Korean scholarships aimed at supporting domestic students abroad, the programme uniquely welcomes outstanding individuals from around the world to study in Korea and build meaningful connections with Korean society",
            "Through academic coursework and immersive experiences including industry visits and cultural programs, awardees gain in-depth knowledge of Korea's economy, society and values",
            "As they complete their degrees, awardees are equipped to become globally-minded leaders who bridge their home countries with Korea and contribute to a more interconnected world",
            "Umbrella rationale published by the Foundation: POSCO Global Scholarship is founded on the belief that deeper mutual understanding among individuals leads to stronger global connections, ultimately contributing to peace and shared prosperity around the world",
            "The Foundation operates the programme to promote mutual understanding through global talent exchange and collaboration, and to help build a global network of next-generation leaders"
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [],
          "degree_levels": [
            "Master's",
            "PhD"
          ],
          "study_type": [
            "Inbound scholarship degree programme (Master's, Doctoral and Integrated Master's and Doctoral)",
            "Institutional recommendation route: the admitting graduate school submits the recommendation",
            "Delivered in English-language academic study at Korean graduate schools, with Korean language education support and cultural programmes as published extras"
          ],
          "degree_award": "A full degree. The award funds a Master's program (full tuition for 4 semesters and living expenses for 22 months) or a Doctoral program / Integrated Master's and Doctoral program (full tuition for 6 semesters and living expenses for 36 months) at a designated Korean graduate school. Awardees attend a certificate award ceremony, published as stage 5 of the selection procedure in March.",
          "duration": "Master's: full tuition for 4 semesters, living expenses for 22 months. Doctoral or integrated master's and doctoral: full tuition for 6 semesters, living expenses for 36 months.",
          "application_cycle": "Annual: graduate school admission around November, recommendation submission around December, foundation interview around January, final selection announcement around February, certificate award ceremony in March.",
          "deadline_central": null,
          "deadline_central_display": "Recommendation submission by the graduate school around December; the page publishes approximate months only.",
          "deadline_institutional": "The recommendation is submitted by the admitting graduate school, so the effective institutional deadline is set by that university.",
          "deadline_note": "The Foundation publishes only approximate months, marked with a tilde (~Nov, ~Dec, ~Jan, ~Feb). There is no day-level date for any stage. Because the recommendation is institutional, the binding date is the graduate school's own, which the Foundation does not publish either.",
          "status": "UPCOMING",
          "funding_type": "Foundation scholarship",
          "funding_label": "Full tuition, living expenses of KRW 1,000,000 per month, one-time settlement fee of KRW 1,000,000, National Health Insurance premium",
