      "selection_notes": "A specialized OAS and UDD committee selects the recipients. Elements considered in awarding the scholarships are geographic distribution of the candidates, the applicant's profile including education and project outline and recommendation, the applicant's potential impact on completion of the course, and gender distribution. A selection committee pre-selects participants on that profile; pre-selected participants may be interviewed in English. Results are published at www.oas.org/scholarships by February 2027, and unsuccessful applicants are not contacted.",
      "notes": "This is a fee-reduction award, not a living stipend: the scholarship covers USD 3,400 of a USD 3,800 course fee and the recipient must find USD 400 plus study materials, equipment and internet access themselves. No living cost, travel or health insurance funding is published, so applicants must not budget this as full funding. Not eligible: current OAS scholarship recipients, GS/OAS staff and their immediate family, GS/OAS consultants, and permanent OAS staff and their immediate family. The recipient may decline the scholarship before the program start date without financial penalty, but declining after that date without proof of force majeure may require repayment of all funds awarded. The GS/OAS reserves the right to cancel this scholarship announcement at any time during the process.",
