      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The SG/OAS awards tuition discounts for online postgraduate study with UNIR (Spain), the Escuela de Posgrado Peruana de NEWMAN (Peru) and UNIR Mexico. Up to 885 places are offered, with a 60% discount on total tuition for official master's programmes and official degrees, and a 50% discount for UNIR Formación Permanente programmes, applicable only to the value of the study programme. Admission fees, translation and notarisation, study materials, titulation and degree-awarding procedures, and any other cost not listed are explicitly excluded, and recipients must personally demonstrate the financial capacity to cover the uncovered programme costs, so this is not full funding.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Citizens or permanent legal residents of OAS Member States other than Nicaragua, from a country other than the one they plan to study in, who have already been admitted to a participating online programme and can fund the non-discounted portion of the tuition themselves.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must be nationals or permanent legal residents of an OAS Member State except Nicaragua, must not study in their own country of origin, must already have completed admission to a participating programme, must not have held another OAS scholarship at the same level, and must prove they can fund the costs not covered.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Seran elegibles los interesados con nacionalidad y/o residencia legal permanente de cualquiera de los Estados Miembros de la SG/OEA, excepto Nicaragua.",
        "No se puede estudiar en su propio pais de origen.",
        "Para ser beneficiario de la beca, el candidato debera haber finalizado el proceso de admision y haber sido admitido en uno de los programas de estudios en una de las instituciones.",
        "No haber recibido otras becas academicas de la OEA, en el mismo nivel de estudios propuesto a esta convocatoria.",
        "Antes de iniciar cualquier Programa, todo Becario debera demostrar su capacidad financiera para solventar los costos del Programa no cubierto por la Beca dentro de un plazo establecido."
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "60% discount on the total tuition (colegiatura) for UNIR official master's programmes and official degrees, and for EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico official master's programmes.",
        "50% discount on the total tuition for UNIR Formación Permanente programmes.",
        "The discount applies only to the value of the study programme."
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Up to 885 places available across the three institutions for the 2026 academic course."
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Have been admitted to one of the programmes listed in the call, evidenced by an application letter issued by the institution.",
        "Pay the admission fee (cuota de admision) required by the institution in order to be admitted to the study programme.",
        "Before starting the programme, demonstrate financial capacity to cover the programme costs not covered by the scholarship within the established period.",
        "Maintain an average of 5/10 or higher to keep the scholarship for the duration of the programme.",
        "Not be reported with baja academica through absences from the programme and/or failure of subjects."
      ],
      "english_requirement": null,
      "application_method": [
        "Step 1: Follow the admission process for the chosen programme directly with the institution, submitting all documentation the institution requires, and pay the admission fee.",
        "Step 2: Once admitted and in receipt of the institution's application letter (carta de aplicacion), the applicant is automatically considered a candidate for the OAS-UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico scholarship; there is no separate scholarship application form.",
        "Step 3: UNIR, EP NEWMAN, UNIR Mexico and the OAS form a specialised committee to select the scholarship holders.",
        "Step 4: Await publication of results at www.oea.org/becas, announced from November 2026 for the 2a convocatoria.",
        "Step 5: Only selected candidates are contacted by email by UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico with the scholarship offer and acceptance instructions; after accepting, the scholarship holder starts the corresponding payment procedures with the chosen institution."
      ],
      "selection_notes": "A specialised committee of UNIR, EP NEWMAN, UNIR Mexico and the OAS selects the scholarship holders, considering the geographic distribution of candidates according to the needs of Member States as reflected in the UNDP Human Development Index, the academic profile and merit and academic credentials, the applicant's potential impact on completing the programme, and gender distribution.",
      "notes": "This is a tuition discount only and it does not cover the whole fee, so applicants must not treat it as full funding. The 2a convocatoria deadlines fall between 19 and 30 October 2026, so the UNIR and EP NEWMAN lines close first on 19 October 2026. Excluded from eligibility: SG/OAS officials, persons under contract by results with the SG/OAS, Permanent Mission staff, and relatives of all of the above. Nicaraguan nationals and permanent legal residents are excluded. Applicants cannot study in their own country of origin. The call states programme costs shown in the document are orientative and may be lower in some countries, and it repeatedly warns that neither the OAS nor the institutions take responsibility for recognition, legalisation, homologation or convalidacion of the resulting title in the applicant's country of country of origin. The scholarship is conditional on academic performance, and it applies only to the value of the study programme. The SG/OAS reserves the right to cancel this announcement at any point in the process. The document's benefits section refers to a 'Responsabilidades del Becario' section on page 27, but the official PDF available at this URL contains only 10 pages, so that section could not be read.",
      "image_url": "https://www.oas.org/imgs/en/OEA-ENG-Main-Updated-AUG2025.svg",
      "image_source_url": "https://www.oas.org/en/scholarships/",
      "image_source_type": "official_government",
      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
      "image_alt_text": "Organization of American States",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The SG/OAS and three partner institutions (UNIR Spain, EP NEWMAN Peru and UNIR Mexico) sponsor tuition discounts for distance/online postgraduate study. Up to 885 places are offered: a 60% discount on total tuition for official master's programmes and official degrees, and a 50% discount for UNIR Formacion Permanente programmes, applicable only to the value of the study programme. Admission fees, translation and notarisation, study materials, titulation and degree-awarding procedures, and any other cost not listed are explicitly excluded, and the holder must cover the uncovered 40% (or 50%) personally and demonstrate that financial capacity in a set period before starting, so this is not full funding.",
          "purpose": [
            "The Secretariat General of the Organization of American States (SG/OAS) and UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico decided to support outstanding individuals from the Americas through the sponsorship of these academic scholarships, in order to continue their postgraduate studies.",
            "UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico state a mission of integral student training to form professionals with the competencies society currently demands, and specifically target those who, for various circumstances, cannot access in-person centres or who prefer more open and innovative online solutions offered by emerging technologies.",
            "The SG/OAS, through its Department of Human Development, Education and Employment (DDHEE), supports its Member States in creating and running programmes that promote human development at all educational levels, working to strengthen democratic values and regional security and to improve the quality and equity of education."
          ],
          "sdg_requirement": false,
          "sdg_requirement_details": [],
          "study_type": [
            "Postgraduate study (maestrias/master's degrees and grados/official undergraduate degrees)",
            "Distance (virtual) study only, delivered in Spanish",
            "Formacion Permanente (permanent training) programmes, which are not degree-awarding"
          ],
          "degree_award": "Mixed. Official master's programmes and official degrees (Grados Oficiales) award a recognised title; Formacion Permanente programmes are professional training and are not presented as degree-awarding. The call states that neither the OAS nor the institutions take any responsibility for acceptance of titles or diplomas in the student's country of origin.",
          "duration": "UNIR Maestrias Oficiales 12 months; UNIR Grados Oficiales 4 years (programas de Grado), with the beca de Grado applying only to the first teaching year; UNIR Formacion Permanente 21 to 34 weeks depending on the programme; EP NEWMAN maestrias 12 months; UNIR Mexico maestrias 18 or 24 months",
          "application_cycle": "Curso Academico 2026 with two calls: 1a convocatoria Primavera 2026 (closed) and 2a convocatoria Otono 2026 (open at the time of reading). Each institution publishes its own deadline inside the same convocatoria, and results are published on different dates for each institution.",
          "deadline_central": "2026-10-19",
          "deadline_central_display": "2a convocatoria: 19 de octubre de 2026 (UNIR Maestrías Oficiales y Grados Oficiales, and EP NEWMAN); 26 de octubre de 2026 (UNIR Mexico); 30 de octubre de 2026 (UNIR Formacion Permanente)",
          "deadline_institutional": "Three different institutional deadlines fall inside the same convocatoria: 19 October 2026, 26 October 2026 and 30 October 2026, depending on the institution and programme. The 1a convocatoria equivalents were 16 March 2026 (UNIR Maestrías Oficiales y Grados Oficiales), 31 March 2026 (UNIR Formación Permanente) and 10 April 2026 (EP NEWMAN and UNIR México).",
          "deadline_note": "There is no single central deadline. Each institution's table publishes its own closing date for the 2a convocatoria: 19 October 2026 for UNIR official master's and official degrees and for EP NEWMAN, 26 October 2026 for UNIR Mexico, and 30 October 2026 for UNIR Formacion Permanente. Results are also published per institution: October 2026 for UNIR official master's and degrees, November 2026 for UNIR Formacion Permanente, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico. Programme start for the 2a convocatoria is October/November 2026 depending on the programme. The SG/OAS reserves the right to cancel this announcement at any moment during the process.",
          "status": "OPEN",
          "funding_type": "Partial Funding (percentage tuition discount scholarship)",
          "funding_label": "OAS tuition discount scholarship: 60% off total tuition for official master's programmes and official degrees; 50% off total tuition for UNIR Formacion Permanente programmes",
          "funding_amount": null,
          "funding_currency": null,
          "funding_period": null,
          "tuition_coverage": true,
          "tuition_coverage_note": "Partial only. The discount applies exclusively to the tuition (colegiatura) and only to the value of the study programme. The beneficiary must personally cover the remaining 40% (official master's and degrees) or 50% (Formacion Permanente) of the total programme cost.",
          "living_cost_coverage": false,
          "travel_coverage": false,
          "fully_funded": false,
          "tuition_rule": "No institution waives tuition under this scholarship. The discount is applied by the awarding institution against the total tuition of the study programme, and only to the value of that programme. The holder remains liable for the uncovered 40% (official master's and degrees at UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico) or 50% (UNIR Formacion Permanente) of the total programme cost.",
          "home_tuition_rule": "Not applicable to the published terms, because the programmes are delivered distance/online by institutions in Spain, Peru and Mexico and the call states the applicant cannot study in their own country of origin. The call is silent on whether home-country tuition is suspended, so nothing can be established.",
          "host_institution_fee": "The admission fee (cuota de admision) required by the institution must be paid by the applicant in order to be admitted, and it is expressly excluded from the scholarship. Any additional cost incurred by the applicant to be admitted is not reimbursable and confers no acquired right to the scholarship. The call advises consulting the institution directly before paying the admission fee, as admission costs are not published.",
          "tax_status": null,
          "covered_expenses": [
            "A 60% discount on the total tuition (colegiatura) for UNIR Maestrias Oficiales",
            "A 60% discount on the total tuition for UNIR Grados Oficiales, applying only to the first teaching year",
            "A 60% discount on the total tuition for EP NEWMAN maestrias",
            "A 60% discount on the total tuition for UNIR Mexico maestrias oficiales",
            "A 50% discount on the total tuition for UNIR Formacion Permanente programmes"
          ],
          "not_covered_or_excluded": [
            "Admission fee (cuota de admision), expressly excluded",
            "Translation of documents",
            "Notarisation or authentication of documents",
            "Study materials",
            "Titulation procedures and obtaining the degree (titulos, examenes de admision, servicios de graduacion, expedicion de grado)",
            "Issuance of certificates or constancias",
            "Legalisation of documents",
            "Any other cost not expressly listed in the call",
            "All living costs, accommodation and subsistence: the call does not address them at all",
            "Travel costs: the call does not address them at all",
            "Health insurance: the call does not address it at all"
          ],
          "benefits": [
            "Discount conditional on academic performance: the beneficiary must maintain an average of 5/10 or higher for each academic period",
            "The beneficiary must not be reported with baja academica for absences from the programme and/or failure of subjects",
            "May decline the scholarship up to one week before the start of the programme without financial penalty",
            "The discount is applied only to the value of the study programme, so no cash stipend is paid"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Nacionalidad y/o residencia legal permanente de cualquiera de los Estados Miembros de la SG/OAE, excepto Nicaragua.",
            "No se puede estudiar en su propio pais de origen.",
            "Haber finalizado el proceso de admision y haber sido admitido en uno de los programas de estudios en una de las instituciones.",
            "No haber recibido otras becas academicas de la OEA en el mismo nivel de estudios propuesto a esta convocatoria.",
            "Demostrar la capacidad financiera para solventar los costos del Programa no cubierto por la Beca antes de iniciar el Programa."
          ],
          "general_eligibility": [
            "Nationality and/or permanent legal residence of any SG/OAS Member State, except Nicaragua",
            "Cannot study in their own country of origin",
            "Must have completed the admission process and been admitted to one of the study programmes at one of the institutions",
            "Must not have received other OAS academic scholarships at the same level of study proposed in this call",
            "Must demonstrate the financial capacity to cover the programme costs not covered by the scholarship before starting the programme"
          ],
          "ineligibility_conditions": [
            "Officials of the SG/OAS are not eligible",
            "People who are under a results-based contract with the SG/OAS are not eligible",
            "Personnel of the Permanent Missions to the OAS are not eligible",
            "Family members of all of the persons listed above are not eligible",
            "Nicaraguan nationals and permanent legal residents are excluded",
            "Anyone proposing to study in their own country of origin is excluded",
            "Holders of other OAS academic scholarships at the same level of study are excluded",
            "Applicants who have not been admitted to a participating programme are excluded, since admission is a precondition of the candidacy"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Nationals or permanent legal residents of any SG/OAS Member State except Nicaragua, who are not studying in their own country of origin.",
          "international_eligibility": "Explicitly for OAS Member States. Eligibility is by nationality or permanent legal residence, with Nicaragua excluded, and the applicant must not be studying in their country of origin. The programme is delivered in Spanish at institutions in Spain, Peru and Mexico.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "Grados Oficiales are 4-year programmes, but the beca de Grado applies only to the first teaching year (1 ano), as the call states explicitly",
              "Study is distance/virtual and in Spanish"
            ],
            "masters": [
              "UNIR Maestrias Oficiales: 12 months",
              "EP NEWMAN maestrias: 12 months",
              "UNIR Mexico maestrias oficiales: 18 or 24 months",
              "Study is distance/virtual and in Spanish",
              "Must maintain an average of 5/10 or higher for each academic period and pass all subjects within the time set by the programme to keep the scholarship"
            ],
            "phd": []
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "Must be admitted to one of the programmes listed in the call's programme tables at one of the three named institutions: Universidad Internacional de La Rioja (UNIR), Escuela de Posgrado Peruana de NEWMAN (EP NEWMAN) or Universidad Internacional de La Rioja en Mexico (UNIR Mexico)",
            "Must follow the institution's own admission process and present all documentation that institution requires",
            "The institution issues the carta de aplicacion to the admitted student; receipt of that letter automatically makes the applicant a candidate for the scholarship",
            "Must comply with all the academic guidelines and admission requirements set by the institution and any updates the academic authorities make"
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Be admitted to a participating programme and obtain the institution's carta de aplicacion.",
            "Pay the admission fee required by the institution in order to be admitted.",
            "Demonstrate financial capacity for the uncovered programme costs within the established period before starting.",
            "Maintain an average of 5/10 or higher for each academic period.",
            "Pass all subjects of the curriculum within the time established by the programme.",
            "Not be reported with baja academica for absences or failed subjects."
          ],
          "documents": [
            "The admission documentation required by the chosen institution. The call states the applicant must present all documentation that the institution requires, and that once admitted the institution issues the scholarship holder a carta de aplicacion.",
            "No separate document list is published for the scholarship itself, because the candidacy is automatic on admission."
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Distribucion geografica de los candidatos, tomando en cuenta las necesidades mas importantes de los Estados Miembros, conforme al Indice de Desarrollo Humano reportado por el PNUD.",
            "Perfil academico, merito y credenciales academicas.",
            "Potencial de impacto del postulante en la finalizacion del programa de estudios.",
            "Distribucion de genero."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "UNIR, EP NEWMAN, UNIR Mexico and the OAS constitute a specialised committee to select the awardees, considering four published elements: geographic distribution of candidates according to the UNDP Human Development Index and the needs of Member States; academic profile, merit and academic credentials; the applicant's potential impact on completing the programme of study; and gender distribution. The same three of the four criteria are also listed in the eligibility section of the call. The OAS does not provide individual feedback on why an applicant was not selected.",
          "application_method": [
            "Paso 1 - Admission to the study programme: it is indispensable to have been admitted to one of the programmes listed in the call's programme tables; applicants follow the admission process of the programme of interest and present all documentation the institution requires; once admitted, the institution issues the applicant a carta de aplicacion.",
            "Paso 2 - Candidacy to the OEA scholarship: on being admitted and receiving the carta de aplicacion, the applicant is automatically considered a candidate for the scholarship. There is no separate scholarship application form.",
            "Paso 3 - Selection: UNIR, EP NEWMAN, UNIR Mexico and the OAS constitute a specialised committee to select the awardees.",
            "Paso 4 - Publication of results: the applicant waits for the results, announced at www.oas.org/becas from April 2026 and November 2026 depending on the call.",
            "Paso 5 - Acceptance and start of classes: only selected candidates are contacted by email with the scholarship offer and the instructions to accept it; once accepted, the beneficiary starts the corresponding payment procedures with the chosen institution."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Choose one of the three institutions and one of the programmes listed in the call's programme tables, and note that institution's own 2a convocatoria deadline",
            "2. Follow that institution's admission process directly and present all documentation the institution requires",
            "3. Pay the admission fee (cuota de admision) required by the institution to be admitted",
            "4. Receive the carta de aplicacion from the institution on admission - this automatically enters you as a candidate for the OEA scholarship",
            "5. Prepare and be ready to demonstrate your financial capacity for the costs the scholarship does not cover, within the period established before the programme starts",
            "6. Await the results of the selection committee, published at www.oas.org/becas in November 2026 for the 2a convocatoria",
            "7. If selected, receive the offer and acceptance instructions by email, accept, and begin the payment procedures with the institution",
            "8. Programmes start in October/November 2026 depending on the programme"
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant applies directly to the chosen institution through that institution's own admission process; there is no OAS scholarship form to submit",
            "On admission the institution issues the carta de aplicacion, which is the document that generates the scholarship candidacy",
            "Results are published by the OAS at www.oas.org/becas"
          ],
          "application_portal": "Each institution's own admission process; the call links programme tables and enrolment-information forms for UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico. Results are published at www.oas.org/becas",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "official_application_route": [
            "Direct to the host institution for admission; the scholarship candidacy is automatic on admission, so no separate OAS submission exists",
            "A carta de aplicacion issued by the institution is what places the applicant in the pool",
            "Offers and acceptance instructions come by email from the institution to selected candidates only"
          ],
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "The beneficiary must cover 40% (Maestrias Oficiales and Grados at UNIR, EP NEWMAN and UNIR Mexico) or 50% (UNIR Formacion Permanente) of the total programme cost that the institutions do not cover.",
            "Any additional expense the applicant incurs to be admitted is not reimbursable and confers no acquired right to the scholarship.",
            "The beneficiary must bear all other programme costs, for example issuance of certificates or constancias, admission examinations, graduation services, issuance of the degree, and legalisation of documents.",
            "The beneficiary must comply with all academic guidelines and admission requirements set by the institution and any updates made by the academic authorities.",
            "To keep the scholarship, the beneficiary must pass all subjects of the curriculum within the time set by the programme and obtain an average of 5/10 or higher for each academic period; otherwise UNIR, EP NEWMAN, UNIR Mexico and/or the OAS reserve the right to demand repayment of the value corresponding to the amount invested in the scholarship.",
            "The beneficiary may decline the scholarship up to one week before the start of the programme with no financial penalty; declining after the programme has started, without proof of force majeure, exposes the candidate to a demand for repayment of the total funds invested in the scholarship up to the moment of declining.",
            "The beneficiary must commit to working in their country of origin or of legal residence, in one of the OAS Member States, or in an international organisation, for a minimum time equal to the duration of the scholarship; failing that, the institutions and/or the OAS reserve the right to require reimbursement of the total value of the award."
          ],
          "deferrable": false,
          "renewable": null,
          "return_home_required": true,
          "clinical_restriction": null,
          "arrival_rules": [],
          "timeline_rules": [
            "2a convocatoria (Otono 2026) deadlines: 19 October 2026 (UNIR Maestrías Oficiales y Grados Oficiales, and EP NEWMAN), 26 October 2026 (UNIR México), 30 October 2026 (UNIR Formación Permanente)",
            "Publication of selected candidates for the 2a convocatoria: October 2026 (UNIR Maestrías Oficiales y Grados Oficiales) and November 2026 (UNIR Formación Permanente, EP NEWMAN, UNIR México)",
            "Start of study programmes for the 2a convocatoria: October/November 2026 depending on the programme",
            "The scholarship may be declined up to one week before the start of the programme without financial penalty",
            "The SG/OAS reserves the right to cancel this announcement at any moment during the process"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "Admisiones: +34 91 567 44 94, atencion.estudiante@unir.net. Para dudas sobre programas de estudio o instituciones educativas: masterunir@unir.net, www.unir.net. Informacion general de becas OEA: Scholarships@oas.org.",
            "email": "atencion.estudiante@unir.net; masterunir@unir.net; Scholarships@oas.org"
