          "deadline_note": "Three separate date sets fall inside the 2026-2027 cycle. The portal opens 7 September 2026 for most graduate programmes but 30 September 2026 for M.Sc. and Ph.D. Computational Biology. The final deadline is 15 December 2026 at 5p.m. GST for all graduate programmes except the Master in Applied Artificial Intelligence, whose deadline is 28 February 2027 at 5p.m. GST. Decision notification is 31 March 2027 at 5p.m. GST for all except MAAI (15 April 2027), and the offer response deadline is 15 April 2027 for all except MAAI (30 April 2027). Only one application per admission cycle must be submitted; multiple submissions will not be processed, and applicants can only apply to one programme per intake. The English language proficiency component must be in the submission by the application deadline or the application is considered incomplete.",
          "status": "OPEN",
          "funding_type": "Fully Funded (for students who secure funding; M.Sc. students are fee-paying by default)",
          "funding_label": "MBZUAI graduate funding: free tuition fees, a monthly stipend, one return airfare each year to the home country, health insurance for the approved funding period, and University-sponsored UAE residence visa and Emirates ID (where eligible). Published AED table: UAE nationals M.Sc. 37,500 / Ph.D. 43,500; international students M.Sc. 15,500 / Ph.D. 17,500 - period not stated on the page.",
          "funding_amount": null,
          "funding_currency": "AED",
          "funding_period": null,
          "tuition_coverage": true,
          "tuition_coverage_note": "Free tuition fees for funded students. Tuition is only free if funding is actually secured: M.Sc. students are fee-paying by default unless they obtain a faculty advisor-sponsored research or teaching assistantship or, for UAE nationals, an approved government scholarship. Cost of Attendance figures for Fall 2027 are stated to be still being finalized.",
          "living_cost_coverage": true,
          "travel_coverage": true,
          "fully_funded": true,
          "tuition_rule": "MBZUAI, as the awarding university, covers tuition in full for students it classifies as funded. Nobody waives tuition for the Master in Applied Artificial Intelligence, which is a fee-based programme explicitly not eligible for University or faculty-sponsored funding. Tuition for M.Sc. students who do not obtain a funding source applies as normal, and the Fall 2027 cost of attendance for those students is not yet published.",
          "home_tuition_rule": null,
          "host_institution_fee": "The published application fee is AED 200 for all applicants, payable after completing the screening exam. It is not refunded for a funded student except in the fee-waiver cases the University publishes (screening exam score of 75% or above, or reimbursement upon enrolment). The MAAI programme is charged AED 5,000 per credit, 34 credit hours, total AED 170,000, paid each semester.",
          "tax_status": null,
