          ],
          "selection_notes": "Applicants are evaluated on academic excellence, technical preparation, research potential, and alignment with their chosen programme. The screening exam is a substantive gate: it assesses foundational knowledge in areas relevant to the programme, including advanced mathematics, programming and core computer science topics, plus machine learning for Ph.D. applicants. A subset of applicants is then invited to a technical interview with admissions committee members, with instructions provided before the interview. Applications with unpaid fees are considered incomplete and do not proceed to review. MBZUAI states that admission is highly competitive and that space in the incoming cohort is limited, and it publishes no weighting between the four evaluation criteria.",
