          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "Do not assume an M.Sc. admission includes funding. M.Sc. students are fee-paying by default and need a faculty-sponsored assistantship or, if a UAE national, an approved government scholarship; funding is not guaranteed for all admitted students.",
            "Budget the uncovered tuition deliberately if you are an unfunded M.Sc. student. MBZUAI states the Fall 2027 cost of attendance is still being finalized, so you must ask the University for the figure rather than assume it.",
            "If you already hold external funding, disclose it. External money normally replaces the University stipend rather than being paid alongside it, so you may end up with less than you expected.",
            "The AED 200 fee comes after the screening exam, not before. Unpaid applications are considered incomplete and are never reviewed, so treat it as mandatory rather than optional.",
            "Watch the residency-specific document list. UAE nationals, children of Emirati mothers, and UAE residents each have a different set of identity documents beyond the passport and white-background photo.",
