          "selection_notes": "Scholarship consideration is not a separate competitive process with published criteria: HBKU states candidates are considered for scholarships during the admissions process, that no separate application is needed, and that scholarships are not automatically awarded to admitted students but are offered based on merit or financial need and available funds. The published selection path is therefore the ordinary admissions path - HBKU admissions team preliminary review for completion and eligibility, then assessment by the relevant college - with the funding decision embedded in it. HBKU publishes no ranking criteria, weighting or interview requirement for funding, and no individual feedback route. Continued eligibility is reviewed annually against academic progress and available funds, and stipend exceptions can be considered case by case depending on availability of funds and with the approval of the dean and the provost.",
          "application_method": [
            "Create a user account through the HBKU Apply Now portal",
            "Submit the application by choosing the desired college and program; up to two applications per academic year are permitted",
            "Log back into the account using the confirmation email instructions to submit supplementary documents and provide contact details for references",
            "The HBKU admissions team checks the application for completion and eligibility, then forwards it to the relevant college for assessment",
            "Await the college's decision and offer letter",
            "Scholarship consideration happens as part of the admissions process; no separate scholarship application is required"
          ],
