      "application_period": "No published opening or closing dates. Applicants register through the MOFA scholarship service form and are notified of results by email or SMS; amendments after submission are handled through the call centre at +971 80044444.",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The UAE Ministry of Foreign Affairs runs a scholarship programme for Emirati students to study a Bachelor's degree at one of the world's top universities approved by MOFA, specialising in fields that meet the needs of the UAE diplomatic corps. MOFA states in its FAQ that the programme covers all tuition costs in accordance with the programme's policies, and the applicant must already hold an unconditional direct academic acceptance from an approved university indicating the programme start and end dates and the total cost. The programme is not a general study-abroad scholarship: it carries a service obligation, requiring the holder to join the MOFA diplomatic corps for a period equivalent to the number of academic years covered by the scholarship and to join the Anwar Gargash Diplomatic Academy upon graduation.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Emirati nationals aged 17 to 21 (up to 22 at the time of application) with a high school diploma meeting the published percentage thresholds, an IELTS Academic score of 6.5 or equivalent, and an unconditional offer from a MOFA-approved university, who are willing to enter the UAE diplomatic corps.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must be UAE nationals holding a UAE passport and family book, aged between 17 and 21 with legal guardian approval, hold a high school diploma meeting the published percentage thresholds, have an IELTS Academic score of 6.5 or equivalent, and hold an acceptance letter from a MOFA-approved university.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Must be UAE nationals (holders of UAE passports and family book)",
        "Must be between 17 and 21 years old and have legal guardian approval; the FAQ states previous-year high school graduates may apply provided the applicant is between 17 and 22 years old at the time of application",
        "Must provide a certificate of Good Conduct and Behavior from the relevant official authorities in the UAE",
        "Must have a high school diploma: General Stream, General Technical Stream, American System and other systems require 90% and above; Advanced Stream, Advanced Technical Stream and SABIS System require 85% and above; Elite Stream and Advanced Science Program require 80% and above",
        "British System / IGCSE: completion of five IGCSE/GCSE subjects with a grade of B or higher and two AS/A Level subjects with a grade of C or higher",
        "International Baccalaureate (IB): completion of the IB Diploma with a minimum average of 30 points or higher",
        "School transcript listing all related instructional subjects",
        "Applicants must have an IELTS (Academic Module) score of 6.5 or above, or equivalent",
        "Applicants must hold an acceptance letter from an approved university listed and approved by MOFA",
        "Applicants must agree to study a third language, if required",
        "Male applicants must provide a certificate of exemption or completion of national service",
        "Applicants must agree to join the UAE diplomatic corps at the Ministry of Foreign Affairs for a period equivalent to the number of academic years covered by the scholarship",
        "Applicants must agree to join Anwar Gargash Diplomatic Academy (AGDA) upon graduation",
        "Applicants must provide parental consent to join the scholarship program",
        "Applicants cannot choose a university outside the MOFA-approved list"
