          "selection_notes": "The programme does not publish ranking criteria or a weighting. It publishes a process instead: the admission procedure includes a number of tests, interviews and additional conditions, and the interview is mandatory and must be passed successfully for the applicant to complete the scholarship requirements. Candidates are screened on published objective conditions first (nationality, age, conduct, high school stream threshold, English score, national service) and must already hold an unconditional acceptance from an approved university, in an approved specialty and country. Review and final approval then take between 3 to 5 months. MOFA publishes no individual feedback route and no appeal process.",
