      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowship supports excellent postdoctoral researchers throughout Europe and the world for up to two years, with international mobility as a key requirement. In EMBC Member States EMBO gives the host institution a grant to issue the fellow an employment contract covering employer and awardee social contributions, taxes and net salary; elsewhere the fellow receives a stipend, with a child daycare allowance, a dependent-child allowance and a travel and relocation lump sum. The award explicitly does not cover bench fees, overheads or consumables for the host supervisor or institute, and the actual rate depends on the country visited, so there is no single published amount. Applications are accepted year-round and enter one of two evaluation cycles each year, with the next hard deadline on Friday 22 January 2027 at 14:00 CET.",
          "purpose": [
            "EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowships support excellent postdoctoral researchers throughout Europe and the world for a period of up to two years.",
