          "citizenship_residency": "No nationality or residency requirement is published. The scheme supports postdoctoral researchers throughout Europe and the world, and the award route depends on the host location: a host-institution grant in EMBC Member States, a stipend elsewhere, and the same stipend route for fellowships in EMBC/EMBO global partner states (Chile, India, Singapore, Taiwan) and non-member states.",
          "international_eligibility": "Open to postdoctoral researchers from anywhere, subject to the mobility requirements, which are the core of the scheme: all applications must involve movement between countries, and applications to the country of the PhD, to a previous laboratory where the candidate worked for more than six months, to the PhD laboratory, institute or department, or to the previous supervisor's laboratory anywhere, are not considered. Hosts in EMBC Member States, in EMBC/EMBO global partner states (Chile, India, Singapore, Taiwan) and in non-member states are all supported, on different financial terms.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [],
            "masters": [],
            "phd": [
              "Not eligible at the pre-doctoral stage: applicants must hold a doctorate or equivalent at the start of the fellowship.",
              "A PhD already held at the time of application is acceptable only if it was obtained during the two years prior to the submission date.",
              "Applicants must already have at least one first author peer-reviewed publication, or a qualifying refereed preprint, at the time of application."
            ]
          },
          "host_requirements": [
            "The host must be a laboratory, institute or department in a different country from the candidate's PhD country, and not one where the candidate has previously worked for more than six months, and not the candidate's PhD laboratory, institute or department, and must not be a laboratory of the candidate's previous supervisor.",
            "If the candidate has already started working in the host laboratory, they must have been living in the host country for less than six months at the time the application is submitted.",
            "In EMBC Member States, the host institution issues the employment contract to the awardee according to the national and local regulations of that Member State, and signs a grant agreement with EMBO regulating the transfer of funds.",
            "EMBC-based fellows have access to the welfare system of the hosting country, including child benefits, and parental-leave costs covered by that system and/or by the hosting institute can support a fellowship extension at no cost to EMBO."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Hold a doctorate or equivalent at the start of the fellowship, obtained within the two years before application if already held.",
            "Have at least one first author publication accepted in or published in an international peer reviewed journal at the time of application, or a qualifying first author preprint with public in-depth peer reviews from an independent peer review service.",
            "Be moving between countries, and satisfy all the mobility exclusions.",
            "Be living in the host country for less than six months if you have already started in the host laboratory.",
            "Submit one application for one project at one host laboratory, through the online application system, with two references and receiving institute acceptance.",
            "Confirm completion of the application, because the confirmation date is the reference date for eligibility and evaluation.",
            "If you need an exception, contact the Fellowship Office before submitting; applications outside the eligibility criteria without prior approval are deemed ineligible.",
            "Start the fellowship within one calendar year from the relevant evaluation cut-off."
          ],
          "documents": [
            "Two references, submitted via the online application system",
            "Receiving institute acceptance, submitted via the online application system",
            "The application itself, with all required information, completed and confirmed through the online application system"
