          "document_format_rules": [
            "Applications and supporting documentation (two references, receiving institute acceptance) are only accepted via the online application system.",
            "Only fully completed applications will be considered.",
            "Registration for an EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowship online application account is not sufficient to enter the corresponding evaluation round; an application is only regarded as complete once all the required information is submitted and the candidate confirms completion.",
            "The EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowships guidelines (June 2026) are the governing document for detailed eligibility criteria, the definition of a refereed preprint, and further benefit information; the pages read point to them repeatedly for detail.",
            "The pages read publish no file type, file size, translation or signature rules for the reference letters or the institute acceptance."
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "EMBO considers a first author refereed preprint equivalent to a first author publication as one of the eligibility and assessment criteria for the EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowship scheme.",
            "The programme supports excellent postdoctoral researchers, with international mobility as a key requirement.",
            "At least one first author publication in an international peer reviewed journal (or a qualifying refereed preprint) is both an eligibility and an assessment criterion."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Applications are assessed within the spring or autumn evaluation round, using the scheme's eligibility and assessment criteria, which explicitly include the treatment of a first author refereed preprint as equivalent to a first author publication. EMBO publishes a separate Selection page and a Research Integrity page, neither of which was read, and an EMBO Fellowship Committee is named in the page's related links. The detailed assessment criteria sit in the EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowships guidelines (June 2026), which could not be read here because it is a PDF.",
          "application_method": [
            "Apply through the EMBO online application system; applications and supporting documentation are only accepted there.",
            "Submit two references and the receiving institute's acceptance as part of the application.",
            "Complete all required information and confirm completion, because the confirmation date is the reference date for eligibility and evaluation.",
            "Contact the EMBO Fellowship Office before submitting if you need an exception to any eligibility rule."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Check the eligibility rules, especially the two-year window on the PhD, the first author publication requirement, and every mobility exclusion.",
            "2. Secure a host laboratory in a different country that satisfies the mobility rules, and obtain the receiving institute's acceptance.",
            "3. If you need an exception, contact the EMBO Fellowship Office before submitting; do not submit a non-compliant application.",
            "4. Prepare two references and ask your referees to submit them through the online system, leaving time before the cut-off.",
            "5. Complete the online application in full, including the project description, and upload the two references and the receiving institute acceptance.",
            "6. Confirm completion of the application before 14:00 CET on the cut-off date - Friday 22 January 2027 for the spring evaluation, or the second Friday of July at 14:00 CEST for the autumn evaluation. Anything confirmed after 14:00 CET on the deadline day goes into the next round.",
            "7. Await the results: around mid-June for the spring round and around mid-December for the autumn round.",
            "8. If awarded, start the fellowship within one calendar year from the relevant evaluation cut-off, and request any parental-leave or part-time arrangement through your host supervisor as published."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits directly through the EMBO online application system, with two references and the receiving institute acceptance.",
            "Exceptions must be agreed with the EMBO Fellowship Office before submission."
          ],
          "application_portal": "The EMBO online application system for Postdoctoral Fellowships. The pages read state that applications are only accepted via the online application system but do not publish the portal URL directly.",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Fellows must inform the EMBO Fellowship Office of their intention to take parental leave.",
            "Parental leave must begin within six months of the birth of a child (non-EMBC fellows).",
            "A parental-leave extension must be requested by the host supervisor to the EMBO Fellowship office - before the end of the fellowship for EMBC-based fellows, and at the end of the fellowship for non-EMBC fellows.",
            "Part-time working must be discussed with the Host Institute and Host Supervisor (EMBC-based fellows) or with the Host Supervisor and the EMBO Fellowship Office (non-EMBC fellows), and the EMBO Fellowship Office must be notified; the maximum fellowship duration, full-time plus part-time, must not exceed 36 months.",
            "The fellowship must be started within one calendar year from the relevant evaluation cut-off.",
            "The EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowship does not cover bench fees, overheads, funds for consumables or any other financial benefits to the host supervisor or receiving institute, and the fellow must not expect the host to fund these from the award.",
            "The stipend outside EMBC Member States is solely intended to cover the cost of living in the host country.",
            "EMBO cannot advise on national tax regulations and recommends fellows contact the relevant authorities in the host country."
