      "description": "The Royal Society Career Development Fellowship is a four-year postdoctoral research fellowship supporting early career scientists from underrepresented backgrounds to establish research in a UK institution. Applicants can apply for up to £703,800 over four years, covering a contribution to the Research Fellow's salary and associated on-costs (at 80%), directly allocated costs (at 80%), and research expenses (at 100%). Relocation and visa costs for the applicant and dependants can be requested in addition to the grant cap. The scheme is funded by the Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade (BIST) and Royal Society charitable funds, with a variant funding research directly relevant to dementia in partnership with the Alzheimer's Society.",
      "program_type": "Research organisation fellowship",
      "best_fit": "Researchers who self-identify as being from a Black heritage background, including mixed Black background, with fewer than 24 months of postdoctoral experience, who meet the UK connection requirement and want a four-year postdoctoral fellowship in the UK.",
