          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "This is a postdoctoral fellowship, not a PhD scholarship. The 24-month post-doctoral ceiling is the most common disqualifier for people who apply too late in their postdoc.",
            "If you are not from a Black heritage background, this scheme is not for you in the current pilot. The Royal Society says the pilot may be broadened to other underrepresented groups if it succeeds, so re-check the criteria in later rounds rather than assuming a permanent closure.",
            "Do not budget the full Â£703,800. Salary and on-costs and directly allocated costs are funded at 80%, so the salary you can actually pay yourself is a fraction of the cap, and the remaining headroom goes to research expenses at 100%.",
            "Claim relocation and visa costs separately. They are the one item the Royal Society says you can request in addition to the cap, which materially changes your first-year budget if you are moving from outside the UK.",
            "Use the childcare support. It is published as available for conferences, collaborative research visits and invited talks, and it is one of the few costs that sit outside the salary.",
            "The success rate is low: 3% in the inaugural 2024/25 round and 7% in 2025/26. Treat the interview preparation, not just the form, as the main task.",
            "If you need an adjustment, ask early. A deadline extension is available but has to be arranged with the Grants Team, and requests are treated confidentially and are not normally shared with panel members.",
            "The scheme carries a bespoke training, mentoring and engagement programme on top of the grant, and broader Royal Society career development opportunities. That is part of what you are applying for, so use it."
