            "Evidence base: cross-sector roundtables, Royal Society-commissioned reports using 11 years of HESA data, and benchmarking of the Society's early career fellowships against the eligible applicant pool; the identified need focuses on Black or Mixed Black African, Black Caribbean or other Black heritage researchers moving from postgraduate to early postdoctoral stages",
