      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Submit the necessary documents to the Alexander von Humboldt Foundation online only",
        "You may only submit your application once you have uploaded all required documents in the application form",
        "Two expert reviews must be uploaded in a protected area by the expert reviewers personally; you can only submit once these have been uploaded if the portal is open at that time",
        "Your host will receive a link to upload a host's statement and mentoring agreement; the application is only forwarded to the Foundation once the host has uploaded all necessary documents",
        "Applications that fail to include important documents or information, or that diverge substantially from the specifications, will be formally rejected without further review"
      ],
      "english_requirement": "Natural sciences and engineering: you must have a good knowledge of German or English. Humanities, social sciences and medicine: you must have a good knowledge of German if this is necessary for conducting your research successfully; otherwise, good knowledge of English will suffice. No language certificate is required if English or German is your native language. An English language certificate is not required if you have worked in an English-speaking country for several years.",
      "application_method": [
        "Wait for an open call; the current call has reached the maximum of 800 applications and the next opens 15 November 2026",
        "Register in the application portal and complete the application form",
        "Upload the required applicant documents (CV, research outline, publication lists, key publications, doctoral certificate)",
        "Send the reviewer links in your application form to your two expert reviewers, who upload their reviews in the protected area",
        "Submit the application; the application is automatically forwarded to your host, who uploads the host's statement and mentoring agreement",
        "The application is only received by the Foundation once all documents, including the host's, have been submitted"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "The decision to award research fellowships is taken by a selection committee consisting of 60-70 researchers from various fields. Applications are academically evaluated by a peer review process based on: academic career and academic record to date (mobility, determination, thematic scope, academic productivity); quality of the key publications named in the application; originality and innovative potential of your proposed research; your future potential; and your independent research profile (for experienced researchers). The assessment also considers the individual life journey and educational background in terms of equal opportunities and accessibility. The Foundation expects 20-25% of the applications received to be approved.",
      "notes": "The current call has reached the maximum of 800 applications, so no new applications can be created at present; the next call opens on 15 November 2026. Applicants who have already started an application can save and continue working on it but cannot submit until the next application round opens. Applications are forwarded to the Foundation only after the host has uploaded their documents, so the host's speed determines your effective submission. Applicant who has already worked in Germany for 12 months or more should look for a new academic environment; applications involving returning to the doctoral supervisor or mentor of a longer postdoctoral stay are generally rejected. Individuals with whom you are in a close personal or familial relationship cannot be selected as hosts. In the case of unanimously rejected applications you must wait a minimum of 18 months before re-applying. Decisions cannot be appealed.",
      "image_url": "https://assets.humboldt-foundation.de/2/images/AvH-Logo.svg",
      "image_source_url": "https://www.humboldt-foundation.de/en/apply/sponsorship-programmes/humboldt-research-fellowship",
      "image_source_type": "official_ngo",
      "image_verified_at": "2026-10-01",
      "image_alt_text": "Alexander von Humboldt Foundation logo",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "description": "The Humboldt Research Fellowship is the Alexander von Humboldt Foundation's flagship sponsorship for post-doctoral researchers and experienced researchers of all nationalities and all research fields, funding their own research in Germany at a host institution of their choice. Two levels are published: the postdoc level pays a monthly fellowship of â‚¬3,000 plus additional benefits for 6 to 24 months, and the experienced researcher level pays â‚¬3,600 plus additional benefits for 6 to 18 months; both can be split into up to three stays within three years. Applications are accepted online only, in three calls a year, each capped at 800 applications - the current call has already reached that cap and the next call opens on 15 November 2026. The award requires international mobility: you may not have lived in Germany for more than 90 days in the 18 months before applying.",
          "purpose": [
            "Through the Humboldt Research Fellowship, the Alexander von Humboldt Foundation sponsors researchers with above-average qualifications from across the globe. As a fellow, you will benefit from individual support from the Humboldt Foundation and our diverse sponsorship portfolio.",
            "The Humboldt Research Fellowship for researchers of all nationalities and research areas: we support you with your research in Germany.",
            "The Humboldt Research Fellowship enables you to conduct your own research at various stages of your career in collaboration with a host at a German research institution of your choice. Hosts may apply for a subsidy towards research costs.",
            "The Alexander von Humboldt Foundation aims to achieve a good balance between genders and a high level of diversity among its fellows in all areas. We therefore expressly invite female scientists and members of underrepresented groups to apply. We welcome all applications, regardless of ethnic, cultural or social background, gender identity, age, religion, worldview, disability or sexual orientation.",
            "The programme is part of the Global Minds Initiative Germany of the Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space."
