          "duration": "Postdocs: fellowships may last from 6 to 24 months and can be divided into up to three stays within three years. Experienced researchers: fellowships may last from 6 to 18 months and can be divided into up to three stays within three years. You are flexible in determining when you would like to start your fellowship.",
          "application_cycle": "Three calls for applications annually, each opening approximately eight months before the respective selection meeting, and each capped at 800 applications. The published calls schedule is: call opens 15 March for a selection meeting in November and an earliest possible fellowship start in February of the following year; call opens 15 July for a selection meeting in March and an earliest start in May of the following year; call opens 15 November for a selection meeting in July and an earliest start in September of the following year. For 2026 the Foundation gives: 15 March 2026 / November 2026 / February 2027; 15 July 2026 / March 2027 / May 2027; 15 November 2026 / July 2027 / September 2027.",
          "deadline_central": null,
          "deadline_central_display": "There is no fixed closing date. Each call closes once it has reached the maximum of currently 800 applications; applicants who have already started an application at that point can save and continue working on it but cannot submit until the next application round opens. The current call has reached the maximum number of applications, and the next call opens on 15 November 2026.",
          "deadline_institutional": null,
          "deadline_note": "The Foundation has replaced fixed closing dates with a capacity cap: 'Once a call has reached the maximum number of currently 800 applications, the application round will be closed.' There is therefore no calendar deadline to publish. Two timing rules that do matter: the deadline for meeting formal conditions, in particular those on career-stage limits and previous stays in Germany, is the date the application is received; and if you cannot submit before the portal closes, your application is treated as received on the date the portal closed, provided you submit no more than 14 days after the next call opens.",
          "status": "UPCOMING - the Foundation states that it has received the maximum number of applications for the current call, so no new applications can be created at present, and that the next call will open on 15 November 2026. Applicants without an account are asked to wait for that opening before registering.",
