          "eligibility": [
            "You are not a German national.",
            "For postdocs: you completed your doctorate, or equivalent academic qualification, during the last four years, or you will be completing your doctorate before the envisaged selection meeting and can already provide a written summary of your findings; and you have been published in academic journals and by publishing houses that are reviewed according to international standards.",
            "For experienced researchers: you completed your doctorate, or equivalent academic qualification, during the last twelve years; your academic profile is substantiated by an extensive list of publications including important papers in which you acted as thematic lead; and you hold a leadership role commensurate with your career level in a corresponding position, for example assistant professor, lecturer, head of an independent research group, or a higher-level position.",
            "If a doctorate in your field or country of origin is not possible or uncommon, you can still apply up to 16 years after completing your master's or other postgraduate degree, provided you have a publication record commensurate with your career level.",
