          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Researchers of all nationalities and all research fields, excluding German nationals and applicants with a full German education and degree history. German nationals, or those who obtained their university entrance qualification and degree, or degree and doctorate, in Germany, may apply only if they have lived and worked abroad for more than ten years and intend to continue doing so long-term; those who have lived and worked abroad for more than five years may still apply where there is a strong connection to their current country of residence, such as permanent employment or additional citizenship. For researchers from Brazil the Foundation offers the separate CAPES-Humboldt Research Fellowship, and those not eligible there may apply for the Humboldt Research Fellowship Programme.",
          "international_eligibility": "Open to researchers of all nationalities and all research areas, subject to the Germany-residence limit of 90 days in the preceding 18 months and to the German-national and German-degree-history exclusions. Researchers from Brazil should first check eligibility for the CAPES-Humboldt Research Fellowship.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "Not applicable. The scheme is for post-doctoral and experienced researchers; where a doctorate is not possible or uncommon in the field or country of origin, a master's or other postgraduate degree may substitute, but only for the 16-year exception route."
            ],
            "masters": [
              "Not a level at which the fellowship is normally taken. A master's or other postgraduate degree qualifies an applicant only under the exception where a doctorate in the field or country of origin is not possible or uncommon, and then only up to 16 years after completing it, with a commensurate publication record."
            ],
            "phd": [
              "Postdocs: the doctorate or equivalent must have been completed during the last four years, or must be completed before the envisaged selection meeting, in which case a written summary of the findings must already be provided. Publication in journals and by publishing houses reviewed to international standards is required.",
              "Experienced researchers: the doctorate or equivalent must have been completed during the last twelve years, with an extensive publication list including important papers where the applicant acted as thematic lead, plus a leadership role commensurate with the career level.",
              "Exception: where a doctorate is not possible or uncommon, up to 16 years after a master's or other postgraduate degree."
            ]
