          "host_requirements": [
            "A researcher from an academic institution of your choice in Germany will provide you with a mentoring agreement and written confirmation that research facilities are available, and will compile a detailed review for you.",
            "Hosts may apply for a subsidy towards research costs.",
            "After you submit your application, your host receives a link allowing insight into your application documents as well as the upload of any relevant documents, and your application is only forwarded to the Humboldt Foundation once your host has uploaded all the necessary documents.",
            "You can check the status of your application in the corresponding field in the application form."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Meet the nationality rule and the 90-day Germany-residence limit in the 18 months before submission.",
            "Meet the career-stage and publication requirements for postdocs or for experienced researchers.",
            "Secure a German host who will provide a mentoring agreement, written confirmation of research facilities, and a detailed review.",
            "Have a good knowledge of German or English for natural sciences and engineering; for humanities, social sciences and medicine, a good knowledge of German if needed for the research, otherwise English.",
            "Commission two expert reviews, which the reviewers must upload themselves in the protected area of the portal.",
            "Upload every required document in the application form - the application can only be submitted once the documents are uploaded.",
            "Submit online only, during an open call that has not yet reached its 800-application cap.",
            "Abide by the rules of good scientific practice and the principles of scientific ethics, and read the Foundation's guidance on generative AI in the selection area."
