            "A detailed statement of your host in Germany as well as a confirmation of research facilities, uploaded by your host after you submit"
          ],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "Applications are submitted online only to the Alexander von Humboldt Foundation.",
            "You may only submit your application once you have uploaded the listed documents in the application form.",
            "Curriculum vitae: two pages maximum. Research outline: five pages maximum.",
            "The complete list of publications and the list of selected key publications must follow the published sample list format, and applications that diverge substantially from the specifications for creating a publication list are formally rejected without further review.",
            "The two expert reviews can only be uploaded in a protected area by the expert reviewers personally, and you can only submit your application once these documents have been uploaded, if the portal is open at that time.",
            "Once you have submitted, your host receives a link to view your application documents and upload the host statement and confirmation of research facilities; the application is only forwarded to the Foundation once the host has uploaded all necessary documents.",
            "Summaries and translations of key publications that are not available in German or English are required where applicable, along with publisher's acceptance notifications and/or acknowledgement of receipt.",
            "The Foundation advises checking documents carefully to ensure they are complete, accurate and fully compliant with the specifications before submitting, because ambiguities requiring clarification usually postpone the decision to a following selection meeting.",
            "No file type or file size limits are published on this page."
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Researchers with above-average qualifications from across the globe, in all research fields.",
            "For postdocs: publication in academic journals and by publishing houses reviewed according to international standards.",
            "For experienced researchers: an extensive publication list including important papers in which the applicant acted as thematic lead, plus a leadership role commensurate with the career level.",
            "The Foundation expects 20-25% of applications received to be approved for the upcoming selection committee meetings.",
            "Candidates must be able to demonstrate how their research will be conducted with the host and that research facilities are available."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Applications are assessed for the relevant selection meeting among three per year. The Foundation publishes an expected approval rate of 20-25% of applications received. Applications failing to include important documents or information, or diverging substantially from the specifications, are formally rejected without further review, and ambiguities requiring the applicant to be contacted usually result in the decision being postponed to the following selection meeting. Detailed information on the selection process and timeline is published under 'Selection Procedure', and the Foundation provides information pages for hosts, for expert reviewers and for independent peer reviewers. If an application is unsuccessful, the Foundation may provide the reasons for its decision.",
          "application_method": [
            "Submit the necessary documents to the Alexander von Humboldt Foundation online only.",
            "Ask your host in Germany for a mentoring agreement, written confirmation that research facilities are available, and a detailed review.",
            "Have your two expert reviewers upload their reviews personally in the portal's protected area.",
            "Contact the Foundation at info[at]avh.de before submitting if you have any doubts or questions.",
            "Note that the current call has reached its 800-application cap and the next call opens on 15 November 2026; applicants without an account are asked to wait for that opening before registering."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Check the nationality rule and the 90-day Germany-residence limit for the 18 months before you would submit.",
            "2. Decide whether you are a postdoc (doctorate within four years) or an experienced researcher (doctorate within twelve years plus a leadership role), and confirm your publication record meets that level.",
            "3. Check your language qualification for your field.",
            "4. Identify a German host who will provide a mentoring agreement, written confirmation of research facilities and a detailed review, and agree the timing - the host uploads after you submit.",
            "5. Commission two expert reviews: for postdocs, your doctoral supervisor and one other researcher, outside your institute if possible; for experienced researchers, important collaborative partners and/or researchers at your own and other institutes, outside your country of origin if possible.",
            "6. Prepare the documents: a CV of two pages maximum, a research outline of five pages maximum, a complete publication list and a selected key publication list in the published sample format, the key publications themselves, your doctoral certificate or proof of completion, a German language certificate if required, and any publisher acceptance notifications plus summaries/translations of key publications not available in German or English.",
            "7. Wait for an open call with capacity remaining. The current call is full; the next call opens on 15 November 2026.",
            "8. Create your account when the call opens if you do not already have one, upload all documents, and have your two reviewers upload their reviews in the protected area.",
            "9. Submit the application online, then monitor the status field in the application form until your host has uploaded the host statement and confirmation of research facilities, which is when the application is forwarded to the Foundation.",
            "10. If unsuccessful, you may request the reasons for the decision."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
            "The applicant submits directly and online only to the Alexander von Humboldt Foundation.",
            "The host in Germany uploads the detailed host statement and the confirmation of research facilities after the applicant submits, via a link sent to the host.",
            "The two expert reviewers upload their own reviews in the protected area of the portal.",
            "Queries before submission: info[at]avh.de."
          ],
          "application_portal": "The Alexander von Humboldt Foundation's online application portal. Applications are accepted online only; the portal URL is not printed on the page read.",
          "student_direct_application": true,
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "You must abide by the rules of good scientific practice and the principles of scientific ethics.",
            "The Foundation provides information on dealing with generative AI in the selection area, which applicants should read.",
            "You and your partner will be able to attend an intensive language course prior to your research fellowship.",
            "Personal support is provided throughout the sponsorship, and you are flexible in determining when you start your fellowship.",
