        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Count your days in Germany. You may not have lived in Germany for more than 90 days in total in the 18 months before you submit, and this is checked at the date your application is received.",
            "Sort out your career stage first: postdoc means the doctorate was completed within four years, or will be completed before the selection meeting with a written summary of findings; experienced researcher means within twelve years plus a leadership role and important papers where you were thematic lead.",
            "If a doctorate is not possible or uncommon in your field or country, check the 16-year postgraduate-degree exception and be ready to evidence a commensurate publication record.",
            "Check the German-education rule. If you are a German national, or your entrance qualification plus degree, or degree plus doctorate, are all German, you need more than ten years abroad and an intention to continue; more than five years abroad needs a strong connection to your current country.",
            "Line up a German host early - they must provide a mentoring agreement, written confirmation of research facilities, and a detailed review, and their upload is what forwards your application.",
            "Commission your two expert reviews early: for postdocs, your doctoral supervisor plus one other researcher outside your institute if possible; for experienced researchers, collaborators and/or researchers at your own and other institutes, outside your country of origin if possible. They must upload the reviews themselves.",
            "Prepare the documents to the published page limits: CV two pages maximum, research outline five pages maximum, and both publication lists in the sample format.",
            "Gather the language evidence you need: German or English for natural sciences and engineering; German if needed for your research in humanities, social sciences and medicine, otherwise English.",
            "Watch the calendar, not a deadline. Each call closes at 800 applications with no fixed date, and the current call is already full. The next call opens 15 November 2026.",
            "Read the Foundation's guidance on generative AI in the selection area before you draft anything."
          ],
          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "This is a research fellowship for Germany, not a degree programme. If you are looking for tuition funding for a taught course, this is the wrong scheme.",
            "The Germany-residence limit is the most common hard stop. More than 90 days in Germany in the preceding 18 months ends the application, so check your own travel history carefully before you invest time.",
            "Do not wait for a deadline, because there is none. Each call shuts when 800 applications arrive, which is why the current call is closed. The practical consequence is that you should submit early in a call rather than late, and you should have your documents finished before the call opens.",
            "If you do not yet have an account, the Foundation explicitly asks you to wait for the next call to open before registering.",
            "Budget for the fellowship amount only. â‚¬3,000 or â‚¬3,600 per month plus family benefits, health-insurance subsidies and travel allowances is the whole published package, and nothing about tuition appears anywhere.",
            "Your host's upload is the last step, not a formality. The application is only forwarded to the Foundation once the host has uploaded the detailed statement and the confirmation of research facilities, so build that time into your plan.",
            "Be precise with the publication lists. The Foundation states that applications diverging substantially from the specifications, including for the publication list, are formally rejected without further review.",
            "Expect roughly a one-in-four to one-in-five success rate, and know that incomplete or inaccurate applications often get postponed to a later meeting rather than decided."
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
