          "citizenship_residency": "No nationality requirement is published. The constraint is organisational and geographic: the administering organisation must be based in the UK, the Republic of Ireland, or a low- or middle-income country apart from India and mainland China.",
          "international_eligibility": "Open to applicants of any nationality, provided the administering organisation is in the UK, the Republic of Ireland, or a low- or middle-income country other than India or mainland China. Applicants based in a low- or middle-income country may hold a permanent, open-ended or long-term rolling contract, and Wellcome will fund their salary for the duration of the award. Applicants who intend to transfer grant funds into mainland China are not eligible.",
          "academic_level_rules": {
            "undergraduate": [
              "Not applicable. Research undertaken during an undergraduate or Master's degree is expressly not counted as equivalent research experience."
            ],
            "masters": [
              "Not applicable as a qualifying level. Master's research experience cannot count toward the four-year equivalent, and applicants must not have started a PhD or equivalent higher research degree."
            ],
            "phd": [
              "The applicant must have passed their PhD viva by the date of submission, or have at least four years' research experience equivalent to a PhD.",
              "Typically equivalent higher research degrees: a Doctor of Medicine (DM) or similar doctorate where it includes a substantial, sustained research component comparable to a PhD.",
              "Typically not equivalent: professional doctorates primarily based on taught modules, structured training, or shorter research projects; and qualifications where the research component is limited in duration (for example less than two years full-time or equivalent) or scope, such as MD, DClinPsy, DrPH, DVM and similar awards with directed programmes and limited independent research.",
              "Postdoctoral experience is counted as any periods spent in research after passing the PhD or higher research degree viva, and is limited to three years in the proposed field at the date of submission.",
              "Applicants who have spent time away from research - a career break, parental leave or long-term sick leave - may apply, with Wellcome allowing for this."
            ]
