          "host_requirements": [
            "The administering organisation is the organisation responsible for submitting your final application to Wellcome and managing the finances of the grant if awarded, and must be able to sign up to Wellcome's grant conditions.",
            "It must be not-for-profit and can be a higher education institution, research institute or healthcare organisation, based in the UK, the Republic of Ireland, or a low- or middle-income country apart from India and mainland China.",
            "If it is a core-funded research organisation, an Early-Career Award should not replace or lead to a reduction in existing or planned core support.",
            "A sponsor must be an individual at the administering organisation holding an established post or honorary academic appointment for the duration of the award, and will be expected to guarantee the space and resources needed from the start date to the end date of the award, ensure the research environment supports completion of the project, and confirm workload expectations.",
            "If you plan to work for more than three months outside the administering organisation, you must also have an additional sponsor at that location, who must guarantee the space and resources needed during your visit.",
            "Wellcome encourages you to choose a research environment that provides appropriate training, resources and experience, and to move away from your current research environment, which may mean moving from your group or department, but moving organisations is not essential."
          ],
          "requirements": [
            "Have passed your PhD viva by the submission date, or have at least four years' equivalent research experience, and not have started a PhD.",
            "Be within three years of postdoctoral experience in your proposed field at the date of submission.",
            "Be able to contribute at least 80% of your research time to the project.",
            "Have a research proposal that fits what Wellcome supports in Discovery Research and has the potential to improve human life, health and wellbeing.",
            "Have an eligible not-for-profit administering organisation in the UK, Republic of Ireland, or a low- or middle-income country other than India or mainland China, able to sign up to Wellcome's grant conditions.",
            "Secure a sponsor at that organisation holding an established post or honorary academic appointment for the duration of the award.",
            "Identify a mentor with a track record in training and mentorship for the period of your award; your sponsor can also be your mentor.",
            "If you will work for more than three months outside the administering organisation, secure an additional sponsor at that location.",
            "If you are a health professional continuing clinical activities, be registered with and licensed by the relevant professional regulator in the country you intend to work in.",
            "Cost the application at 1.0 (100%) full-time equivalent, and ask for a level and duration of funding that is justifiable for your proposed research."
