          "documents": [],
          "document_format_rules": [
            "The page does not publish a required-document list, file types, file sizes, word limits, translation or signature rules for the application.",
            "It does publish that Wellcome may update the application form periodically to reflect technical changes or new policies and occasionally broader changes to the scheme, and that changes will be made clear on the Wellcome Funding platform.",
            "The salary element is costed against the administering organisation's pay scales, so salary documentation follows the organisation's own processes rather than a Wellcome template."
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "The ability to conduct independent, original research that makes a meaningful contribution to knowledge.",
            "The research must fit what Wellcome supports in Discovery Research and have the potential to improve human life, health and wellbeing.",
            "A good understanding of research methodology, and evidence of project delivery and analysis.",
            "The applicant should not need close supervision to complete the proposed research, although they may need training in new techniques and experimental approaches.",
            "The research should be in any discipline - including science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM), experimental medicine, humanities and social science, clinical/allied health sciences, and public health.",
            "Wellcome asks applicants to consider carefully before resubmitting, because a resubmission must reflect clear progress and not respond solely to reviewer comments."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Applications are reviewed by shortlisting Advisory Groups and then, if shortlisted, by an interview meeting. Shortlisting meetings take place three times a year (February, June and September) and interviews three times a year (May, September and January); all confirmed shortlisting and interview meeting dates are published on the scheme page. Once Wellcome has received an application and confirmed which meeting it will go to, it tells the applicant the date, and a shortlisted application goes to the next scheduled interview meeting. Resubmission is limited to a maximum of two times for the same project across all Wellcome schemes and themed funding calls, from 1 July 2026 for new applications, with resubmissions of earlier applications following the previous rules. Applications are most often withdrawn by Wellcome because the applicant is ineligible or because the proposal is not right for the scheme, usually because it is not sufficiently related to human health. If an application scores in the lowest levels at shortlisting, resubmission is not permitted and Wellcome says so in the decision letter.",
          "application_method": [
            "Submit the application through the Wellcome Funding platform at any time, as there is no deadline.",
            "Your administering organisation submits the final application and manages the finances of the grant.",
            "Use Wellcome's eligibility self-assessment tool before applying, and its funding information advisers if you have questions on eligibility, what Wellcome offers, or what it does and does not fund."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Check your eligibility, including the PhD viva date, the four-year equivalent route, the three-year postdoctoral limit in your proposed field, and the 80% time commitment, using Wellcome's self-assessment tool.",
            "2. Confirm your administering organisation is an eligible not-for-profit in the UK, the Republic of Ireland, or a low- or middle-income country other than India or mainland China, and that it can sign up to Wellcome's grant conditions.",
            "3. Confirm your research fits what Wellcome supports in Discovery Research and has the potential to improve human life, health and wellbeing, and that you do not intend to transfer grant funds into mainland China.",
            "4. Secure a sponsor at the administering organisation holding an established post or honorary academic appointment for the duration of the award, and an additional sponsor if you will spend more than three months elsewhere.",
            "5. Identify a mentor with a track record in training and mentorship; your sponsor may also be your mentor.",
            "6. Cost the application at 1.0 (100%) full-time equivalent, using the organisation's pay scales, and ask for a level and duration that is justifiable.",
            "7. Build your budget around the Â£400,000 research expenses limit, and request overheads, overseas allowances, macaque costs and adjustment support separately if you are eligible, since they do not count against the limit.",
            "8. Submit through the Wellcome Funding platform at any time, and note Wellcome's advice to check whether it has updated the application form.",
            "9. Await confirmation of which shortlisting meeting your application will go to, and if shortlisted, prepare for the next scheduled interview meeting.",
            "10. If unsuccessful, note the resubmission limits: one further application for the same project to any Wellcome scheme, permitted at any time while you still meet the eligibility criteria, unless you scored in the lowest levels at shortlisting."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
