        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Check the career-stage arithmetic before anything else: PhD viva passed by your submission date, or four years of equivalent research experience, and no more than three years of postdoctoral experience in the field you are proposing to work in.",
            "Run Wellcome's self-assessment tool before drafting. Wellcome says applications are most often withdrawn for ineligibility, so this check has real value.",
            "Confirm your administering organisation is an eligible not-for-profit higher education institution, research institute or healthcare organisation in the UK, Republic of Ireland, or a low- or middle-income country other than India or mainland China, and that it can sign up to Wellcome's grant conditions.",
            "Check you are not barred by an equivalent award at this career stage, and that you are not waiting on a decision from this scheme.",
            "Secure a sponsor holding an established post or honorary academic appointment at the organisation for the whole award period, plus an additional sponsor if you will spend more than three months elsewhere.",
            "Identify a mentor; your sponsor can double as mentor, and neither is paid.",
            "Build the budget knowing that the Â£400,000 cap covers research expenses only, and that overheads, overseas allowances, macaque costs and adjustment support sit outside it if you are eligible.",
            "Cost the salary at 1.0 FTE and exclude promotion costs and any previous Wellcome fellowship supplement.",
            "Confirm at least 80% of your research time is committed to the project, and work out your clinical-duty percentage if you are in a clinical craft speciality.",
            "Submit at any time, but check the Wellcome Funding platform for form updates before you start, because Wellcome updates the form periodically."
          ],
          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "The award is about human health, not just good science. Wellcome says the most common reason for withdrawal is that the proposal is not sufficiently related to human health, so test that first, before you polish the methodology.",
            "There is no deadline, but there is no rush either: shortlisting happens three times a year. Submit early in a cycle to reach a meeting comfortably.",
            "Budget carefully around the Â£400,000 limit. It is for research expenses, your salary is separate, and overheads, overseas allowances, macaque costs and adjustment support do not eat into the limit if you are eligible. That last point matters most if you need assistive technology or support staff.",
            "If you are in a clinical craft speciality, you may spend up to 40% of your time on clinical duties instead of the standard 20% cap on non-research activities. That is a real accommodation, but it must be built into the application.",
            "Wellcome explicitly encourages you to move away from your current research environment. Moving organisations is not required, but moving group or department is encouraged, and it will be noticed if your proposal looks like a continuation of where you already are.",
            "If you took a career break, parental leave or long-term sick leave, that is allowed and will be taken into account. Do not hide it and do not count it as postdoctoral experience you do not have.",
            "Time away counts differently for the three-year postdoctoral test than you might expect: Wellcome allows for part-time work, career breaks and clinical training, and considers discipline changes, so a genuine field switch can be accommodated.",
            "No renewals, and you can only hold one of these awards. Plan the five years as the whole opportunity rather than a first step to a longer Wellcome career.",
            "You may submit to other Wellcome schemes at the same time, provided the proposals are distinct and you meet each scheme's eligibility and time-commitment requirements - but the same project has a hard two-submission limit across all Wellcome schemes and themed calls from 1 July 2026."
