            "Exclusions: existing tenured post for the award duration unless in a low- or middle-income country and the post is not research-based; pending application to this scheme; an equivalent award at this career stage; transfer of grant funds into mainland China",
            "Resubmission rules for applications submitted on or after 1 July 2026: a maximum of two submissions of the same project across all Wellcome schemes and themed calls, with significant changes required, and no resubmission after a lowest-level shortlisting score",
            "Round structure: shortlisting three times a year (February, June, September) and interviews three times a year (May, September, January); a shortlisted application goes to the next scheduled interview meeting; all confirmed meeting dates are published on the page",
            "Rounds: current open round from 25 August 2026 with no deadline; previous July 2026 round closed on 21 July 2026 at 15:00 BST",
            "Concurrent applications allowed to other Wellcome schemes with distinct proposals and separate eligibility and time-commitment compliance; coapplicant on Discovery Award applications permitted",
            "Allowed short-term funding: from the administering organisation or a learned society, supporting the transition from doctoral to postdoctoral research, such as new research ideas, career progression, networking, or travel or residencies after the PhD, with a combined maximum duration of three years",
            "Research environment guidance: choose an environment with appropriate training, resources and experience; moving away from the current environment is encouraged and may mean moving group or department, but moving organisations is not essential",
            "Contact: funding information advisers by on-page message form or phone (0)20 7611 5757; Wellcome does not answer questions on competitiveness; no direct email published"
          ],
          "institution_check_required": [
            "The required-document list, file formats, size limits, word limits, translation and signature rules, none of which are published on the scheme page - all of which sit in the Wellcome Funding platform application form.",
            "The Wellcome Funding platform URL, named on the page but not printed.",
            "The Q&As for health professionals, the 'what we do and don't fund in discovery research' pages, the 'what we don't fund' page, and the 'staff' section referenced for adjustment support - linked but not fetched.",
            "The database of previously funded projects for this scheme, which can be filtered by research subject area, country and organisation - linked but not fetched.",
            "Wellcome's guidance on project management, data sharing and research integrity, which are not on this page.",
            "Whether the organisation-specific overhead rate and overseas allowance eligibility that apply to a given host institution qualify those costs to sit outside the Â£400,000 limit.",
            "The exact dates of the 2027 shortlisting and interview meetings, which the page says are published on it but which were not captured in the text read."
          ],
          "unverified_or_removed_claims": [
            "Rejected 'fully funded': the award funds a salary and up to Â£400,000 of research expenses, and tuition is not mentioned at all, so tuition, living costs and all required expenses are not established and fully_funded is false.",
            "Rejected a single funding_amount: Â£400,000 is a ceiling for research expenses over a multi-year award, the salary is a separate element set by the organisation's pay scales, and several other cost heads sit outside the limit, so the figure stays in text and funding_amount is null with funding_currency GBP confirmed by the pound sign.",
            "Rejected tuition_coverage and tuition_rule: no page read mentions tuition, so both are null.",
            "Left deadline_central null: Wellcome states there are no deadlines, which is recorded in deadline_central_display, and the binding date for eligibility is the submission date rather than a closing date.",
            "Set renewable to false on the explicit published basis that Wellcome does not offer renewals and the applicant can only hold one of these awards.",
            "Set deferrable to null: no deferral provision is published; the part-time extension of duration is a duration rule, not a deferral.",
            "Set clinical_restriction to the published clinical-duty accommodation (up to 40% on clinical duties in a clinical craft speciality) plus the professional registration requirement, rather than leaving it null, because that is the only clinical-related rule the page states.",
            "Left official_contacts.email null: the page provides an on-page message form and a phone number but no direct email address, and an address must not be guessed.",
            "Did not import the Career Development Award, Discovery Award or any other Wellcome scheme's terms, though they are listed on the same page."
          ],
          "source_conflict_rule": "The scheme page governs this award. Where it refers to separate Wellcome guidance - what is and is not funded in Discovery Research, health professional Q&As, the staff section on adjustment support, and previously funded projects - that guidance governs the underlying question and is treated as authoritative for those points. Where the page shows both an open round and a closed July 2026 round, the open round governs the current status and both are recorded.",
          "source_freshness_rule": "The scheme page is undated, so the open-round status, the shortlisting and interview meeting pattern, the Â£400,000 limit, the salary rules and the resubmission policy are re-checked on every verification. The resubmission rules in particular are time-stamped, applying to applications submitted on or after 1 July 2026, so both the current rule and the legacy rule for earlier applications are recorded. The application form version is re-checked on the Wellcome Funding platform, because Wellcome states it updates the form periodically.",
          "source_citations": [
            "https://wellcome.org/grant-funding/schemes/early-career-awards"
          ],
          "researched_by": "f2",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
          "data_quality": {
            "source_level": "Official provider page (Wellcome Trust, wellcome.org)",
            "coverage": "High for award value, duration, cost heads, career-stage and time-commitment eligibility, exclusions, resubmission rules, organisational and host requirements, round structure, current open-round status and contacts, all of which are published on the page; Low for document and format requirements, which sit in the application form itself.",
            "pages_read": [
              "https://wellcome.org/grant-funding/schemes/early-career-awards"
