      "application_period": "Two application rounds per cycle, organised to match the academic calendars of the participating programmes. For the 2027 cycle: Application Window #1 January 18 - February 26, 2027; Application Window #2 March 29 - May 21, 2027. Each participating university sets its own admission deadlines, which fall before the JJ/WBGSP window closes.",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "The JJ/WBGSP is a fully funded master's scholarship for mid-career professionals from listed World Bank developing countries who are already admitted to one of a fixed set of participating development-related master's programmes. For the 2027 cycle the World Bank states that a scholarship provides tuition, a monthly subsistence allowance to cover all living expenses while on campus, economy class round-trip airfare, basic medical insurance obtained through the university, and a US$600 travel allowance for each trip. The amount of the monthly subsistence allowance varies depending on the host country and is not published on the programme page. The Government of Japan solely funds the scholarship on an annual basis, and scholars commit to return to their home country after earning their degree.",
      "program_type": "Development bank scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Nationals of listed developing countries who hold a bachelor's degree earned at least three years before the deadline, have at least three years of paid development-related work experience acquired within the past six years, and can first secure unconditional admission (except funding) to one of only 44 participating master's programmes outside their country of citizenship and residence.",
      "funding_amount": 600,
      "funding_currency": "USD",
      "funding_period": "per trip (published travel allowance only; the monthly subsistence allowance amount is not published)",
      "eligibility_summary": "National of a listed World Bank developing country with a bachelor's degree earned at least three years before the application deadline, at least three years of paid development-related employment acquired within the past six years, and unconditional admission (except funding) to a JJ/WBGSP participating master's programme outside their country of citizenship and residence.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a national of a World Bank member developing country on the published 2027 eligible list",
        "Not hold dual citizenship of any developed country",
        "Be in good health",
        "Hold a bachelor's (or equivalent) degree earned at least 3 years prior to the Application Deadline date",
        "Be employed in development-related work in a paid full-time position at the time of submitting the scholarship application, with at least 3 years of paid development-related employment since earning a bachelor's degree (or equivalent university degree) and acquired within the past 6 years from the date of the application deadline",
        "On or before the scholarship application deadline date, be admitted unconditionally (except for funding) for the upcoming academic year to at least one of the JJ/WBGSP participating master's programs located outside of the applicant's country of citizenship and country of residence listed at the time the call for scholarship applications opens; the letter of admission must be uploaded before submitting the scholarship application",
        "Not be an Executive Director, his/her alternate, and/or staff of any type of appointment of the World Bank Group, and not be a close relative of any of the aforementioned by blood or adoption (close relative defined as Mother, Father, Sister, Half-sister, Brother, Half-brother, Son, Daughter, Aunt, Uncle, Niece, or Nephew)",
        "Individuals who have previously been offered a JJ/WBGSP scholarship but declined it, or who previously received a JJ/WBGSP scholarship but did not graduate, are not eligible to apply again",
