    {
      "name": "Joint Japan/World Bank Graduate Scholarship Program (JJ/WBGSP) 2027 - Application Window for Japanese Nationals",
      "country": "Japan",
      "degree_levels": "Master's, PhD",
      "funding_type": "Fully Funded",
      "official_source": "World Bank, Development Economics Vice Presidency, JJ/WBGSP Secretariat (scholarship fully funded by the Government of Japan)",
      "official_source_url": "https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/scholarships/japanese-nationals",
      "catalogue_url": "https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/scholarships/jj-wbgsp",
      "official_updates_url": "https://www.worldbank.org/en/programs/scholarships",
      "region": "Japan (applicants must be Japanese nationals). The graduate programme must be outside Japan, in a development-related field, and may be in a developing country where the scholar has secured employment.",
      "duration": "Up to two years; all JJ/WBGSP scholarships cover the duration of the graduate program or two years, whichever is less",
      "deadline": "The 2027 application window for Japanese nationals will open from February 15 to April 16, 2027. As from February 15, 2027, prospective candidates are invited to express their interest to the JJ/WBGSP Secretariat with an email to scholarshipapplicants@worldbank.org. Winners are informed by mid-July, after the JJ/WBGSC approval. The 2026 application window for Japanese nationals closed on Friday 17 April 2026.",
      "deadline_date": "2027-04-16",
      "deadline_precision": "day",
      "application_period": "A single application window for the 2027 cycle for Japanese nationals, from February 15 to April 16, 2027. From the opening date, prospective candidates are invited to register interest with the Secretariat by email. Results are communicated by mid-July 2027.",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-01",
      "description": "This is the Japanese-nationals track of the Joint Japan/World Bank Graduate Scholarship Program, which the World Bank states is fully funded by the Government of Japan. It funds up to two years for a limited number of Japanese mid-career professionals dedicated to the alleviation of poverty and enhanced shared prosperity in developing countries who have been admitted to or are currently enrolled in a master's or PhD programme outside Japan in a development-related field. Benefits include one economy class air travel to the host university and a $600 travel allowance at the start, one economy class return travel and a $600 travel allowance at the end, tuition, basic medical insurance obtainable through the university, and a monthly subsistence allowance to cover all living expenses while on campus. The amount of the monthly subsistence allowance varies by host country and is not published on the page.",
      "program_type": "Development bank scholarship (bilateral government-funded graduate scholarship)",
      "best_fit": "Japanese nationals with a bachelor's degree earned at least three years before the deadline and at least three years of paid development-related employment acquired within the past six years, who are admitted unconditionally (except financing) to, or already enrolled full-time in, a development-related master's or PhD programme outside Japan.",
      "funding_amount": 600,
      "funding_currency": "USD",
      "funding_period": "per trip, paid twice (one $600 travel allowance each way; the monthly subsistence allowance amount is not published)",
      "eligibility_summary": "Be a Japanese national; hold a bachelor's degree (or equivalent) earned at least three years before the Application Deadline; have at least 3 years of paid development-related employment acquired within the past six years from the deadline; and be admitted unconditionally except for financing to, or currently enrolled full-time in, a development-related graduate programme outside Japan.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a Japanese national",
        "On or after the date the call for scholarship applications opens, not be an Executive Director, his/her alternate, and/or staff of any type of appointment (including temporary and consultant) of the World Bank Group (The World Bank, International Development Association, International Finance Corporation, Multilateral Investment Guarantee Agency, and International Center for Settlements of Investment Disputes), and not be a close relative of any of the aforementioned by blood or adoption (close relative defined as Mother, Father, Sister, Half-sister, Brother, Half-brother, Son, Daughter, Aunt, Uncle, Niece, or Nephew)",
        "Hold a bachelor's degree (or equivalent university degree) earned at least three years before the date of the Application Deadline",
        "On or after the date the JJ/WBGSP scholarship application process opens, not be employed (as a staff or any type of employment) by the Government of Japan or its related agencies, including JICA, local governments and the Central Bank",
        "Have at least 3 years of paid development-related employment acquired since earning a bachelor's degree (or equivalent university degree) and acquired within the past six years from the date of the Application Deadline",
        "At the time of the application submission, be either admitted unconditionally (except for financing) or currently enrolled full-time in a graduate program outside of Japan in an area of study related to development, or be currently employed full-time in development-related work pertaining directly to developing countries"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "One economy class air travel from the scholar's home country to the host university at the start of the graduate degree program, if the scholar is not already attending the graduate program, plus a $600 travel allowance",
