          "degree_award": "Not a degree in itself. The scholar receives funding towards a master's or PhD at a university outside Japan, together with an expectation of advancing a career focused on alleviating poverty and enhanced shared prosperity in developing countries.",
          "duration": "Up to two years. All JJ/WBGSP scholarships cover the duration of the graduate program or two years, whichever is less.",
          "application_cycle": "Annual. The 2027 application window for Japanese nationals will open from February 15 to April 16, 2027. As from February 15, 2027, prospective candidates are invited to express their interest to the JJ/WBGSP Secretariat by emailing scholarshipapplicants@worldbank.org. The previous cycle's window closed on Friday 17 April 2026.",
          "deadline_central": "2027-04-16",
          "deadline_central_display": "The 2027 application window for Japanese nationals will open from February 15 to April 16, 2027.",
          "deadline_institutional": null,
          "deadline_note": "The page publishes a single window for Japanese nationals, opening 15 February 2027 and closing 16 April 2027, in contrast to the two windows used for developing country nationals. The World Bank states that details on eligibility criteria for each call are provided in that call's Application Guidelines and that these detailed criteria are strictly adhered to with no exceptions made; those Guidelines are published only as a PDF. The previous cycle's Japanese nationals window closed on Friday 17 April 2026.",
          "status": "UPCOMING - the 2027 application window for Japanese nationals opens on 15 February 2027 and closes on 16 April 2027, both after the 2026-10-01 verification date, so the window is announced but not yet open. From 15 February 2027 candidates are invited to express their interest to the Secretariat by email.",
          "funding_type": "Fully Funded | Partial Funding",
          "funding_label": "JJ/WBGSP scholarship for Japanese nationals, fully funded by the Government of Japan - one-way air travel and a US$600 travel allowance each way, tuition, basic medical insurance, and a monthly subsistence allowance while on campus",
          "funding_amount": null,
          "funding_currency": "USD",
          "funding_period": "Tuition and basic medical insurance for the duration of the graduate program or two years, whichever is less; a monthly subsistence allowance while on campus during the scholarship period, with the amount varying by host country; and a US$600 travel allowance with each of the two funded flights.",
          "tuition_coverage": "For the duration of the scholarship period, tuition for the scholar's graduate program and the cost of basic medical insurance that can be obtained through the university are funded.",
          "living_cost_coverage": "While on campus during the scholarship period, a monthly subsistence allowance to cover all living expenses (accommodations, food, etc., including books). The amount of the allowance varies depending on the host country. It is payable only while on campus.",
          "travel_coverage": "If the scholar is not already attending the graduate program, the scholarship funds one economy class air travel from the scholar's home country to the host university at the start of the graduate degree program, plus a $600 travel allowance. If at the end of the scholarship period the scholar has completed all requirements to earn the graduate degree, the scholarship funds one economy class air travel from the host university to Japan or to a developing country where the scholar has secured employment, plus a $600 travel allowance. Additional travel during the course of the study program is not covered.",
          "fully_funded": false,
          "tuition_rule": "Tuition for the scholar's graduate program and the cost of basic medical insurance obtainable through the university are funded for the duration of the scholarship period, which is the duration of the graduate program or two years, whichever is less. The scholarship is not a complete package: the page lists visa application costs, family expenses, extra-curricular courses and training, courses that do not meet the minimum credits required to earn the graduate degree, language training not provided by the graduate program, additional travel during the study program, research and supplementary educational expenses, field trips, workshops, seminars and internships, educational equipment such as computers, and the resident permit fee as costs it does not cover.",
          "home_tuition_rule": null,
          "host_institution_fee": "No host fee is payable in place of tuition, because tuition is the item covered. The scholarship does not cover the resident permit fee, which the scholar must meet personally.",
