          "document_format_rules": [
            "The page publishes no required-document list, file types, file sizes, signatures, translations or date rules beyond the notice that detailed eligibility criteria are in the call's Application Guidelines.",
            "The 2027 Application Guidelines for Japanese Nationals and the 2027 FAQ for Japanese Nationals are published only as PDFs from this page. PDF text cannot be extracted, so the document list, annexes and form requirements must be read directly from those documents.",
            "The page requires the applicant to inform and document to the JJ/WBGSP Secretariat any other sources of scholarship funds if notified as a semi-finalist or awardee, which is a documentation obligation at that stage rather than at application."
          ],
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Two qualified assessors independently review each eligible application and score it on a scale of 1 to 10, taking into account four main factors and the degree of cohesion among them: Quality of Academic Experience and Recommendation (20% weight); Quality of Professional Recommendations (20% weight); Quality of Professional Experience (20%); Commitment to International Development Career (40% weight).",
            "The JJ/WBGSP Secretariat uses the average score of the two assessors together with criteria for maintaining a reasonable distribution of awards across gender, and for giving scholarships to those applicants who, other things being equal, have limited access to financial resources for graduate studies abroad.",
            "The aim is to identify the candidates with the highest potential, after completion of their graduate studies, to impact international development."
          ],
          "selection_notes": "Each eligible application is independently reviewed and scored 1-10 by two qualified assessors across four weighted factors: Quality of Academic Experience and Recommendation 20%, Quality of Professional Recommendations 20%, Quality of Professional Experience 20%, and Commitment to International Development Career 40%, with the degree of cohesion among the factors also taken into account. The Secretariat uses the average of the two scores plus two balancing criteria - a reasonable distribution of awards across gender, and preference for applicants with limited access to financial resources for graduate studies abroad. Finalists are presented to the JJ/WBG Steering Committee, composed of members of the World Bank Board of Directors and World Bank management, for approval, and winners are informed by mid-July after that approval.",
          "application_method": [
            "Express your interest to the JJ/WBGSP Secretariat by emailing scholarshipapplicants@worldbank.org from 15 February 2027.",
            "Submit the application within the window, which closes on 16 April 2027.",
            "Follow the detailed criteria in the 2027 Application Guidelines for Japanese Nationals, which the World Bank states are strictly adhered to with no exceptions."
          ],
          "application_steps": [
            "1. Confirm your Japanese nationality, that your bachelor's degree or equivalent was earned at least three years before the Application Deadline, and that you have at least 3 years of paid development-related employment acquired since the degree and within the past six years from the Application Deadline.",
            "2. Confirm you hold no Government of Japan or related agency employment - JICA, local governments, the Central Bank - on or after the date the application process opens, and no World Bank Group role or close-relative relationship on or after the date the call opens.",
            "3. Confirm you are either admitted unconditionally (except for financing) to, or currently enrolled full-time in, a development-related graduate programme outside Japan, or currently employed full-time in development-related work pertaining directly to developing countries.",
            "4. Read the 2027 Application Guidelines for Japanese Nationals for the detailed eligibility criteria, which the World Bank says are strictly adhered to with no exceptions.",
            "5. From 15 February 2027, email the JJ/WBGSP Secretariat at scholarshipapplicants@worldbank.org to express your interest.",
            "6. Submit the application before the window closes on 16 April 2027.",
            "7. If notified as a semi-finalist or awarded, inform and document to the Secretariat any other sources of scholarship funds, since the award supplements rather than duplicates them.",
            "8. Await the two-assessor review, the Secretariat's selection, and JJ/WBG Steering Committee approval; winners are informed by mid-July."
          ],
          "applicant_submission_route": [
