        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are a Japanese national. This window is not open to any other nationality, and the developing country nationals window is a separate scheme with a separate eligible-country list.",
            "Check the degree timing: your bachelor's degree or equivalent must have been earned at least three years before the Application Deadline.",
            "Check the employment test: at least 3 years of paid development-related employment, acquired since earning the degree and acquired within the past six years from the Application Deadline.",
            "Confirm you are free of Government of Japan and related agency employment - JICA, local governments, the Central Bank - on or after the date the application process opens, including temporary or any other type of employment.",
            "Confirm you have no World Bank Group role, and are not a close relative of one by blood or adoption, on or after the date the call opens.",
            "Confirm you are either admitted unconditionally (except for financing) to, or currently enrolled full-time in, a development-related graduate programme outside Japan - or that you are currently employed full-time in development-related work pertaining directly to developing countries.",
            "Read the 2027 Application Guidelines for Japanese Nationals, because the World Bank states the detailed eligibility criteria in that document are strictly adhered to with no exceptions.",
            "From 15 February 2027, email scholarshipapplicants@worldbank.org to express your interest to the Secretariat.",
            "Submit before 16 April 2027, and be ready to disclose and document any other scholarship funds if you reach the semi-finalist or award stage.",
            "Note that the outbound flight is only funded if you are not already attending the programme, and the return flight is only funded if you complete all degree requirements by the end of the scholarship period."
          ],
          "important_advice_for_students": [
            "This is a mid-career scheme for Japanese professionals, not a scholarship for fresh graduates. The three-year post-degree employment requirement and the three-year degree-timing rule are the two filters that catch people out.",
            "Weight your application around commitment. Commitment to an International Development Career carries 40% of the score - double each of the other three factors at 20% - so your development orientation and how you evidence it matter more than your grades or your references.",
            "Plan around the two-year cap. The award covers the duration of the programme or two years, whichever is less, so a three-year PhD is only two years funded unless the programme itself is shorter.",
            "The return flight depends on completion. If you have not completed all requirements to earn the degree by the end of the scholarship period, the funded flight back to Japan or a developing country is not available, so plan your completion date.",
            "The subsistence allowance is paid only while you are on campus, and its amount varies by host country. Check the host country's cost level before you commit, and budget for time away from campus that the allowance does not cover.",
            "You must disclose other funding. The award supplements rather than duplicates other support, and you are required to inform and document any other scholarship funds once you are notified as a semi-finalist or awardee.",
            "Note the Government of Japan employment bar, which includes JICA, local governments and the Central Bank, and applies from the moment the application process opens. Leaving a Japanese government post to take this scholarship is not permitted under the published rule.",
            "Do not expect the scholarship to cover your extra costs. Visa fees, family, computers, field trips, workshops, seminars, internships, additional travel, non-provided language training and the resident permit fee are all yours."
