      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Suborno Jayanti Scholarship Scheme is the ICCR scheme for nationals of Bangladesh, subsuming the earlier Bangladesh schemes previously offered by ICCR. Under it, the Government of India through ICCR provides scholarship at UG, PG and Ph.D level in Indian universities. Applications are made online on the ICCR A2A Scholarship Portal and must be submitted through the Indian Mission in the applicant's country, which then forwards them to empanelled Indian State and Central Universities. Registration for the 2026-27 academic year is closed and the portal currently lists 2026-27 as the only registration year.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship (ICCR administered for the Government of India)",
      "deadline": "Registration for the academic year 2026-27 is closed. The portal displays '04 Oct, 2026' and offers only the 2026-27 registration year; the portal has not published dates for the next academic year.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "Annual cycle. The A2A portal opens a registration year at a time; for 2026-27 it was open from late February until April 2026, and the next cycle's dates are not yet published.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must be nationals of Bangladesh, hold a valid passport, and meet the eligibility criteria of the Indian university chosen. ICCR scholarships are only for studies at Indian State and Central Universities, not private or deemed universities. English proficiency is mandatory, and medical-stream courses are not covered.",
      "eligibility": [
        "National of Bangladesh (the scheme is reserved for Bangladesh nationals)",
        "Valid passport issued by the relevant authorities of the applicant's government",
        "Pass 12th standard to join an undergraduate course",
        "Study only at an ICCR-empanelled Indian State or Central University (private and deemed universities are excluded)",
        "Sufficient proficiency in English, since the medium of instruction in Indian universities is English",
        "No scholarships are offered in the medicine stream"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Monthly stipend (three months' advance stipend paid on arrival)",
        "House rent allowance, where applicable",
        "Medical treatment under Central Government Health Scheme (CGHS) rules",
        "Hostel accommodation at institutions offering residential facilities"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Stipend disbursed on academic progress; three months' advance stipend on arrival",
        "Medical treatment as per Government of India CGHS rules, reimbursed to the extent possible",
        "Mandatory hostel stay in institutions with residential facilities",
        "Air ticket is not provided under all ICCR schemes; students may have to pay for their own air passage"
      ],
      "required_documents": [
        "Mark sheets",
        "Birth certificate",
        "School leaving certificate",
        "Nationality certificate",
        "Government-issued ID card",
