      "description": "The Global Korea Scholarship is the Republic of Korea's representative government-invited scholarship programme, administered by the National Institute for International Education (NIIED), which invites outstanding students from around the world to study at Korean universities. It funds Korean language training plus associate degree, bachelor's, master's and doctoral degree programmes across more than 80 GKS universities, and also runs an exchange students programme and Korea-Japan exchange programmes. Applicants apply either through their Korean embassy (Embassy Track) or directly to a GKS university (University Track), and the scholarship covers airfare, Korean language training fees, tuition and monthly allowances.",
      "program_type": "Government-invited scholarship degree programme (NIIED, Ministry of Education)",
      "duration": "Korean language training (1 year) + associate degree (2-3 years), bachelor's degree (4-6 years), master's degree (2 years), doctoral degree (3 years)",
      "deadline": "Embassy Track applications are submitted online through Study in Korea in September; University Track applicants apply directly to the university on its own schedule in September to November. The official 2027 GKS-U application window for the Embassy Track ran 15 September 2026 11:00 to 30 September 2026 18:00 Korea time, and the site now displays 'It is not the application period.'",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "Annual cycle: NIIED announces in September, Embassy Track applications are submitted in September and University Track applications in September to November, screening runs October to December and final results are announced in December.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Undergraduate applicants and both parents must hold non-Korean citizenship, must be under 25 years of age, must be high school or associate degree graduates (or expected graduates) and must meet the academic performance requirement. Graduate applicants must be under 40, hold a bachelor's or master's degree and have an average GPA of at least 80%.",
