      "official_source_url": "https://www.studyinjapan.go.jp",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Japanese Government (Monbukagakusho) Scholarship is MEXT's scholarship programme for international students, offered in seven types: Research students, Teacher training students, Undergraduate students, Japanese studies students, College of technology students, Specialized training college students and Young Leaders Program students. There are two application routes: a recommendation from a Japanese embassy or other Japanese diplomatic mission, or a recommendation from a Japanese university. The scholarship pays a monthly stipend, exempts tuition and provides a round-trip travel allowance (airfare), and in most tracks includes Japanese language training before or during study.",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship (MEXT, Ministry of Education, Culture, Sports, Science and Technology)",
      "duration": "Research students: embassy recommendation - irregular course within 2 years, regular course the standard school year (6 months preparatory education added if necessary); university recommendation - depends on each school's quota, up to a standard school year. Teacher training students: within 1 year and 6 months including Japanese language education. Undergraduate students: embassy recommendation - 5 years including Japanese language training (7 years for medicine, dentistry, pharmacy and veterinary science); university recommendation - up to a standard school year. Japanese studies students: one academic year. College of technology students: 4 years including Japanese language training (4 years 6 months for merchant marine studies). Specialized training college students: 3 years including Japanese language training. YLP students: 1 year.",
      "deadline": "For embassy recommendation, recruitment for those arriving in Japan in April 2027 or September/October 2027 was made between April and May of the previous year, with first screening between May and July by the Japanese embassies or consulates general. As the application process and schedule differ by country, applicants must inquire with the Japanese embassy or consulate general in their country; applications must not be sent directly to MEXT.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "Annual cycle. Embassy-recommendation recruitment runs between April and May of the year before arrival in Japan, first screening runs May to July, and university-recommendation recruitment is set by each university.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Eligibility depends on the scholarship type. Research students must be under 35 and eligible for admission to a master's or doctoral programme at a Japanese graduate school. Undergraduate students must be under 25 and have completed 12 years of schooling. Japanese studies students must be 18-29. College of technology and specialized training college students must be under 25 with 11 or 12 years of schooling. YLP students must be under 40 in principle. Applicants must also submit a health certificate and be willing to learn Japanese.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Research students: under 35 years of age and eligible for admission to a master's or doctoral programme (first or second stage) at a Japanese graduate school",
        "Teacher training students: under 35, graduate of a college or teacher training college, with at least five years of active teaching experience at primary, secondary or teacher training level; college and university teachers currently in service are not eligible",
        "Undergraduate students: under 25 and have completed 12 years of school education or a course comparable to a Japanese high school, including prospective graduates",
        "Japanese studies students: between 18 and 29 years old and enrolled as an undergraduate in a Japanese language or Japanese culture faculty outside Japan, remaining enrolled at home on return",
        "College of technology students: under 25 with 11 or more years of education, including prospective graduates",
        "Specialized training college students: under 25 with 12 years of schooling or education comparable to a Japanese high school, including prospective graduates",
        "Young Leaders Program students: under 40 in principle, and university or college graduates with practical work experience, young public administrators and similar candidates expected to play an active role in Asia and other countries",
        "Research students additionally must submit a health certificate in the prescribed format signed by a physician"
      ],
