      "official_source_url": "https://www.sbfi.admin.ch",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Swiss Government Excellence Scholarships are awarded annually by the Swiss Confederation to encourage international exchange and research cooperation between Switzerland and more than 180 other countries. Recipients are selected by the Federal Commission for Scholarships for Foreign Students (FCS, also known as ESKAS), an independent decentralised federal body that is not bound by directives. The programme has two components: research scholarships for talented early career researchers from abroad who have already completed a Master's degree, and art scholarships for students from a limited number of countries wishing to pursue an initial Master's degree in an artistic field in Switzerland. Applicants are aged 35 or less and the scholarship pays CHF 2,450 per month.",
      "program_type": "Government research scholarship (Federal Commission for Scholarships for Foreign Students, FCS/ESKAS)",
      "duration": "Research fellowships: maximum 12 months (minimum 6 months), no extension possible, start 1 September 2027. PhD scholarships: 12 months, renewable twice for up to 36 months subject to academic progress, start 1 September 2027.",
      "deadline": "Applications are open from 20 August 2026. Applications are submitted to the applicant's Swiss diplomatic representation, and the deadline is set country by country: information on application deadlines and scholarship opportunities by country of origin is published by the Federal Commission in August each year.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "Annual cycle. Applications open on 20 August 2026, country-specific deadlines apply between August and December 2026, and the Federal Commission announces its award decisions by the end of May at the latest for the following academic year.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to applicants from 183 countries who are aged 35 or less and already hold a Master's degree or equivalent. Applicants must not have been living, studying or working in Switzerland for more than 13 months before the scholarship start, must not already have held a Swiss Government Excellence Scholarship, and every research scholarship application must be backed by an academic supervisor at a Swiss higher education institution.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Maximum age 35 (date of birth after 31 December 1991 for the 2027-2028 cycle)",
        "Master's degree or equivalent completed by 31 July 2027 (30 June 2027 for ETH Zurich)",
        "Applicants from one of the 183 eligible countries of origin",
        "For PhD scholarships at graduate schools only: confirmation of admission to a doctoral school must be submitted together with the application",
        "Letter of support from an academic supervisor in Switzerland, with a short CV of that supervisor",
        "Applicants already residing in Switzerland must have entered Switzerland no earlier than 1 August 2026, evidenced by the registration confirmation or residence permit",
        "For art scholarships: initial Master's degree in an artistic field in Switzerland, and nationality of one of the limited number of eligible countries"
      ],
      "coverage": [
