          "description": "Each year the Swiss Confederation awards Government Excellence Scholarships to encourage international exchange and research cooperation between Switzerland and over 180 other countries. Recipients are selected by the awarding body, the Federal Commission for Scholarships for Foreign Students (FCS aka ESKAS). Research scholarships are available to postgraduate researchers in any discipline wishing to pursue research at a Swiss cantonal university, university of applied sciences, ETHZ or EPFL or at one of the four research institutes within the ETH Domain, with a maximum age of 35 and funding of CHF 2,450 per month. Art scholarships are open to students wishing to pursue an initial Master's degree in an artistic field in Switzerland and are limited to students from a limited number of countries. Applications are submitted to Swiss diplomatic representations and the FCS assesses applications according to three criteria: candidate profile, quality of the research project or artistic work, and synergies and potential for future research cooperation.",
