          },
          "description": "SEMP is part of the Swiss solution to the EU's Erasmus+ programme. Swiss higher education institutions and colleges of higher education can send their own students and staff abroad (outgoing) or host people from abroad (incoming). Students, including PhD students, may spend one or two semesters at a higher education institution abroad, remain enrolled at their home institution and earn ECTS credits; they do not pay study fees abroad and receive financial support for travelling and accommodation. The programme is part of the Swiss Programme for Erasmus+, funded by SERI and implemented by Movetia.",
