      "duration": "2 to 12 months per mobility (minimum 60 days); one or two semesters for study mobility; traineeships of at least 60 days",
      "deadline": "There is no central deadline for individual students: applications are handled by the international relations office of the Swiss host institution, which sets its own dates. At institutional level, accreditation and funding applications go to Movetia annually in early March for a funding period starting 1 June. Movetia currently states that the next application deadline is spring 2027, likely under Erasmus+.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "Annual institutional cycle with applications each March and a funding period from 1 June; student-level applications run through the Swiss host institution's own deadlines. Movetia expects the next call to be launched under Erasmus+ following Switzerland's planned participation from 2027.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Participants must be enrolled at a higher education institution (university, university of applied sciences, university of teacher education) or a college of higher education outside Switzerland, the stay must last between 60 days and 12 months, and there must be an interinstitutional agreement between the home and host institutions. Students from abroad apply for the grant directly with the Swiss higher education institution where they plan to study or train; if the placement is at a Swiss company or NGO, they must still find a Swiss institution willing to coordinate the application and pay out the grant.",
