          "description": "The Swiss-European Mobility Programme (SEMP) enables students to go on exchange for one or two semesters or to do an internship abroad. Both students from Switzerland (outgoing) and students from abroad (incoming) can receive financial support for their stay. Stays abroad for students, including PhD students, take place at a university or college of higher education, last between 2 and 12 months, and are coordinated by the international relations office of a Swiss higher education institution. Students do not pay study fees abroad and receive financial support for travelling and accommodation.",
          "program_type": "Government mobility programme (higher education), Swiss solution to Erasmus+ - incoming mobility",
          "region": "Europe",
          "coverage": "Mobility grant contributing to travel and accommodation, fee waiver at the Swiss host, and a possible special-needs top-up",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Identify a SEMP-accredited Swiss university or college of higher education willing to host and coordinate your application",
            "Confirm an interinstitutional agreement exists between your home institution and that Swiss host",
            "Check whether the host actually offers SEMP grants - not all institutions do",
            "Apply through your home institution first, since it runs the application and the nomination",
            "Agree the study plan so that credits count towards your home degree, and prepare the learning agreement",
            "For a traineeship at a company or NGO, find a Swiss higher education institution willing to coordinate and pay the grant",
            "If you have a disability or a physical, mental or chronic illness, request the special-needs grant via the International Relations Office before departure",
            "Travel sustainably where possible to qualify for the CHF 100 top-up"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "The Swiss host institution is not SEMP-accredited",
            "No interinstitutional agreement with the host institution",
            "Assuming Movetia pays grants directly to students - only Swiss higher education institutions can pay out SEMP grants",
            "Host institution does not offer grants for the mobility type",
            "Missing the host or home institution's own deadline",
            "Stay shorter than 60 days or longer than 12 months",
            "Submitting an incomplete learning agreement or missing Declaration of Honour"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "The grant is a flat mobility amount calibrated by duration, not a living-cost stipend: CHF 1,430 to CHF 4,500 for European mobility incoming, CHF 1,750 to CHF 5,000 worldwide, so remaining living costs in Switzerland must be budgeted",
            "Swiss higher education tuition is not charged to the mobility student, but housing and living costs above the grant are not covered",
            "Special-needs support is capped at CHF 12,000 and reimbursed against evidenced actual costs"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Learning agreement validated by sending institution, Swiss host and participant",
            "Declaration of Honour for student mobility, finalised by the Swiss institution before the mobility period",
            "Mobility agreement or Grant Agreement for staff mobility",
            "Proof of enrolment and transcripts from the home institution, with certified translations if not in English, French, Italian or German",
            "Copy of the interinstitutional agreement or nomination confirmation",
            "Requirement note for any special-needs grant, submitted before departure"
          ],
          "alerts": [
