      "description": "The Study in India (SII) programme is a flagship project of the Government of India executed by the Ministry of Education, and the SII Scholarship is the financial-assistance component attached to it. Financial aid takes the form of institute-driven tuition fee waivers or scholarships decided at each partner institute's discretion, ranging from 10% to 100% of tuition depending on the applicant's prior academic scores. Students register on the Study in India portal, submit applications to partner institutes, and the resulting waiver appears on their student dashboard alongside the allotted institute and course. There is no central award amount and no single application deadline; eligibility and concessions vary institute by institute.",
