      "official_source": "European Commission (Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions)",
      "official_source_url": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/actions/postdoctoral-fellowships",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "deadline": "The 2026 call is closed. For the 2027 call, the official indicative timeline gives '7 April 2027: launch of the call for proposals (TBC)' and '8 September 2027: deadline for submitting proposals (TBC)'.",
      "deadline_date": "2027-09-08",
      "deadline_precision": "approximate",
      "application_period": "Annual call. The 2026 call ran from 9 April 2026 and closed on 9 September 2026 at 17:00 CEST. The 2027 call opens 7 April 2027 and closes 8 September 2027, both marked to be confirmed.",
      "application_method": [
        "Identify a host organisation, which may be a university, research institution, business, SME or other organisation in an EU Member State or Horizon Europe Associated Country",
        "Develop the application jointly with the host organisation",
        "The host organisation submits the proposal on the Funding and Tender Opportunities Portal",
        "Optionally post or follow hosting offers (expressions of interest) on Euraxess to find a partner"
      ],
      "eligibility_summary": "For researchers holding a PhD who wish to carry out research activities abroad. Applicants need a PhD at the time of the application deadline (a successfully defended but not yet formally awarded thesis also qualifies), a maximum of eight years of research experience counted from the award of the PhD, and compliance with the mobility rule of no more than 12 months of residence or main activity in the beneficiary country (European Postdoctoral Fellowships) or outgoing-phase host country (Global Postdoctoral Fellowships) in the 36 months before the call deadline. European Postdoctoral Fellowships are open to researchers of any nationality; Global Postdoctoral Fellowships are restricted to nationals or long-term residents of EU Member States or Horizon Europe Associated Countries.",
      "eligibility": [
        "PhD degree held at the time of the application deadline, or doctoral thesis successfully defended even if the degree is not yet formally awarded",
        "Maximum of eight years of research experience counted from the award of the PhD, with years outside research, career breaks and, for reintegration cases, research in third countries excluded",
        "Mobility rule: not more than 12 months of residence or main activity in the beneficiary country for a European Postdoctoral Fellowship, or in the outgoing-phase host organisation's country for a Global Postdoctoral Fellowship, during the 36 months immediately before the call deadline",
        "European Postdoctoral Fellowships: any nationality",
        "Global Postdoctoral Fellowships: nationals or long-term residents of EU Member States or Horizon Europe Associated Countries",
        "For Euratom Research and Training Programme research areas: national or long-term resident of an EU Member State or Euratom Associated Country, and the beneficiary organisation must also be established in an EU Member State or Euratom Associated Country"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Living allowance",
        "Mobility allowance",
        "Family, long-term leave and special needs allowances where applicable",
        "Research, training and networking activities",
        "Management and indirect costs",
        "Up to a 6-month non-academic placement, and short-term secondments"
      ],
      "required_documents": [
        "Proposal and all annexes submitted through the Funding and Tender Opportunities Portal by the host organisation",
        "Application and evaluation forms for the chosen call",
        "Documents listed on the dedicated call page of the Funding and Tender Opportunities Portal"
      ],
      "catalogue_url": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/funding",
      "official_updates_url": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/funding",
      "duration": "European Postdoctoral Fellowships: 12 to 24 months. Global Postdoctoral Fellowships: an outgoing phase of 12 to 24 months in a non-associated Third Country plus a mandatory 12-month return phase in an EU Member State or Horizon Europe Associated Country.",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "funding_period": null,
      "program_type": "EU research grant / research fellowship under Horizon Europe, administered by the European Research Executive Agency",
      "best_fit": "Researchers holding a PhD with up to eight years of research experience who need a funded, mobile postdoctoral research placement in Europe or, for Global Postdoctoral Fellowships, in a Third Country with a mandatory return phase.",
      "notes": "The award is delivered as a salaried employment contract: 'The beneficiary receiving EU funding needs to recruit the researcher for the total period of the fellowship.' There are no tuition fees, since this is a research employment rather than a degree programme. From 2026, resubmission restrictions apply to applications that scored below 80% the previous year. A Seal of Excellence is awarded to applications scoring 85% or higher that cannot be funded for lack of budget. The 2027 call carries an indicative budget of EUR 388.57 million (TBC) for the whole call, not per fellowship.",
      "description": "MSCA Postdoctoral Fellowships support researchers holding a PhD who wish to carry out their research activities abroad, acquire new skills and develop their careers. There are two types: European Postdoctoral Fellowships, lasting 12 to 24 months in an EU Member State or Horizon Europe Associated Country and open to any nationality; and Global Postdoctoral Fellowships, lasting an outgoing phase of 12 to 24 months in a non-associated Third Country followed by a mandatory 12-month return phase, open only to nationals or long-term residents of EU Member States or Horizon Europe Associated Countries. The researcher is recruited by a host organisation, which submits the proposal through the EU Funding and Tender Opportunities Portal, and receives a living allowance, a mobility allowance and, where applicable, family, long-term leave and special needs allowances. The 2026 call closed on 9 September 2026 and the 2027 call opens on 7 April 2027 with a deadline of 8 September 2027, both indicative.",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "official_source_urls": [
            "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/actions/postdoctoral-fellowships",
            "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/funding/msca-postdoctoral-fellowships-2027"
          ],
          "application_link": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/funding/msca-postdoctoral-fellowships-2027",
          "official_updates_url": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/funding",
          "catalogue_url": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/funding",
          "application_cycle": "Annual Horizon Europe call. 2026 call: 9 April to 9 September 2026, closed. 2027 call: opens 7 April 2027, deadline 8 September 2027, results February 2028, first projects start May 2028.",
          "deadline_central": "2027-09-08",
          "deadline_central_display": "8 September 2027: deadline for submitting proposals (TBC); the 2027 call opens 7 April 2027 (TBC)",
          "deadline_central_timezone": "Europe/Brussels",
          "deadline_note": "The action page carries the banner 'The call is closed. The 2027 call will open on 7 April 2027.' The 2027 call page labels its whole timeline indicative, marking both '7 April 2027: launch of the call for proposals (TBC)' and '8 September 2027: deadline for submitting proposals (TBC)'. For reference, the just-closed 2026 call had a precise deadline of 9 September 2026 at 17:00 CEST. Because the published 2027 date is explicitly flagged TBC, precision is recorded as approximate.",
          "status": "UPCOMING",
          "status_note": "The current (2026) call is closed. The next call opens on 7 April 2027, so as of 2026-10-04 no proposals can be submitted and the next application window is months away.",
          "funding_amount": null,
