          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "https://marie-sklodowska-curie-actions.ec.europa.eu/contact",
            "email": null,
            "phone": null
          },
          "description": "MSCA Postdoctoral Fellowships support researchers holding a PhD who wish to carry out their research activities abroad, acquire new skills and develop their careers. European Postdoctoral Fellowships run for 12 to 24 months in an EU Member State or Horizon Europe Associated Country and are open to any nationality; Global Postdoctoral Fellowships require an outgoing phase of 12 to 24 months in a non-associated Third Country followed by a mandatory 12-month return phase and are open to nationals or long-term residents of EU Member States or Horizon Europe Associated Countries. The researcher is recruited by the host organisation and receives a living allowance, a mobility allowance and conditional family, long-term leave and special needs allowances. The 2026 call closed on 9 September 2026 and the 2027 call opens on 7 April 2027.",
          "program_type": "EU research grant under Horizon Europe (MSCA Postdoctoral Fellowships), administered by the European Research Executive Agency",
          "region": "Europe",
