      "notes": "This page covers mobilities within countries fully part of the Erasmus+ programme and to and from countries associated to Erasmus+. Additional support exists for students with fewer opportunities and for those from outermost regions, and students may combine a study mobility with a traineeship abroad. Grant agreements are signed by the sending or receiving institution, which applies for funding on behalf of its students; small fees for insurance or student union membership may still apply.",
      "description": "Erasmus+ helps organise student and doctoral candidate exchanges within countries fully part of the Erasmus+ programme and to and from countries associated to Erasmus+. It is open to short-cycle, Bachelor's and Master's students and to doctoral candidates registered at a participating higher education institution and enrolled in studies leading to a recognised degree. There is no central application form: students apply through the international or Erasmus+ office of their own institution, which selects applicants fairly and transparently. The grant contributes to travel and daily living costs with amounts varying by destination and demand, and Erasmus+ students are exempt from tuition, registration, examination and laboratory or library fees at the receiving institution. Mobilities run from 2 to 12 months for long-term study, or 5 to 30 days for short-term blended mobility, with up to 12 months in total per study cycle.",
