          "description": "Erasmus+ supports study periods abroad for short-cycle, Bachelor's and Master's students and for doctoral candidates registered at a participating higher education institution. There is no central application form; the sending institution selects applicants fairly and transparently, signs the grant agreement and applies for funding on the student's behalf. Students receive a grant contributing to travel and daily living costs and are exempt from tuition, registration, examination and laboratory or library fees at the receiving institution. Before departure a learning agreement for studies is signed, and afterwards the receiving institution issues a transcript of records so that the sending institution recognises the credits.",
