      ],
      "eligibility_summary": "Doctoral Networks are applied for by international consortia, not by individual candidates. A consortium must include at least three independent legal entities, each established in a different EU Member State or Horizon Europe Associated Country, with at least one established in an EU Member State; organisations from any country in the world may join on top of that minimum, and specific conditions apply to Industrial and Joint Doctorates. Recruited doctoral candidates must not already hold a doctoral degree at the date of recruitment, may be of any nationality, must be enrolled in a doctoral programme during the project, must spend at least 50% of their time outside academia for Industrial Doctorates, and must comply with the mobility rule of no more than 12 months in the recruiting organisation's country in the 36 months before recruitment.",
