      "notes": "This is a doctoral training programme funding salaried research positions, not a tuition scholarship, so there is no tuition component. The 2026 call carries an indicative budget of EUR 593.034 million (TBC) for the whole call, which is not a per-fellowship amount. As from 2022, resubmission restrictions apply to applications scoring below 80% the previous year. Candidates seeking PhD positions are directed to the EURAXESS vacancy list, which is updated daily.",
      "description": "MSCA Doctoral Networks implement doctoral programmes through international, intersectoral partnerships of universities, research institutions, businesses including SMEs and other socio-economic actors, in order to train highly skilled doctoral candidates. Besides standard Doctoral Networks, the action promotes Industrial Doctorates, which place PhD candidates largely outside academia, and Joint Doctorates, which lead to a joint or multiple doctoral degrees. Each beneficiary must recruit at least one doctoral candidate, who must not already hold a doctoral degree at recruitment, may be of any nationality and is funded through a living allowance, mobility allowance and applicable family, long-term leave and special needs allowances. The 2026 call is currently open, having launched on 28 May 2026 with a deadline of 24 November 2026.",
