          "description": "MSCA Doctoral Networks implement doctoral programmes through partnerships of universities, research institutions and infrastructures, businesses including SMEs, and other socio-economic actors from different countries across Europe and beyond, in order to train highly skilled doctoral candidates. Alongside standard networks, the action offers incentives for Industrial Doctorates, where candidates work largely outside academia, and Joint Doctorates leading to joint or multiple doctoral degrees. A consortium must include at least three independent legal entities in different EU Member States or Horizon Europe Associated Countries, with at least one in an EU Member State. Recruited candidates must not already hold a doctoral degree, may be of any nationality and receive a living allowance, a mobility allowance and applicable family, long-term leave and special needs allowances. The 2026 call opened on 28 May 2026 and closes on 24 November 2026.",
