      "description": "The MAEC-AECID programme family (Becas Cooperación Española) is run by the Spanish Agency for International Development Cooperation (AECID) and funds training for Spanish citizens and for citizens of Spanish-cooperation partner countries, both in Spain and abroad. The official page groups the live 2026/2027 calls into four blocks: scholarships for young Spaniards, readerships (Lectorados) for Spaniards teaching Spanish abroad, scholarships for citizens of Latin America, Africa and Asia, and artistic or research residencies at the Real Academia de España en Roma. As of 2026-10-04 every 2026/2027 sub-programme listed on the official pages is marked \"Plazo cerrado\", so the next cycle is upcoming. Awards are financial support (a monthly stipend plus, for some programmes, Social Security registration or health insurance); the official pages reviewed do not state that tuition fees are paid.",
