          "description": "The Hubert H. Humphrey Fellowship Program is funded by the U.S. Department of State and administered by the Institute of International Education. It is a non-degree, ten-month program for mid-career professionals who hold an undergraduate degree, have at least five years of full-time professional experience, and show leadership and public service. Fellows are assigned to one of the host institutions, study without a degree requirement, and complete a six-week Professional Affiliation. The package covers host-university tuition and fees, a maintenance allowance with a one-time settling-in allowance, accident and sickness coverage, a book allowance, a one-time computer subsidy, air travel, and a professional development allowance. Applicants apply through their country's Binational Fulbright Commission or U.S. Embassy, whose internal deadlines are published locally.",
