      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Cohort 11 (Fall 2027 entry): apply to UW-Madison International Admissions by November 1, 2026 and submit the WiSH KMSP application by November 15, 2026. Free virtual information sessions are offered on September 22 (9-10am), September 30 (3-4pm) and October 9 (12pm-1pm), all in US Central time; attendance does not affect consideration.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to enterprising, creative and dedicated students committed to applying their talents toward poverty alleviation around the globe, joining King-Morgridge Scholars from Africa, the Caribbean, Latin America, South Asia and Southeast Asia. Six scholarships are awarded each year. Scholars must enrol full-time at UW-Madison, maintain a minimum 3.0 GPA, complete at least 12 credits each semester, participate actively in program activities, attend Orientation and the Wisconsin Experience Seminar in their first fall semester, and follow University policies and state and federal laws.",
