      "selection_notes": "Six scholarships are made each year. Selection is made by the UW-Madison Office of Admissions and Recruitment together with KMSP staff, who actively recruit candidates from Africa, the Caribbean, Latin America and South and Southeast Asia, review applications for admission to UW-Madison, and participate in the selection of candidates for the program. Selected scholars are chosen for their drive, academic success and commitment to addressing problems of poverty in their own countries.",
