      "description": "The King-Morgridge Scholars Program is a four-year, full-tuition scholarship at the University of Wisconsin-Madison for international students from Africa, the Caribbean, Latin America, South Asia and Southeast Asia who are committed to applying their talents toward poverty alleviation around the globe. Scholars receive a full-time, four-year/eight-semester award covering tuition and fees, on-campus room and board, health insurance, airfare and a stipend for miscellaneous expenses, with six scholarships awarded each year. Applicants must apply to UW-Madison International Admissions by November 1, 2026 and submit the Wisconsin Scholarship Hub KMSP application by November 15, 2026 for Cohort 11 (Fall 2027 entry). Scholars must maintain a 3.0 GPA, take at least 12 credits a semester, and participate actively in the program.",
