          "description": "The King-Morgridge Scholars Program is a four-year, full-tuition scholarship at the University of Wisconsin-Madison for students from Africa, the Caribbean, Latin America, South Asia and Southeast Asia who are committed to poverty alleviation. The award covers tuition and fees, on-campus room and board, health insurance, airfare and a stipend for miscellaneous expenses for four years (eight semesters), and six scholarships are made each year. For Cohort 11 (Fall 2027 entry) the UW-Madison International Admissions application is due November 1, 2026 and the WiSH KMSP application is due November 15, 2026. Scholars must maintain a 3.0 GPA, complete at least 12 credits each semester, participate actively in the program and comply with University policies.",
