          "description": "The Wien International Scholarship Program (WISP), established at Brandeis University in 1958, brings undergraduate students from every corner of the globe to campus and has brought over 894 scholars from 115 countries. It meets the full demonstrated financial need of each recipient based on a complete review of financial documentation, and is awarded to exceptional international applicants who demonstrate strong academic achievement and extracurricular or community involvement. There is no separate application process: candidates apply directly to Brandeis through the Common Application or Coalition Application, file the CSS Profile by the international aid deadline (Nov. 2 for Early Decision I / Early Action, Jan. 15 for Early Decision II / Regular Decision for Fall 2027), and are informed of a Wien or other Brandeis scholarship with their admission decision. Awards are renewed annually with a March 1 renewal filing and continued satisfactory academic progress.",
