      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "deadline": "No separate scholarship application exists. Global Excellence Scholarships are awarded to admitted international freshmen or transfer students whose admission application was completed by the applicable deadline: Early Action I by November 1 (decision by January 31), Early Action II by December 1 (decision by February 15), Regular by January 1 (decision by March 31). Applications completed after those dates are considered on a space-available and funds-available basis.",
      "deadline_date": "2026-11-01",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "For fall 2027 entry, submit a complete admission application on the Common App by November 1 (Early Action I) for the earliest full scholarship consideration, or by December 1 (Early Action II) or January 1 (Regular). Admitted freshmen on an F-1 visa who completed their application by the deadline are automatically reviewed for a Global Excellence Scholarship; admitted transfer students on an F-1 visa who complete by the priority deadline are automatically considered. Applicants must also complete the Certification of Finances form.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to international freshmen and transfer students admitted to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities, primarily those studying on an F-1 visa, who complete their admission application by the applicable deadline. All admitted freshmen studying on an F-1 visa who completed their application by the deadlines are reviewed for the award, and admitted transfer students on an F-1 visa who complete by the priority deadline are automatically considered. No separate scholarship application is required.",
      "eligibility": [
        "International student (F-1 visa status) applying to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities",
        "Admitted as a freshman or a transfer student",
        "Completed the admission application by the applicable deadline for full consideration",
        "Freshmen: all admitted F-1 students who completed their application by the deadlines are reviewed",
        "Transfer students: admitted F-1 students who complete their application by the priority deadline are automatically considered",
        "Complete the Certification of Finances form"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Partial financial support only: the University of Minnesota Twin Cities states it does not offer a full tuition waiver or scholarship"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Competitive merit-based award of up to $15,000 per year for up to four years, as published in the University's International Undergraduate Fact Book"
      ],
      "funding_amount": 15000,
      "funding_currency": "USD",
      "funding_period": "per year for up to four years",
      "duration": "Up to four years of undergraduate study",
      "required_documents": [
