        "Certification of Finances form"
      ],
      "application_method": [
        "Submit the Common Application for admission to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities by the applicable deadline",
        "Complete the Certification of Finances form when notified through the Application Tracker"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Hold F-1 student visa status",
        "Complete the admission application by the applicable deadline for full scholarship consideration",
        "Complete the Certification of Finances form for applicants on temporary visas or who will need a visa"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Global Excellence Scholarships are competitive and merit-based. All admitted freshmen studying on an F-1 visa who have completed their applications for admission by the deadlines are reviewed for the award; all admitted transfer students attending on an F-1 visa who complete their applications by the priority deadline are automatically considered. There is no separate scholarship application. Students whose admission applications are complete by the published deadlines receive full consideration for the University Honors Program and scholarships.",
      "program_type": "Merit-based university scholarship for international undergraduates",
      "best_fit": "Academically strong international applicants admitted to the University of Minnesota Twin Cities on an F-1 visa who apply by the earliest published deadline; the award is partial, so finalists must still fund the majority of the published cost of attendance.",
      "description": "The Global Excellence Scholarship (GES) is a competitive, merit-based award for international freshmen and transfer students at the University of Minnesota Twin Cities. All admitted freshmen studying on an F-1 visa who complete their admission application by the published deadlines are automatically reviewed, and admitted transfer students on an F-1 visa who complete by the priority deadline are automatically considered; there is no separate scholarship application. The award is partial - the University states it does not offer a full tuition waiver or scholarship - and the University's International Undergraduate Fact Book states the value as up to $15,000 each year for up to four years. Deadlines follow admission: Early Action I November 1, Early Action II December 1, Regular January 1. Applicants on temporary visas must also complete the Certification of Finances form.",
