          "description": "Reach Oxford is a University of Oxford undergraduate scholarship, formerly called Oxford Student Scholarships, for nationals of countries receiving official development assistance from the OECD Development Assistance Committee who cannot study for a degree in their own country. It covers course fees, a grant for living costs and one return air fare per year for three or four years, and around two to three awards are made each year. Applicants must already hold an Oxford offer, be of the highest academic ability, and expect to return home after their studies. Applications for 2026 entry are closed; 2027 entry details will be published in January 2027 with a 26 January 2027 deadline.",
