          "description": "The Gates Cambridge Scholarship is a full-cost postgraduate scholarship at the University of Cambridge, funded by the Gates Cambridge Trust, which was established in October 2000 by a US$210m donation from the Gates Foundation. Around 70 awards are made each year, roughly two-thirds to PhD students, open to citizens of any country outside the UK applying for a PhD, MLitt or one-year postgraduate course in any subject. The award covers the University Composition Fee, a maintenance allowance of Â£23,152 for 12 months at the 2026-27 rate, one economy return airfare and inbound visa costs including the Immigration Health Surcharge, with discretionary top-ups for academic development, dependants, fieldwork, maternity or paternity and hardship.",
