          "description": "The Global Futures Scholarship for South Asia is a partial merit-based award from The University of Manchester for international master's students domiciled in Bangladesh, Pakistan and Sri Lanka. For 2027 entry the master's award is worth GBP 12,000, awarded as a discount on published overseas tuition fees rather than as a cash payment. Applicants must hold a conditional or unconditional offer for a full-time, on-campus master's course starting September 2027 and submit the online scholarship application form by 25 April 2027. The University aims to balance the awards by gender, domicile and course, and Manchester describes the whole 2027 portfolio as more than 350 partial merit-based scholarships worth over GBP 6 million.",
