          "description": "HEC Paris runs two families of scholarships for Master's and MBA applicants: merit-based awards decided automatically once a candidate is admitted, and need-based awards requiring a separate form in the Applicant Space. All merit-based awards are tuition-fee reductions, ranging from €5,000 (AVENIR) to up to €20,000 (Women in Finance & Technology), with several awards of up to €10,000–€15,000. Need-based awards include up to 35% of tuition fees (Equal Opportunity), €15,000 per Master's year (Garzouzi) and case-by-case jury amounts (Imagine Fellowship, CMA-CGM). Four admissions rounds each carry a 12pm noon need-based deadline, starting with 26 October 2026.",
