          "description": "The President's Graduate Fellowship is awarded by the NUS Graduate School to PhD candidates who show exceptional promise or accomplishment in research, with a number of PhD research students selected each semester by the University. It pays a monthly stipend, provides a full waiver of tuition fees at the University, and from the AY2023/24 intake adds the NUSGS Research Incentive Award. Newly registered international students receive a one-off settling allowance of S$1,000 and a one-off air travel allowance of up to S$750. The Fellowship is tenable for one year in the first instance, may be renewed each semester, and has a maximum period of four years. International fellows admitted from AY2014/2015 must perform 312 hours of teaching duties under the Graduate Assistantship Programme.",
