      "notes": "Although no bond is attached to the scholarship itself, recipients must take up the MOE Tuition Grant, which bonds Singapore Permanent Residents and international students to work for a Singapore-registered company for three years immediately after graduation. Scholarship recipients admitted to Dentistry and Medicine must additionally undertake a service bond with the Singapore Ministry of Health for five and six years respectively. The scholarship does not cover the NUS Bachelor of Science / University of Melbourne Doctor of Veterinary Medicine Concurrent Degree Programme, and for other Concurrent Degree Programmes it covers only the undergraduate programme.",
      "description": "The NUS International Undergraduate Scholarship is a University-level scholarship offered by the National University of Singapore to support exceptional students from all countries except Singapore who apply as freshmen to a full-time undergraduate degree programme at NUS. Candidates are considered and shortlisted through their application for undergraduate admission to NUS, and selection interviews are held from January to July with outcomes notified by mid-July. Benefits comprise 100% coverage of subsidised undergraduate tuition fees after the MOE Tuition Grant, an S$5,800 annual living allowance, an S$5,000 annual accommodation allowance and a S$1,750 one-time computer allowance upon enrolment. The award is renewed each semester provided the holder maintains a GPA of at least 3.5 (or top 80% of cohort for Dentistry, Law and Medicine) and good conduct.",
