      "best_fit": "Outstanding Bachelor's graduates or final-year students with an Honours (Highest Distinction) degree or equivalent, of any nationality, intending to study full-time for a PhD at NTU and able to take on Graduate Assistantship Programme teaching or laboratory supervision duties.",
      "notes": "Stipend figures shown are the international-student rate because this row targets international applicants. The official page notes that the stipend 'remains the same for existing students receiving higher stipend rates', so the January 2026 rates apply to new recipients. The official page also warns that 'Scholarship coverage and award terms are subject to change. The university reserves the right to vary the amount of the Award stipend at any time.' The stored record's official_source_url is a general NTU graduate scholarships index rather than this award's own page; per the merge rules the stored URL is preserved unchanged and the correct page is recorded in url_observed.",
      "description": "The Nanyang President's Graduate Scholarship (NPGS) is a competitive and prestigious scholarship scheme offered by Nanyang Technological University to encourage outstanding graduates or final-year students to take their first step towards a leading research career by studying full-time for a PhD at NTU. It is described as the premier scholarship granted by NTU's President, recognising PhD students who exemplify exceptional academic, research and leadership qualities. Open to all nationalities, it requires an Honours (Highest Distinction) or equivalent at Bachelor's level, or official documentation confirming the candidate is on track to achieve it. Monthly stipends revised with effect from January 2026 are S$5,300 for Singapore Citizens, S$4,800 for Singapore Permanent Residents and S$4,300 for international students, with CPF contributions on top for Citizens. The award also covers the annual tuition fee and provides an overseas conference allowance of up to S$5,000 per financial year, an annual book allowance of S$500, a one-off IT allowance of S$1,500, a one-off thesis allowance of S$600 and priority for campus accommodation. There is no bond attached to the scholarship, though international students must perform teaching or laboratory supervision duties under the Graduate Assistantship Programme.",
