          "description": "The Nanyang President's Graduate Scholarship (NPGS) is a competitive and prestigious scholarship scheme offered by Nanyang Technological University to encourage outstanding graduates or final-year students to take their first step towards a leading research career by studying full-time for a PhD at NTU. It is the premier scholarship granted by NTU's President and recognises PhD students who exemplify exceptional academic, research and leadership qualities. All nationalities are eligible, and applicants must hold an Honours (Highest Distinction) or equivalent at Bachelor's level or provide documentation confirming they are on track to achieve it. Monthly stipends revised with effect from January 2026 are S$5,300 for Singapore Citizens, S$4,800 for Singapore Permanent Residents and S$4,300 for international students, with CPF contributions on top for Citizens. The award covers the annual tuition fee and provides an overseas conference allowance of up to S$5,000 per financial year, an annual book allowance of S$500, a one-off IT allowance of S$1,500, a one-off thesis allowance of S$600 and priority for campus accommodation. The award is tenable for one year in the first instance, renewable subject to good progress, for a maximum of four years. There is no bond attached to the scholarship, but international students must perform teaching or laboratory supervision duties under the Graduate Assistantship Programme.",
