          "description": "The UGC Junior Research Fellowship and Research Associateship for Foreign Nationals is a Government of India scheme, implemented by the University Grants Commission, that gives students and teachers from developing countries of Asia, Africa and Latin America the opportunity to undertake advanced study and research in sciences, humanities and social sciences at Indian universities. Twenty JRF slots and seven RA slots are available each year, each with a four-year non-extendable tenure. Applications are circulated to Indian embassies and missions abroad, which screen them locally before forwarding them to UGC. Award is a monthly research stipend plus contingency and departmental assistance to the host institution.",
