          "description": "The TWAS-CSIR Postgraduate Fellowship Programme is run jointly by UNESCO-TWAS and the Council of Scientific and Industrial Research of India. It allows foreign scholars from developing countries to pursue research toward a PhD in emerging areas of science and technology in CSIR laboratories and institutes in India, across nine named fields including agricultural sciences, chemical sciences, engineering sciences, mathematical sciences and physics. Applicants may either be registered for a PhD in their home country under the sandwich option or enrol in a PhD course at a university in India under the full-time option. CSIR provides a monthly stipend covering living costs, food and health insurance, together with subsidized accommodation. Applications are submitted only through the TWAS online portal.",
