          "description": "The Netaji Subhas-ICAR International Fellowships, administered by the Indian Council of Agricultural Research under the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, support doctoral study in agriculture and allied sciences in priority areas identified by ICAR. The programme is open to both Indian and overseas nationals holding a Master's degree in Agriculture and Allied Sciences. Thirty fellowships of three years each are awarded annually. Overseas candidates study at identified Indian Agricultural Universities in the ICAR-AU system, while Indian candidates study at identified overseas universities and institutions. Applications are submitted by email to the Assistant Director General of Human Resource Development.",
          "program_type": "International doctoral research fellowship",
          "region": "Asia",
          "coverage": "Three-year doctoral fellowship support with placement at an identified host institution. The published call does not itemise tuition, living-cost or travel components, so no specific coverage can be asserted.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Check that your Master's degree is in Agriculture and Allied Sciences, as the fellowship is restricted to that field",
            "Confirm your proposed research sits inside one of ICAR's identified priority areas, which are notified one year in advance",
            "Obtain an acceptance letter for admission to the PhD programme from the host university and enclose it with the application",
            "Line up two referees with working email addresses, ideally including your current supervisor",
            "Get a certificate of good conduct from the Competent Authority of your university or employer",
            "If you are an in-service Indian candidate, secure deputation approval from the Director of your ICAR institute or the Vice-Chancellor",
            "Send the application to adg.hrd.applications@gmail.com with the exact subject line \"Application for NSIF: Name of Applicant and contact number\""
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Master's degree outside Agriculture and Allied Sciences",
            "Research proposal outside the identified priority areas",
            "Missing or undated acceptance letter from the host university",
            "Fewer than two referees, or referees who cannot be contacted at the email addresses given",
            "Missing certificate of good conduct",
            "Missing deputation approval for in-service Indian candidates",
            "Missing the required subject line on the application email",
            "Failure to register within one year of the award letter, which terminates the offer automatically"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Any costs the ICAR call does not itemise, since it publishes no coverage breakdown",
            "Travel and relocation costs, which are not mentioned in the published call",
            "Personal expenses beyond the three-year fellowship period"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Prescribed NS-ICARIF application form, completed",
            "Letter of acceptance for admission to the PhD programme in the identified area",
            "Two referee names with valid contact email addresses",
            "Certificate of good conduct from the Competent Authority",
            "Deputation approval for in-service Indian candidates",
            "Evidence of Master's degree in Agriculture and Allied Sciences"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "2026 deadline passed",
              "message": "Applications for 2026 closed on 25 September 2026. Watch the ICAR notifications page and Indian national newspapers for the 2027 announcement."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Annual announcement only",
              "message": "There is no rolling portal. ICAR invites applications annually via national newspapers, its website notification and Indian diplomatic missions."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Priority areas drive eligibility",
              "message": "A strong academic record is not enough if the proposed research falls outside the priority areas notified one year in advance."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "One-year registration window",
              "message": "If selected, you must register for the programme within one year of the award letter or the offer ends automatically."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Read the ICAR notification and identify the priority areas relevant to your research",
            "Contact the host university or overseas institution and apply for admission to the PhD programme in that area",
            "Collect the acceptance letter, good conduct certificate and, if applicable, deputation approval",
            "Identify two referees and confirm their email addresses",
            "Complete the prescribed application proforma",
            "Email everything to adg.hrd.applications@gmail.com with the subject line \"Application for NSIF: Name of Applicant and contact number\" before the published last date",
            "Retain the sent email, since the interview stage requires the admission acceptance letter again"
          ]
        },
