          "description": "KUISP is the KIIT University India Scholarships Programme for foreign national applicants, covering undergraduate, postgraduate and doctoral study as well as short-term training programmes at KIIT Deemed to be University in Bhubaneswar. It awards a scholarship of between 50% and 100% on tuition fees for the whole course duration, together with free books, examination and registration fees, sports facilities, internet access, airport pickup and student society membership. KIIT publishes 100 international scholarships, with two students per country receiving a full tuition waiver and ten students per country receiving a half waiver. KUISP is explicitly not fully funded: airfare, visa fees, medical insurance, stipends, personal living expenses and laptops are excluded, and students pay accommodation and food charges. Applications are free and are submitted through the KIIT International Admission Portal or directly to the international office, and in some cycles through Indian embassies and missions.",
          "program_type": "International tuition fee scholarship",
          "region": "Asia",
          "coverage": "Between 50% and 100% of tuition fees for the whole course duration, plus books, examination and registration fees and campus services. Airfare, visa, medical insurance, stipends, personal living expenses, laptops, accommodation and food are not covered.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Check whether KUISP is open to your nationality, since recent cycles excluded SAARC citizens",
            "Confirm your chosen programme appears in the KUISP annexure list of programmes eligible for a 100% tuition scholarship",
            "Have a valid passport ready, as a scanned copy is required",
            "Arrange English-translated academic documents if you studied in a non-English-speaking country",
            "Gather your academic transcripts and certificates from previous institutions",
            "Decide whether to apply through the KIIT portal or by emailing internationaloffice@kiit.ac.in, and note there is no application fee",
            "Budget separately for accommodation and food, airfare, visa, insurance and personal expenses, because KUISP does not cover them"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Being a SAARC national, which recent cycles excluded from the special KUISP offer",
            "Applying to a programme not listed in the KUISP annexure",
            "Missing the annual 1 March to end-August application window",
            "Missing the embassy or mission recommendation, where that is the cycle's route",
            "Not supplying an English translation of non-English documents",
            "Expecting accommodation, food, airfare, visa, insurance or stipend support, none of which KUISP provides"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Accommodation and food charges, payable annually on campus",
            "Annual registration fee as published by the university",
            "Airfare tickets to and from India",
            "Student visa fees",
            "Medical insurance",
            "Personal living expenses",
            "Laptop and personal equipment"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Recent passport-sized photograph",
            "Scanned copy of the passport, valid",
            "Academic transcripts and certificates from previous institutions",
            "Proof of English proficiency such as TOEFL or IELTS if applicable",
