          "description": "The Alan and Jane Handler Endowed Scholarship is the University of Rochester's premier undergraduate scholarship, funded from a permanent endowment created by a $25 million gift in 2007 from Rich and Martha Handler in honour of Alan and Jane Handler. It is awarded to first-year, fall-term domestic and international applicants who have demonstrated academic excellence, have outstanding potential to be future leaders, have shown resilience in the face of complex challenges, and have substantial financial need as demonstrated on the CSS Profile and FAFSA. Recipients receive complete financial support covering tuition, mandatory fees, housing, food, books, personal expenses and transportation for the regular four-year academic programme, plus health insurance where applicable, mentoring and an enrichment fund of up to $5,000. A nomination from an unrelated third party is required between 15 September and 30 November, and students are considered automatically if they submit the admission application and financial aid documents by 1 December.",
