          "description": "Harvard College's Griffin Financial Aid Office provides need-based financial aid that meets demonstrated need for admitted students, including international students, on the same basis as for U.S. students. Aid is need-blind with respect to admission and carries no academic, athletic or merit conditions. Families with income of $100,000 or below and typical assets have all billed expenses covered, including tuition, fees, food, housing, health insurance if needed, travel between campus and home, plus $2,000 start-up and launch grants. Deadlines are November 1 for Restrictive Early Action, February 1 for Regular Decision, March 1 for Transfer and May 1 for current students.",
