      "selection_notes": "Once the Admissions office has selected students to admit, the Financial Aid Office determines each student's need and awards aid accordingly, so financial need plays no part in the admission decision for admitted students. Aid is evaluated individually and annually.",
      "program_type": "Need-based undergraduate financial aid programme",
      "best_fit": "Students from families with low to middle incomes, including international applicants, who cannot afford Dartmouth's full cost of attendance.",
      "notes": "Dartmouth adopted universal need-blind admissions covering all international citizens, made possible by a $40 million anonymous gift, and states it is the sixth U.S. institution with universal need-blind admissions paired with a commitment to meet 100 percent of demonstrated need. A qualifying student is expected to meet the cost of attendance through a student contribution from leave-term earnings, a part-time on-campus job and/or personal savings. Contact: financial.aid@dartmouth.edu, 6024 McNutt Hall, Hanover NH 03755.",
      "description": "Dartmouth College meets 100% of the demonstrated need of all admitted financial aid applicants, regardless of citizenship or entry round, and its financial aid packages never include a required student loan. Need is calculated as cost of attendance minus family contribution, with direct expenses of tuition, fees, food and housing and indirect expenses such as travel, books, supplies and laundry. Families with total annual income below $125,000 with typical assets can expect no parent contribution, while families earning between $125,000 and $175,000 with typical assets can expect a scholarship or grants covering the full cost of tuition. International applicants file the CSS Profile with school code 3351, or the International Student Financial Aid Application if the CSS fee is a serious hardship. Financial aid deadlines are November 1 for Early Decision and February 1 for Regular Decision.",
