          "description": "Dartmouth College guarantees that it will meet 100% of the demonstrated need of all admitted financial aid applicants, regardless of citizenship, and no aid package includes a required student loan. Need equals cost of attendance minus family contribution, with tuition, fees, food and housing as direct expenses and travel, books, supplies and laundry considered as indirect expenses. Families with total annual income below $125,000 with typical assets can expect no parent contribution, and families between $125,000 and $175,000 can expect a scholarship or grants covering full tuition. International applicants file the CSS Profile with school code 3351 or, if the CSS fee is a serious hardship, the International Student Financial Aid Application, and submit parental tax statements from their country of residence in English and home currency. Financial aid deadlines are November 1 for Early Decision, February 1 for Regular Decision and March 1 for transfer.",
