      "selection_notes": "Rotary members and clubs are central to recruiting candidates. Clubs and districts are not required to fund candidates. Applications are reviewed by Rotary Peace Centers staff and all qualified applications move forward for further consideration.",
      "program_type": "Fully funded postgraduate fellowship in peace and development studies",
      "best_fit": "Experienced peace and development professionals and committed community leaders seeking a funded master's degree or professional development certificate at one of Rotary's partner peace centers.",
      "notes": "Rotary awards up to 170 funded fellowships a year across eight peace centers. Since 2002 the program has trained more than 1,900 fellows who now work in over 140 countries, many in governments, NGOs, education and research institutions, peacekeeping and law enforcement agencies, and organizations such as the United Nations and the World Bank. Master's programmes last 15 to 24 months and include a self-designed two- to three-month field study. The certificate programme is a one-year blended learning option for working professionals who complete field studies and design and carry out a social change initiative. Rotary Peace Fellowships may not be used for doctoral study.",
      "description": "The Rotary Peace Fellowship is funded by The Rotary Foundation and awards up to 170 fellowships a year for leaders with work experience in peace and development to study at one of eight Rotary Peace Centers. Each year up to 50 fellowships fund master's degrees and up to 120 fund professional development certificate studies at partner universities. Fellowships cover tuition and fees, room and board, round-trip transportation, and internship and field-study expenses. Master's programmes run 15 to 24 months and include a self-designed two- to three-month field study, while the certificate programme is a one-year blended learning course for working professionals that includes field studies and a social change initiative. Fellowships cannot be used for doctoral study. Applications open in February and the global deadline is 15 May; the 2027-28 cycle is closed and the 2028-29 cycle opens in February 2027.",
