            "application_portal": "https://my.rotary.org/en/peace-fellowship-application"
          },
          "description": "The Rotary Peace Fellowship, funded by The Rotary Foundation, awards up to 170 fellowships a year for leaders with work experience in peace and development to study at one of eight Rotary Peace Centers. Up to 50 fellowships fund master's degrees and up to 120 fund professional development certificate studies. Coverage includes tuition and fees, room and board, round-trip transportation, and internship and field-study expenses. Master's programmes run 15 to 24 months with a self-designed field study, while the one-year blended certificate programme is aimed at working professionals. Fellowships cannot be used for doctoral study. Applications open in February with a 15 May global deadline; the 2027-28 cycle is closed and the 2028-29 cycle opens in February 2027.",
          "program_type": "Fully funded postgraduate fellowship in peace and development",
          "region": "Global",
          "coverage": "Tuition and fees, room and board, round-trip transportation, internship expenses and field-study expenses.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are not planning doctoral study; Rotary Peace Fellowships cannot be used for doctoral study",
            "Confirm you are not a Rotary member, a former Rotary member within 36 months, or a spouse, lineal descendant, spouse of a lineal descendant, parent or grandparent by blood of a living person in those categories",
            "If you completed a Rotary Peace Centres certificate or master's programme or a Global Grant Scholarship, wait three years from the end date before your intended fellowship start date",
            "Prepare all application materials in English, including any club or district recommendation",
            "Build evidence of work experience in peace and development and of community or international service",
            "Ask your Rotary club or district to submit a recommendation before you submit your application",
            "Submit the online application to The Rotary Foundation by 15 May, since all applications are final on submission",
            "Watch for the next cycle: the 2028-29 application opens in February 2027"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Applying for doctoral study, which Rotary Peace Fellowships do not support",
            "Missing the 15 May global deadline, after which applications are final",
            "Submitting materials in a language other than English",
            "Being a former Rotary member, or a family member of a current Rotary member in the barred categories",
            "Applying too soon after finishing a Rotary Peace Centres programme or Global Grant Scholarship",
            "Applying as a working professional to the master's programme when the certificate programme is the intended track, or vice versa",
            "Expecting the club or district to fund you; Rotary states clubs and districts are not required to provide student funding"
