      "description": "The University of Groningen's NL Scholarship is a one-time grant for international students from outside the EEA who wish to pursue a master's degree in the Netherlands, co-funded by the Dutch Ministry of Education, Culture and Science and the university. It amounts to EUR 5,000, is awarded for one academic year only and can be received only once in a lifetime, and it is intended to help cover living expenses during the first year of study rather than to cover the full cost of studying. Applicants need an admission offer for one of the listed master's programmes, a bachelor's degree obtained outside the Netherlands and excellent undergraduate performance, and they must submit a motivation letter, a transcript of records and the admission letter before the deadline. The published deadline for the 2026-2027 academic year was 1 February 2026, with results notified by 15 March.",
