      "description": "The Radboud Scholarship Programme is a very selective scholarship for talented, highly motivated non-EEA students with outstanding study results applying to a complete English-taught Radboud University master's programme. A Radboud Scholarship reduces the tuition fee to EUR 2,771 for 2027/2028, against an example normal fee of about EUR 19,000, and covers visa, residence permit, health insurance and liability insurance costs, while living and studying costs remain the student's responsibility. A maximum of 26 scholarships are available for 2027/2028 across six faculties, the application is made through the OSIRIS master's application with two reference letters and a CV, the OSIRIS submission deadline is 31 January 2027 and the file must be complete by 14 February 2027, and the decision is communicated before mid-April 2027.",
