          "description": "The Radboud Scholarship Programme is a very selective scholarship for talented, motivated non-EEA students with outstanding results who apply to a full English-taught Radboud University master's programme. For 2027/2028 it reduces the tuition fee to EUR 2,771 against an example fee of EUR 19,000 and covers visa, residence permit and insurance costs, but not living and studying costs. Twenty-six scholarships are available across six faculties, applications run through the OSIRIS master's application with two reference letters and a CV, and the deadlines are 31 January 2027 for submission and 14 February 2027 for completeness, with decisions before mid-April 2027.",
          "program_type": "University tuition-fee scholarship (Profiling Fund)",
          "region": "Europe",
          "coverage": "Tuition fee reduced to EUR 2,771 for 2027/2028 plus visa, residence permit, health and liability insurance; living and studying costs not covered.",
