      "description": "The University of Twente Scholarship is a scholarship for excellent students from non-EU/EEA countries applying for an English-taught master's programme at the University of Twente. Its value ranges from EUR 3,000 to EUR 22,000 for one year and is intended as compensation for study-related costs, with no costs such as tuition fees paid on the student's behalf; for two-year programmes a second-year award of an equal amount is possible if the student obtains an average grade of 7 out of 10 and at least 50 percent of the European Credits at the end of the third quartile of the first year. Applicants must first obtain an academic admission letter for a qualifying 2027/2028 master's programme, hold a UT student number, meet English requirements of IELTS 6.5 or TOEFL iBT 90 with 6.0 in speaking, not be eligible for a Dutch study loan, and belong to the top 5 to 10 percent of their graduating class. The application form opens on 15 October 2026 and closes on 1 April 2027 at 16:00 CET, with results in the first week of May 2027.",
