          "description": "The University of Twente Scholarship (UTS) is a scholarship for excellent students from non-EU/EEA countries applying for an English-taught master's programme at the University of Twente. It pays EUR 3,000 to EUR 22,000 for one year as compensation for study-related costs, with no tuition fees paid on the student's behalf, and can be followed by an equal second-year award for two-year programmes meeting the progress requirements of an average grade of 7 out of 10 and 50 percent of ECTS by the end of the third quartile. Applicants need an academic admission letter for a qualifying 2027/2028 programme, a UT student number, IELTS 6.5 or TOEFL iBT 90 with 6.0 in speaking, must not be eligible for a Dutch study loan or pay the statutory tuition fee, and must be in the top 5 to 10 percent of their graduating class. The application form opens on 15 October 2026 and closes on 1 April 2027 at 16:00 CET, with results in the first week of May 2027.",
