      "selection_notes": "The faculty of the applied Master's programme reviews all VUFP applications received by the deadline and nominates applicants to the Central Scholarship Committee, which awards scholarships to the most talented students. Results are based on academic performance and motivation; GPA is only one of several scoring factors, together with motivation for the university/specific programme, future ambitions and extracurricular activities. Results are expected mid-March 2027 and offers must be accepted by the end of March 2027.",
      "program_type": "Merit-based tuition fee waiver for non-EU/EEA students",
      "best_fit": "Non-EU/EEA applicants with a GPA equivalent to a Dutch 8 who already hold a conditional or unconditional offer for a September 2027 English-taught VU Amsterdam Master's programme and can self-fund living costs.",
      "notes": "The VUFP is financially supported by VUvereniging, a social network of people connected to Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam. Applying for the VUFP automatically also applies for the NL Scholarship (formerly Holland Scholarship Programme), which is a separate one-time EUR 5,000 contribution towards living costs awarded to only about 20-25 candidates per year and only for the first study year. One VUFP scholarship is reserved for applicants who previously completed a semester or full academic year at VU Amsterdam through the Semester in Amsterdam programme. Students already enrolled in a two-year Master's who were not awarded the VUFP in 2026/2027 cannot apply for 2027/2028.",
