            "Not available to doctoral students who began their education in doctoral schools"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Any student admitted from the 2019/2020 academic year onward may receive the rector's scholarship regardless of citizenship or study terms. Students who began before 2019/2020 face additional conditions (for example EU/EFTA/Swiss citizens studying under Polish rules and having sufficient financial means, or holders of a residence card with labour-market access, a Schengen visa or a Polish work visa).",
          "international_eligibility": "Foreign students are explicitly eligible: \"Foreign students may also apply for the Rector's scholarship.\" Students who started in 2019/2020 or later qualify regardless of nationality; earlier cohorts must meet additional residence-status conditions.",
          "degree_levels": [
