            "note": "Programme-specific scholarship coordinator contact details are available in USOSweb under \"For everyone\" -> \"Applications\""
          },
          "description": "Jagiellonian University's Rector's Scholarship is a merit-based financial support from the university Scholarship Fund for students (including foreigners) in first-cycle, second-cycle and long-cycle master's studies, granted for outstanding academic performance, scientific, artistic or sports achievements. It is awarded for one academic year, in principle nine months from October to June, paid monthly by bank transfer into a Polish zloty account. In the first year of first-cycle or long-cycle master's studies it is granted to students admitted in the matura year who won an international olympiad or were laureates or finalists of a central-level olympiad, or who medalled in at least a Polish Championship competition; in higher years it is limited to the top 10% of students in a programme. The amount is set annually by the Rector in consultation with the University Student Government Economic Committee and published in the site's News section.",
