          "description": "Scholarships of the Government of the Czech Republic for students from developing countries are part of Czech foreign development cooperation and are run jointly by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, with DZS (the Czech National Agency for International Education and Research) carrying out the tasks. They fund a standard period of study in an accredited programme at a Czech public university: a master's programme in Czech preceded by a one-year Czech language and professional training course, or a master's or doctoral programme taught in English. Eligibility is limited to nationals of the partner states listed in each annual call who do not hold permanent residence in the Czech Republic. Applicants submit an electronic form by 30 September, sit the required online tests, and if selected attend an interview at the Czech embassy responsible for their country before the file proceeds to the ministries.",
