      "description": "Charles University guarantees every full-time doctoral student a doctoral study income of at least 1.2 times the Czech minimum wage for the standard length of the doctorate (four years). The income may take the form of a doctoral scholarship, a salary or wage for creative work directly related to preparing the dissertation, or a combination of both, and is often supplemented by research-project awards and teaching remuneration. For bachelor's and master's students the university publishes no general scholarship: its page routes applicants to Czech Ministry of Education scholarship schemes (developing-country, general international and International Visegrad Fund), the Vaclav Havel Bursary, the Institute for Language and Preparatory Studies, and faculty-level awards whose amounts are set by each faculty's own regulations.",
