          "description": "The International Visegrad Fund's fellowships and scholarships fund short research and study stays across the Visegrad Group. The Visegrad Fellowship Program is open to full-time doctoral students and PhD holders from Czechia, Hungary, Poland, Slovakia and Ukraine for an in-person stay of 2 to 10 weeks at a host institution in a different V4 country, covering a concrete research project, lectures or seminars, or archival study. It pays a lump-sum scholarship of EUR 500 per week in two instalments of 80% and 20%. Applications are made electronically through My Visegrad with an identity document, proof of doctoral status, a signed invitation letter from the host and a recommendation letter, all in English. Applications are assessed on academic credentials, the coherence and justification of the research plan, and the regional relevance of the topic and host. The separate Visegrad Scholarship Program supports Master's and post-Master's students and researchers for up to two semesters and next opens on 1 January 2027.",
