          "description": "Masaryk University's international office page describes how students use the International Visegrad Fund's scholarship programme to study or research at the university in Brno. The Fund runs the scheme and sets the money, the rules and the selection; Masaryk University is the host and issues the letter of acceptance that the applicant needs. The Fund's scholarships are intended for students at Master's or post-Master's level, support study or research projects abroad, allow stays of one to four semesters, and require at least four completed semesters of university study at the time of application. Eligible applicants are citizens of the Czech Republic, Hungary, Poland and Slovakia, plus citizens of Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Belarus, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Georgia, Kosovo, Macedonia, Moldova, Montenegro, Serbia and Ukraine. The stated application deadline is annually 15 March.",
          "program_type": "Regional study/research mobility scholarship of the International Visegrad Fund, used here to describe a stay hosted by Masaryk University",
          "region": "Europe",
          "coverage": "Not stated on this page; the award level is published by the International Visegrad Fund on visegradfund.org. No tuition coverage is mentioned.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm your nationality is V4 or one of the thirteen listed non-V4 countries",
            "Confirm you are at Master's or post-Master's level with at least four completed semesters of university study",
            "Choose the Masaryk University faculty you want to be hosted by and contact its international office early, because the letter of acceptance is required for the application",
            "Apply to the International Visegrad Fund, not to Masaryk University, before the annual 15 March deadline",
            "Check the Fund's own calendar on visegradfund.org, because its published windows differ from the 15 March date shown here"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Applying to Masaryk University instead of the International Visegrad Fund, which is the awarding body",
            "Missing the annual 15 March deadline",
            "Not having completed four semesters of university by the application date",
            "Applying without the faculty's letter of acceptance",
            "Assuming the university sets the award amount - the Fund does",
            "Expecting a bachelor's or PhD place, since the programme is for Master's and post-Master's level"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Any gap between the Fund's scholarship and the actual cost of living in Brno, since no amount is published on this page",
            "Tuition fees, which this page does not say the scholarship covers",
            "Travel costs before the award is paid",
            "Visa, insurance and dormitory costs not covered by the Fund"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
