      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "region": "Europe",
      "description": "The Foundation for Science and Technology runs an annual call for PhD studentships under its Regulation for Studentships and Fellowships (RBI) and Research Fellowship Holder Statute (EBI). The regular line of application covers all scientific areas and funds research carried out in scientific and academic institutions, including public and private higher education institutions, R&D units, Associated Laboratories and other private non-profit R&D bodies, at home or abroad. Selected applicants receive a monthly allowance plus complementary support such as tuition fees, support for additional training, presentation of work at scientific meetings, personal accident insurance and, where applicable, travel and relocation costs. In the 2026 call FCT received 3,628 applications and approved 1,000, a total funding value of 90,625,000 EUR, an approval rate of 28%.",
      "deadline": "Official wording: \"The Call is open from March 2nd to 5:00 pm (Lisbon time) March 31st, 2026.\" FCT adds that the call \"takes place each year in March or, occasionally, between March and April\", but no 2027 dates had been published on the page as of 2026-10-04.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
