      "selection_notes": "Applications are graded from 0.000 to 5.000 on three criteria: Criterion A, merit of the applicant (30%), Criterion B, merit of the work plan (40%) and Criterion C, merit of the hosting conditions (30%). Applicant merit is split equally between academic career (50%) and personal CV (50%). Ranking is by weighted average, with tie-breaks in the order Criterion B, then Criterion A, then Criterion C. Applications scoring below 3.000 are not eligible for a studentship.",
