          "description": "The Foundation for Science and Technology's annual Call for PhD Studentships finances doctoral research in Portugal and abroad under its Regulation for Studentships and Fellowships. The regular line of application covers all scientific areas and is aimed at research in scientific and academic institutions, including public and private higher education institutions, R&D units and Associated Laboratories. Applicants must be enrolled in or eligible to enter a PhD programme, may be of any nationality, must not have held an FCT-funded PhD studentship before, must not already hold a doctorate, and must reside permanently in Portugal if applying for an abroad-based studentship. Applications are submitted exclusively through myFCT, and the Contracting Institution named in the form must validate the application within ten working days or the application is excluded. Selected applicants receive a monthly allowance plus complementary support covering tuition fees, additional training, conference presentation, personal accident insurance and, where applicable, travel and relocation costs. Applications are scored on applicant merit (30%), work plan (40%) and hosting conditions (30%), with a minimum passing classification of 3.000.",
