    {
      "name": "Nova SBE Master's Scholarships and Awards (including the Nova SBE Merit Scholarship)",
      "legacy_titles": [
        "Nova School of Business and Economics (Nova SBE) Merit Scholarships"
      ],
      "country": "Portugal",
      "degree_levels": "Master's",
      "funding_type": "Partially Funded",
      "official_source": "Nova School of Business and Economics (Nova SBE), Universidade NOVA de Lisboa",
      "official_source_url": "https://www.novasbe.unl.pt/en/programs/scholarships-funding/masters",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "region": "Europe",
      "description": "Nova SBE funds its master's students through an institutional portfolio of tuition-fee scholarships and awards. The Nova SBE Merit Scholarship is open to all candidates regardless of country of origin and covers 20% or 50% of the master's tuition fee value. Alongside it sit the Nova SBE Social Mobility Scholarship (20%, 50% or 100% of tuition, for candidates with proven financial need), the Nova SBE Continuity Scholarship (50% or 100%, for Nova SBE bachelor's graduates within a widened income threshold), and a series of partner-funded awards including Accenture (100%), Antonio Serrenho (100%), Banco Primus (100%), Deloitte (100%), Andre Sousa Bessa (100%), Women in Finance (20% or 50%), plus CEMS-specific awards. Scholarships are awarded on a rolling basis, so the available budget can be exhausted before the end of the master's admission cycle, and combined Nova SBE funding is normally capped at 70% of total tuition.",
      "deadline": "No fixed date is published for the Nova SBE Merit Scholarship. The official wording is \"Applications are open for the Fall Intake and cannot be considered after the application to the Master's program has been submitted\", and \"Scholarships are awarded on a rolling basis to applicants\". Partner scholarships with published windows on the same page ran from 13 November 2025 to 23 March 2026 for the Fall Intake.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "rolling",
      "application_period": "Rolling award during the master's admission cycle, for the Fall Intake only for the Merit Scholarship. The Social Mobility and Continuity Scholarships are available for both the Fall and Spring intakes. Separate partner scholarships on the same page state explicit windows of 13 November 2025 to 23 March 2026.",
      "eligibility_summary": "For the Nova SBE Merit Scholarship, all candidates can apply regardless of country of origin; interest must be declared in the master's application form, and the award must be reapplied for against merit criteria at the end of the first year. Individual partner scholarships impose extra conditions such as nationality, household income tiers, a minimum converted bachelor's GPA, enrolment in named master's programmes, or eligibility for a 100% Social Mobility or Continuity Scholarship.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Nova SBE Merit Scholarship: all candidates, regardless of country of origin, who indicate interest in the master's application form",
        "Nova SBE Continuity Scholarship: bachelor's obtained at, or being concluded at, Nova SBE and admitted to any Nova SBE master's, with per capita gross income below 40 times the value of the IAS",
        "Nova SBE Social Mobility Scholarship: all candidates regardless of country of origin, with proven financial need evidenced by household tax documentation",
        "Accenture Scholarship: enrolled in Business Analytics, Management, Finance, International Master's in Management or International Master's in Finance, and eligible for a 100% Social Mobility or Continuity Scholarship; priority to a disability rating of 60% or higher",
