          },
          "description": "Nova SBE's master's scholarships and funding page sets out an institutional and partner-funded portfolio. The Nova SBE Merit Scholarship is open to every applicant regardless of country of origin and reduces the master's tuition fee by 20% or 50%, with interest declared in the master's application form and the merit criteria re-checked at the end of the first year. The Social Mobility Scholarship (20%, 50% or 100%) supports candidates with proven financial need, and the Continuity Scholarship (50% or 100%) widens that threshold for Nova SBE bachelor's graduates. Partner awards from Accenture, Antonio Serrenho, Banco Primus, Deloitte, Andre Sousa Bessa and others cover 100% of tuition but impose programme, GPA, nationality and income conditions, and some require an interview or video. Scholarships are awarded on a rolling basis because the budget can be used up before the end of the master's admission cycle, and none of them funds the application fee, the enrolment instalment, CEMS, the Double Degree, additional semesters, exchange programmes or Executive Master's programmes. Combined Nova SBE funding is normally capped at 70% of tuition.",
