          },
          "description": "The Embassy of the People's Republic of China in Bangladesh announces the Chinese Government Scholarship (CGS) - Type A for Bangladeshi students, administered by the China Scholarship Council (CSC). It funds Bachelor's, Master's, Doctoral (PhD) and one-year Chinese language study at Chinese universities. Coverage comprises full tuition fees, on-campus accommodation, comprehensive medical insurance, a monthly living allowance of approximately CNY 2,500-3,500 depending on programme level, and international round-trip airfare. Applications are made online through www.campuschina.org and the stated deadline for the announced cycle was 10 January 2026.",
          "program_type": "Bilateral scholarship administered by the China Scholarship Council",
          "region": "Asia",
          "coverage": "Full tuition, accommodation, medical insurance, monthly living allowance and international round-trip airfare",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you hold Bangladeshi citizenship, the eligibility basis stated in the announcement",
            "Choose the target degree level first: Bachelor's, Master's, Doctoral or one-year Chinese language, because the living allowance band and award type depend on it",
            "Create a China Scholarship Council account on www.campuschina.org and complete the Type A application online",
            "Have scans ready for the documents the CSC portal requests, since the announcement only says to \"submit all required documents within the stipulated time\"",
            "Budget separately for costs the announcement does not name, such as local transport in China and the visa fee",
            "Re-check the Embassy's press release page for the next cycle's announcement before the assumed January window"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Applying through a national portal other than www.campuschina.org, which the announcement names as the only route",
            "Missing the 10 January cut-off, which is an exact date rather than a rolling window",
            "Applying to a degree level outside the four listed in the announcement",
            "Incomplete document upload, since the announcement places the burden on submitting all required documents in time",
            "Assuming the CNY 2,500-3,500 allowance applies to every level, as the announcement states it varies by programme level"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Local transport and daily expenses beyond the stated monthly living allowance",
            "Chinese student visa and residence-permit fees",
            "Any university charges not covered by \"Full tuition fees\", such as bench or laboratory fees"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "The Embassy page itself names no document list; the authoritative list is the one loaded in the CSC portal at www.campuschina.org",
            "Confirm the passport validity window covers the intended study period before submitting",
            "Check that academic certificates and transcripts match the degree level selected in the portal"
