      "official_updates_url": "https://www.helsinki.fi/en/research/doctoral-school/resdoc-project/how-apply",
      "description": "RESDOC (Resilient and Just Systems Doctoral Project) is an international doctoral training project at the University of Helsinki, co-funded by the Marie Skłodowska-Curie Actions COFUND scheme under Horizon Europe and the University itself. It recruits 30 doctoral researchers for four-year, 100% employment contracts running 2027-2030, at a gross salary of approximately EUR 2,900 per month including a mobility allowance, plus an annual travel allowance for conferences and secondments. Research must fit one of four interdisciplinary themes: Infectious Diseases and Antimicrobial Resistance in Changing Environment; Biodiversity and Nature's Resilience; Secure and Sustainable Food and Water Systems; and Just Socio-Ecological Transition. The 2026 call closed on 31 August 2026 with 2,159 applications, and evaluation by external evaluators was under way in September 2026.",
