          },
          "description": "RESDOC is an interdisciplinary doctoral training project at the University of Helsinki that recruits 30 doctoral researchers on four-year, full-time employment contracts for 2027-2030. It is co-funded by the MSCA COFUND programme under Horizon Europe and the University. Holders receive a gross salary of approximately EUR 2,900 per month including a mobility allowance for relocation costs, plus an annual travel allowance for conferences and secondments. The 2026 call closed on 31 August 2026 with 2,159 applications, of which 1,023 passed the eligibility check, and external evaluation was running in September-October 2026.",
