          "description": "The University Research Fellowship (URF) is an eight-year fellowship for outstanding early career scientists with the potential to become leaders in their field, designed to build an independent research career in the UK or the Republic of Ireland. Awards based in the UK are funded by the Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade, while awards based in the Republic of Ireland are funded by Research Ireland and must be hosted within a Research Ireland Eligible Research Body. Applicants can request up to £1,907,400 over eight years to cover a contribution to salary, indirect and estate costs, equipment and research expenses, staff costs, and relocation and visa costs. Shortlisted applicants attend an in-person interview at the Royal Society, and years six to eight of funding are subject to a mid-fellowship review.",
