      "best_fit": "Non-Italian students without Italian residency applying to an English-taught bachelor's, single-cycle or master's degree at the University of Padua with an outstanding academic record.",
      "notes": "The scholarship may be revoked if a recipient does not earn at least 20 CFU by 30 November of the following academic year, or decides to transfer to another university or withdraw; in that case the instalments already received must be returned. Beneficiaries remain liable for the regional fee and the revenue stamp each academic year, and must pay the tuition fees due until graduation after the maximum scholarship period ends. The degree course application automatically makes the candidate eligible, so no separate application or additional documentation is required.",
      "description": "The Padua International Excellence Scholarship Programme awards up to 76 scholarships to high-achieving international students entering an English-taught first-cycle or master's degree at the University of Padua. Each award is worth €8,000.00 gross per academic year plus exemption from student fees, with beneficiaries paying only the regional fee and the revenue stamp. Scholarships run for a maximum of two years on master's courses and three years on bachelor's or single-cycle courses, paid in two instalments and conditional on earning at least 20 CFU by 30 November each year. Eligibility follows automatically from the degree course application.",
