      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Tilburg University Waiver halves the institutional tuition fee for up to 21 non-EEA international applicants each year, as part of the university's Diversity, Equity and Inclusion commitment. It applies to all regular one-year Master's programmes starting in September 2027, with the two-year Master in Cognitive Science and Artificial Intelligence as an explicit exception; Research Master's and Pre-Master's students are not eligible. Applicants must have completed their most recent degree in a designated country and must not already hold any other tuition-fee waiver. If more eligible applicants apply than there are waivers, recipients are chosen by random lottery, and outcomes are notified by 1 June 2027.",
      "region": "Europe",
      "duration": "One year of tuition for a regular Master's programme; the two-year Master in Cognitive Science and Artificial Intelligence is also eligible",
      "deadline": "Both the Master's programme application and the waiver webform must be completed by the same date: \"Submit your application for a Tilburg University Master's program by April 1, 2027\" and \"Complete the Tilburg University Waiver application form before April 1, 2027\". Outcomes are notified by June 1, 2027.",
