          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "All English-taught Master's programmes are eligible, with the exception of Erasmus Mundus Master's programmes and joint-degree Master's programmes. For 2027/2028 a maximum of 26 scholarships are distributed as: Faculty of Arts 2, Faculty of Law 2, Nijmegen School of Management 5, Faculty of Philosophy, Theology and Religious Studies 1, Faculty of Science 9, Faculty of Social Sciences 7.",
          "application_method": "Apply through the OSIRIS Application System as part of the Master's admission application, ticking the Radboud Scholarship option; the system then requests three additional uploads (two reference letters and a CV). Submit by 31 January 2027 23:59 CET and complete the application by 14 February 2027 23:59 CET.",
          "application_route": "Submit a Master's programme application via the OSIRIS Application System, indicating the wish to apply for a Radboud Scholarship, and upload the two reference letters and CV when requested. Do not email the scholarship team; the page states not to use that address for the application.",
