          "description": "A highly selective Radboud University scholarship for talented, highly motivated non-EU/non-EEA students with outstanding study results, covering English-taught Master's programmes starting September 2027. The scholarship reduces the tuition fee to EUR 2,771 (to be confirmed) from an illustrative EUR 19,000 and covers visa, residence permit, health insurance and liability insurance costs, but not living or study costs. A maximum of 26 scholarships are available for 2027/2028 across six faculties. Applications are made through OSIRIS alongside the Master's admission application by 31 January 2027, with the application complete by 14 February 2027 and decisions before mid-April 2027.",
