      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "Türkiye Bursları is the Republic of Türkiye's government-funded, competitive scholarship programme for international students, run under the coordination of the Presidency of Turks Abroad and Relatives of Overseas Citizens (YTB). It funds associate, bachelor's, master's, PhD and research places at the most prestigious Turkish universities and is distinctive in providing university and department placement rather than a fellowship to be spent at a chosen institution. The package covers tuition, a monthly stipend, health insurance, accommodation, a one-year Turkish language course, a once-off return flight ticket and free academic and cultural programmes. Applications are submitted online, free of charge, through the Türkiye Scholarships Application System (TBBS).",
      "program_type": "Government scholarship (YTB, Türkiye Scholarships)",
      "duration": "One year of free Turkish language education before or alongside the degree programme; associate degree is a two-year programme, with bachelor's, master's and PhD programmes of standard length. Research Scholarships have their own application periods.",
      "deadline": "Applications for the full-time programmes (associate, bachelor's, master's, PhD and art scholarships) are received through the Türkiye Scholarships Application System (TBBS) between 10 January and 20 February, which is the application period every year. Research Scholarships have different application periods, announced regularly on the official website. For the 2026 cycle the window was 10 January to 20 February 2026, so the next cycle is expected in the same annual window.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "One annual period each year: 10 January to 20 February for international applicants, for associate, bachelor's, master's and doctoral scholarships. Research Scholarships run on separate, individually announced periods.",
      "eligibility_summary": "The programme is competitive and merit-based with a strong emphasis on academic excellence. It is open to applicants from all countries, and candidates choose between up to 12 university and department options in the online application, subject to what the system offers them and to the equivalence and validity of their fields in their own country. Türkiye Scholarships does not award scholarships in the field of health sciences.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Open to citizens of all countries",
