            "Competitive, merit-based selection with a strong emphasis on candidates' academic excellence",
            "High grade point average and high scores in the international language proficiency and academic qualification examinations determined by the Presidency (Merit Scholarship Program)",
            "Candidates are evaluated centrally by YTB, which then assigns university and department placement"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": null,
          "duration": "One year of free Turkish language education plus the degree programme; associate programmes run two years, and the Art Scholarship Programme covers undergraduate, graduate and PhD study in three named universities",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "The flight ticket must be requested through TBBS before travelling to Türkiye, after the commitment is completed, and before returning to the home country upon graduation",
            "Scholarship students are placed by the programme at a Turkish university rather than selecting an arbitrary institution",
            "Students are expected to study full time at the assigned university and department"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "Merit Scholarship Program: monthly stipend 2 times higher than the regular payment for academically qualified students",
            "Art Scholarship Programme at Ankara Music and Fine Arts University, Ankara Hacı Bayram Veli University and İstanbul Technical University",
            "Research Scholarships for international researchers and academicians, with separate application periods",
            "YTB - Islamic Development Bank (ISDB) Joint Scholarship Programme with its own announcement cycle",
            "International Student Academy, student congresses, art competitions and the Türkiye Alumni Network (150,000+ members in 160 countries)"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "general": "Presidency of Turks Abroad and Relatives of Overseas Citizens (YTB), Türkiye Scholarships - https://www.ytb.gov.tr; programme contact and office directory at https://www.turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/about/ouroffices and https://www.turkiyeburslari.gov.tr/about/iletisim",
            "email": null
          },
          "description": "Türkiye Scholarships is a government-funded, competitive scholarship programme awarded to outstanding international students and researchers to pursue full-time or short-term programmes at the top universities in Türkiye. It provides university and department placement, covers tuition fees, provides a monthly stipend, accommodation, general health insurance, a one-year Turkish language course and a once-off flight ticket, and offers free academic and cultural programmes. Applications are received online, free of charge, through the Türkiye Scholarships Application System between 10 January and 20 February every year.",
          "program_type": "Government scholarship (YTB, Türkiye Scholarships)",
          "region": "Middle East / Europe",
          "coverage": "Tuition, monthly stipend, accommodation, health insurance, one-year Turkish language course and a once-off return flight ticket",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Register on the Türkiye Scholarships Application System (TBBS) at tbbs.turkiyeburslari.gov.tr - the application is free of charge",
            "Note the annual window: 10 January to 20 February",
            "Search the programme database by education field and level, and check the equivalence and validity of your field in your own country",
            "Rank your university and department preferences, remembering that the system lets you choose between 12 options and only shows what is available to you",
            "Confirm your field is funded - Türkiye Scholarships does not award scholarships in health sciences",
            "Prepare your certificates, transcripts, identity document and passport photograph for upload",
            "Budget for the first arrival: the once-off flight ticket is requested through TBBS only after the commitment process is completed, so have funds for the first journey",
            "Plan for the one-year Turkish language course and for dormitory rules, which differ between undergraduate and graduate students"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Missing the 10 January to 20 February window - the programme receives applications in one period only each year",
            "Choosing a field that the programme does not fund, notably health sciences",
            "Expecting to attend a specific university that the system does not offer to you - placement is decided centrally",
            "Not accounting for the one-year Turkish language course when planning degree start dates",
            "Assuming the flight ticket is arranged automatically - it must be requested via TBBS after completing the commitment",
            "Assuming graduate students keep free dormitory accommodation beyond the first year",
            "Selecting an art programme outside the three participating universities"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Master's and doctoral students receive free dormitory accommodation only in the first year; from the second year a housing allowance of 6,000 TL (Istanbul and Ankara) or 5,000 TL (other cities) applies, so actual rent above the allowance is not covered",
            "The official pages publish no figure for incidental or private accommodation costs, so budget separately for a private room or property",
            "The once-off flight ticket covers one outbound and one return journey; any additional travel, excess baggage or personal trips are not mentioned as covered"
          ],
