      "best_fit": "Non-French secondary school students finishing their terminale year in a recognised French school abroad who intend to study for a state-recognised diploma in French higher education.",
      "notes": "Two benefit systems coexist since 2023. Holders selected before 2023 receive a EUR 500 per year start-of-year grant, EUR 235 per month at taux 1 or EUR 725 per month at taux 2, and taux 1 and 2 holders could claim complementary benefits including tuition fees, round-trip travel and CROUS housing. Holders selected from 2023 receive the social coverage grant, EUR 280 per month at taux 1 or EUR 860 per month at taux 2, automatic affiliation to the Campus France mutuelle, and complementary benefits for taux 1 and 2 holders including round-trip travel and CROUS housing; tuition fee coverage is not listed for this cohort.",
      "description": "France Excellence-Major is a French government scholarship run by AEFE for the Ministry for Europe and Foreign Affairs that supports the best non-French baccalaureat holders from the network of French schools abroad to continue their higher education in France. Around 800 foreign students are supported at any one time over five years of study, and about 200 new holders join each year. Applications require pre-selection by the head of the French school abroad and online entry on the dedicated Cascade application, followed by assessment by the French embassy's cultural cooperation service and a selection commission convened by AEFE each May. Selection weighs school results, a coherent orientation project, involvement in school life and extracurricular activity, and motivation for demanding French higher education. Holders receive a family-need-rated monthly allowance of EUR 280 or EUR 860, complementary health cover, and, at the higher rates, round-trip travel and CROUS housing.",
