          "description": "France Excellence-Major is a French government scholarship operated by AEFE for the Ministry for Europe and Foreign Affairs, supporting the best non-French baccalaureat holders from the worldwide network of French schools to study in France. About 800 foreign students are supported at any one time over five years of study, and roughly 200 new holders are selected each year after their terminale year. Candidates must be pre-selected by the head of their French school, enter their file on the dedicated Cascade application, and pass assessment by the French embassy and an AEFE selection commission convened each May. Ranking weighs school results, a coherent orientation project, involvement in school life and extracurricular activity, and motivation for demanding French higher education. Holders receive a family-need-rated monthly allowance of EUR 280 or EUR 860, complementary health cover through the Campus France mutuelle, and at the higher rates round-trip travel and CROUS housing; tuition fees are not among the benefits listed for the current cohort.",
