          "description": "The Cambridge Trust International Scholarship is a full-cost postgraduate award from the Cambridge Trust, an independent UK charity, for applicants from countries other than the United Kingdom or Ireland who are highly ranked by their prospective Cambridge department. It covers the University tuition fee at the International rate, annual maintenance sufficient for a single person, the student visa and the Student Immigration Health Surcharge, and is tenable at any College in any subject except premium rate courses. Unlike most Trust postgraduate awards, selection is on academic merit alone: 'The financial situation of applicants does not affect selection.' There is no separate application; candidates apply only through the University of Cambridge admissions application by the funding deadline for their course.",
