      "notes": "The official page states: \"This scholarship is bond-free. However, non-Singaporean students (including Singapore Permanent Residents) are required to sign a Tuition Grant agreement with the Ministry of Education and will be contractually obliged to work for Singapore-based companies for 3 years upon graduation from SMU.\" SMU's international-students listing summarises the same award slightly differently, referring to \"a full four-year tuition fee waiver, a one-off notebook grant, sponsorship for an international exchange programme, an overseas study mission, and an international community service project\"; the dedicated LKCSP page figures are used here as the authoritative statement.",
      "description": "The Lee Kong Chian Scholars' Programme is one of Singapore Management University's most prestigious undergraduate scholarships, made possible by a gift from the Lee Foundation, with up to 60 scholarships funded. It is open to full-time SMU first-year undergraduates of any nationality taking a single or double degree programme, and requires a second major or an equivalent breadth requirement, demonstrated leadership and communications skills, and a substantial record of co-curricular activity or community service. Benefits comprise a waiver of annual subsidised tuition fees for regular terms for up to four years, a S$16,000 Global Opportunities grant funding overseas exchange, community service or competitions, a S$5,000 annual living allowance, a S$1,800 one-time computer allowance, and development opportunities from SMU's Student Success Centre. Applicants are considered through the Scholarship section of the standard admission application, with no separate scholarship form. The scholarship is bond-free, but non-Singaporean scholars must sign a Ministry of Education Tuition Grant agreement obliging them to work for Singapore-based companies for three years after graduation.",
