          "description": "The Helmut Veith Stipend is an annually awarded grant for women in the field of computer science who (plan to) pursue one of the Master's programmes in Computer Science at TU Wien taught in English and who have, or have the interest to develop, a solid mathematical and technical background in at least one of the areas in which Austrian scientist Helmut Veith worked. TU Wien lists the benefits as EUR 7000 per year and a waiver of tuition fees at TU Wien, for study in Austria at TU Wien. The fund is set up by TU Wien, the Wolfgang Pauli Institute and the colleagues and friends of the late Prof. Veith, and the stipend is dedicated to the memory of Professor Helmut Veith (1971-2016). Applications are submitted electronically via the TU Wien job portal and the annual application deadline is November 30th.",
