          "description": "The Václav Havel Bursary is Charles University's own financial support for international students whose studies are hindered or prevented by repression under totalitarian, authoritarian or other non-democratic regimes. Students from countries where humanitarian organisations report violated human rights and freedoms, and where discriminatory measures restrict access to education, may apply once they have been admitted and enrolled in a degree programme at a Charles University faculty through the standard admissions procedure. The student submits the Application Form and all documents required under Rector's Directive (Article 2, point 3) to the faculty's Student Affairs Office, and the faculty forwards the complete file digitally via the Dean or an authorised Vice-Dean to the Chair of the Václav Havel Bursary Board. Applications are submitted twice a year, by 31 March and 31 October, with the next round closing on 31 October 2026. Proof-of-persecution documents may be submitted in English, and students preparing for Czech-language study may also apply for a contribution towards living expenses. The bursary is governed by Rector's Directive No. 56/2025, effective from 22 December 2025.",
