          "description": "The OeAD, Austria's Agency for Education and Internationalisation, is a non-profit limited liability company owned by the Republic of Austria, with ownership rights exercised by the Austrian Federal Ministry for Women, Science and Research. It funds study and research stays in Austria through many separate programmes, listed with their calls, target groups, amounts and deadlines in the Austrian Database for Scholarships and Research Grants at www.grants.at. Incoming programmes cover Bachelor's, Master's and PhD study as well as postdoctoral research, and include the Ernst Mach Grant family of programmes, the ASEA-UNINET grants and the Franz Werfel Fellowship. The agency also runs outgoing programmes for Austrians, which are outside the scope of this record.",
