          "description": "The Study in Canada Scholarships programme, funded by Global Affairs Canada through the Academic Relations program, lets Canadian post-secondary institutions host international students for short-term study or research exchanges. Individual students cannot apply directly: a Canadian Designated Learning Institution that waives tuition fees selects and nominates them through the My EduCanada portal, and the institution submits a Management and Accountability Framework to the scholarship administrator. Awards are CAD 10,200 for four months or one academic term at college, undergraduate or graduate level, and CAD 14,000 for five to six months at graduate level, covering round-trip airfare, health insurance, visa or study/work permit fees, living expenses and study supplies. Eligibility is restricted to citizens of 20 named countries and territories who remain full-time, tuition-paying students at a home institution during the stay, and all project activity must be completed by September 30, 2027.",
