    {
      "name": "Berea College Tuition Promise Scholarship",
      "legacy_titles": [
        "Berea College Tuition Promise Scholarship"
      ],
      "country": "USA",
      "degree_levels": "Bachelor's",
      "funding_type": "Tuition Fee Waiver",
      "official_source": "Berea College",
      "official_source_url": "https://www.berea.edu/admissions",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "region": "North America",
      "duration": "Four years, renewed annually while the student remains enrolled and files the FAFSA each year",
      "deadline": "Official wording for first-year domestic applicants: \"Early Action I: November 1\", \"Early Action II: January 31\", \"Regular Decision: March 31\". International applicants may apply by October 15 for Early Action or January 15 for Regular Decision. Berea advises that \"Applying by the Early Action deadlines is highly recommended, as admission is selective and space in the incoming class is limited.\" All applicants must also submit a FAFSA, which is available from October 1 with an expected priority filing date of October 31.",
      "deadline_date": "2026-11-01",
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "Rolling admission with three advised domestic first-year deadlines each cycle: Early Action I on 1 November, Early Action II on 31 January and Regular Decision on 31 March. International applicants use 15 October for Early Action and 15 January for Regular Decision. The FAFSA is refiled every year, available from 1 October with a 31 October priority date.",
      "eligibility_summary": "First-year applicants, domestic or international, who show strong academic accomplishments and come from families with limited financial resources and who meet Berea's financial eligibility requirement, which the College assesses from the FAFSA using household size and adjusted gross income bands. Admitted students average a 3.65 high school GPA and qualify for federal Pell Grants. Every applicant must submit a FAFSA to be considered for admission.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Apply as a first-year student to Berea College",
        "Meet the College's financial eligibility requirement, assessed from the FAFSA using household size and adjusted gross income",
        "Show strong academic accomplishments; admitted students average a 3.65 high school GPA",
        "Come from a family with limited financial resources; most admitted families have an annual household income within the range of the federal poverty guidelines",
        "Domestic applicants must use the 1 November, 31 January or 31 March cycle; international applicants the 15 October or 15 January dates",
        "All applicants must submit a FAFSA to be considered for admission"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Remaining cost of tuition after all federal, state, institutional and private grants and scholarships are considered, so the student never pays tuition from personal income",
        "Published 2026-27 tuition of $56,900",
        "From Fall 2027, extension of coverage to 100% of housing, food, fees and supplies without loans for all students until graduation"
      ],
      "required_documents": [
        "Application for Admission and Scholarship, submitted free of charge",
        "Free Application for Federal Student Aid (FAFSA)",
        "School Counselor Evaluation Form, not required for GED holders and home-school applicants",
        "One teacher recommendation from a core subject teacher",
        "Official academic records and transcripts",
        "ACT or SAT scores, unless applying test-optional",
        "Non-Custodial Financial Questionnaire, Self-Employed/Business Owner Questionnaire or additional documentation, if requested during financial eligibility assessment"
      ],
      "catalogue_url": "https://www.berea.edu/admissions/admission-information/apply/checklist-items/first-year",
      "official_updates_url": "https://www.berea.edu/student-financial-aid/",
      "english_requirement": "Not specified on the Berea Tuition Promise pages. International applicants are welcomed and must meet the College's general admission requirements; the College states it welcomes applicants \"from across the United States and from other countries\".",
      "requirements": [
        "File the FAFSA, which is required for admission consideration because of Berea's financial eligibility requirement, and refile it every year while enrolled",
        "Apply within the advised cycle, with Early Action strongly recommended because admission is selective and space is limited",
        "Meet the minimum admissions criteria, which the catalog describes as an ACT composite of 19 or SAT of 980 and ranking in the top three-fifths of the high school class, though the College is test-optional",
        "Submit the School Counselor Evaluation Form unless you hold a GED or are home-schooled",
        "Submit one teacher recommendation from a core subject",
        "Complete the application in full, as incomplete applications are not considered",
        "If requested, complete the Non-Custodial Financial Questionnaire or provide additional financial documentation"
      ],
      "application_method": [
        "Complete the Application for Admission and Scholarship online at the Berea admissions portal at no cost",
        "File the FAFSA, which the FAFSA becomes available each October 1",
        "Ask a high school guidance counsellor to complete the School Counselor Evaluation Form, unless exempt",
        "Ask a core subject teacher to submit the teacher recommendation",
        "Submit by the applicable Early Action or Regular Decision date for domestic or international applicants",
        "Complete any additional financial documentation the Office of Admissions requests during the financial eligibility assessment"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "The admissions process is holistic, weighing the completed application, official academic records, test scores where submitted, financial eligibility, recommendations and endorsements, conversations with an admissions counsellor, extracurricular and co-curricular activity, community service, character and personal qualities, and demonstrated interest in the College. Admitted students average a 3.65 high school GPA and qualify for federal Pell Grants, and Berea is academically competitive with an average ACT of about 25 and more than half of first-year students ranked in the top fifth of their high school class. Well qualified applicants may be accepted for fall admission as early as December, though an early application alone does not ensure admission.",
      "program_type": "Need-aware tuition promise awarded to all admitted students, not a competitive merit scholarship",
      "best_fit": "Students with strong academic potential from families with limited financial resources who want a tuition-free bachelor's degree at a work college in Kentucky, and who are willing to meet Berea's unique financial eligibility test.",
      "notes": "This is not a competitive merit award that applicants win. Berea has not charged tuition for more than 130 years, and the Tuition Promise Scholarship is applied after all other aid is considered, so every admitted student receives it. It is awarded to admitted students rather than at application stage, which matters for applicants who assume they must win it. Housing, food and fees remain payable for current cohorts, but from Fall 2027 the College's Financial Freedom Pledge guarantees 100% of tuition, housing, food, fees and supplies without loans for all students until graduation. Endowment earnings provide 74% of the College's operating budget, state and federal aid 19% and donors the remaining 7%.",
