      "program_type": "Graduate research scholarship",
      "description": "The Melbourne Research Scholarship is offered to high-achieving domestic and international students enrolling in, or already enrolled in, a graduate research degree at the University of Melbourne. It exists in three forms: a Fee Offset award, a Stipend award, and a combined Stipend and Fee Offset award. The Stipend award combines a full fee offset with a fortnightly stipend of $41,100 per year pro rata (2027 full-time rate), a one-off relocation allowance and OSHC Single Membership for international students who need a student visa. No separate application is required: applicants who apply for a graduate research course by that course's closing date are assessed automatically. Around 350 scholarships are available, and selection is by ranking on academic results for previous study and research potential.",
      "deadline": "No application required. If you have applied for a graduate research course by the application closing date for that course, you will receive confirmation within seven days that you are automatically considered.",
