            "manage": "https://students.unimelb.edu.au/student-support/scholarships-and-financial-support/manage-your-scholarship"
          },
          "description": "The Melbourne Research Scholarship is offered to high-achieving domestic and international students enrolling in a graduate research degree at the University of Melbourne. Around 350 are available each year in three forms: Fee Offset, Stipend, and combined Stipend and Fee Offset. The Stipend and combined awards provide a full fee offset plus a fortnightly stipend of $41,100 per year pro rata, a one-off relocation allowance and OSHC Single Membership for international students who need a student visa. No separate application is required: applicants who apply for a graduate research course by that course's closing date are assessed automatically, and offers for stipend and fee offset awards are made separately from, but around the same time as, course offers.",
