          "description": "The ESPRIT program (Early-Stage Program: Research - Innovation - Training) is intended to improve the skills and support the professional development of researchers from all disciplines early in their research careers by giving them the opportunity to lead an independent research project. It is aimed at highly qualified postdoc-level researchers in the early stages of their scientific career and provides a funding period of 36 months. Funding covers the principal investigator's salary at the current senior postdoc rate plus project-specific costs from EUR 45,000 as a flat rate, up to EUR 75,000 if justifiable. Requirements include a completed doctoral degree awarded no more than 5 years before application, a mentor, and a project at an Austrian research institution. Submissions are rolling through the elane portal, and the Scientific Board decides at five approval meetings per year, with priority given to women in cases of equal merit.",
