          "description": "The FWF launched the ASTRA Awards in July 2024 as a career funding programme giving advanced postdocs in Austria the opportunity to make the leap to the top of their research field. It is aimed at successful, internationally visible researchers from all disciplines, including arts-based research, who already have experience of independent research work at R3 level. Project-specific funding runs from EUR 500,000 up to a maximum of EUR 1 million over five years, with an additional EUR 200,000 tenure package for female principal investigators who are granted a permanent position within the first three years of the project. The Scientific Board decides on the recommendation of an international jury following international peer review and a hearing; half of the awards go to women and projects presented at the hearing that miss out are funded as three-year Principal Investigator Projects of up to EUR 450,000 as Merit Awards. The programme is applied for online through the elane portal during a published annual window.",
