      "description": "Scholarship of the Heinrich Böll Foundation for international students who have completed their first degree abroad and intend to start a Master's degree in Germany, and for international PhD candidates who completed their graduate degree abroad. Applications are accepted in two rounds a year. Master's students funded by the Federal Foreign Office receive a base scholarship of EUR 992 per month plus a health insurance allowance of up to EUR 100 and optional components; PhD candidates funded by the Federal Foreign Office receive EUR 1,500 per month plus health insurance of up to EUR 200 per month. The funds come from the Federal Ministry of Research, Technology and Space (BMFTR) and the Federal Foreign Office (AA).",
      "region": "Europe",
      "deadline": "Two rounds per year. Spring 2027: 15 January 2027 until 1 March 2027 (online portal opens 15 January 2027 and closes 1 March 2027). Fall 2027: 15 July 2027 until 1 September 2027.",
