      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "15 January 2027 to 1 March 2027, and 15 July 2027 to 1 September 2027",
      "eligibility_summary": "International students who have completed their first degree abroad can apply before starting a Master's programme in Germany. International PhD students who completed their graduate degree abroad can apply for a PhD in Germany. Priority is given to applicants from DAC countries who have not yet taken up residence in Germany at the time of their application.",
      "eligibility": [
        "First degree completed abroad (Bildungsauslaender) before starting a Master's programme in Germany",
        "Graduate degree completed abroad before starting a PhD in Germany",
        "Priority for applicants from DAC countries who have not yet taken up residence in Germany at the time of application",
        "AA-funded track requires a nationality from outside the EU; BMFTR track is aimed at German nationals, Bildungsauslaender educated in Germany and EU nationals"
