      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": null,
      "description": "Study in Finland, the official guide operated by the Finnish National Agency for Education, states that all scholarships and tuition fee waivers in Finland are awarded by individual universities and that no governmental scholarship programmes exist. Where a university offers a scholarship it is competitive and normally covers tuition fees only, partially or in full; the student must independently cover living costs. Applications are made through the university's own admissions process, either together with the admission application or after studies have started. Applicants are directed to Studyinfo.fi and to the universities' own websites for the actual schemes and deadlines.",
