          "description": "Erasmus Mundus Joint Masters are prestigious, integrated international master's programmes at master level, designed and delivered by an international partnership of higher education institutions involving at least three institutions from at least three different countries, of which at least two are EU Member States or Programme-associated third countries. The European Commission funds both the programmes and competitive scholarships to the best students worldwide: the EU scholarship for individuals is EUR 1,400 per month for a maximum of 24 months, and scholarships cover participation costs while contributing to travel, visa costs and a living allowance. Students apply directly to the institution running their chosen programme, and in most cases submit applications between October and January for courses starting the following academic year. The award is a joint degree (recommended) or multiple degrees, for editions lasting 1 to 2 academic years (60, 90 or 120 ECTS credits).",
