      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The University of Amsterdam runs several scholarship programmes for talented and motivated international students, published from one official Fees and funding hub. The flagship is the Amsterdam Merit Scholarship for outstanding students from outside the EU/EEA planning a Master's programme at the UvA. Each faculty also runs its own scholarships for international Master's students, covering Economics and Business, Humanities, Law, Science and Social and Behavioural Sciences, and a separate set of Bachelor's scholarships exists. The Amsterdam Merit Scholarship equals the tuition fee but the UvA states it cannot be used as a partial tuition waiver, so the recipient still pays the full tuition, payable in monthly instalments. Amounts are set annually and are published by each faculty.",
      "region": "Europe",
      "deadline": "The umbrella hub page publishes no single deadline. Deadlines are set per scheme and per faculty: faculty scholarship pages for the Amsterdam Merit Scholarship give an application deadline of 15 January, with results announced at the end of April, while some faculties run a later round with a 2 February deadline. Amounts are determined each year and published in late autumn.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "Annual. The main Amsterdam Merit Scholarship round opens at the beginning of October with a 15 January deadline and results at the end of April; individual faculties publish their own rounds, amounts and deadlines, and amounts are published in late autumn.",
      "eligibility_summary": "The umbrella covers several schemes, so eligibility is scheme-specific. The Amsterdam Merit Scholarship requires outstanding academic results and is open to students from outside the EU/EEA who plan a Master's at the UvA. Individual faculty schemes add their own criteria, and the UvA directs applicants to the relevant faculty page for details.",
      "eligibility": [
        "For the Amsterdam Merit Scholarship: hold a non-EU/EEA nationality and plan to do a Master's programme at the University of Amsterdam",
        "Be an outstanding student with excellent study results; the UvA states the programme is highly selective and that only applicants with excellent study results and motivation might be eligible",
        "Meet the admission requirements of the chosen UvA degree programme",
        "Satisfy the additional criteria set by the specific faculty scheme, which differ per faculty"
