          "description": "A New Zealand Ministry of Education scholarship, administered by the Pacific Education Foundation, that reduces financial barriers to tertiary study and vocational training for Pacific people. It is part of the reconciliation response to the 2021 apology for the Dawn Raids. Awards cover full-time course costs including tuition fees and help with living costs, can be made for one, two or three years, and are tiered by level: NZD 12,500 each year at NZQA levels 4-7 and for undergraduate study, and NZD 17,500 each year for postgraduate study. Applicants must be full-time, New Zealand citizens or permanent residents who have lived in New Zealand for three years, of indigenous Pacific cultural heritage, and meet NCEA 3 and age requirements. The 2027 round is closed, with outcomes notified by 18 March 2027.",
