      "duration": "Four years of full-time undergraduate study",
      "description": "The Lester B. Pearson International Scholarship is the University of Toronto's most prestigious award for international students and one of the largest scholarship programmes for international students in Canada. It covers tuition, books, incidental fees and full residence support for four years and is tenable only at the University of Toronto for first-entry undergraduate programmes. Around 37 scholars are named each year from a pool representing 188 countries, with more than CAD 12 million of funding in 2024. Candidates must be nominated by their secondary school, which can nominate only one student per year, and must also apply for admission to the University of Toronto through the Ontario Universities' Application Centre. The scholarship is restricted to the applicant's top-choice programme at the time scholarship decisions are made.",
      "deadline": "\"The deadline to complete the Pearson International Scholarship application and submit all required documentation is November 6, 2026.\" Earlier steps: school nomination deadline October 9, 2026 and student OUAC admission application deadline October 16, 2026.",
