          "description": "ARES offers scholarships for study in Belgium through its international training programme, aimed at strengthening the capacities of young professionals from its partner countries. Under the 2027-2028 call, ARES offered one bachelor of specialisation, eight specialised master's degrees and one continuing-education certificate in Fédération Wallonie-Bruxelles institutions, each of up to 12 months for degrees and 6 months for short courses. Applicants must be permanent residents working in one of ARES's 32 partner countries, hold a higher education diploma and have at least two years of relevant professional experience. Applications are submitted free of charge through the GIRAF platform, closing on 18 September 2026 at 12h Belgian time for that cycle. The scholarship covers travel, a subsistence allowance, visa costs, registration fees, insurance and, for short courses, indirect mission costs.",
