      "selection_notes": "Around ten excellence scholarships are awarded each year. The SASME checks completeness, the Admissions Office (SII) decides formal eligibility, the faculty decides admission to the chosen master's, and finally the Selection Board for the Master's Scholarship selects the scholarship holders in March, with applicants notified in early April. Decisions may not be appealed.",
      "best_fit": "Graduates of a foreign university with outstanding academic results seeking a place in a UNIL master's programme in a faculty other than Medicine, and able to supplement the CHF 1,600 per month with their own resources (about CHF 2,000 per month is needed to live in Lausanne).",
      "funding_amount": 1600,
      "funding_currency": "CHF",
      "funding_period": "per month",
      "notes": "The scholarship application doubles as the application for admission to the chosen master's programme; a separate application to the Admissions Office is not needed. Around ten awards are made each year. Master programmes in Medicine, Sciences and Practices of Education, most of Law, Physical Education and Sport Didactics, Health Sciences, Sustainable Management & Technology, Human Taphonomy and all MAS programmes are excluded. The page warns the amount does not cover the full cost of living in Switzerland.",
      "description": "The University of Lausanne awards around ten excellence scholarships each year, exclusively to students who have graduated from a foreign university and whose academic results are of a very high standard. The scholarship is paid for the minimum statutory period of the Master's programme at CHF 1,600 per month, and recipients are exempt from the standard course registration fees, with only the CHF 80 semester fees remaining payable. UNIL states explicitly that the amount does not constitute full funding, since about CHF 2,000 per month is needed to live in Lausanne. Applications for the 2027/2028 academic year are open until 1 November 2026.",
