          "description": "The Doctoral Student Programme at CERN is an opportunity designed for PhD students to engage in cutting-edge research at CERN in collaboration with their university. CERN offers a monthly net allowance of 3907 Swiss Francs, coverage by its comprehensive health insurance scheme with the contribution automatically deducted from the allowance, a family supplement to the subsistence allowance depending on individual circumstances, travel expenses to Geneva upon joining depending on individual circumstances, and 30 days of paid leave per year plus 2 weeks of annual closure. The contract duration is 6 months, renewable up to 3 years, with the possibility of spreading it over a maximum duration of 4 consecutive years to allow time at the student's university. Applicants must be nationals of a CERN Member or Associate Member State; applications from Pakistani, Lithuanian, Latvian, Cypriot, Croatian and Turkish nationals are currently not considered because the ceiling under Article II.5 of the Associate Membership Agreement has been reached. The candidate must have started or be about to start a doctoral programme, the university must accept that the CERN research contributes to the doctoral thesis, and a good knowledge of English or French is required.",
