      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "program_type": "Paid postdoctoral research employment contract at an international research organisation",
      "duration": "6 to 24 months, with the possibility of extension up to 36 months",
      "deadline": "Vacancies are published as recruitment rounds on the CERN careers site, with the deadline set on each individual vacancy. As of 2026-10-04 the Research Fellowship page lists live vacancies including 'ATS Research Fellowship (Applied Physics and Engineering)', reference REF4103L, and 'Research Fellowship: Theoretical Physics', reference TH-2026-1/Cat1, both 24-month contracts.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "rolling",
      "application_period": "Continuous, round-based recruitment. Each published vacancy carries its own application deadline, and the page warns that vacancies under Experimental Physics, Applied Science and Engineering, and Theoretical Physics each correspond to distinct and separate recruitment processes.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Nationals of a CERN Member State or Associate Member State, with a few exceptions possible annually and with Pakistani, Lithuanian, Latvian, Cypriot, Croatian and Turkish nationals currently excluded because the Article II.5 ceiling has been reached. Applicants must hold a PhD or obtain one within six months, and must not previously have held a CERN fellow or graduate contract. The research-experience cap is 6 years after the PhD for Theoretical and Experimental Physics and 3 years for Applied Sciences and Engineering, extendable to 6 years exceptionally.",
      "eligibility": [
        "National of a CERN Member State or Associate Member State, with a few exceptions possible annually",
        "Applications from Pakistani, Lithuanian, Latvian, Cypriot, Croatian and Turkish nationals are currently not considered because the Article II.5 ceiling has been reached",
        "For Theoretical and Experimental Physics: PhD completed or obtainable within six months, and no more than 6 years of research experience after the PhD by the application deadline",
        "For Applied Sciences and Engineering: PhD completed or obtainable within six months, and no more than 3 years of research experience after the PhD by the application deadline; candidates with up to 6 years may exceptionally be considered",
        "You have never had a CERN fellow or graduate contract before"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Monthly net stipend of CHF 7,004 or CHF 7,425 depending on degree and years of post-graduation experience",
        "Coverage by CERN's comprehensive health insurance scheme for the fellow, their partner and children",
        "Contribution to the CERN Pension Fund",
        "Depending on individual circumstances: installation grant, family, child and infant allowances, and travel expenses to Geneva on joining",
        "30 days of paid leave per year plus 2 weeks during CERN's annual closure"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Monthly net stipend of CHF 7,004 or CHF 7,425",
        "CERN comprehensive health insurance covering the fellow, their partner and children",
        "Contribution to the CERN Pension Fund",
        "Installation grant where applicable",
        "Family, child and infant allowances where applicable",
        "Travel expenses to Geneva on joining where applicable",
        "30 days paid leave per year plus 2 weeks annual closure",
        "On-the-job and formal training including language classes"
      ],
      "required_documents": [
        "Curriculum vitae in English or French",
        "Completed online application submitted before the deadline",
        "Copy of the most relevant university diploma, or a certificate of achievement from the university if the paper diploma is not yet issued",
        "Depending on the advertised position: statement of research interests, recent letters of recommendation, or other relevant documents"
      ],
      "catalogue_url": "https://careers.cern/explore-fields-of-work/",
      "official_updates_url": "https://careers.cern/jobs/",
      "english_requirement": "A good knowledge of English or French is expected, and the CV may be submitted in English or French. The fellowship also offers formal language classes as part of the training package.",
      "requirements": [
        "CV in English or French",
        "Online application completed before the deadline of the chosen vacancy",
        "Copy of the most relevant university diploma or a certificate of achievement",
        "Statement of research interests, letters of recommendation or other documents where the advertised position requires them",
        "Never previously held a CERN fellow or graduate contract"
      ],
      "application_method": [
        "Apply through the CERN careers portal on the advertised vacancy",
        "Submit a CV in English or French with the online application before the deadline",
        "Attach a copy of the relevant university diploma or certificate of achievement",
        "Add a statement of research interests, letters of recommendation or other documents if the position advertises them",
        "Attend an online interview with the hiring manager if invited",
        "Accept the job offer and complete onboarding"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Applications are reviewed by CERN and shortlisted candidates may be invited to an online interview with the hiring manager or managers. The page stresses that vacancies published under Experimental Physics, Applied Science and Engineering, and Theoretical Physics each correspond to distinct and separate recruitment processes, so applying to one does not enter you for the others.",
      "best_fit": "Recent PhD graduates in physics, applied physics or engineering with up to three, or in theoretical and experimental physics up to six, years of post-PhD research experience, who hold the nationality of a CERN Member or Associate Member State and have never held a CERN fellowship or graduate contract.",
      "funding_amount": 7004,
      "funding_currency": "CHF",
      "funding_period": "per month",
      "notes": "The official page publishes two stipend tiers, CHF 7,004 or CHF 7,425 net per month, depending on the candidate's degree and years of post-graduation experience. Because the brief permits only a single number, funding_amount records the lower published tier of 7,004 and the two-tier structure is stated in funding_label and in the notes. This is a paid employment contract with CERN pension and insurance contributions, not a grant, so no tuition component exists or is claimed. CERN's stipends are periodically revised, so the figures should be re-checked against the live page before publication.",
      "description": "The CERN Research Fellowship Programme, part of CERN's broader Graduate Programme, is an opportunity for recent PhD graduates in physics and engineering to conduct advanced research in science, technology, engineering and mathematics at CERN. It pays a monthly net stipend of either CHF 7,004 or CHF 7,425 depending on the degree and years of post-graduation experience, together with CERN health insurance for the fellow, their partner and children, a contribution to the CERN Pension Fund, and depending on individual circumstances an installation grant, family, child and infant allowances and travel to Geneva on joining. Fellows receive 30 days of paid leave per year plus two weeks of CERN's annual closure, and on-the-job and formal training including language classes. Contracts run 6 to 24 months with the possibility of extension up to 36 months. Applicants must be nationals of a CERN Member or Associate Member State, must hold a PhD or obtain one within six months, must respect a research-experience cap of six years for Theoretical and Experimental Physics or three years for Applied Sciences and Engineering, and must never previously have held a CERN fellow or graduate contract.",
