          "description": "The CERN Research Fellowship Programme, part of CERN's broader Graduate Programme, is an exceptional opportunity for recent PhD graduates in physics and engineering to dive into advanced research in science, technology, engineering and mathematics at CERN. CERN offers a monthly net stipend of either 7004 or 7425 Swiss Francs depending on the candidate's degree and years of post-graduation experience, coverage by its comprehensive health insurance scheme for the fellow, their partner and children, a contribution to the CERN Pension Fund, and depending on individual circumstances an installation grant, family, child and infant allowances and travel expenses to Geneva on joining. Fellows also receive 30 days of paid leave per year plus 2 weeks during CERN's annual closure, and on-the-job and formal training including language classes. The contract duration is 6 to 24 months with the possibility to extend up to 36 months. Applicants must be nationals of a CERN Member or Associate Member State, must hold a PhD or obtain one within six months, must have no more than 6 years of research experience for Theoretical and Experimental Physics or no more than 3 years for Applied Sciences and Engineering by the application deadline, and must never have had a CERN fellow or graduate contract before.",
