          "description": "The ANU University Research Scholarship supports high-achieving higher degree by research students whose research aligns with the strategic directions of the Australian National University. It is awarded through ANU's two annual central scholarship rounds, and no separate application is required because all eligible candidates are considered on the basis of their admission application. Recipients receive a fortnightly stipend of $40,475 per annum (2027 full-time base rate) for 3.5 years of a PhD or 1.5 years of an MPhil, together with travel and removal allowances, a thesis allowance, a dependant child allowance for international students, and paid medical, maternity and parental leave. Each College ranks all eligible H1 or equivalent applicants on academic record, research potential, supervisor support, referee reports and English language competency.",
