      "description": "The University of Sydney International Stipend Scholarship (USYDIS) is a competitively awarded stipend scholarship for international students commencing or already enrolled in a higher degree by research at the University of Sydney. It pays a stipend of $44,293 per annum at the 2027 rate, indexed annually, plus relocation and thesis allowances. Holders are automatically awarded the companion University of Sydney Tuition Fee Scholarship, which covers 100% of tuition fees for up to 14 research periods together with Overseas Student Health Cover, making the combined package a full funding package for international research students. Preference may be given to applicants intending to enrol in, or already enrolled in, a PhD, and to applicants who have not previously completed an HDR course or held an equivalent scholarship at the same level.",
      "deadline": "Submission deadlines for the international RTP/USYDIS rounds are published in the University application and award timeline: 11 September 2026 for Research Period 1 and 2, 2027 (outcomes issued from 10 November 2026, finalised 17 December 2026); 18 December 2026 for Research Period 3 and 4, 2027; and 10 September 2027 for Research Period 1 and 2, 2028. All required admission documentation must be submitted through Sydney Courses and the scholarship application form submitted by the deadline.",
