      "description": "The Deakin Vice-Chancellor's International Scholarship recognises international students with consistently high academic performance and the potential to make a leading contribution to Deakin and the communities it serves. The award covers 100% or 50% of tuition fees depending on the scholarship outcome, for the normal duration of the program, and requires participation in the Vice-Chancellor's Professional Excellence Program. Applicants must be new international students enrolling in a Deakin coursework degree with at least an 85% average or equivalent in previous studies, and must submit a 300-word personal statement, two references and their academic transcripts. Scholarships are assessed on a rolling basis in the lead-up to each trimester, and the award is not available to the Doctor of Medicine (H911) program.",
