          "description": "The Deakin Vice-Chancellor's International Scholarship recognises international students with consistently high academic performance and the potential to make a leading contribution to Deakin and the communities it serves. It covers 100% or 50% of tuition fees, depending on the scholarship outcome, for the normal duration of the program. Participation in the Vice-Chancellor's Professional Excellence Program is a requirement of the award, and recipients get priority access to on-campus accommodation at their own cost. Applicants must be new international students entering a Deakin coursework degree with at least an 85% average or equivalent in previous studies, submit a 300-word personal statement and two references, and have their application emailed to Deakin International Admissions at least one month before the program starts. The award is not available to the Doctor of Medicine (H911) program and does not cover study beyond the standard program duration.",
