      "program_type": "Academic merit - high-achieving commencing international students",
      "description": "The UTS Vice-Chancellor's International Undergraduate Scholarship supports high-achieving commencing international students enrolling in an undergraduate program at UTS in Sydney. The value is UTS tuition fees for the standard duration of the course. Applicants must remain an international student, meet UTS admission criteria for their chosen undergraduate program by the scholarship closing date, commence full-time on-campus study in Sydney, have completed an Australian Year 12 or comparable high school qualification within three years before commencing at UTS and be admitted on that basis, and hold an overall average of 85% where the pass mark is 50%. The scholarship is awarded to the highest ranked applicant on academic merit in the admission qualification combined with their responses in the UTS online scholarship application. For the Autumn session 2027 (February 2027 commencement) the application period runs from Thursday 1 October 2026 to Monday 2 November 2026 at 11.55pm AEST.",
