            "Completed UTS online Scholarships Application form, submitted before 2 November 2026 11.55pm AEST",
            "UTS admission offer or application for the selected undergraduate program",
            "Year 12 or equivalent high school qualification transcript, showing the completion date",
            "Evidence that admission is based on that high school qualification",
            "English language evidence required by the chosen program",
            "Confirmation that you hold no other UTS International Grant or Scholarship"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "Exact deadline with a time",
              "message": "\"Thursday 01 October 2026 to Monday 02 November 2026 11.55pm AEST\". The cutoff is 11.55pm Sydney time on 2 November 2026 - do not treat it as end of day."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Two separate requirements",
              "message": "You must both meet UTS admission criteria for your program by the closing date and submit the scholarship application form. UTS states \"All applicants must apply using the UTS online Scholarships Application form to be eligible\"."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Recent secondary studies only",
              "message": "You must have completed Year 12 or comparable studies \"within three (3) years prior to commencing at UTS\". Gap-year applicants beyond three years are ineligible."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Tuition only",
              "message": "Value is \"UTS Tuition Fees\" for the standard duration of the course. UTS confirms it is a full tuition scholarship, but no living-cost component is listed."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "On-campus only",
              "message": "\"Commence full-time studies and on campus (Sydney)\" and you must not be studying \"a UTS online degree or distance mode degree\". Note that on-campus status still permits online (remote) learning within a degree that is not itself an online or distance mode degree."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "No stacking with other UTS awards",
              "message": "You must not be \"A recipient of other UTS International Grants or Scholarships, unless approved by exception and outlined in the Conditions of Award\"."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Ranked, not first-come",
              "message": "The award goes to \"the highest ranked applicant\" on academic merit plus scholarship application responses, so submitting early does not itself improve the ranking."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Choose an on-campus Sydney undergraduate degree that admits on the basis of your Year 12 or equivalent qualification",
            "Confirm your secondary qualification was completed within three years before your intended UTS commencement",
            "Convert your result to the UTS scale and confirm an overall average of at least 85% where the pass mark is 50%",
            "Meet the program's English language and other admission requirements",
            "Prepare your UTS course application so admission criteria are satisfied by 2 November 2026",
            "Complete the UTS online Scholarships Application form and answer its questions carefully, since they feed the ranking",
            "Submit the scholarship form before 11.55pm AEST on Monday 2 November 2026",
            "Await the outcome; UTS advises contacting Future Learner Recruitment and Admissions on +61 2 9514 1531 or reps@uts.edu.au with any questions",
            "On award, accept the Conditions of Award and confirm you are not enrolled in an online or distance mode degree"
          ]
