      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The DAAD Research Grants in Germany fund a research project at a state or state-recognised university or non-university research institute in Germany, carried out with a German scientific supervisor. Doctoral candidates may be funded for 2 to 12 months and early postdocs for 2 to 6 months; the grant cannot be extended and cannot be split within the funding period. The current DAAD announcement sets a monthly scholarship payment of EUR 1,400 plus insurance cover, a travel allowance, and for stays over six months a research allowance of EUR 460, a monthly rent subsidy and a monthly family allowance. Applications are submitted online through the DAAD Portal and are open annually, with deadlines updated in the second quarter of each year; on 2026-10-04 the DAAD stated that applications for the 2027 funding period were closed.",
      "funding_amount": 1400,
      "funding_currency": "EUR",
      "funding_period": "per month",
      "deadline": "\"Application deadlines are updated annually in the second quarter. In most cases, they are in the same period as the previous year.\" The DAAD page for the 2027 funding period showed \"Currently you cannot apply for this programme\" on 2026-10-04; the exact calendar date was not rendered on the page read.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "Annual cycle. The DAAD portal opens at least six weeks before the deadline and closes at 24:00 CET or CEST on the last application day. For the 2027 funding round the applications were closed on the 2026-10-04 verification date.",
      "duration": "2 to 12 months for doctoral candidates; 2 to 6 months for postdocs",
      "program_type": "Research stay grant for doctoral candidates and early postdocs",
      "eligibility_summary": "Doctoral candidates whose doctorate started no more than 3 years before the application deadline, or postdocs who completed their doctorate no more than 4 years before the deadline, who are doing their doctorate outside Germany, with a German host institution and supervisor.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Doctoral students: the start of the doctorate should not be more than 3 years ago at the application deadline",
        "Postdocs: the doctorate should not have been completed more than 4 years before the application deadline",
