          "description": "The DAAD research grant offers doctoral candidates and early postdocs the opportunity to realise a research project at a state or state-recognised university or a non-university research institute in Germany, in agreement with a German scientific supervisor. Doctoral candidates can be funded for 2 to 12 months and postdocs for 2 to 6 months; the funding cannot be extended and cannot be split within the funding period. Value is a monthly scholarship payment of EUR 1,400 plus payments towards health, accident and personal liability insurance, a travel allowance, and for stays over six months a research allowance of EUR 460, a monthly rent subsidy and a monthly allowance for accompanying family members. German language support and TestDaF or DSH fee reimbursement are also limited to stays over six months. Eligibility requires that the doctorate started no more than 3 years before the deadline (or that a postdoc doctorate was completed no more than 4 years before it), that the doctorate is being done outside Germany, and that the applicant has not been resident in Germany for more than 15 months at the deadline. An independent selection committee of specialist scientists assesses academic qualification, the quality of the research project and the applicant's potential, also giving due consideration to equal opportunities. Applications are submitted online through the DAAD Portal, with deadlines updated annually in the second quarter.",
