      "description": "The DAAD University Summer Courses programme funds four-week German language, cultural studies and technical language courses at German universities and affiliated language schools for students and graduates from eligible countries. The scholarship covers the cost of the language course, provides accommodation in a single room through the course provider for the duration of the course, pays a one-time allowance of EUR 475, a country-specific travel allowance, and health, accident and personal liability insurance. Applications are accepted each year from 1 September to 30 October at 23:59 Central European Time, and courses run between June and September.",
      "funding_amount": 475,
      "funding_currency": "EUR",
      "notes": "The courses run for four weeks between June and September, and the grants are not extendable. The DAAD transfers the one-time allowance and any travel allowance to the course provider, who disburses it in cash to scholarship holders on site, so those amounts are not paid into a bank account abroad. Accepted language certificates are onSET-Deutsch, TestDaF, Goethe Institut Zertifikat, DSD, DSH, telc Deutsch and OSD-Zertifikat; for subject-specific language courses the Abitur is also accepted as proof of German proficiency.",
      "deadline": "\"30 October of each year, 23:59 (Central European Time). Applications are possible from 01 September each year\"",
