          },
          "description": "The aim of the DAAD University Summer Courses programme is to deepen knowledge of the German language, both general and technical, and to augment knowledge of regional studies. It funds students and graduates from eligible countries to attend four-week language, cultural studies and technical language courses at state or state-recognised German universities and affiliated language schools, taught exclusively in German and attended in person between June and September. The scholarship covers the cost of the language course, provides single-room accommodation through the course provider for the duration of the course, pays a one-time allowance of EUR 475, a country-specific travel allowance, and health, accident and personal liability insurance. Applicants must be enrolled at a university in a programme country other than Germany both at application and throughout the scholarship, be at least 18 at the start of the course, and prove German proficiency with a certificate no older than one year. Applications run from 1 September to 30 October each year, closing at 23:59 CET, and a selection committee reviews previous academic achievements and the letter of motivation.",
