          },
          "description": "The DAAD Helmut-Schmidt-Programme, also known as Public Policy and Good Governance, is designed to academically qualify future leaders in social and political science, law, economics, public policy and administration according to the principles of Good Governance. Funded by the Federal Foreign Office, it gives very well qualified graduates with a first university degree from developing or emerging countries the chance to obtain a master's degree in disciplines of special relevance for the social, political and economic development of their home country or region, and prepares them for future leadership positions in the Global South. Scholarships are granted for selected English-taught master's courses at seven participating German higher education institutions: Social Protection at Hochschule Bonn-Rhein-Sieg; Development and Governance at the University of Duisburg-Essen; Public Policy at the Erfurt School of Public Policy; Peace and Conflict Studies at the University of Magdeburg; Management in Nonprofit Organisations at Osnabrueck University of Applied Sciences; Development Studies and Governance and Public Policy at the University of Passau. Both young graduates and mid-career professionals may apply. Applications are submitted directly to the universities, not to the DAAD, during the 1 June to 31 July window. Scholarship holders study in small groups with special tutoring, take part in networking events and tailor-made workshops, and attend a German language course in Germany for up to six months before the master's studies.",
