      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "Japanese Government (MEXT) Scholarship for students from abroad who want to study as undergraduate students at Japanese national universities, selected through the recommendation of a Japanese embassy or consulate general. Applicants first pass a First Screening (documents, written academic examinations and interview) at the diplomatic mission in their country, are recommended to MEXT, and then pass MEXT's Second Screening. The scholarship pays a monthly allowance of JPY 117,000, waives entrance examination, matriculation and tuition fees, and provides an economy-class airline ticket to Japan and, on return, back to the grantee's home country. The scholarship period is five years from April 2027 to March 2032 including one year of preparatory Japanese language education, or seven years for medicine, dentistry, veterinary medicine and six-year pharmacy courses.",
      "region": "Asia",
      "duration": "Five years from April 2027 to March 2032 including one year of preparatory Japanese language education; seven years for medicine, dentistry, veterinary medicine or a six-year pharmacy course; four years for grantees placed directly at a university",
      "deadline": "No single central date: applicants must submit to the Japanese diplomatic mission in the country of their nationality by the deadline that mission sets, and that date is not published by MEXT. MEXT states applicants are informed of the final selection result by their diplomatic mission after February 2027, and that grantees must in principle arrive in Japan between 1 April 2027 and 7 April 2027.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "Annually; the 2027 cycle guidelines were published by MEXT in April 2026 and applications were made to Japanese diplomatic missions during the first half of the year",
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must hold the nationality of a country that has diplomatic relations with Japan and must not hold Japanese nationality at the time of application. They must satisfy one of the listed academic-background conditions (normally 12 years of schooling outside Japan, completed by March 2027), must be willing to learn Japanese and to study in Japanese in principle, and must in principle be within MEXT's eligible age limit. Grantees must be able to arrive in Japan between 1 April 2027 and 7 April 2027.",
      "eligibility": [
