      "selection_notes": "The Japanese diplomatic mission conducts the First Screening through examination of submitted documents, written academic examinations and interviews; MEXT then conducts the Second Screening of the recommended applicants and selects candidates from each course. Written examination subjects depend on the chosen field: Social Sciences and Humanities applicants take Japanese, English and Mathematics; Natural Sciences applicants take Japanese, English, Mathematics and either Chemistry or Physics. Reasons for screening results are not disclosed and objections to the decision on university placement are not accepted.",
