      "description": "Japanese Government (MEXT) Scholarship for Japanese Studies Students, an embassy-recommendation programme for students from abroad who are already enrolled at a university outside Japan, major in Japanese language or Japanese culture, and come to Japan for a one-year non-degree training course at a Japanese university. The scholarship pays JPY 117,000 per month after arrival, does not collect the university's entrance fee, tuition or entrance examination fee, and provides an economy-class airline ticket to Japan and, on completing the course, back to the grantee's home country. The scholarship period runs from October 2026, or from the month the training course starts, for up to one year, and cannot be extended.",
      "region": "Asia",
      "duration": "Up to one year from October 2026, or from the month the training course starts, covering the period needed to complete that university's training course; extension of the scholarship period is not permitted",
