      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "varies",
      "application_period": "School-by-school, twice a year, matching the Japanese enrolment cycles: spring enrolment (April) and autumn enrolment (September or October). JASSO publishes the eligible school and department lists for each cycle; for 2026 the autumn lists were published in June 2026 and the spring lists in January 2026.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Privately-financed international students planning to enrol as full-time students in Japan using pre-arrival admission, either on the graduate level reservation, the EJU exam reservation, or the English courses reservation, and who face financial difficulties. Research students, trainees, non-degree students, advanced course students, special course students, auditing students and special students are excluded from the 'full-time student' definition for this programme.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Privately-financed international student (not a Japanese Government MEXT Scholarship holder)",
