            "administrator": "Education New Zealand | Manapou ki te Ao"
          },
          "description": "The Manaaki New Zealand Scholarships are offered by the New Zealand Government to eligible citizens from developing countries to study at a New Zealand or Pacific education institution. The tertiary strand is a full scholarship for eligible international students to study full-time, at one of eight universities or three institutes of technology in New Zealand or one of two Pacific universities. Separate strands cover vocational skills training, thematic short-term cohort training and English language training for officials. Applications are made online through the Manaaki applicant portal and require an academic transcript including the grading scale; shortlisted applicants must supply verified English translations.",
