      "description": "The Stipendium Hungaricum is a Hungarian Government scholarship programme, implemented by Tempus Public Foundation, to promote the internationalisation of Hungarian higher education and to attract international students. Applicants must be nominated by the responsible Sending Partner in their own country or region and apply through the Tempus Public Foundation online system, which lists 30 Hungarian universities and colleges and more than 900 study programmes, with a maximum of two programme choices. Holders have their tuition fees covered and receive a monthly stipend plus an accommodation contribution, and must reside in Hungary during the study period. The programme runs a single annual application round, and for 2026/2027 the deadline was 15 January 2026, 2 p.m. CET.",
