          "description": "The Hungarian Diaspora Scholarship Programme was established by Government Decree 203/2020 and is implemented by Tempus Public Foundation under regulations approved by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Hungary on 29 August 2026. It funds people with Hungarian roots living in the diaspora, who must hold citizenship entitling them to participate and must live in the diaspora region with a foreign address of residence, on the recommendation of a Hungarian diplomatic mission or a Hungarian diaspora organisation. For 2026/2027, 33 Hungarian higher education institutions offered nearly 1300 study programmes, around 1000 of them full-time, mostly in English and Hungarian. The complete application was due by 2 February 2026 at 14:00 CET, with selection running through five points and results notified in June 2026.",
