      "description": "The Ontario Graduate Scholarship program encourages excellence in graduate studies at publicly-assisted universities in Ontario and has provided merit-based scholarships to Ontario's best graduate students in all disciplines since 1975. At the University of Toronto the program is jointly funded by the Province of Ontario and the University of Toronto, and the Province allocates OGS awards to universities specifying how many each may offer annually. The OGS is worth $5,000 per session at U of T, and the awarding graduate unit contributes one-third of the total award cost. Deadlines and application dates are set by each graduate unit, with results in mid-July.",
