            "Identify your proposed U of T graduate unit first - OGS is not transferable between units or universities, and you must apply separately to each unit and each Ontario institution",
            "Get the unit's own deadline and apply well before it; SGS states the institutional deadline is typically earlier than any central date",
            "Secure a valid study permit effective by the unit's OGS international deadline if applying as an international student",
            "Prepare unofficial student-issued transcripts (ACORN screenshots are accepted) from every post-secondary institution you have attended",
            "Draft a plan of study within the strict 2-page limit (1 page plan, 1 page references)",
            "Line up two academic referees who can submit online, and brief them on the Academic Assessment Report criteria"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Missing the graduate unit's internal deadline, which SGS says is set by the unit and is often earlier than any central date",
            "A study permit that is not effective by the unit's OGS international application deadline for international applicants",
            "Failing the A- minimum, unless the unit grants a discretionary exception for highly meritorious applicants",
            "A plan of study exceeding the 2-page maximum",
            "Holding an OGS concurrently with SSHRC, NSERC, CIHR, QEII-GSST or another OGS in the same session",
            "An OSAP restriction or loan default discovered after the award offer",
            "Taking full-time paid employment, which typically makes a student ineligible at U of T"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "Tuition fees: the OGS is a cash award and does not waive tuition; instalments posted to the student account go towards tuition, with any remainder refunded",
            "Living costs well beyond $5,000 per session",
            "Any shortfall if the graduate unit contribution differs, since units may impose additional conditions"
          ],
          "document_audit": [
            "Completed SGS centralized online OGS application form",
            "Transcripts from all post-secondary institutions (unofficial/student-issued accepted)",
            "Record of previous awards, publications, conference and research experience",
            "Plan of study, maximum 2 pages including references",
            "Two academic referees confirmed to submit online"
          ],
          "alerts": [
            {
              "trigger": "No single OGS deadline",
              "message": "SGS states the student deadline is 'Date set by graduate unit'. Use the SGS Student deadlines spreadsheet and your unit's own date, not an aggregator's date."
            },
