              "trigger": "Repayment obligation",
              "message": "Recipients who withdraw, go part-time, finish degree requirements early or fail to complete the session must repay the funds for the incomplete session."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Concurrent award ban",
              "message": "You cannot hold an OGS in the same session or award year as an SSHRC, NSERC, CIHR, QEII-GSST or other OGS award."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "OSAP good standing",
              "message": "You must be in good standing with OSAP. An OSAP restriction does not bar you from applying but must be cleared within 30 days of notification to hold the award."
            },
            {
              "trigger": "Inclusive Excellence automatic consideration",
              "message": "If you are Black and/or Indigenous to Canada, identifying as such on the OGS application puts you into the SGS Inclusive Excellence Graduate Scholarship competition automatically, with offers issued by July 31."
            }
          ],
          "submission_workflow": [
            "Choose your proposed graduate unit and check its OGS internal deadline and programme eligibility",
            "If international, confirm your study permit is valid and effective by the unit's OGS international deadline",
            "Assemble transcripts, the 2-page plan of study and referee details",
            "Complete the SGS centralized online OGS application and submit it to the unit",
            "Confirm your referees have received and submitted their online assessments",
            "If offered, accept by completing the SGS Award Payment Activation form (PAF) through the SGS Forms Tool",
            "Set up direct deposit on ACORN so instalments arrive on time"
