    {
      "name": "Merit Scholarship Program for Foreign Students (PBEEE) - Fonds de recherche du Quebec",
      "legacy_titles": [
        "Quebec Merit Scholarship Program for Foreign Students (PBEEE)"
      ],
      "country": "Canada",
      "region": "Quebec",
      "degree_levels": "Master's, PhD, Postdoctoral",
      "funding_type": "Fully Funded",
      "official_source": "Fonds de recherche du Quebec (FRQ) - secteur Nature et technologies, commissioned by the Ministere de l'Enseignement superieur du Quebec",
      "official_source_url": "https://frq.gouv.qc.ca/en/program/merit-scholarship-program-for-foreign-students-pbeee-2026-2027-2",
      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "deadline": "Deadline (application): December 2nd, 2025 at 16:00 (EST) for the 2026-2027 competition. University and CCTT Network preselection of applications to FRQ: October 23, 2025, 4 p.m. Candidates preselected by the China Scholarship Council: before March 31, 2026. The 2026-2027 rules are marked out of competition and no next-cycle date was published as at 2026-10-04.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": "CAD",
      "notes": "Funding period: per year for master's and doctoral components; per month for the short-term component",
      "duration": "Master's: maximum 6 instalments (6 semesters). Doctoral: maximum 12 sessions (12 instalments), with $25,000 for the first 9 sessions and $12,000 for the last 3 if an extension is requested. Postdoctoral: maximum 12 months, not renewable. Short-term research or professional development: 4 months, not renewable.",
      "coverage": [
        "Master's research scholarship (VM): $20,000 per year, maximum $40,000 over 6 instalments",
        "Doctoral research scholarship (V1, 1B, 1C, 1I, 1IS, 1W): $25,000 per year for the first 9 sessions, $12,000 for the last 3 sessions if an extension is requested, maximum $87,000 over 12 sessions",
        "Postdoctoral scholarship (V2, 2B, 2C, 2I): $35,000, 3 instalments (one year) totalling $35,000",
        "Short-term research or professional development scholarship (V3, 3B, 3C, 3I, 3IS, 3W): $3,000 per month, maximum 4 instalments (4 months) totalling $12,000",
        "In addition to the scholarship, MES offers all recipients an exemption from paying the higher tuition fees required for foreign students and the medical insurance coverage offered by the RAMQ"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Exemption from the higher tuition fees charged to foreign students in Quebec",
        "Exemption from RAMQ medical insurance coverage costs",
        "Access to all-countries components and to five country-specific components (Quebec-Brazil, Quebec-China, Quebec-India, Quebec-Israel, Quebec-Wallonia) arising from agreements with foreign governments"
      ],
      "eligibility_summary": "These scholarships are intended for foreign students or researchers from all research sectors (health, humanities and social sciences, arts and letters, natural sciences, and engineering) preselected by a Quebec university or the CCTT network, or by the China Scholarship Council for the Quebec-China component, who wish to begin or continue studies or research activities in Quebec. The competition is open to all candidates who are not Canadian citizens or permanent residents of Canada and who have not applied for permanent residence under Canadian immigration laws. Candidates must be preselected to take part, and must not have already received a Merit Scholarship for Foreign Students from the MES.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Not a Canadian citizen or permanent resident of Canada, and not having applied for permanent residence under Canadian immigration laws",
        "Preselected by a Quebec university or the CCTT network as of October 23, 2025 (or by the China Scholarship Council as of March 31, 2026 for the Quebec-China component)",
        "Master's research component: the master's programme must lead to the writing of a thesis - essays, research reports, dissertations and papers are not accepted, and professional master's programmes are not eligible; candidates must have been enrolled for up to three full-time semesters (1 year) or less before May 1, 2026",
        "Doctoral research component: eligible for the first nine semesters of doctoral study, with all prior doctoral semesters subtracted",
        "Postdoctoral component: PhD obtained no more than two years before the competition deadline, or doctoral dissertation submitted by January 15, 2026; research must be in an institution other than the one that granted the doctorate, and prior doctoral supervisors may not act as postdoctoral supervisor",
        "Short-term component: technical and university students (option A) or researchers who completed a doctorate no more than five years before the deadline (option B); research must be in an institution other than the one at which the student was enrolled when they applied",
        "Must not have already received a Merit Scholarship for Foreign Students from the MES",
        "Quebec-Wallonia candidates must have previously studied in a French-language university-level institution in Belgium",
        "Recipients must be physically present in Quebec for the entire funding period and attend the institution at which they were preselected; joint (cotutelle) degree programmes are not eligible"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Be preselected by a Quebec university, the CCTT network or the China Scholarship Council before the FRQ deadline",
        "Create an account in the FRQnet system and complete the electronic form FRQ contacts you for",
        "Attach all required documents, which cannot be updated after the application deadline",
        "Submit electronically by the competition deadline; an application submitted after the deadline is deemed inadmissible",
        "Notifies FRQ of acceptance or refusal of a funding offer no later than 30 days after notification via the FRQnet portal"
      ],
      "application_method": [
        "Institutions submit nominations of preselected candidates through the FRQnet system, transmitted electronically by 4 p.m. on the institution's deadline",
        "Preselected candidates create an FRQnet account, are contacted by FRQ and complete an electronic form with the required documents attached",
        "For the postdoctoral and short-term components, the supervisor submits a letter of acceptance directly through the FRQnet portal"
      ],
      "program_type": "Provincial research scholarship administered by the Fonds de recherche du Quebec on behalf of the Ministere de l'Enseignement superieur du Quebec",
      "catalogue_url": "https://frq.gouv.qc.ca/en/complete-program-directory/",
      "official_updates_url": "https://frq.gouv.qc.ca/en/open-competitions/",
      "english_requirement": "Not stated as a formal requirement. The official page states that 'Documents submitted in a language other than French or English must be accompanied by a basic translation', so French or English is the working language of the application.",
      "description": "In support of the Quebec government's science policy, the Merit Scholarship for Foreign Students (PBEEE) supports the internationalization of research activities in Quebec higher education institutions, attracts top foreign researchers and students, and creates cultural links for joint research projects. It is managed by the Fonds de recherche du Quebec - secteur Nature et technologies, which was commissioned by the Ministere de l'Enseignement superieur du Quebec, which provides the funding. The programme has four component types - master's research, doctoral research, postdoctoral and short-term research or professional development - available both to students of all countries and, through five bilateral components, to students from Brazil, China, India, Israel and Wallonia. Recipients must be preselected by a Quebec university or the CCTT network, and scholarship payments begin only after FRQ receives a copy of the study permit (doctoral) or work permit (postdoctoral).",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
          "official_source_urls": [
            "https://frq.gouv.qc.ca/en/program/merit-scholarship-program-for-foreign-students-pbeee-2026-2027-2",
