          "description": "The Merit Scholarship for Foreign Students (PBEEE) supports the internationalization of research activities in Quebec higher education institutions, attracts top foreign researchers and students, and creates cultural links for joint research projects. It is managed by the Fonds de recherche du Quebec - secteur Nature et technologies on behalf of the Ministere de l'Enseignement superieur du Quebec, which funds it. Four component types are offered - master's research, doctoral research, postdoctoral, and short-term research or professional development - through all-countries components and five bilateral components. Candidates must be preselected by a Quebec institution, the CCTT network, or the China Scholarship Council, and must not be Canadian citizens or permanent residents.",
