        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Identify your component first - master's research (VM), doctoral (V1), postdoctoral (V2) or short-term (V3) - because the values, durations and documents differ completely",
            "Confirm you are not a Canadian citizen or permanent resident and have not applied for permanent residence",
            "Get preselected by a Quebec university, the CCTT network, or the China Scholarship Council for the Quebec-China component; this is the real gate, since 'only candidates preselected ... can be part of this competition'",
            "Check your institution's preselection deadline, which FRQ publishes as a table and which falls months before the FRQ deadline",
            "For a master's award, confirm your programme leads to a written thesis - professional master's programmes are not eligible",
            "Collect transcripts for every year of all university studies, plus a grading-system letter if any transcript is from outside North America",
            "For doctoral and postdoctoral components, have your supervisor ready to submit a letter of acceptance through FRQnet themselves - you must never submit it on their behalf",
            "Do not rely on updating files after the deadline: 'Files cannot be updated after the application deadline'"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Missing institutional preselection - without it the application cannot enter the competition at all",
            "Applying to a professional master's programme or a non-thesis master's, which is ineligible",
            "Exceeding the component's eligibility window (more than three full-time master's semesters before May 1, 2026; beyond nine doctoral semesters)",
            "Submitting the supervisor's letter of acceptance yourself instead of having the supervisor do it, which 'may be considered as incomplete and, consequently, ineligible'",
            "Choosing the wrong application form - the Fonds will not transfer an application between programmes and will deem it ineligible",
            "Submitting after the deadline, when the application 'will be deemed inadmissible by the Fonds'",
            "Holding a concurrent Canadian or Quebec government agency scholarship, which is prohibited",
            "Not being physically present in Quebec for the funding period, or studying at an institution other than the preselecting one",
            "Applying to a cotutelle joint degree, which is not eligible",
            "Illegible or poor-resolution documents, which are rejected outright"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
