          "description": "The Visegrad Scholarship Program of the International Visegrad Fund supports full-time Master's and post-Master's students and researchers in all disciplines and in any language for up to two semesters at more than 190 accredited higher-education institutions across Central and Eastern Europe. It operates in two directions: nationals of the Czech Republic, Hungary, Poland and Slovakia may study in another Visegrad country or in Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Belarus, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Georgia, Kosovo, Moldova, Montenegro, Northern Macedonia, Serbia or Ukraine, and citizens of those Eastern Partnership and Western Balkan countries may study in the Visegrad states. Applicants must already hold a bachelor's or master's degree, and the country of their citizenship must differ from the host institution's country; previous levels of university studies must have been completed in a third country, and the host institution must be more than 150 km from the applicant's current employer, university or permanent residence. Support is EUR 3,500 per semester for the scholar plus EUR 2,000 per semester for the host institution, and tuition is not covered. Applications are submitted online through My Visegrad. For the 2027 cycle the call opens on 1 January 2027 at 12:00 PM, the final deadline is 15 April 2027 at 12:00 PM, and results are announced on 31 May 2027 at 12:00 PM.",
