          },
          "description": "The Czech Technical University in Prague awards a scholarship to foreign students under Act No. 111/1998 Sb. on Universities, section 91(3)(b), in two tracks. The Master's track is a contribution towards covering the costs of a stay in the Czech Republic of up to CZK 10,000 per month, normally awarded for one to two semesters and extendable on excellent study results up to the standard length of the Master programme. The doctoral track is for foreign doctoral students capable of scientific work who study on an English-language doctoral programme at CTU in Prague; it covers the basic doctoral-study scholarship plus living costs of up to CZK 16,000 per month for six to twelve months, extendable on excellent work outcomes, and requires a publication in an internationally reviewed journal or an international grant application as an outcome of the stay. Both are financed equally from the rectorate's scholarship fund and the relevant faculty's fund. Erasmus, Erasmus Mundus and Exchange students, government scholarship holders and other scholarship holders are not eligible. Applicants first obtain their faculty's agreement and then apply through the faculty International Office to the Department of International Relations at the rectorate, and the vice-rector decides on the recommendation of the commission of vice-deans for international relations. The scholarship covers costs of stay and living costs only; tuition fees are not mentioned.",
