          "description": "The Bioceb Erasmus Mundus Joint Master scholarship funds a two-year place on the European Master in Biological and Chemical Engineering for a Sustainable Bioeconomy, run by Aalto University, AgroParisTech, Universite de Liege, TalTech and Universite de Reims Champagne Ardenne and coordinated by AgroParisTech in France. It covers the participation costs and pays a subsistence allowance of EUR 1,400 per month covering travel, visa, installation and subsistence costs, for the whole programme duration up to 24 months, with a maximum of EUR 33,600 per student. About 12 EMJM scholarships are available per cohort, with a 10% per-nationality cap, plus a smaller number of additional awards reserved for targeted world regions.",
