      "region": "Europe",
      "description": "InLife, the Initiative Sciences aux interfaces du vivant of Sorbonne Université, awards three incoming mobility grants of EUR 7,500 for 2026-2027 to Master's students coming from foreign universities to laboratories affiliated with Sorbonne University Alliance. The grant covers travel and accommodation expenses, and the intern also receives the standard stipend for a Master 2 internship; additional stipend funding may be requested from InLife in the project description. The host laboratory must be affiliated with a Sorbonne University Alliance institution and projects must be interdisciplinary at the interface of fields related to the study of living systems. Applications are submitted as a single PDF by email and are evaluated by the members of the InLife Executive Committee.",
      "deadline": "Deadline for application: November 2, 2026 at 6 pm",
      "deadline_date": "2026-11-02",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Single annual call for 2026-2027, published 6 July 2026 and updated 29 September 2026, closing 2 November 2026 at 18:00.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Master's students from foreign universities, hosted by a laboratory affiliated with an institution within Sorbonne University Alliance, on interdisciplinary projects at the interface of fields related to the study of living systems. There are no geographical restrictions regarding the university of origin.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Master's (Master 2) student from a foreign university",
        "Hosting laboratory must be affiliated with an institution within the Sorbonne University Alliance",
        "Project must be interdisciplinary at the interface of fields related to the study of living systems",
        "No geographical restriction on the university of origin"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Travel expenses",
        "Accommodation expenses",
        "Standard stipend for a Master 2 internship paid by the host arrangement",
        "Possible additional InLife stipend funding if requested in the project description"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "EUR 7,500 mobility grant covering travel and accommodation",
        "Standard stipend for a Master 2 internship",
        "Possibility of additional InLife stipend funding if requested in the project description"
      ],
