          "description": "The Erasmus Trustfonds Scholarship / TSH Changemaker Scholarship supports underrepresented students to pursue a Master's programme at Erasmus University Rotterdam. The Erasmus Trustfonds component covers the statutory tuition fee and includes a monthly living allowance of EUR 600, totalling EUR 9,895 for costs of living and the statutory fee for one year, while the TSH Changemaker Scholarship provides one year of housing in a Social Hub Residence. At Erasmus MC the award is limited to applicants to the Health Sciences, Neuroscience and Molecular Medicine Research Master's programmes who have a bachelor average equivalent to Dutch 8.0 and who belong to a disadvantaged or underrepresented group. Applications are submitted through the OSIRIS Cases portal, with the 2026-2027 deadline set at 1 April 2026, 23:59 CET.",
