      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The New Zealand Space Scholarship gives postgraduate STEM students a fully supported three-month internship at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Southern California, working alongside scientists and engineers on space missions and research. Applications for the 2027 scholarship opened on 1 October 2026 and the internship runs from July to September 2027. The scholarship covers return economy flights to the United States, accommodation, a daily living allowance and reasonable travel-related expenses including insurance support where applicable. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens aged 18 or over, enrolled in a postgraduate STEM qualification at a New Zealand tertiary institution in a field relevant to NASA's mission priorities, and hold at least a 3.0 GPA on a 4.0 scale.",
      "region": "Oceania",
      "duration": "3-month internship, July to September 2027 (dates subject to change)",
      "deadline": "The Ministry states \"Applications for the 2027 New Zealand Space Scholarship open on 1 October 2026\" but publishes no closing date for the 2027 round on this page.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "unknown",
      "application_period": "The 2027 round opened on 1 October 2026 and is open now. The internship itself runs July to September 2027. No closing date is published on the official page.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must be New Zealand citizens (a NASA requirement), aged 18 or over, enrolled in a postgraduate STEM qualification at a New Zealand tertiary institution in a field relevant to NASA's mission priorities, hold a minimum GPA of 3.0 on a 4.0 scale with New Zealand grades converted to the US scale, and be proficient in written and spoken English. They must be available in person from July to September 2027, willing to undergo any required health and security checks for US travel and entry to US federal facilities, eligible for a J1 or F1 visa, and able to obtain appropriate travel and medical insurance. Applicants who hold or have held citizenship of a country on NASA's Designated Countries List are not eligible.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a New Zealand citizen (NASA requirement)",
        "Be aged 18 years or older",
        "Be enrolled in a postgraduate STEM qualification at a New Zealand tertiary institution in a field relevant to NASA's mission priorities",
