          },
          "description": "A fully supported three-month research internship at NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory in Southern California for postgraduate STEM students, awarded by the New Zealand Space Agency within the Ministry of Business, Innovation and Employment. The 2027 round opened on 1 October 2026 for an internship running July to September 2027. Funding covers return economy flights to the United States, accommodation, a daily living allowance and reasonable travel-related expenses including insurance support. Applicants must be New Zealand citizens aged 18 or over, enrolled in a postgraduate STEM qualification at a New Zealand tertiary institution in a field relevant to NASA's mission priorities, with a minimum 3.0 GPA on a 4.0 scale. Assessment covers academic excellence, relevance of experience to JPL projects, personal qualities and commitment, with JPL making the final selection.",
