      "selection_notes": "A selection panel assesses applications. The Ministry states it will 'give preference to applicants who demonstrate that their studies aim to improve the social, economic and cultural wellbeing of Māori'. Outcomes for the 2027 study year are expected to be notified to all applicants by late November 2026.",
      "program_type": "Merit scholarship scheme (multiple levels)",
      "best_fit": "Māori students entering or continuing full-time vocational, undergraduate, master's or doctoral study in New Zealand who can evidence achievement and alignment with the values of the 28th (Māori) Battalion.",
      "notes": "The Fund Board was established in 1945 by the Ngarimu VC and 28th (Māori) Battalion Memorial Scholarship Fund Act 1945 and exists to promote the study and maintenance of te reo Māori, Māori history, Māori tradition and Māori culture. The 2026-27 Budget increased Fund funding by $100,000 each year, adding 5 scholarships and bringing the annual total to 14. Winners for the 2025/26 round were announced on 26 March 2026 at a ceremony at Parliament, Te Whanganui-a-Tara.",
