          },
          "description": "The Ngarimu VC and 28th (Māori) Battalion Memorial Scholarships are funded by the Ngarimu VC and 28th (Māori) Battalion Memorial Scholarship Fund Board, established in 1945, and administered through the Ministry of Education. The Board awards scholarships annually to exceptional Māori students for vocational or tertiary study who demonstrate values aligning with those of the 28th (Māori) Battalion, and exists to promote te reo Māori, Māori history, Māori tradition and Māori culture. From 2026, increased government funding provides 14 scholarships each year across five schemes: 5 VET, 4 undergraduate, 3 master's, 1 Master of Education research and 1 doctoral.",
