      "description": "The PSC Scholarships are the Singapore Government's premier merit-based undergraduate scholarships, awarded by the Public Service Commission for entry to the Singapore Public Service. Applicants may apply before beginning their degree or as mid-term applicants up to the penultimate year, and must be Singapore Citizens who demonstrate strong leadership qualities and potential with good academic and non-academic records. Value of award covers tuition fees and other approved charges, return airfare for overseas degrees, maintenance and other allowances, full salary including bonuses on the Uniformed Service track, and sponsorship of PSC development programmes and approved exchange or summer programmes.",
      "duration": "Up to 3 years undergraduate degree in the UK (plus 1 to 2 additional years for a Master's), 4 years in the US (plus 1 to 2 years for a Master's), 1 year plus Master's years in Singapore, 2 years plus 2 years for a Master's in other countries",
      "deadline": "'Applications for PSC Scholarships for 2027 are now open and will close on 15 March 2027.'",
      "deadline_date": "2027-03-15",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Applications open and close on a single annual cycle; the 2027 cycle closes 15 March 2027",
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must be Singapore Citizens who demonstrate strong leadership qualities and potential and present themselves as well-rounded individuals with good academic and non-academic records, holding a GCE A-level, International Baccalaureate, NUS High School Diploma, Polytechnic Diploma with merit or other high school diploma or equivalent. Mid-term applicants additionally need at least one semester of university results and must apply before the final year of study.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a Singapore Citizen",
        "Demonstrate strong leadership qualities and potential",
        "Present themselves as well-rounded individuals with good academic and non-academic records",
        "Hold a GCE A-level, International Baccalaureate, NUS High School Diploma, Polytechnic Diploma with merit or other high school diploma or equivalent",
        "For mid-term applicants: at least one semester of university results and application made before the final year of undergraduate study",
        "For professional schemes with a tied agency: be undertaking an undergraduate degree relevant to that tied agency"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Tuition fees and other approved charges",
        "Return airfare for overseas degrees",
        "Maintenance and other allowances",
        "Full salary including bonuses for those on the Uniformed Service track",
        "Sponsorship of PSC development programmes and approved student exchange or summer programmes",
        "Master's degree sponsorship (if applicable and requirements are met)",
        "Back payment of tuition and other compulsory fees for mid-term candidates"
      ],
      "benefits": [
