            "phone": "800-618-6737 ext. 1",
            "email": "boren@iieus.org"
          },
          "description": "The National Security Education Program awards Boren Scholarships and Fellowships to U.S. undergraduate and graduate students committed to long-term overseas study and to federal service. Boren Scholarships fund study abroad by U.S. undergraduate students in world regions critical to U.S. interests; Boren Fellowships fund research and language study proposals by U.S. graduate students. Maximum awards are determined by duration abroad: $25,000 for 25-52 weeks (preferred), $12,500 for 12-24 weeks, and $8,000 for 8-11 weeks (STEM majors only). There are no minimum language requirements, with the exception of French and Spanish, which require intermediate high [1+] proficiency for advanced study programs in Africa and Latin America. The Boren Awards are an initiative of the Defense Language and National Security Education Office.",
          "program_type": "Federal overseas study and research scholarship",
          "region": "World regions critical to U.S. interests, for U.S. students",
          "coverage": "Maximum award determined by duration abroad: $25,000 for 25-52 weeks (preferred), $12,500 for 12-24 weeks, and $8,000 for 8-11 weeks (STEM majors only, Scholarships). The homepage does not itemise what the award may be applied to, so tuition, living cost and travel coverage are recorded as null.",
