      ],
      "selection_notes": "Selection criteria listed per scholarship are excellence in prior academic and professional work, ambition and leadership potential, career progression and international exposure, and performance during the Assessment Day. Bursary recipients are confirmed on an ongoing basis. Candidates unable to secure a loan because of nationality restrictions are invited to contact the Finance Committee.",
      "best_fit": "Applicants to the one-year full-time IMD MBA in Lausanne who have strong GPA or equivalent and GMAT/GRE scores, and who additionally meet the specific profile of the named scholarship, for example women for the Nestle, Forte and BackPack awards or a STEM background for the Hilti award.",
      "funding_currency": "CHF",
      "funding_period": "one-off, awarded for the MBA programme",
      "notes": "This record aggregates several distinct awards rather than a single scholarship, so no single funding_amount is reported: the named awards are CHF 50,000 (MBA5, Hilti STEM), CHF 40,000 (Nestle for Women, IMD MBA Merit up to), CHF 30,000 (Forte for Women), and one full-funding award (BackPack for Women). IMD states 48% of students received a scholarship and more than 50% of scholarships are awarded to women. Scholarships require an accepted offer, so they cannot be applied for before admission. The fixed 14 July BackPack date carries no year on the page and has passed relative to 2026-10-04, so no exact deadline is recorded.",
      "description": "IMD Business School offers a portfolio of scholarships and need-based bursaries for candidates applying to and entering its one-year full-time MBA in Lausanne. Six named scholarships were listed as open in October 2026: the MBA5 Scholarship of CHF 50,000, the Hilti STEM Scholars Program of CHF 50,000, the Nestle Scholarship for Women of CHF 40,000, the Forté Scholarship for Women of CHF 30,000, IMD MBA Merit Scholarships of up to CHF 40,000, and the BackPack Scholarship for Women with full funding. Most run throughout 2026 on an available-until-allocated basis, while the BackPack Scholarship closes on 14 July. Scholarships are applied for through the Program section of the MBA application form and are awarded to candidates who have applied for and accepted an offer, with selection based on academic and professional excellence, GMAT/GRE scores, career progression, international exposure and Assessment Day performance. Separate need-based bursaries are awarded on proven financial need and confirmed on an ongoing basis.",
