          "description": "IMD is committed to fostering growth in diversity through its merit scholarships and need-based bursaries, which are awarded to candidates who have applied for and accepted an offer to join the IMD MBA programme. Six named scholarships were listed as open: the MBA5 Scholarship of CHF 50K, the Hilti STEM Scholars Program of CHF 50K, the Nestle Scholarship for Women of CHF 40K, the Forté Scholarship for Women of CHF 30K, IMD MBA Merit Scholarships of up to CHF 40K, and the BackPack Scholarship for Women with full funding. Scholarship applications are made in the Program section of the MBA application form, and the main awards carry the deadline 'Throughout 2026 (available until allocated)' while the BackPack Scholarship closes on 14 July. Bursary applications are made in the admissions application by the admissions deadline, with recipients confirmed on an ongoing basis on the basis of proven financial need, good academic results, a strong reference letter and steady career progression. 48% of students receive a scholarship from IMD and more than 50% of scholarships are awarded to women.",
