      ],
      "selection_notes": "Each fellowship is advertised individually as a call for expressions of interest and assessed against that category's requirements, which may include a minimum level of professional experience, an advanced degree or specific competencies. The page publishes no selection weighting.",
      "best_fit": "Young professionals with at least a bachelor's degree and, depending on the track, a background in translation and terminology, law and internet or trademark dispute resolution, or economics and statistics, who want hands-on experience in intellectual property at an international organisation in Geneva.",
      "funding_currency": "CHF",
      "funding_period": "per month",
      "notes": "The stipend is published as a range of CHF 3,000 to CHF 8,000 per month depending on academic background and experience relevant to the nature of the fellowship, so funding_amount is left null rather than picking one end of the range. This is a paid fellowship contract rather than a grant toward study costs, so no tuition component applies and full funding is not claimed. The page states the programme duration as 12 to 36 months while the benefits section describes contracts of up to 12 months renewable to a total of up to three years, which is consistent. A one-year waiting period applies to former Young Experts Program participants, which is a decision-critical rule that is easy to miss.",
      "description": "WIPO's Fellowship Program places professionals in specialized disciplines at the World Intellectual Property Organization in Geneva, Switzerland, for 12 to 36 months. Fellows are classified into four categories: translation fellows in the PCT Translation and Terminology Fellowship Program, legal case manager fellows in the WIPO Domain Name Fellowship Program, visiting and research fellows in the Research and Visiting Fellowship Program, and other specialized fellows. Applicants must hold at least a first-level university degree, with additional requirements such as professional experience, an advanced degree or specific competencies depending on the category. Fellows receive a monthly stipend of CHF 3,000 to CHF 8,000 depending on academic background and relevant experience, comprehensive medical and professional accident insurance largely paid by WIPO, relocation assistance covering travel at the start and end of the fellowship, assistance with visa formalities, 10 official holidays plus 2.5 days of annual leave per full month, and access to WIPO Academy training with up to six study leave days a year. Positions are advertised through calls for expressions of interest on WIPO's career website and LinkedIn.",
