          },
          "description": "WIPO's Fellowship Program offers hands-on experience, expanded knowledge and network building at the World Intellectual Property Organization in Geneva, Switzerland, for a duration of 12 to 36 months. To be eligible, candidates must possess at least a first-level university degree such as a bachelor's, with additional requirements such as a minimum level of professional experience, advanced degrees or specific competencies depending on the fellowship category. Fellows fall into four categories: translation fellows in the PCT Translation and Terminology Fellowship Program, legal case manager fellows in the WIPO Domain Name Fellowship Program, visiting and research fellows in the Research and Visiting Fellowship Program, and other specialized fellows. Positions are advertised through calls for expressions of interest on WIPO's career website or via WIPO's LinkedIn and other social media channels. Fellows receive a contract of up to 12 months renewable to a total of up to three years, a monthly stipend of CHF 3,000 to CHF 8,000 depending on academic background and relevant experience, medical and professional accident insurance largely paid for by WIPO, relocation travel at the start and end of the fellowship, visa assistance, 10 official holidays plus 2.5 days annual leave per full month, up to six study leave days a year and funded UN official languages training where job duties require it. There is no age limit, and former Young Experts Program participants may not apply for any WIPO position within one year of completing the programme.",
