      "description": "Kyushu University's own support programme for privately financed international students who come to Kyushu University on exchange, special auditing, special research or double degree status and who cannot afford to study in Japan solely at their own expense. It pays a monthly stipend of JPY 80,000, and the total of all scholarships held by the grantee may not exceed that amount. Applicants apply through their prospective host department at Kyushu University, not directly to the university centre. There are two recruitment periods per fiscal year: Period I around February for students who will study from April to September, and Period II around May for students who will study from October to March. The period of stay must be 3 months, 5 months (one semester) or 11 months (two semesters).",
      "region": "Asia",
      "duration": "3 months, 5 months (one semester) or 11 months (two semesters) at Kyushu University; the period of stay must begin within the academic year",
      "deadline": "No exact date is published. There are two recruitment periods in each fiscal year: Period I is recruited around February for grantees starting between April and September, and Period II is recruited around May for grantees starting between October and March. Applications are made through the applicant's prospective host department at Kyushu University, so the department sets its own internal date within the period.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "Two recruitment periods a year. Period I: around February, for study starting between April and September. Period II: around May, for study starting between October and the following March.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Non-Japanese nationals who are students at an overseas university and whose status at Kyushu University is as a special auditing student, special research student or double degree programme student under an inter-university exchange agreement, an inter-departmental exchange agreement, a double degree agreement, or even from a university with no exchange agreement. They must begin their stay within the academic year for 3, 5 or 11 months, be unable to study in Japan solely at their own expense, be certain to obtain Student status of residence, return to their home university afterwards to obtain a degree or graduate, and have excellent academic records and character with a grade evaluation coefficient of 2.30 or higher on a 3-point scale for the previous year.",
