      "description": "Central European University awards need-based financial aid on academic merit to admitted students who indicate their interest in the funding section of the CEU Application Form, and who must begin their studies at the Vienna campus in the fall of the academic year for which the award is made. At bachelor's level the aid is a Partial Tuition Award of up to 50% of the tuition fee, capped at EUR 4,000 per academic year. At master's level candidates receive a Master's Tuition Award covering 50% to 80% of the tuition fee, with a Full Tuition Award only in exceptional cases, plus an optional Master's Stipend Award of EUR 300 to EUR 750 per month. At doctoral level the CEU Doctoral Scholarship covers the full cost of tuition together with a monthly stipend. Candidates from any country may apply. For the 2026/2027 academic year the Round 1 deadline is 15 October 2026 and the Round 2 deadline is 2 February 2027, so the programme is currently open.",
