          "description": "Central European University (CEU) is a non-profit private university founded in 1991 and based in Vienna since 2019, with around 1,500 students from more than 100 countries pursuing bachelor's, master's and doctoral programs accredited in both the United States and Austria. CEU grants need-based financial aid on academic merit to admitted students from any country who indicate their interest in the Funding section of the CEU Application Form, and who are able to begin their studies at the Vienna campus in the fall of the academic year for which the award is made. The packages differ by level: a Partial Tuition Award of up to 50% of tuition, capped at EUR 4,000 per academic year, at bachelor's level; a Master's Tuition Award covering 50% to 80% of tuition, with a Full Tuition Award only in exceptional cases, plus an optional Master's Stipend Award of EUR 300 to EUR 750 per month, at master's level; and the CEU Doctoral Scholarship covering the full cost of tuition together with a stipend of EUR 2,002 gross per month awarded for 48 months in total, at doctoral level. Financial aid can be requested in admission Rounds 1 and 2 only.",
