      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "region": "Europe",
      "description": "The Banach NAWA programme funds full-time second-cycle (master's) studies conducted in Polish or English at universities supervised by the Minister of Science and Higher Education. It is a joint initiative of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Poland and the Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange, delivered as Polish development aid, and is open to citizens of the 36 countries covered by Polish Aid in Eastern Europe, Asia, Africa and Latin America. Benefits published by NAWA are a monthly scholarship of PLN 2,500, exemption from tuition fees at public universities, a PLN 2,500 travel allowance, a NAWA-funded preparatory course for the Polish track, and a Polish language and culture course for the English track. The call for applications for the winter semester 2026/27 is Announcement No. 16/2026 of 13 April 2026.",
      "deadline": "Announcement of a call for applications No. 16/2026 of 13 April 2026, for studies or preparatory course from the winter semester 2026/27. The exact closing date is published inside the call PDF and could not be read.",
