            "general": "Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange (NAWA), ul. Polna 40, 00-635 Warsaw, Poland, telephone +48 22 390 35 00",
            "email": null
          },
          "description": "The Banach NAWA programme offers scholarships for full-time second-cycle studies conducted in Polish or English at universities supervised by the Minister of Science and Higher Education. Its stated main goal is \"to support the socio-economic development of developing countries by improving the level of education and professional qualifications of their citizens\". What the programme offers is a monthly scholarship of PLN 2,500, an exemption from tuition fees at public universities, a preparatory course funded by NAWA on the Polish track, a travel allowance of PLN 2,500, studies in Polish or English, and a Polish language and culture course on the English track. It is open to citizens of the 36 countries covered by Polish Aid, from Eastern Europe, Asia, Africa and Latin America, and the full list of eligible countries is published in the call announcement. The programme is a joint initiative of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and the Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange in the form of Polish development aid. For the winter semester 2026/27 the call was announced as No. 16/2026 of 13 April 2026.",
