      "region": "Europe",
      "description": "The International Visegrad Fund's Visegrad Scholarship Programme supports master's and post-master's students and researchers for up to two semesters at institutions in Central and Eastern Europe, awarded for a period of 1 or 2 semesters; within the In-Coming scheme, master's applicants can be awarded 1- to 4-semester scholarships. It is open to citizens of Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Belarus, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Georgia, Kosovo, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Serbia and Ukraine, and all applicants must have completed at least four semesters of university studies. Because it is a mobility scholarship, the host country varies with the chosen institution rather than being a single destination. The Fund's own site shows the next application round opening on 1 January 2027; no closing date for that round is published yet, and the funding amounts are not stated on the pages read, so funding_type and funding_amount are left unresolved rather than guessed.",
      "deadline": "The International Visegrad Fund's own site states the Visegrad Scholarship Program \"Opens Jan 1, 2027\". No closing date for that round is published yet.",
