          "description": "The International Visegrad Fund awards Visegrad Scholarships for study or research to master's and post-master's students and researchers from twelve countries: Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Belarus, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Georgia, Kosovo, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia, Serbia and Ukraine. Applicants must have completed at least four semesters of university studies. The awards are for one or two semesters at institutions in Central and Eastern Europe, and within the In-Coming scheme master's scholarships can be awarded for one to four semesters. The Fund's stated purpose is to foster creativity and promote understanding between people across borders, looking for individuals pursuing innovative ideas in science and education who wish to engage in conversation on development and cooperation in the Visegrad region. Applications for the next round open on 1 January 2027.",
