      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "deadline": "Canadian institutions must apply on behalf of eligible candidates before the deadline of 11:59 p.m. EDT, March 24, 2026. The page states 'Application period for 2026-27 is closed.' Institutions are encouraged to set an earlier internal deadline with candidates and their home institutions.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "funding_amount": null,
      "funding_currency": "CAD",
      "funding_period": null,
      "duration": "Four to eight months: college/undergraduate 4 months or 8 months (two academic terms); graduate 4 months or 5 to 6 months. Scholarships cannot be deferred and are not renewable.",
      "coverage": [
        "College / undergraduate (4 months): $10,200",
        "College / undergraduate (8 months): $15,900",
        "Graduate (4 months): $10,200",
        "Graduate (5-6 months): $12,700",
        "Eligible expenses: visa or study/work permit fees; airfare via the most direct and economical route; health insurance; living expenses such as accommodation, utilities and food; ground transportation including a public transportation pass; books and supplies required for the study or research, excluding computers and other equipment",
        "Tuition must be waived by the Canadian host institution"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Airfare to Canada via the most direct and economical route",
        "Health insurance",
        "Visa or study/work permit fees",
        "Living expenses including accommodation, utilities and food",
        "Ground transportation including a public transportation pass",
        "Books and supplies for the study or research (computers and other equipment excluded)",
        "Canadian institutions additionally receive $500 per scholarship recipient for administrative costs and, in some cases, reimbursement of additional employer compliance fees paid to IRCC"
      ],
      "eligibility_summary": "Candidates must be citizens of an ASEAN Member State (Brunei Darussalam, Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Timor-Leste or Vietnam), a Pacific Island Country (Cook Islands, Fiji, Kiribati, Marshall Islands, Micronesia, Nauru, Niue, Palau, Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Tonga, Tuvalu or Vanuatu), or Mongolia; be enrolled full-time at a post-secondary institution in an eligible country; and be paying tuition fees to that institution at the time of application and for the full duration of the exchange. Hosting Canadian institutions must be a Designated Learning Institution, must waive tuition fees for scholarship recipients, and must centralize applications through their international office.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Citizen of an ASEAN Member State, a Pacific Island Country or Mongolia (the 30 eligible countries are listed on the official page)",
        "Enrolled full-time at a post-secondary institution in an eligible country",
        "Paying tuition fees to that institution at the time of application and for the full duration of the exchange",
        "Not hold or have pending an application for Canadian citizenship or permanent residency",
        "Not already participating in a scholarship program funded by the Government of Canada",
        "Not already enrolled in a degree, diploma or certificate program at a Canadian post-secondary institution",
        "Not have previously received a scholarship under the first phase of the program (Canada-ASEAN SEED)",
        "Canadian host institution must be a Designated Learning Institution, must waive tuition fees for scholarship recipients, and must centralize applications through its international office"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Be nominated by a Canadian host institution, which must apply on the candidate's behalf through My EduCanada",
        "Provide a one-page letter of intent that identifies the Sustainable Development Goal the proposed study or research aligns with - 'letters that do not identify an SDG will be deemed incomplete and not eligible'",
        "Provide country-specific poverty-impact explanations where required",
        "Provide a letter of proof of full-time enrolment on official letterhead dated within the last six months",
        "Provide a one-page letter of support from the home institution on official letterhead dated within the last six months",
        "Graduate applicants must provide a one-page letter of invitation from the Canadian supervisor",
        "Upload all supporting documents in the accepted formats, each smaller than 5 MB"
      ],
      "application_method": [
        "The Canadian institution assigns a program coordinator, creates a My EduCanada account via Global Affairs Canada Single Sign-On (a GCKey account is recommended), selects the SEED-2 programme and clicks Apply",
        "The institution enters candidate data, validates and saves, uploads all required supporting documents, accepts the Declaration and permission statement and submits",
        "The institution separately emails a ranking of applications based on its strategic priorities to seed-bpeed@international.gc.ca, indicating each candidate's MyEduCanada application number",
        "Institutions are encouraged to set an earlier internal deadline with candidates and their home institutions"
