      "program_type": "Government exchange scholarship (Indo-Pacific Strategy initiative)",
      "catalogue_url": "https://www.educanada.ca/scholarships-bourses/non_can/index.aspx?lang=eng",
      "official_updates_url": "https://www.educanada.ca/scholarships-bourses/can/institutions/seed-bpeed.aspx?lang=eng",
      "description": "The Scholarships and Educational Exchanges for Development - Phase 2 (SEED-2) program is offered by Global Affairs Canada as a key initiative under Canada's Indo-Pacific Strategy, funded under that strategy. It expands the Canada-ASEAN Scholarships and Educational Exchanges for Development (SEED) programme to students from ASEAN Member States, Pacific Island Countries and Mongolia, who conduct short-term study or research at Canadian post-secondary institutions in areas contributing to the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. Canadian institutions must apply on behalf of eligible candidates, must be Designated Learning Institutions, and must waive tuition fees for recipients. Four award components are offered, from $10,200 to $15,900, with durations of four to eight months.",
      "english_requirement": "Not stated as an applicant requirement. The official page states that 'Documents in a language other than English or French must be accompanied by a translation', so English or French is the working language of the application.",
