          "application_method": "There is no direct student application. A Canadian post-secondary institution applies on the candidate's behalf: it assigns a program coordinator, creates a My EduCanada account through Global Affairs Canada Single Sign-On (a GCKey account is recommended for institutions), selects the SEED-2 programme and clicks Apply, enters the required data, uploads all supporting documents (each under 5 MB, in .jpg, .gif, .png, .pdf, .doc, .docx, .txt or .xlsx format), accepts the Declaration and permission statement, and submits. The institution must separately email a ranking of applications based on its strategic priorities, indicating each candidate's MyEduCanada application number.",
          "application_route": "My EduCanada portal, accessed via Global Affairs Canada Single Sign-On, on the institution's behalf. Programme page: https://www.educanada.ca/scholarships-bourses/can/institutions/seed-bpeed.aspx?lang=eng",
