            "Country-specific poverty explanation: candidates from Cambodia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, Myanmar, the Philippines, Thailand, Timor-Leste or Vietnam must explain how their learning will help reduce poverty in their home country; candidates from Brunei or Singapore must explain how it will help one of the other nine ASEAN countries; candidates from Fiji, Kiribati, Marshall Islands, Micronesia, Nauru, Niue, Palau, Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Solomon Islands, Tonga or Vanuatu must explain how it will help reduce poverty in their home country; candidates from the Cook Islands must explain how it will help one of the other thirteen eligible Pacific Island Countries; candidates from Mongolia must explain how their learning will help reduce poverty in their home country",
