          },
          "description": "The Scholarships and Educational Exchanges for Development - Phase 2 (SEED-2) program is offered by Global Affairs Canada as a key initiative under Canada's Indo-Pacific Strategy. It expands the Canada-ASEAN SEED programme to students from ASEAN Member States, Pacific Island Countries and Mongolia to conduct short-term study or research in Canadian post-secondary institutions in areas contributing to the implementation of the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development. Canadian institutions must apply on behalf of eligible candidates before 11:59 p.m. EDT on March 24, 2026. Four components are offered: college/undergraduate 4 months ($10,200), college/undergraduate 8 months ($15,900), graduate 4 months ($10,200) and graduate 5-6 months ($12,700), covering airfare, health insurance, permit fees, living expenses, ground transport and books, with tuition waived by the host institution.",
