          "description": "The KB Fellowship at NIAS offers researchers and creative practitioners five months to work on the future of the (public) library, on the library as a public institution, or on the library as a pillar of liberal democracy. NIAS and the KB, the National Library of the Netherlands, established the current fellowship in 2025, continuing an earlier KB Fellowship that ran from 2004 to 2018, and one fellowship is awarded each academic year from September to January. Applicants must be scholars at least three years past their PhD or creative practitioners with at least three years of independent practice, with or without institutional affiliation, and submit a project proposal of no more than 1,500 words, a CV of no more than four pages and a statement of no more than 300 words. The fellow receives a personal stipend, or a Dutch University Grant paid to the institution for scholars at a Dutch university or research institute, plus an office, research facilities and, where eligible, subsidised Amsterdam accommodation or local transport reimbursement. The call for 2027-2028 opens on 15 January 2027 and closes on 15 March 2027 at 12.00 noon CET.",
