      "selection_notes": "The Willem F. Duisenberg Fellowship Foundation gives particular priority to researchers with an outstanding record in applied monetary economics, macroeconomics or public finance. Applicants are encouraged to reflect on the collaborative and multidisciplinary environment at NIAS and to consider how their research might both benefit from and contribute to the NIAS research community and beyond.",
      "program_type": "Residual research fellowship in economics at a national advanced-study institute, funded by the Willem F. Duisenberg Fellowship Foundation",
      "best_fit": "An established researcher with at least three years of post-PhD experience and a strong publication record in applied monetary economics, macroeconomics or public finance, who can spend five or ten months in Amsterdam and wants to engage with Dutch policymakers and financial institutions.",
      "notes": "The Willem F. Duisenberg Fellowship Foundation was established in 2007 in honour of Willem F. Duisenberg to foster excellence in economic research in the Netherlands, and is supported by De Nederlandsche Bank, the Dutch Ministry of Finance and several major Dutch financial institutions: ING Group, Rabobank Nederland, ABN AMRO and AEGON. The Foundation has no employees and receives administrative and organisational support from NIAS. Its board consists of Chair Prof. Dr Klaas Knot, Treasurer Prof. dr. Antoine Buyse (Director NIAS) and Board Member Joanne Kellermann; board members receive no remuneration. The funding route depends on affiliation: a personal stipend for the fellow, or a Dutch University Grant paid to the institution for fellows at a Dutch university or research institute. NIAS publishes no euro amount for either route.",
