          "description": "The Willem F. Duisenberg Fellowship at NIAS offers researchers and policymakers the opportunity to work on topics in applied monetary economics, macroeconomics, macroeconomic policy and public finance. The Willem F. Duisenberg Fellowship Foundation, established in 2007 in honour of Willem F. Duisenberg and supported by De Nederlandsche Bank, the Dutch Ministry of Finance, ING Group, Rabobank Nederland, ABN AMRO and AEGON, offers one five-month and one ten-month fellowship per academic year. Applicants need a minimum of three years of post-PhD academic experience; the fellowship targets prominent mid- to late-career researchers while encouraging exceptionally talented early-career candidates. Fellows receive a personal stipend, or a Dutch University Grant paid to their institution if affiliated with a Dutch university, plus an office, research facilities and subsidised accommodation where eligible. The 2027-2028 call ran from 15 January to 13 April 2026 and is now closed.",
