      ],
      "selection_notes": "Not published on the pages read; CEEPUS selection runs at network level.",
      "program_type": "Multilateral university exchange programme",
      "best_fit": "Students from CEEPUS countries whose home university participates in a CEEPUS network in their field, seeking a 3-10 month tuition-free exchange with a host-country living grant.",
      "notes": "CEEPUS expands 'Central European Exchange Program for University Studies' and unites universities from 16 Central and Eastern European countries (Albania, Austria, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Bulgaria, Croatia, the Czech Republic, Hungary, Macedonia, Moldova, Montenegro, Poland, Romania, Serbia, the Slovak Republic and Slovenia, with Prishtina/Kosovo also participating). The grant is paid by the host country and its amount varies, so no single figure can be quoted for the whole programme.",
      "description": "CEEPUS is a multilateral exchange programme with Central and Eastern Europe, organised as a transnational university network of subject-specific networks, each containing at least three higher education institutions from at least two different CEEPUS contractual countries. Exchanges last 3 to 10 months. Within a network, incoming students are exempted from paying tuition fees and receive a comprehensive grant from the host country sized according to local living costs. Eligibility requires CEEPUS-country nationality and participation through a member institution.",
      "detail": {
        "official_details": {
