      "degree_levels": "Bachelor's",
      "funding_type": "Fully Funded (4-year bond)",
      "description": "The Temasek Undergraduate Overseas Scholarship is awarded to exceptional polytechnic graduates who show academic excellence, outstanding extracurricular involvement and a strong passion for STEM, to study a STEM undergraduate degree at an overseas university, with Medicine and Dentistry excluded. Temasek lists tuition and other compulsory fees for the whole course, a monthly living allowance, one-time relocation and pre-studies allowances, reimbursed application fees for up to five universities and visa fees, plus exchange programmes, internships and mentoring. Eligibility is capped by a Gross Monthly Household Income of S$15,000 or less at the point of admission, and graduates must serve a 4-year bond in a STEM-related role in Singapore or with a Singapore-headquartered company.",
