      "best_fit": "Singapore Citizen polytechnic graduates or final-year polytechnic students from households with a Gross Monthly Household Income of S$15,000 or less, strong STEM passion and academic results, who intend to read a STEM undergraduate degree at an overseas university and will work in a STEM-related role in Singapore or a Singapore-headquartered company afterwards.",
      "notes": "The award is means-tested through the Gross Monthly Household Income cap of S$15,000 at the point of admission, and excludes Medicine and Dentistry. Temasek publishes no monetary amounts for the tuition, living, relocation, pre-studies, application or visa components on this page, so no funding figure is recorded. The scholarship is part of Temasek's T-Spring community gift and sits under the Temasek Scholarship family alongside the Temasek Undergraduate Local Scholarship. Note that the page's own text says the AY2026/2027 window \"is now open\" while the closing date it gives, 15 September 2026, had already passed as at this verification date, so the page text appears not to have been refreshed after the extension lapsed.",
