          "description": "The Temasek Undergraduate Overseas Scholarship is awarded to exceptional polytechnic graduates who show academic excellence, outstanding extracurricular involvement and a strong passion for STEM, to study a STEM undergraduate degree at a top overseas university, with Medicine and Dentistry excluded. Temasek lists tuition and other compulsory fees for the whole course, a monthly living allowance, one-time relocation and pre-studies allowances, reimbursed application fees for up to five universities and visa fees, plus exchange programmes, internships and mentoring. Eligibility is capped by a Gross Monthly Household Income of S$15,000 or less at the point of admission, and graduates must serve a 4-year bond in a STEM-related role in Singapore or with a Singapore-headquartered company.",
          "program_type": "Undergraduate STEM Scholarship",
          "region": "Asia",
          "coverage": "Full tuition and compulsory fees for the whole course plus living, relocation, pre-studies, application and visa costs; conditional on a 4-year bond.",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Confirm you are a Singapore Citizen and a local polytechnic graduate or final-year polytechnic student",
            "Check your Gross Monthly Household Income is S$15,000 or less at the point of admission, since the award is means-tested",
            "Line up acceptance or a planned application to a STEM undergraduate programme at an overseas university, excluding Medicine and Dentistry",
            "Consolidate your certificates, pre-tertiary results, co-curricular records, prizes and awards, and any university application outcomes into one file for upload under CV submission",
            "Prepare to declare your Gross Monthly Household Income in the application",
            "Apply from the official page via the Brightsparks button inside the published window, which has historically opened on 1 July",
            "Block time for the four-stage assessment if shortlisted, including a one-day in-person group assessment and a final 60-minute interview"
