      "description": "The Heart Failure Association of the European Society of Cardiology awards grants of EUR 2,500 per month up to a maximum of EUR 10,000 so that young members can carry out heart failure research or training in an ESC member country other than their own. The project must be prepared jointly with the host centre for at least three months. Applicants must be under 40 and hold an MD without a permanent, senior staff or consultant post, or hold or have submitted a PhD thesis, and they must be an HFA member or Fellow. The annual application period is 10 April to 30 September.",
