      "description": "EMBO Postdoctoral Fellowships support postdoctoral researchers in the life sciences for up to two years, with international mobility between countries as a core condition of eligibility. In EMBC Member States EMBO grants the host institution funds so it can issue an employment contract to the fellow; fellows based outside EMBC Member States receive a stipend intended to cover living costs. The fellowship also carries a travel and relocation allowance, child daycare support for non-EMBC fellows, and access to EMBO Laboratory Leadership courses. Applications are accepted throughout the year, with hard cutoffs for each evaluation round.",
      "duration": "Up to two years; minimum one year; maximum combined full-time and part-time duration 36 months",
