      "description": "The Maria Leptin | EMBO Science Journalism Fellowships scheme funds placements for working science journalists at research institutions and for life scientists seeking to move into full-time science journalism in media newsrooms. It is restricted to applicants resident in an EMBC Member State whose placements also take place in an EMBC Member State, in person. Successful applicants receive a daily subsistence stipend based on the cost of living in the host country, covering living expenses and travel. Applications are accepted at any time but must be registered in the EMBO portal by 23:59 Central European Summer Time on 30 October each year.",
      "duration": "Journalists: minimum three months, maximum six months. Researchers transitioning to journalism: minimum three months, maximum twelve months.",
      "deadline": "30 October each year, 23:59 Central European Summer Time (applications may be submitted at any time but must be registered by this deadline)",
      "deadline_date": "2026-10-30",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Applications can be submitted at any time; selection takes place once a year and fully completed applications must be registered in the EMBO portal by 23:59 CEST on 30 October each year. Applicants are notified by mid-November.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Either an employed or freelance working journalist with demonstrable relevant experience and samples of published or broadcast work who wants to deepen their science knowledge, or a life scientist with a master's degree or higher who wants to transition into full-time science journalism and has prior reporting on the life sciences.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Applicants must reside in an EMBC Member State",
        "The placement or placements must also occur in an EMBC Member State",
        "Placements must be in person; virtual placements are not eligible",
        "If Fellows undertake two or more placements, at least one must be in a different EMBC Member State than the others",
        "Applicants are not subject to any age restriction",
        "Journalists must demonstrate relevant experience of working as an employed or freelance journalist as their main occupation",
        "Journalists must provide samples of their published or broadcast work",
        "Journalists must show a genuine desire to broaden and deepen their knowledge of science, not a search for immediate publication opportunities",
        "Life scientists seeking to transition to full-time journalism must hold a master's degree or higher, preferably in a life sciences discipline",
        "Life scientists must demonstrate a genuine intention to move into journalism as a profession, with evidence of prior reporting on the life sciences or associated disciplines",
        "Personal blog posts, social media postings, or commentary and review articles in academic journals are not accepted as evidence of prior journalism",
        "Fellows are expected not to undertake other work during the fellowship and must not report on their host research institution during the fellowship term"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Daily subsistence stipend sized to the cost of living in the host country",
