      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The University of Manitoba awards one International Excellence Entrance Scholarship valued at $25,000 and two valued at $10,000 each to international high school graduates entering University 1 or any faculty, college or school with a direct entry option. The $25,000 award requires a minimum admission average of 90% across five senior level high school courses, while the two $10,000 awards require only the minimum admission requirements for the programme. Short-listed applicants are ranked first, second and third place using the award application and the admissions application. This is a separate application from the admissions application, although both must be completed.",
      "duration": "Entrance award for the first year of study",
      "deadline": "December 1 (2027/28 cycle)",
      "deadline_date": "2026-12-01",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Application for the 2027/28 International Excellence Entrance Scholarship is open now; the complete application and all required documentation must be received by December 1.",
      "eligibility_summary": "International high school graduates applying to University 1 or any faculty, college or school at the University of Manitoba with a direct entry option, enrolled full-time in the first year of study (minimum 80% course load). The $25,000 first-place award requires a 90% minimum admission average across five senior level courses plus demonstrated leadership; the two $10,000 awards require the minimum admission requirements for the programme plus demonstrated leadership.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Are international students",
        "Are enrolled full-time (minimum 80% course load) in the first year of study in University 1 or any faculty, college or school at the University of Manitoba with a direct entry option",
        "For the $25,000 award: have achieved a minimum admission average of 90% across five of the following senior level high school courses: Math, Biology, Chemistry, Physics, Computer Sciences, English, First Language Literature, Geography, History, Music and Visual Arts",
        "For the $10,000 awards: have achieved the minimum admission requirements for University 1 or any faculty, college or school with a direct entry option",
        "Have demonstrated strong leadership qualities and sustained, meaningful community involvement",
        "Have completed a University of Manitoba application for admission by December 1, including payment of the application fee"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Cash award of $25,000 for first place",
        "Cash award of $10,000 each for second and third place"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "One award valued at $25,000",
        "Two awards valued at $10,000 each",
        "Separate funding recognition from the general entrance award pool, which runs on a different deadline"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Submit a separate award application in addition to the admission application",
        "Nominate one recommender who is a current teacher or principal",
        "Ensure the recommender submits their letter by the December 1 deadline"
      ],
      "required_documents": [
        "Completed award application",
        "One letter of recommendation from a current teacher or principal, translated into English if required",
        "Completed University of Manitoba admission application with the application fee paid",
        "The documentation package the official page collectively refers to as 'all required documentation'"
      ],
      "application_method": [
