      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Faculty of Graduate Studies at Dalhousie University awards Killam Predoctoral Scholarships competitively to outstanding doctoral students across all disciplines, with a base value of $42,000 per year ($14,000 per term) for up to three years. The scholarship is open to both Canadian and international students in a full-time PhD at Dalhousie, and international recipients may only use the funds for study and research in Canada. Applicants who are not eligible to apply for a Tri-agency CGRS-D through Dalhousie in the current competition apply through the Faculty of Graduate Studies scholarship platform. The scholarship is supported by the Killam Trusts.",
      "duration": "Up to three years",
      "deadline": "Round one: October 16, 2026 at midnight AT. Round two: opens January 5, 2027, submissions due February 28, 2027 at midnight AT",
      "deadline_date": "2026-10-16",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Round one is open now and closes October 16, 2026 at midnight Atlantic Time; round two opens January 5, 2027 and closes February 28, 2027 at midnight AT. These rounds are stated for non-Tri-agency applicants.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Full-time doctoral (PhD) students at Dalhousie University, Canadian or international. Applicants must demonstrate exceptional academic achievement, strong research potential and a clear likelihood of contributing to the advancement of learning in their field, with character, ethical conduct and contributions to a respectful and inclusive community also considered. The award must be taken up no later than the 7th term of the PhD, and applicants must have spent fewer than six terms (24 months) in the PhD as of May 1 of the award year.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Enrolled in a full-time doctoral (PhD) degree at Dalhousie University",
        "Canadian or international student",
        "Demonstrates exceptional academic achievement, strong research potential and a clear likelihood of contributing to the advancement of learning in their field",
        "Award taken up no later than the 7th term in the PhD program",
        "Has spent less than six terms (24 months) in the PhD as of May 1 of the award year; for students who transferred or intend to transfer from a Master's to a PhD without completing the Master's, time-in-program begins at the transfer date"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Cash stipend of $42,000 per year ($14,000 per term) for up to three years",
        "Relocation travel reimbursement for new scholars relocating to Nova Scotia, capped at the lowest cost airfare by the most direct route",
        "Paid parental leave benefits for predoctoral Killam scholars who lack other paid parental leave support"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Base value $42,000 per year ($14,000 per term) for up to three years",
        "If a Tri-agency CGRS-D is awarded, the CGRS-D value of $40,000 per year is topped up to $48,000 per year ($16,000 per term) while both awards are held concurrently",
        "If the CGRS-D expires before the end of the award holder's fourth year in the PhD, Killam funding is extended into the remaining terms of the fourth year at $14,000 per term",
        "Relocation allowance reimbursing travel to Nova Scotia, not exceeding the lowest cost airfare available by the most direct route",
        "Paid parental leave benefits for predoctoral Killam scholars without access to other paid parental leave support",
        "Non-paid interruption of the award for up to 12 months for an approved leave of absence, with the end date extended by the leave duration"
