          "description": "Residential fellowship of the National Humanities Center, an independent nonprofit humanities institute in Durham, North Carolina, for mid-career and senior scholars in all areas of the humanities. The award provides an individually determined stipend intended to cover about half the Fellow's salary and pays round-trip travel to Durham for the Fellow and accompanying immediate family. It is a research and writing award: it does not fund tuition, postdoctoral positions or doctoral research, and it requires full-time residence at the Center.",
