            "The merits and overall credentials of the candidate, including academic and professional background",
            "Geographical distribution of applicants, taking into account the greater needs of the smaller and relatively less developed economies",
            "Applicants whose essays portray the highest potential for impact upon return to their countries of origin",
            "Gender diversity"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": "AUWCL and the OAS select awardees jointly on the criteria listed; no numeric weighting is published. Names of recipients are published in August and December at www.oas.org/scholarships.",
          "duration": "2-3 semesters for the LL.M. in International Human Rights and Humanitarian Law; 2-10 semesters for the LL.M. en Derechos Humanos y Derecho Humanitario; 9-18 months for the LL.M. in International Arbitration and Business Law. Classes begin in August for the Fall intake and January for the Spring intake.",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Sign the OAS/AUWCL Acceptance Form accepting the scholarship and its terms and conditions",
            "Maintain a GPA of at least equivalent to 3.0/4.0; low academic performance due to absence or course failure jeopardises retention",
            "Refrain from activities inconsistent with the status of an OAS scholarship recipient and comply with AUWCL academic guidelines and admission requirements",
            "Pay the remaining 50% of tuition and all other costs listed as the recipient's financial responsibility",
