            "general": "Questions on the scholarship: humanrightsllm@wcl.american.edu or arbitration@wcl.american.edu, subject 'OAS-AUWCL Scholarship Program'",
            "email": "llm@wcl.american.edu"
          },
          "description": "Under the OAS Partnerships Program for Education and Training (PAEC), the OAS General Secretariat and American University Washington College of Law award a 50% tuition waiver for the LL.M. in International Human Rights and Humanitarian Law (English and Spanish versions) and the LL.M. in International Arbitration and Business Law. The award is open to citizens and permanent legal residents of any active OAS member state other than the United States who hold a qualifying law degree and are admitted to an AUWCL LL.M. programme. Spring 2027 applications close on 1 November 2026 for residential study and 30 November 2026 for hybrid and online study. The award pays USD 30,972 of the USD 61,944 published total tuition and is subject to academic performance and the availability of funds; recipients pay the balance of tuition and all other costs and must return to work in an OAS member state for the duration of the scholarship.",
