      "duration": "2 to 3 months of in-residence research at a CALAS regional centre, starting between March and June 2027",
      "deadline": "Applications close 12 October 2026",
      "deadline_date": "2026-10-12",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Opened 11 August 2026, closes 12 October 2026; results notified 30 November 2026; fellowships begin between March and June 2027",
      "description": "CALAS, the Maria Sibylla Merian Centre for Advanced Latin American Studies, together with Bielefeld University, offers two research fellowships of two to three months for qualified researchers to work in residence at one of its Latin American regional centres: the Central America and the Caribbean centre in San Jose, Costa Rica, or the Andean centre located at FLACSO in Ecuador. Fellows sit within the transdisciplinary research programme \"Creando horizontes: aceleraciones, transformaciones, emergencias\". The successful applicant receives a competitive remuneration and reimbursement of the return airfare to the host centre; CALAS does not provide housing.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Academics and researchers in the social sciences and humanities with at least a completed doctorate, working operational Spanish, and a track record judged on scientific work, reputation, publications and research experience. Open to applicants of any nationality.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Training in the social sciences or humanities (formacion en Ciencias Sociales y Humanidades)",
        "Minimum academic degree of a doctorate (doctorado)",
        "Operational command of Spanish (dominio operativo del espanol)",
        "Ideally recognised nationally or internationally for the impact of the candidate's research in their field",
        "Experience in the field of research, evidenced by publications and reputation"
      ],
