      "description": "The Colombia Biodiversa scholarship fund of the Fundación Alejandro Ángel Escobar supports undergraduate and master's thesis research on the knowledge, conservation or sustainable use of Colombian biodiversity, from any area of knowledge. For its II-2026 call the foundation awards grants of up to three million five hundred thousand Colombian pesos per grantee, and the money may be used for equipment, which then belongs to the student. Only Colombian students enrolled at a recognised Colombian university or a formally recognised foreign university may apply, and the thesis must already be approved and be at the start or early stage of execution. One grantee in this call is additionally offered a placement at the AKAE Conservación reserve in the Colombian Orinoquía, covering field research, land and sea transport to the reserve, and accommodation and food on site.",
