      "english_requirement": null,
      "selection_notes": "Preselection is scored out of 100 base points: related professional experience 40% (more than 85 months 40 pts; 61-84 months 35 pts; 37-60 months 30 pts; 12-36 months 25 pts); academic average 40% (4.6-5.0 gives 40 pts; 4.3-4.5 gives 30 pts; 4.0-4.2 gives 20 pts); socioeconomic factor 20% (SISBEN IV categories A1-B7 give 20 pts, C1-C18 18 pts, D1-D3 16 pts, D4-D21 14 pts; where no SISBEN IV is available, estratos 1-2 give 12 pts, estratos 3-4 10 pts, estratos 5-6 8 pts). Up to 10 non-cumulative bonus points are available for working as a public official or as academic, teaching or research staff at a recognised higher-education institution; for a master's in a Chilean-government priority area; for membership of an ethnic community recognised by the Ministry of the Interior; for being certified a victim of the armed conflict through the RUV; and for having been a beneficiary of an ICETEX credit or administered fund. A minimum of 55 base points is required. Tiebreakers in order: highest academic average, then preference for women as recorded on the identity card, then earliest completed submission.",
