          "selection_criteria": [
            "Related professional experience, 40% of the base score",
            "Weighted undergraduate academic average, 40% of the base score, minimum 4.0/5.0",
            "Socioeconomic factor via SISBEN IV category or public-utility-bill estrato, 20% of the base score",
            "Bonus up to 10 points for public official or recognised higher-education academic, teaching or research staff status",
            "Bonus up to 10 points for a master's in a Chilean-government priority area",
            "Bonus up to 10 points for membership of an ethnic community recognised by the Colombian Ministry of the Interior",
            "Bonus up to 10 points for certification as a victim of the armed conflict through the RUV",
            "Bonus up to 10 points for having been a beneficiary of an ICETEX credit or administered fund",
            "Minimum of 55 base points to be considered for preselection"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": "Base score of 100 points weighted 40% experience, 40% academic average and 20% socioeconomic, with up to 10 non-cumulative bonus points for a maximum of 110. Tiebreakers in order: highest academic average, preference for women as recorded on the identity card, then earliest completed submission.",
          "duration": "Up to 24 months, matching the official duration of the selected master's programme, with a maximum of four academic semesters or six quarters of funding",
