          },
          "description": "The Programa de Becas de Cooperacion Sur-Sur - Republica de Chile is financed by the Agencia Chilena de Cooperacion Internacional para el Desarrollo (AGCID) and funds master's studies at accredited Chilean universities and higher-education institutions for professionals from Latin America and the Caribbean. For the 2027 academic year the scholarship covers 100% of matricula, tuition and graduation costs and pays a monthly maintenance allowance, together with insurance, study materials and thesis support. Applicants must already hold unconditional admission to one of the master's programmes listed in Anexo 1 of the call, and the final award is decided by AGCID's Selection Committee after national preselection by each country's focal point. Selection weighting explicitly favours low-income applicants, ethnic communities and victims of the armed conflict.",
