      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "Asian University for Women is an independent international women's university in Chittagong, Bangladesh, chartered by the Parliament of Bangladesh in 2006. Its Financial Aid Committee awards full and partial scholarships against demonstrated financial need, and the university states that 85% of students receive scholarship support. A full scholarship covers tuition, room and board, books, course supplies, healthcare and student activities. The university waives all fees and covers all costs for students who are first in their family to enter university and for entrants through the Pathways for Promise programme.",
      "duration": "Financial aid is assessed before the start of each academic programme and continued year by year; students must maintain a CGPA of 2.5 each year to retain it.",
