      "selection_notes": "Admission is need-blind; the university states it seeks women who show high potential, leadership qualities and motivation regardless of economic background. Financial aid is then assessed by the Financial Aid Committee, which considers family composition, parental education and income, earnings of other family members, number of non-earning dependants, movable and immovable property, community assessment of the family's socio-economic status, the cost of schooling attended by the student or her siblings, the socio-economic situation of the area of residence, and luxury items owned. The Committee may investigate and verify all submitted information.",
      "best_fit": "Women from low-income households in South, Southeast and West Asia and the Middle East who have completed secondary school with 60% or better and cannot afford the USD 15,000 annual cost of attendance, including first-in-family university entrants and Pathways for Promise students.",
