      "status": "upcoming",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The New Zealand Refugee Health Scholarship pays health-related study costs for former refugees and their children already living in New Zealand. The programme was developed in 2025 by the National Leadership and Coordination Service, a joint function of MBIE, the Ministry of Health and Health New Zealand, and is administered through Universities New Zealand. Each successful applicant receives up to NZD 25,000 for one academic year, made up of up to NZD 5,000 toward course-related costs and NZD 20,000 as a living stipend. The 2027 intake window ran from 1 July 2026 to 1 October 2026 and has closed; the programme is confirmed multi-year and runs annually.",
      "duration": "One academic year; recipients must reapply each year",
      "deadline": "1 October 2026 (2027 intake, now closed)",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "The 2027 intake opened 1 July 2026 and closed 1 October 2026. The first intake opened 15 October 2025. The programme is described as multi-year and annual, so the next window is expected to open in July 2027, but no 2028 closing date is published.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to former refugees and the children of refugees who resettled in New Zealand through the UNHCR Quota Programme, the Convention Refugee pathway, or the Community Organisation Refugee Sponsorship Category, who are studying a health-related qualification in New Zealand.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a former refugee or the child of a refugee",
        "Have resettled in New Zealand through the UNHCR Quota Programme, the Convention Refugee pathway, or the Community Organisation Refugee Sponsorship Category",
        "Be studying or intending to study a health-related qualification in New Zealand"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Up to NZD 5,000 toward course-related costs, covering 50% of tuition fees, compulsory student services fees and required equipment",
        "NZD 20,000 living stipend, regardless of living situation or location of study"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Up to NZD 25,000 total for one academic year",
        "Living stipend paid regardless of where the scholar lives or studies in New Zealand",
        "Tailored mentoring support reported alongside the programme"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Must pass all first semester courses to receive second semester funding",
        "Must submit a satisfactory report and an academic transcript at the end of each semester",
        "Must reapply each year to be considered for further funding",
        "Must take up the scholarship in the year it is offered",
        "Must apply through Universities New Zealand using the Community Force platform"
      ],
      "required_documents": [
        "Completed application form on the Universities New Zealand Community Force platform",
        "Documents uploaded through the Community Force platform as specified in the application guidance"
      ],
      "application_method": [
        "Apply online through Universities New Zealand once applications open",
        "Complete the application form and upload the required documents on the Universities New Zealand Community Force platform",
        "Optional: attend an information webinar, which the programme ran in June and September 2026"
      ],
      "english_requirement": "Not stated as a separate requirement on the awarding body's page; study is in New Zealand, so English ability is implied by enrolment in a New Zealand qualification.",
      "selection_notes": "The selection committee assesses each application on the impact of the scholar on refugee health outcomes, the impact of the scholar on the refugee health workforce, the impact of the scholarship on the scholar, and the likelihood of successfully attaining the qualification. Immigration New Zealand notes the programme particularly values scholars with cultural knowledge and indigenous language skills.",
