          "description": "Study in Saudi is the Ministry of Education's official platform for international students, researchers and professional learners, covering study, research and training at Saudi universities together with the educational visa pathway. Its Study Visa & Pathways page defines three funding routes: Full Scholarships, which the Ministry of Education describes as 'Tuition, housing & living - all covered'; Partial Scholarships, covering part of tuition costs; and paid self-funded study programmes. Students apply by submitting an admission application to the institution they wish to attend; the institution reviews it and issues an admission decision, and the Ministry of Education then completes final admission procedures. The Ministry publishes an application window for international and resident students each semester, and the currently published window for the Second Semester Academic Calendar 2026 closes on 6 October 2026.",
