      "description": "The \"World in Serbia\" project is a Government of the Republic of Serbia scholarship programme run by the Ministry of Education for candidates from member and observer states of the Non-Aligned Movement, covering candidates from Africa, Asia, Central and South America. Scholarship holders study free of charge at public higher education institutions founded by the Republic of Serbia, in all study programmes and at all study levels, after a preparatory Serbian-language year. The February 2026 official call covers Serbian-language study in the 2026/2027 academic year and enrolment at Serbian higher education institutions in the 2027/2028 academic year, with applications due no later than 1 June 2026.",
      "duration": "One year of Serbian-language preparation (2026/2027) followed by the enrolled degree cycle beginning in the 2027/2028 academic year",
      "deadline": "No later than 1 June 2026 for the 2026 call; the call is reissued annually, so the next cycle is expected to close around the same date in 2027",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "Serbian language study in the 2026/2027 academic year, then enrolment in higher education institutions founded by the Republic of Serbia in the 2027/2028 academic year",
      "eligibility_summary": "Citizens of Non-Aligned Movement member or observer states, nominated by the competent authority of their country, with age limits of under 21 for first-level studies, under 25 for second-level studies and under 35 for third-level (doctoral) studies, an overall 80% pass grade at undergraduate and master level, English or Serbian at A1 level, and good health.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Citizen of a member state or observer state of the Non-Aligned Movement",
        "Nominated by the competent authority of the participating state in the Project",
        "Younger than 21 years old for enrolment in first-level studies",
        "Younger than 25 years old for second-level studies (master's, specialist and specialist vocational)",
        "Younger than 35 years old for third-level studies (doctoral)",
        "Overall pass grade of at least 80% at undergraduate and master level",
        "Knowledge of English at least at A1 level, or Serbian at least at A1 level on arrival",
        "In overall good health, verified by the Student Health Care Institute of Belgrade"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "Free tuition at higher education institutions founded by the Republic of Serbia",
        "Accommodation and meals in the student standard (student centre) system",
        "Monthly financial allowance",
        "Health insurance"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "Free of charge study (tuition) at all study programmes and levels at institutions founded by the Republic of Serbia",
        "Accommodation and food in the student standard system of the Republic of Serbia (Belgrade, Novi Sad, Nis, Kragujevac)",
        "Financial scholarship of RSD 18,000 per month",
        "Health insurance",
        "Free intensive Serbian-language courses before enrolment",
        "Assistance with translation and recognition of prior diplomas by the Ministry of Education and the Qualifications Agency"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Pass the Serbian language examination before commencing higher education studies",
        "Pass the entrance exam at the chosen faculty and complete enrolment",
        "Earn a minimum of 37 ECTS credits during the academic year for budget-funded re-enrolment",
        "Regularly attend classes and sit the prescribed examinations",
        "Obtain and maintain temporary residence status in the Republic of Serbia",
        "Inform the Ministry of Education of material changes to scholarship status within 30 days",
        "Return to the country that nominated them upon completion of studies"
