      "funding_period": null,
      "description": "The Cusanuswerk is the talent development body of the Catholic Church in Germany and funds doctoral candidates through its Promotionsförderung. The current round (Verfahren I-2027) accepts registrations until 1 November 2026 with a selection decision in March 2027. Funding is a parent-independent stipend of EUR 1,750 plus a EUR 100 research cost allowance, with optional health-insurance, child-care and family supplements and possible support for research stays abroad; the official page states no tuition-fee coverage. Foreign applicants must be admitted to a doctorate at a recognised university in Germany and prove German at C1, and applicants from developing or emerging countries are referred to the KAAD before applying to Cusanuswerk.",
