          "description": "The University of Innsbruck's doctoral scholarship provides a monthly allowance of EUR 1,120 for a maximum of 24 months and is described by the University as start-up, interim, bridge or final financing for doctoral students. It is granted in six-month blocks with an interim progress report confirmed by the dissertation supervisor, and the 24-month period may be interrupted twice for no more than six months each. Applicants must be enrolled as regular students registered for continuation with a registered dissertation, and must show excellent academic success or scientific achievements. The University aims to award at least half of the available funding to women and prioritises applicants in its main research areas.",
