          "description": "The Government of Ireland International Education Scholarship, managed by the Higher Education Authority and funded by the Government of Ireland in partnership with Irish higher education institutions, awards 60 scholarships a year to international students who wish to study at NFQ levels 9 or 10 in Ireland. Each award comprises a EUR 10,000 stipend for one year of full-time study plus a full fee waiver from the host institution for that year. Applicants must be domiciled outside the EU/EEA, Switzerland and the UK, must already hold an offer from an eligible Irish institution and submit proof of admission, must upload two references, and may submit only one application per cycle. Applications pass institutional eligibility screening and shortlisting before an independent panel assessment. The 2026 deadline was 5pm Irish time on 12 March 2026.",
