      "description": "Hungarian bilateral state scholarships are awarded under scientific and educational cooperation agreements signed by the governments of two countries, with the Hungarian side offering places to foreign students, researchers or lecturers in Hungarian higher education institutions and in scientific or art institutions. Tempus Public Foundation, a background organisation of the Hungarian Ministry of Culture and Innovation, is Hungary's national scholarship office. Applicants can apply either through nomination by their home country's national scholarship office or by submitting an individual application, and in both cases they must also submit into Tempus Public Foundation's online system. Applications undergo a formal eligibility check and are then scored by Tempus Public Foundation's external experts against several professional criteria.",
