      "description": "The Hungarian Diaspora Scholarship supports foreign students with Hungarian roots to study in Hungarian higher education institutions. It is administered by the Tempus Public Foundation and its website states it is a fully covered scholarship. Applications run once a year through the DreamApply system, with a detailed selection process of technical check, validation of recommendations, institutional admissions and entrance examinations, evaluation of motivation letters, and a final Diaspora Scholarship Committee session. Applicants need a recommendation letter from a Diaspora organisation or the Hungarian diplomatic representation in their territory, must prove they finished secondary school in a foreign country, and may also apply with dual Hungarian citizenship. Hungarian language is not an application requirement except for Hungarian-taught programmes, and a one-year Hungarian preparatory course is available.",
