      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Lee Kuan Yew Scholarship is described by the Public Service Commission as the premier postgraduate scholarship in Singapore. It was set up in 1991 by the Tanjong Pagar Citizens' Consultative Committee with public funding to commemorate Lee Kuan Yew's contributions to Singapore. Recipients receive full tuition fee coverage and an annual allowance of S$50,000 for up to two years of Master's study or up to five years of PhD study, may study at local or overseas universities with no restriction on course of study, and carry no bond.",
      "duration": "Up to 2 years of Master's study or up to 5 years of PhD study",
      "deadline": "The page states 'Applications for Lee Kuan Yew (LKY) Scholarship for the year of 2026 is currently closed.' A separate Application Process section on the same page says 'All applications must be submitted via the Gateway application portal by 28 February 2026.' No date is published for the next cycle.",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "Annual cycle; the most recent published deadline was 28 February 2026 and no future date is published as at 2026-10-04",
