        "Applicants and hosts are expected to have consulted and worked together before submitting"
      ],
      "selection_notes": "Each application is reviewed by two members of the EAN Education Committee with final approval by the Education Committee Chair, using a scoring sheet combining a score for the application, a score for the CV and a score for the overall impression. Applicants are asked to explain the gains expected from the fellowship in the context of their usual practice, which EAN states is a major factor in the rating. At most 10%, and no more than two per country, of accepted applicants may come from Corresponding Institutional Member countries or low and lower-middle income sub-Saharan African countries.",
      "notes": "Travel costs are reimbursed only after the fellowship ends, on receipt of the final report, a confirmation from the host mentor and the evaluation forms. From 2027 one grant of nine weeks is reserved for members working in EAN Full or Corresponding Institutional Member countries, defined as low, lower-middle and upper-middle income countries, funded by an endowed fellowship from Prof. Abhijit Chaudhuri's family. Five additional fellowships are available to RRFS members from Ukraine. The grant should ideally be used by a fellow who knows the language of the host department, because not all patient rounds can be held in English.",
