      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The EAN Research Fellowship supports European neurologists to carry out research at an academic neurological department outside their country of residence, at EUR 2,000 per month plus up to EUR 500 of travel costs reimbursed after the fellowship. It runs two tracks: Research Training Fellowships of typically 12 months and no less than six months, and Research Experience Fellowships of typically six months and no less than three months. The annual budget covers 72 fellowship months, usually four to five training and two to three experience awards. Applications for 2027 ran from 1 June to 31 August 2026 and are now closed, with results due by the end of November 2026.",
      "duration": "Research Training Fellowship: typically 12 months, minimum 6. Research Experience Fellowship: typically 6 months, minimum 3",
      "deadline": "31 August (annual close; the 2027 window ran 1 June - 31 August 2026)",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "recurring",
      "application_period": "1 June - 31 August each year",
      "funding_amount": 2000,
      "funding_currency": "EUR",
      "funding_period": "per month",
      "eligibility_summary": "Applicants must hold an active EAN RRFS or Full membership, be affiliated with a European academic neurological department, be fluent in English or the host country's language, and be either an RRFS member with more than two years of neurology residency in an EAN Full Institutional Member country or a Full member in such a country within five years of their latest neurology degree.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Active EAN RRFS or Full membership; approval can take up to 10 working days, so membership should be applied for at least three weeks before the deadline",
        "Affiliated with a European academic neurological department",
        "RRFS member working in an EAN Full Institutional Member country with more than two years of clinical neurology training at the time of the event",
        "Full member working in an EAN Full Institutional Member country, up to a maximum of five years after the latest degree in neurology",
        "Fluent in English or in the local language of the hosting country",
        "Research work must be carried out at a European academic neurological department outside the applicant's country of residence"
      ],
      "coverage": [
