      ],
      "selection_notes": "Each application is reviewed by two experts drawn from the EAN Scientific Panels and one Education Committee member, with results communicated by the end of November 2026. The public scoring sheet applies nine separate scores: four for the project (originality, feasibility, usefulness for career, methods), two for the candidate (CV, publications), two for the proposed host (department, supervisor) and one for the overall impression. Feasibility, methods, host department, own CV and overall impression carry more weight than the other components.",
      "notes": "Travel costs are reimbursed only after the fellowship ends, against the fellow's final report and the evaluation forms from both the fellow and the host mentor. Successful fellowships may be applied retroactively from 1 September 2026 where the stay started earlier. Previous awardees receive no preference.",
