      "name": "Beca al Talento Académico Internacional",
      "country": "Mexico",
      "region": "North America",
      "degree_levels": "Bachelor's",
      "funding_type": "Partial tuition waiver",
      "program_type": "University international merit scholarship",
      "official_source": "Tecnológico de Monterrey",
      "official_source_url": "https://tec.mx/es/profesional/becas/internacional",
      "catalogue_url": "https://tec.mx/es/profesional/becas",
      "official_updates_url": "https://tec.mx/es/profesional/becas/internacional",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Beca al Talento Académico Internacional is the Tecnológico de Monterrey scholarship for international applicants, reserved for candidates coming from secondary schools in a named group of Latin American and Caribbean countries. It recognises students with an outstanding academic record and can award support of between 40% and 60% of the tuition cost, valid for the campus to which the applicant has been admitted. The call is published once a year for new entrants to the August–December semester, requires a minimum average of 90/100 in bachillerato or high school study, and is limited to candidates under 21 years of age at the time of application. Applicants must be admitted to a professional programme starting in August 2027 and must present the Prueba de Aptitud Académica with a minimum score of 1,360 points, or an equivalent SAT or ACT score converted to that scale.",
      "duration": "Entrance scholarship for a professional degree beginning in August 2027, subject to annual conservation requirements",
      "deadline": "January 22, 2027 (Cierre de convocatoria). Applications open from August 24, 2026; admission deadline January 20, 2027; results February 18, 2027",
      "deadline_date": "2027-01-22",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Applications are accepted from August 24, 2026 and the call closes on January 22, 2027. The general admission deadline is January 20, 2027, although some programmes have earlier deadlines of December 10, 2026 or January 13, 2027, and a second PAA sitting may be taken up to January 16, 2027.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Candidates in their final year of, or who have completed, bachillerato or high school study in a named Latin American or Caribbean country, who are under 21 at the time of application, hold an average of at least 90/100, have been admitted to a professional programme at the Tecnológico de Monterrey starting in August 2027, and score at least 1,360 on the PAA or the equivalent converted SAT or ACT.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be applying from an institution in one of the listed countries: El Salvador, Colombia, Bolivia, Nicaragua, Peru, Costa Rica, Panama, Dominican Republic, Brazil, Argentina, Chile, Venezuela, Honduras, Ecuador, Guatemala, Paraguay, Uruguay, Cuba, Trinidad and Tobago, Puerto Rico or Haiti",
        "Be in the last year of bachillerato or high school, or have already completed those studies",
        "Be under 21 years of age at the time of application",
