      "description": "The Janelia Research Campus of the Howard Hughes Medical Institute runs two fully-funded graduate training programmes with Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine, in neuroscience and in cross-disciplinary biology (XDBio). Students apply directly to the Johns Hopkins Neuroscience programme in the autumn, naming one to four Janelia group leaders in the Statement of Interest; the published deadline for completed applications including letters of recommendation is December 3, and decisions are communicated by April 15. Janelia states that graduate scholars are fully supported financially by their labs and the graduate programme during their research, with a first-year Johns Hopkins stipend plus health insurance while in Baltimore, and a Janelia Graduate Scholar stipend, health insurance and travel support while at Janelia.",
