          "description": "The Janelia Research Campus, part of the Howard Hughes Medical Institute, runs two fully-funded graduate training programmes with Johns Hopkins University School of Medicine: neuroscience and cross-disciplinary biology (XDBio). Students apply directly to the Johns Hopkins neuroscience programme in the autumn, naming one to four Janelia group leaders in the Statement of Interest; the deadline for completed applications including letters of recommendation is December 3 and decisions are notified by April 15. Janelia states that graduate scholars are fully supported financially by their labs and the graduate programme during their research, with a first-year Johns Hopkins stipend, health insurance, payment of all programmatic travel costs and free housing at Janelia during rotations, followed by a Janelia Graduate Scholar stipend while based at Janelia.",
