      "description": "Mexico's Ministry of Foreign Affairs, through AMEXCID, invites foreign nationals to study in Mexico under the Becas de Excelencia del Gobierno de México para Extranjeros. The 2026 call was offered to more than 170 countries and covered 90 Mexican higher education institutions whose programmes are registered in the National Postgraduate System. Benefits stated in the official call include a monthly stipend of four times the UMA for undergraduate and master's mobility and of five times the UMA for doctoral and postdoctoral research fellowships, enrolment and tuition fees, health insurance through the Mexican Social Security Institute, exemption from Mexican visa fees, international airfare in economy class on successful completion, and domestic transportation to the host city.",
      "duration": "Up to 12 months for undergraduate and master's mobility, up to 24 months for a master's degree, and 6 to 12 months for doctoral and postdoctoral research fellowships",
