      "description": "The Laboratorio de Investigacion para el Desarrollo del Ecuador, in collaboration with the data-education company DataCamp, opened applications for the Becas El Quantificador 2026-2027. The programme aims to widen access to data training and support people with economic need, commitment and motivation to study independently. Successful candidates receive a free DataCamp licence, access to programming and data-science courses, and an invitation to a four-session course on 28 and 29 October and 4 and 5 November 2026. The programme page states an annual budget of USD 6,000 and location across the whole of Ecuador, with beneficiaries described as tertiary-level students and underemployed workers of limited means. In the 2026-2027 round LIDE states there are no restrictions by nationality or place of residence, and previous DataCamp scholarship holders of LIDE may apply again.",
