      "description": "The Directorate of the Instituto Riva-Aguero, a research institute of the Pontificia Universidad Catolica del Peru, has published its 2027 research support call. Two modalities are offered: an individual research grant of PEN 10,000 and a group research grant of PEN 20,000, each for a maximum of ten months between 2 November 2026 and 3 September 2027. Project topics must fall within the institute's five research lines, covering Peruvian and Latin American history, the state and social processes, literature, art and cultural practices, tangible and intangible heritage, and philosophy, science and education in Peru. Winners must publish their results in a Scopus or Web of Science indexed journal or in an academic-press book, with their affiliation to the Instituto Riva-Aguero stated explicitly, and the individual modality requires the holder to supervise an undergraduate student assistant, which the institute presents as a way of promoting young researchers.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Ordinary members of the Instituto Riva-Aguero; associate members who hold a doctorate and are contracted PUCP teaching staff (TPA, TPC or TC) who have taught at least one two-credit course in the last four regular semesters; and affiliated or honorary members who hold a doctorate and form part of a research group and have no pending academic activity, article or research owed to the institute. For the group modality, any study or research group registered and approved by the institute's council is eligible.",
