      ],
      "english_requirement": "B2",
      "selection_notes": "Candidates are scored on a 0 to 20 scale by the doctoral programme's own Directing Committee against four criteria: the doctoral research project, academic and research experience, the motivation letter, and the recommendation letters. A score of 18 or higher (90th percentile) is required to reach the selection stage. Selection is then made by the VRI on the strength of the final merit ranking, in two rounds: one grant for the best-ranked candidate of each doctoral programme that has eligible candidates, then the second-ranked candidates up to a maximum of two grantees per doctoral programme. Results are final and not appealable.",
      "best_fit": "A master's graduate anywhere in the world who will enter a PUCP doctorate full time, has a named PUCP thesis adviser, holds English at CEFR B2 or above, and can commit to the exclusive dedication the programme demands.",
      "notes": "The programme excludes PUCP full-time teaching staff and anyone who during doctoral studies holds a full-time executive, research or administrative post inside or outside PUCP. It also excludes the doctorates of Centrum PUCP and the Consortium of Universities' Doctorado en Gestión Estratégica. Applicants who have not graduated from PUCP receive differentiated registration-fee discounts between 10 August and 18 September and between 19 September and 12 October. The maintenance allowance is granted under the figure of a scholarship and is therefore not subject to withholdings.",
