          "description": "The PUCP Beca Doctoral is a support programme from the university's Vice-Rectorate for Research and School of Postgraduate Studies for candidates entering a PUCP doctorate with exclusive full-time dedication to a high-quality research project. It covers academic fees and enrolment, pays a monthly maintenance allowance of four thousand soles for twelve renewable months, and adds accident insurance, institutional affiliation and a campus workspace. The grant lasts one calendar year and may be renewed up to twice, and candidates must hold unconditional admission from the 2027-1 process. Applications run from 10 August to 4 November 2026.",
          "program_type": "Doctoral scholarship",
