      "description": "The scholarship is set up and funded by the International School of Medicine of Zhejiang University and is open only to doctoral candidates in medical programmes at that school, whose teaching base is in Yiwu, in central Zhejiang Province. The official page sets out two full-scholarship tiers (A and B): both exempt tuition and provide free on-campus accommodation and comprehensive medical insurance for international students, with a monthly living allowance of RMB 7,000 under tier A and RMB 3,500 under tier B. Applicants apply by emailing the school's scholarship application form and uploading the same form into the Zhejiang University international student application system. The page is a standing terms document; the application deadline it currently publishes is 28 February for the cycle whose results are read out in late July or early August.",
