      "selection_notes": "The university states that applicants are selected on the basis of research ability, academic performance, language level and video interview performance (学校将根据申请人的研究能力、学业成绩、语言水平和视频面试情况等因素综合考虑择优录取). No minimum English test score is published on the scholarship page; it refers applicants to the Zhejiang University international student (doctoral) admission guide for admission-level language requirements. Recipients are subject to an annual scholarship review, and scholarship status can be suspended or cancelled if the review is failed. If a holder suspends studies for serious illness they must return home at their own travel cost; with university approval the scholarship entitlement can be retained for up to one year but the living allowance stops during the suspension, and suspension for other reasons forfeits the entitlement. The living allowance is paid monthly from the date of enrolment: a full month if registered on or before the 15th, half a month if after the 15th; it continues over official holidays and can be paid retrospectively on return, but is suspended for that month if a holder is absent from registration or leaves without leave or is absent from class for more than two weeks for non-health reasons.",
