      "description": "Fu Jen Catholic University's International Student Admissions Office publishes a set of Fu Jen-funded scholarships for newly admitted international students. For doctoral degree programmes the university states that the scholarship runs for eight consecutive semesters from the semester of admission, that tuition and miscellaneous fees are waived or reduced as part of the award, and that the holder receives a stipend of NT$50,000 per semester paid out in monthly instalments of NT$10,000. The scholarship is requested inside the admission application itself rather than through a separate form. Applications for Spring 2027 are open until 14 October 2026, and the first round for Fall 2027 opens on 15 October 2026.",
      "duration": "Eight consecutive semesters for doctoral degree programmes, beginning in the semester of admission; for undergraduate and Master's programmes the university publishes different, shorter terms (see notes)",
