      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "description": "The Pragati Scholarship Scheme is implemented by the All India Council for Technical Education for girl students taking admission to AICTE-approved technical institutions at degree level. Each award is a lump sum of Rs 50,000 per year of study, given for up to four years for students admitted to the first year of a degree course and up to three years for degree students admitted through lateral entry. Eligibility is limited to female students from families with an annual income below Rs 8 lakh, with up to two girls per family eligible. The scheme is applied for through the National Scholarship Portal, which lists the award as open for academic year 2026-27 with student applications closing on 31 October 2026.",
      "duration": "For every year of study: up to 4 years for first-year degree entrants and up to 3 years for degree entrants admitted through lateral entry",
      "deadline": "31 October 2026 for student applications for academic year 2026-27",
      "deadline_date": "2026-10-31",
      "deadline_precision": "exact",
      "application_period": "Academic year 2026-27: scheme open from 1 June 2026, student applications open until 31 October 2026, with defective application, institute and district verification windows running to 15 and 30 November 2026",
      "eligibility_summary": "Girl students only, up to two per family, with family income below Rs 8 lakh per annum, admitted to the first year of an AICTE-approved undergraduate degree programme or to the second year through lateral entry. Renewal requires admission to the subsequent year of the same course.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Only female students are eligible",
        "Up to two girls per family",
        "Family income below Rs 8 lakh per annum",
        "Admitted to an undergraduate degree level programme or course in an AICTE-approved institution",
