      "description": "Run since 1997 by the Arab Fund for Economic and Social Development, the Fellowship for Academic Excellence sends Arab PhD holders to prestigious foreign universities to conduct advanced research and/or teach. The Fund states that since its inception the programme has awarded about 191 fellowships to Arab researchers of different nationalities and fields. Support is described as full: a fixed maintenance allowance, round-trip airfare for the beneficiary and eligible family members, and health and personal accident insurance for the whole stay. The grant is usually awarded for twelve months, with shorter periods considered only in very special cases, and applications are accepted on a continuous basis provided they reach the Fund at least a year before the intended start date at the host university.",
