      "application_period": "Yearly, on a first-come, first-served basis while places remain; 10 fellowships available. The official page shows Call Status: 'The call is currently open'.",
      "duration": "3 to 6 months, extendable upon recommendation from the host institution",
      "description": "OIC-COMSTECH and member institutions of its Consortium of Excellence jointly offer short- to medium-term research placements for young researchers from OIC member states in agriculture, food security and related fields. The fellowship covers eight thematic areas: plant biotechnology; human nutrition; the water-food-energy nexus; food science and technology; nutraceuticals and the food-medicine continuum; agro-business, trade and food value chains; agricultural technology and innovations; and neglected food crops. Only 10 fellowships are available and they are awarded on a first-come, first-served basis subject to eligibility, so the call functions as a rolling award rather than a fixed-deadline competition. COMSTECH covers low-cost international airfare and visa fees where applicable, and host institutions are expected to provide accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to citizens of all OIC member states. Applicants need at least a Bachelor's degree, with a Master's or PhD an asset, and an academic background in food security, agriculture, food science, food safety or a related field. Experience requirements differ by degree level, and applicants must be fluent in English and available full-time for the whole fellowship.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a citizen of an OIC member state (the page explicitly names Afghanistan, Bangladesh, Benin, Burkina Faso, Chad, Comoros, Djibouti, Gambia, Guinea, Guinea-Bissau, Mali, Mauritania, Mozambique, Niger, Senegal, Sierra Leone, Somalia, Sudan, Togo, Uganda and Yemen among the OIC least-developed countries)",
        "Hold at least a Bachelor's degree; a Master's or PhD is an asset",
        "Hold an academic background in food security, agriculture, food science, food safety or another related field",
        "Bachelor's degree holders: at least 5 years of substantive professional experience, preferably in a government or national research institution, after university graduation",
        "Master's or PhD holders: at least 3 years of professional experience, preferably in a government or national research institution",
        "Be fluent and proficient in English, with excellent written and oral communication skills",
        "Be available full-time, 40 hours per week, for the entire duration of the fellowship",
        "Be aged 35 or under for Master's/PhD holders, or 45 or under for post-doctoral researchers"
      ],
