      "english_requirement": "Fluent and proficient in English, with excellent written and oral communication skills. The fellowship is conducted in the English language.",
      "selection_notes": "Awards are made by OIC-COMSTECH together with the Joint Scholarship Committee of the host institutions, based on scientific merit. Only 10 fellowships are available and they are awarded first-come, first-served subject to eligibility. The page also states that COMSTECH accepts applications on a yearly basis and selects candidates against pre-approved selection criteria.",
      "best_fit": "Early-career researchers and professionals from OIC member states who hold a Master's or PhD (or a Bachelor's plus five years' experience) in food security, agriculture, food science, food safety, plant biotechnology, nutrition or agri-business, are under 35 (or 45 for post-docs), and can commit three to six full-time months.",
      "notes": "This is a first-come, first-served fellowship with only 10 places, so delay is effectively equivalent to missing the award. The official page does not state a fixed closing date, so deadline_precision is recorded as rolling and deadline_date is null. The page itemises airfare, visa fees, accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring, but it does not explicitly state that tuition or enrolment fees are paid, so tuition_coverage is recorded as false and fully_funded as false rather than inferred. Eligibility spans OIC member states across Africa, the Middle East and Asia; the region is set to Africa because the explicitly enumerated OIC least-developed-country list on the page is predominantly African.",
