          "description": "OIC-COMSTECH, together with member institutions of its Consortium of Excellence, offers short- to medium-term research placements for young researchers from OIC member states in agriculture, food security and related areas. The stated rationale is that food insecurity remains a pressing global issue in many OIC countries, where economic instability, climate change, conflict and malnutrition have disrupted food systems, and that addressing this requires investment in research, knowledge transfer and capacity building. Eight thematic areas are offered: plant biotechnology, human nutrition, the water-food-energy nexus, food science and technology, nutraceuticals and the food-medicine continuum, agro-business and food value chains, agricultural technology and innovations, and neglected food crops. Ten fellowships are available per round and are awarded first-come, first-served. COMSTECH covers low-cost international airfare and visa fees where applicable, while host institutions provide accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring.",
          "program_type": "Inter-governmental research fellowship",
          "region": "Africa",
          "coverage": "All OIC member states; host country varies as placements are at OIC research and higher-education institutions across member states",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
