      "description": "COMSTECH, together with key centres of excellence in OIC countries, runs a training scholarship in virology and vaccine technology for young scientists from OIC member states. Selected fellows spend three months at a relevant centre of excellence in another OIC country, and the aim is to strengthen research and development capacity among scientists early in their careers and to build linkages for further collaboration. Training themes include the epidemiology of viral diseases, biorisk assessment and the identification of zoonotic sources, development of diagnostics and therapeutics against viral outbreaks, real-time data collection on the spread of viral infections and preparation for future outbreaks, and vaccine development. COMSTECH provides international low-cost airfare, and host institutions are expected to provide subsistence, supervision and mentoring.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to citizens of OIC member states who are young scientists employed by a research institution in an OIC country, holding at least an M.S. in Biomedical or Health Sciences for graduate-level application or a Ph.D. in Biomedical or Health Sciences for post-graduate-level application. Age limits are 35 for graduate studies and 45 for post-graduate studies, with preference given to women scientists, those early in their research career, and those working in OIC least-developed countries or Muslim-majority areas in non-OIC states.",
