      "best_fit": "Biomedical or health-science scientists aged 35 or under (45 for post-doctorals), citizens of OIC member states and employed at an OIC research institution, who hold an M.S. or PhD in a biomedical or health science and can spend three months at a centre of excellence in a different OIC country.",
      "notes": "Applicants may apply for only one COMSTECH programme per calendar year, so this cannot be combined with another COMSTECH fellowship in the same year. The page states COMSTECH provides international low-cost airfare and that host institutions are expected to provide subsistence, supervision and mentoring; it does not state that tuition or enrolment fees are paid, so tuition_coverage is recorded as false and fully_funded as false. Eligibility spans OIC member states across Africa, the Middle East and Asia; region is set to Middle East because the awarding body's centres of excellence and the programme's framing are OIC-wide with heavy Middle East membership. The page lists awardee lists for cycle-1, cycle-2 and cycle-3, confirming this is a recurring annual cycle, and no closing date is published for the current round.",
