      "duration": "6 to 12 months, extendable upon recommendation of the host institution",
      "description": "COMSTECH and member institutions of its Consortium of Excellence jointly offer research fellowships to young women researchers, scientists and engineers in OIC countries so they can spend six to twelve months at a relevant centre of excellence in an OIC member state. The stated purpose is to enhance the research and development capacity of promising women researchers and engineers from OIC least-developed countries who are at the beginning of their research career, and to help them build linkages for further collaboration in their fields. The field of study is natural sciences, applied sciences, engineering and technology. COMSTECH bears international low-cost airfare, and host institutions are expected to provide accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to young women scientists and engineers who are citizens of an OIC least-developed country, or who are employed by a research institution in an OIC country, and who hold at least an M.S. or equivalent for graduate studies or a Ph.D. for post-graduate studies, or who are engaged in active research. Age limits are 35 for graduate studies and 45 for post-graduate studies, with preference for women scientists at the beginning of their research career in OIC least-developed countries.",
