      "best_fit": "Women researchers and engineers from OIC least-developed countries - 14 of the 15 named countries are African - who hold an M.S. or PhD (or are actively researching), are aged 35 or under (45 or under for post-doctorals), and can commit six to twelve months to a placement at a centre of excellence.",
      "notes": "This is a rolling all-year call, so there is no deadline to miss, but it is not a guaranteed award: selection is by scientific merit. The page itemises airfare, accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring but does not state that tuition or enrolment fees are paid, so tuition_coverage is recorded as false and fully_funded as false. The named OIC least-developed countries are Afghanistan, Benin, Burkina Faso, Chad, Comoros, Guinea, Guinea-Bissau, Mali, Mozambique, Niger, Sierra Leone, Somalia, The Gambia, Togo, Mauritania and Uganda, of which 14 are African, so the region is recorded as Africa. The awarding body requires one COMSTECH programme application per calendar year, so this cannot be combined with the other COMSTECH fellowships recorded in this shard.",
