      "english_requirement": "Applications must be submitted in English. Supporting documents in languages other than English must be submitted with both the original and an English translation by an accredited language translation provider. An English language proficiency certificate such as IELTS or TOEFL is an optional supporting document where applicable.",
      "selection_notes": "Only complete applications for eligible programmes, submitted before the deadline, in English and in accordance with the guidelines, are considered; missing mandatory documents make an application incomplete and ineligible. Only shortlisted applicants are contacted. IUCEA reserves the right to verify any information submitted, and providing false, misleading or incomplete information can lead to automatic disqualification or withdrawal of an award. Female applicants, persons with disabilities and applicants from other disadvantaged backgrounds are strongly encouraged to apply, and the programme aims for at least 50% female participation among beneficiaries.",
      "best_fit": "Financially disadvantaged EAC nationals under 35 with a Second Class Upper Division or Distinction Bachelor's degree, seeking a two-year Master's in mathematics, engineering, informatics, science, technology or business science at a participating university in a neighbouring EAC country.",
      "notes": "The Cohort 4 window (20 August to 10 September 2026) has closed, so this record is recorded as upcoming/recurring rather than open. The official call states that Phase II commenced in October 2025 and is expected to support at least 280 students across three cohorts, which confirms further cohorts beyond Cohort 4 within this phase, but no next-cohort window is published as of 2026-10-04, so deadline_date is null. The published timeline runs past the closing date: successful students and host universities are to be informed in December 2026, and scholars would begin at the earliest available intake in line with each host university's academic calendar. Applying for university admission does not constitute an application for the scholarship; the separate scholarship application is mandatory.\nFunding period: Monthly stipend for the 2-year scholarship period; allowances as one-off payments on arrival",
      "funding_amount": "Monthly stipend EUR 380, plus EUR 200 arrival allowance, EUR 650 study-materials allowance and a one-time EUR 1,500 study and research allowance, with full tuition, return economy air ticket, medical insurance and visa or entry pass fees also covered",
