          "study_mode": "Full-time two-year Master's study at a participating university in an EAC Partner State. Successful applicants may commence at the earliest available intake, depending on each host university's admission schedule and academic calendar.",
          "research_requirement": "No separate research proposal or supervisor requirement is published. A one-time study and research allowance is included in the package, but the call does not attach a research obligation to it.",
          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "Six thematic areas only: Mathematics, Engineering, Informatics, Science, and Business Science, plus Technology. Cohort 4 offered 60 approved Master's programmes across partner universities in Kenya, Rwanda, Uganda and Tanzania, each mapped to one of these thematic areas - for example Master of Science in Applied Mathematics, Civil Engineering, Electrical and Electronics Engineering, Materials Engineering, Data Science, Information Technology, Computing and Information Systems, Public Health, Biomedical Laboratory Sciences, Food Science and Technology, Human Nutrition and Dietetics, Animal Nutrition, Agricultural Extension, Pharmacy-relevant Pharmaceutical Analysis and Quality Assurance, Data Science and Artificial Intelligence, Cyber Security and Digital Forensics, and Master of Science in Manufacturing Engineering.",
          "application_method": "Two-stage process. Part A: apply for admission to a partner university in an EAC Partner State other than the applicant's country of citizenship, declaring the intention to apply for the EAC Scholarship Programme and paying any university application fee. Part B: complete the online EAC Scholarship Application form, compile all required supporting documents into one folder named by the prescribed document codes, compress them into a single zipped PDF folder, and email that folder to eacsp@iucea.org and scholarships@adroitconsultinternational.com with the subject line '[Applicant Name] - Application for [Master's Programme] at [University] - Phase II EACSP'. Applicants may apply to more than one eligible programme or university, but each programme application must be a separate online form plus a separate email submission with its own complete document set.",
          "application_route": "Online scholarship application form at https://ee-eu.kobotoolbox.org/J4W9xHf7 (open from 20 August 2026), with documents emailed to eacsp@iucea.org and scholarships@adroitconsultinternational.com. A virtual pre-application information session was held on 28 August 2026 at 11:00 EAT.",
