          "description": "The EAC Scholarship Programme is a regional initiative of the East African Community and the Federal Republic of Germany, implemented by the Inter-University Council for East Africa. Its vision is 'Leadership to Foster Regional Integration'. Phase I, launched in 2018, supported 180 Master's students across the community. Phase II commenced in October 2025 and is expected to support at least 280 students across three cohorts from all current EAC partner states: Burundi, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Kenya, Rwanda, Somalia, South Sudan, Tanzania and Uganda. Cohort 4 offered up to 120 scholarships for two-year Master's study in mathematics, engineering, informatics, science, technology and business science, at 60 approved programmes across partner universities in Kenya, Rwanda, Uganda and Tanzania, for applicants under 35 who hold a Bachelor's degree at Second Class Upper Division or Distinction and who agree to study in a partner state other than their own.",
          "program_type": "Regional scholarship",
          "region": "Africa",
          "coverage": "Citizens of the 8 EAC Partner States (Burundi, DRC, Kenya, Rwanda, Somalia, South Sudan, Tanzania, Uganda); study at participating universities in any EAC Partner State other than the applicant's own",
