      "name": "COMSTECH Research Fellowships for Least Developed Countries (LDCs) in the OIC",
      "country": "Multiple countries",
      "region": "Africa",
      "degree_levels": "PhD",
      "funding_type": "Partially Funded",
      "program_type": "Inter-governmental research fellowship",
      "official_source": "OIC-COMSTECH (Ministerial Standing Committee on Scientific and Technological Cooperation of the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation)",
      "official_source_url": "https://comstech.org/comstech-research-fellowships-for-least-developed-countries-2/",
      "catalogue_url": "https://comstech.org/comstech-research-fellowships-for-least-developed-countries-2/",
      "official_updates_url": "https://comstech.org/comstech-research-fellowships-for-least-developed-countries-2/",
      "status": "open",
      "is_verified": true,
      "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04",
      "deadline": "No fixed deadline; the awarding body states 'Applications / Nominations are open all around the year'",
      "deadline_date": null,
      "deadline_precision": "rolling",
      "application_period": "Open all year on a rolling basis; the page records Call Status: 'The call is currently open'",
      "duration": "6 to 12 months, extendable upon recommendation of the host institution",
      "description": "COMSTECH and member institutions of its Consortium of Excellence jointly offer research fellowships to young researchers and engineers from OIC least-developed countries so they can spend six to twelve months at a relevant centre of excellence in an OIC member state. The stated purpose is to enhance the research and development capacity of promising researchers and engineers from least-developed countries who are at the beginning of their research career, and to help them build linkages for further collaboration in their fields. The field of study is natural sciences, applied sciences, engineering and technology. COMSTECH bears international low-cost airfare, and host institutions are expected to provide accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring. Applications are submitted only by email to the COMSTECH headquarters in Islamabad and are jointly reviewed by an expert committee of COMSTECH and the host institutions.",
      "eligibility_summary": "Open to young scientists and engineers who are citizens of an OIC least-developed country, or who are employed by a research institution in an OIC country, and who hold at least an M.S. or equivalent for graduate studies or a Ph.D. for post-graduate studies, or who are involved in active research. Age limits are 35 for graduate studies and 45 for post-graduate studies, with preference given to young scientists, particularly women scientists, at the beginning of their research career and those working in OIC least-developed countries.",
      "eligibility": [
        "Be a citizen of an OIC least-developed country, or be employed by a research institution in an OIC country",
        "Hold at least an M.S. or equivalent degree for graduate studies, or a Ph.D. for post-graduate studies, or be involved in active research",
        "Be aged 35 or under for graduate studies, or 45 or under for post-graduate studies",
        "Submit the completed form by email to COMSTECH headquarters with the full document set"
      ],
      "coverage": [
        "International low-cost airfare",
        "Accommodation at the host institution",
        "Subsistence support",
        "Supervision and mentoring of local training"
      ],
      "benefits": [
        "6-12 month funded research placement at a centre of excellence, extendable on host recommendation",
        "International low-cost airfare paid by COMSTECH",
        "Accommodation and subsistence provided by the host institution",
        "Supervision and mentoring during the placement",
        "Research linkages for further collaboration"
      ],
      "requirements": [
        "Match the field: natural sciences, applied sciences, engineering and technology",
        "Complete the application form and email it to khazima@comstech.org or comstech@comstech.org",
        "Send a scanned copy of a valid passport",
        "Send a CV of maximum five pages including publications",
        "Send a supporting statement from the head of the home institution",
        "Send two reference letters from senior scientists, where the head of the home institution cannot be one of the referees",
        "Send M.S./Ph.D. degrees and relevant university transcripts",
        "Apply for only one COMSTECH programme per calendar year"
