      "best_fit": "Researchers and engineers from OIC least-developed countries - the majority of which are African - who hold an M.S. or PhD (or are actively researching) in natural sciences, applied sciences, engineering or technology, are aged 35 or under (45 or under for post-doctorals), and can commit six to twelve months to a placement.",
      "notes": "This is a rolling all-year call with no published deadline. Unlike the women-only sibling fellowship, this scheme is open to all genders. The page itemises airfare, accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring but does not state that tuition or enrolment fees are paid, so tuition_coverage is recorded as false and fully_funded as false. Applications are submitted only by email, unlike the sibling schemes that use an online form, and the page requires a valid passport where the virology scheme accepts an expired copy. COMSTECH permits only one programme application per calendar year, so this cannot be combined with the other COMSTECH fellowships recorded in this shard.",
