          "description": "COMSTECH and member institutions of its Consortium of Excellence jointly offer research fellowships to young researchers and engineers in OIC countries to spend six to twelve months at a relevant centre of excellence in an OIC member state. The purpose is to enhance the research and development capacity of promising researchers and engineers, especially those from least-developed countries who are at the beginning of their research career, and to help them foster linkages for further collaboration in their fields. The field is natural sciences, applied sciences, engineering and technology. Applications and nominations are open all around the year and must be submitted by email to COMSTECH headquarters, where they are jointly reviewed by an expert committee of COMSTECH and the host institutions. COMSTECH bears international low-cost airfare, and host institutions are expected to provide accommodation, subsistence, supervision and mentoring.",
