        "Read the application requirements on the PTDF Scholarship Management Portal",
        "Access the online application form through the PTDF Scholarship Management Portal at scholarship.ptdf.gov.ng",
        "Complete the online application form and upload all required documents as legible PDFs at the sizes indicated",
        "Download the PhD proposal template from the applicant profile on the portal if applying to the PhD scheme",
        "Postgraduate applicants who meet the requirements are shortlisted and invited for oral interviews before final selection"
      ],
      "english_requirement": "Not published as a test requirement. English Language is one of the five mandatory WAEC/SSCE/NECO credits required of all applicants, which is a secondary-school pass requirement rather than a language-proficiency test.",
      "selection_notes": "The scholarship is described as highly competitive and merit-driven. Undergraduate final selection is based on grades on transcripts, which must be signed and stamped by the HOD, Exams Officer or other authorised university personnel. A selection panel assesses postgraduate applications on academic merit as evidenced by quality of degrees, full academic transcripts, other professional qualifications and relevant publications; membership of professional bodies; the viability of the study or research plan for PhD applicants; the statement of purpose for undergraduate and MSc applicants; and the research proposal for PhD applicants. Selection is based on equitable representation of the 36 states of the Federation and the Federal Capital Territory, except where a state does not have the requisite number of candidates to fill its allotted slots.",
      "best_fit": "Nigerian public-university students at 200 level, or MSc/PhD applicants with a 2:2 or better in an oil and gas, energy or management-related discipline, pursuing one of the Fund's named sponsored courses and prepared to serve the oil and gas sector and national development.",
      "notes": "The 2026/27 window closed on 5 June 2026, so this record is status upcoming/recurring rather than open, and deadline_date is null because no 2027/28 window is published. The published guidelines do not itemise what the scholarship pays for, so tuition_coverage is recorded as false and funding_amount as null rather than assumed. Part-time admission is not considered in any category, and previous PTDF scholarship holders cannot apply for the same or a lower degree category. Note also that certificate of indigeneship and a state-level quota operate together, which makes the geographic distribution of candidates a practical constraint on who can be shortlisted.",
