          "funding_duration": "Not published as a fixed award term. The scheme covers Undergraduate, Master's and PhD awards; undergraduate eligibility is anchored to study at 200 level, implying continuation through the remainder of the degree.",
          "tuition_coverage": false,
          "tuition_coverage_note": "The published application guidelines describe the scheme as a scholarship award but do not itemise what is paid - no tuition, stipend, living allowance, travel or insurance amounts are stated anywhere on the guidelines page. tuition_coverage is therefore recorded as false and funding_amount as null rather than inferred from the word 'scholarship'. This is a genuine gap in the official material, not an omission in this record.",
          "living_cost_coverage": null,
          "travel_coverage": null,
          "fully_funded": false,
          "funding_label": "Scholarship award for Undergraduate, Master's and PhD study at Nigerian public universities on published sponsored courses. The official guidelines do not itemise tuition, stipend or any other covered component, so no coverage claim is asserted. No bond or service obligation is published.",
          "benefits": [
            "Scholarship award for Undergraduate, Master's or PhD study in a Nigerian public university",
            "Eligibility for the full published list of sponsored engineering, science, environmental science, renewable energy and management courses",
            "Merit-driven selection with postgraduate oral interviews"
          ],
          "eligibility": [
            "Nigerian citizen admitted to a Nigerian public university only",
            "Possess a National Identity Number and complete NIMC verification before applying",
            "Not a previous PTDF scholarship holder applying at the same or a lower degree category",
            "Not a current beneficiary of another scholarship",
            "Study full time; part-time admission is not considered",
            "Be at 200 level and have completed first-year examinations (undergraduate)",
            "Hold a valid admission letter (undergraduate, mandatory)",
            "Hold at least 5 WAEC/SSCE/NECO credits including English Language and Mathematics, within 2 sittings (undergraduate)",
            "Hold a minimum CGPA of 2.4 on a scale of 5.0 (undergraduate)",
            "Hold a full-time admission letter into a public university (postgraduate)",
            "Hold a minimum of Second Class Lower (2:2) in an oil and gas-related field (postgraduate)",
            "Hold at least a Merit in a second-degree certificate in an oil and gas-related discipline (PhD)",
            "Possess an NYSC certificate or letter of exemption (postgraduate)",
            "Hold a valid research area relevant to the oil and gas industry (PhD)",
            "Submit a certificate of indigeneship showing state of origin and local government"
          ],
          "citizenship_residency": "Nigerian citizens only, studying at Nigerian public universities only. No residence concept applies because the award is domestic. Selection also operates on equitable representation of the 36 states of the Federation and the Federal Capital Territory, so state of origin is materially relevant, supported by a mandatory certificate of indigeneship.",
          "international_eligibility": "Not open to international applicants. The guidelines restrict the scheme to 'interested and qualified Nigerians' applying to 'Nigerian public universities only'.",
          "degree_levels": [
            "Bachelor's",
            "Master's",
            "PhD"
          ],
          "study_mode": "Full time only. The guidelines state that admission for part-time studies shall not be considered for all categories of applications.",
          "research_requirement": "PhD applicants must supply a research proposal of no more than 6 pages covering topic, introduction, literature review, research question(s), methodology, mode of data collection, expected outcome(s), novelty, relevance to the industry and appropriate references, using the template available from the applicant profile on the portal. Their research area must be relevant to the oil and gas industry. The viability of the study or research plan is an explicit selection criterion for PhD applicants.",
          "subject_or_agency_requirement": "Course of study must be on the Fund's published sponsored-courses list. Engineering: Chemical, Civil, Computer, Electrical, Electrical and Electronics, Mechanical, Metallurgical and Materials, Telecommunication, Water Resources and Environmental, Petroleum, Information Technology, Mechatronics, Production, Structural, Petroleum and Gas, System, Software, and Industrial and Production Engineering. Science: Applied Geology, Applied Geophysics, Chemistry, Computer Science, Engineering Physics, Industrial Chemistry, Mathematics, Microbiology, Physics, Physics Electronics, Electronics and Computer, Cyber Security, Statistics and Toxicology. Environmental Science: Environmental Management Technology, Industrial Design, Survey and Geo-Informatics, Remote Sensing and Geo-Science Information, and Geographic Information System. Renewable Energy: Mechanical Engineering (Energy and Power option), Renewable Energy, Renewable Energy and Environmental, and Renewable Energy Physics. Management: Business Administration, Law, Accounting, Marketing, Banking and Finance, Economics, Purchasing and Supply, Entrepreneurship and Taxation.",
          "application_method": "Obtain and verify a National Identity Number, then access the online application form from the PTDF Scholarship Management Portal at scholarship.ptdf.gov.ng. Applicants are advised to read the requirements before applying and to scan and attach all documents to the online application form in PDF format, legible and at the file sizes indicated in the portal. Undergraduate applicants upload the WAEC/SSCE/NECO result, admission letter, stamped first-year transcript, certificate of indigeneship and a 300-word personal statement. Postgraduate applicants upload the first-degree certificate or statement of results, NYSC certificate or exemption letter, WAEC/GCE/SSCE/NECO results, admission letter, certificate of indigeneship, and for MSc a personal statement of at least 1,000 words, or for PhD a second-degree certificate plus a proposal of no more than 6 pages. Postgraduate applicants who meet the requirements are shortlisted and invited for oral interviews before final selection.",
          "application_route": "PTDF Scholarship Management Portal at https://scholarship.ptdf.gov.ng, using the online application form and the portal's uploaded-document workflow. PhD proposal templates are accessed via the applicant's profile on the same portal.",
          "requirements": [
            "Obtain a National Identity Number and complete NIMC verification (charges apply) before applying",
            "Apply only to a Nigerian public university and only to a sponsored course",
            "Be a full-time student; part-time admission is not considered",
            "Undergraduates must be at 200 level with a completed first year and a valid admission letter",
            "Upload all documents as legible PDFs at the sizes indicated in the portal",
            "MSc applicants submit a statement of purpose of at least 1,000 words covering reasons for the study, relevance to the proposed study to the industry and expected impact on national development",
            "PhD applicants submit a research proposal of no more than 6 pages with the prescribed sections and use the portal template",
            "Undergraduate transcripts must be signed and stamped by the HOD, Exams Officer or other authorised university personnel",
            "Submit a certificate of indigeneship showing state of origin and local government",
            "Attend an oral interview if shortlisted as a postgraduate",
            "Do not apply if currently a beneficiary of another scholarship or a prior PTDF scholar at the same or lower level"
          ],
          "documents": [
            "National Identity Number with NIMC verification",
            "WAEC/GCE/SSCE/NECO result(s) showing at least 5 credits including English Language and Mathematics, within a maximum of 2 sittings",
            "Letter of admission into the university",
            "First-year academic transcript, signed and stamped by the HOD, Exams Officer or other authorised personnel",
            "Certificate of indigeneship showing state of origin and local government",
            "Personal statement of a minimum 300 words (undergraduate) or 1,000 words (MSc)",
            "First-degree certificate or statement of results (postgraduate)",
            "NYSC certificate or letter of exemption (postgraduate)",
            "Second-degree certificate or statement of results (PhD)",
            "PhD research proposal of no more than 6 pages using the portal template (PhD)"
          ],
          "english_requirement": null,
          "english_requirement_note": "No English language proficiency test or score is published. English Language is however one of the five mandatory WAEC/SSCE/NECO credits that all applicants must possess, so secondary-school English is an entry condition even though no upper-level language test exists.",
          "selection_criteria": [
            "Academic merit, evidenced by quality of degrees, full academic transcripts, other professional qualifications and relevant publications (postgraduate)",
            "Membership of professional bodies (postgraduate)",
            "Viability of the study or research plan (PhD only)",
            "Statement of purpose giving reasons for the study, relevance to the industry and expected impact on national development (undergraduate and MSc)",
            "Research proposal meeting the prescribed sections (PhD)",
            "Undergraduate selection based on grades on the transcript",
            "Equitable representation of the 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory, except where a state lacks enough candidates to fill its slots",
            "Oral interview for shortlisted postgraduate applicants"
          ],
          "selection_weighting": "The guidelines state that the scholarship is highly competitive and merit-driven, that undergraduate final selection is based on transcript grades, and that selection is based on equitable representation of the 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory. A selection panel assesses postgraduate applications against the listed criteria. No numeric weighting or scoring formula is published.",
          "duration": "Not published as a fixed award term; the scheme covers Undergraduate, Master's and PhD awards, with undergraduate eligibility anchored to study at 200 level",
          "award_holder_conditions": [
            "Study must be at a Nigerian public university only",
            "Study must be full time; part-time admission is not considered in any category",
            "Course must be on the published sponsored-courses list",
            "National Identity Number verification is mandatory before the application can proceed",
            "Previous PTDF scholarship holders may not apply for the same or a lower degree category",
            "Current beneficiaries of any other scholarship need not and should not apply",
            "Undergraduate transcript must be signed and stamped by authorised university personnel to be considered",
            "Postgraduate shortlistees must attend an oral interview before final selection",
            "Selection is subject to state-level quota balancing across the 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory"
          ],
          "supplements_or_initiatives": [
            "A separate PTDF Overseas Scholarship Scheme (OSS) runs alongside the In-Country Scholarship Scheme (ISS)",
            "The Fund operates with a National Identity Number verification requirement (NIMC verification charges apply)",
            "PTDF maintains an NDPR compliance function relevant to applicant data handling"
          ],
          "official_contacts": {
            "address": "PTDF House, Plot 1058 Memorial Drive, Central Business District (Cadastral Zone A), Abuja, Nigeria",
            "website": "https://ptdf.gov.ng/",
            "portal": "https://scholarship.ptdf.gov.ng",
            "support": "https://scholarship.ptdf.gov.ng/support",
            "twitter": "@PTDF_Nigeria",
            "facebook": "PTDFng"
          },
          "description": "The Petroleum Technology Development Fund is a Federal Government of Nigeria agency mandated to develop indigenous human capacity and petroleum technology to meet the needs of the oil and gas industry. For its 2026/27 cycle it invited applications from qualified Nigerians for Undergraduate, Master's and PhD scholarships at Nigerian public universities only, restricted to a published list of sponsored courses in engineering, science, environmental science, renewable energy and management. Undergraduates must be at 200 level, hold a valid admission letter, have at least five WAEC/SSCE/NECO credits including English and Mathematics, and hold a minimum CGPA of 2.4 of 5.0. MSc and PhD applicants must hold full-time admission letters, a minimum 2:2 in an oil and gas-related field, and an NYSC certificate or exemption, and PhD applicants must supply a research proposal of no more than six pages in an industry-relevant area. Applications ran from 27 April to 5 June 2026.",
          "program_type": "Government scholarship",
          "region": "Africa",
          "coverage": "Nigerian citizens studying at Nigerian public universities only, on the Fund's published sponsored-course list",
          "last_verified_date": "2026-10-04"
        },
        "applicant_utility": {
          "application_readiness_checklist": [
            "Start by registering and verifying your National Identity Number with NIMC - the portal will not let you proceed without verification and the charge applies",
            "Check your course against the Fund's published sponsored-courses list before anything else; applications are refused for courses that are not on it",
            "Confirm you are at 200 level and have completed first-year examinations, if you are an undergraduate",
            "Secure a valid admission letter from a Nigerian public university",
            "Confirm you have at least five WAEC/SSCE/NECO credits including English Language and Mathematics, within a maximum of two sittings",
            "Undergraduates: check your CGPA is at least 2.4 of 5.0",
            "Postgraduates: confirm a full-time admission letter, a 2:2 or better in an oil and gas-related field, and your NYSC certificate or exemption letter",
            "PhD applicants: download the proposal template from your profile on the portal and write a proposal of no more than six pages covering all prescribed sections",
            "Obtain your certificate of indigeneship showing state of origin and local government",
            "Get your transcript signed and stamped by the HOD, Exams Officer or other authorised personnel before uploading",
            "Write your statement of purpose: 300 words minimum if undergraduate, 1,000 words minimum if MSc",
            "Scan everything as legible PDFs at the file sizes the portal specifies, then submit through the portal",
            "Block time for an oral interview if you are shortlisted as a postgraduate"
          ],
          "common_rejection_risks": [
            "Choosing a course that is not on the published sponsored-courses list, which is an automatic bar because application is restricted to specific courses",
            "Applying before verifying your National Identity Number, which prevents the application from proceeding at all",
            "Being a current beneficiary of another scholarship, which disqualifies you",
            "Having previously held a PTDF scholarship at the same or a lower degree category",
            "Applying at a private university or for part-time study, neither of which is considered",
            "Being an undergraduate who has not completed first-year examinations or is not at 200 level",
            "Failing to produce a valid admission letter as an undergraduate",
            "Holding fewer than five credits or missing English Language or Mathematics in the WAEC/SSCE/NECO result",
            "Submitting an unstamped or unsigned transcript, which makes the grade evidence unusable",
            "Exceeding two sittings for WAEC/SSCE/NECO, or failing the sitting-order rule - undergraduates must upload the first sitting, postgraduates must upload both results preceding the first degree",
            "Missing the certificate of indigeneship, which is a mandatory upload",
            "Submitting a PhD proposal longer than six pages or omitting a prescribed section such as novelty or relevance to the industry",
            "Being in the final year of postgraduate study, which the guidelines state need not apply"
          ],
          "estimated_uncovered_costs": [
            "The official guidelines do not itemise any covered amount, so it cannot be confirmed from official sources whether tuition is paid",
            "No stipend, living allowance, travel grant or insurance benefit is published, so none should be assumed",
            "NIMC verification charges are borne by the applicant and are explicitly noted as applying",
            "Costs of the required stamped transcripts, certificate of indigeneship and any translation or certification of documents",
            "Costs of university admission charges, which are separate from the scholarship and must be paid to the institution",
            "Any examination or registration fees not covered by the award, which cannot be quantified from the published material"
          ],
