      "application_period": "Annual cycle announced by the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. For the 2026/2027 academic session the Ministry published an opening date of 15 December 2025 and a closing date of 15 February 2026.",
      "description": "The Government of Brunei Darussalam Scholarship to Foreign Students Tenable in Brunei Darussalam (BDGS) is administered by Brunei's Ministry of Foreign Affairs and covers Diploma, Undergraduate Degree and Postgraduate Master's Degree study at Universiti Brunei Darussalam, Universiti Islam Sultan Sharif Ali, Universiti Teknologi Brunei, Kolej Universiti Perguruan Ugama Seri Begawan and Politeknik Brunei. The award covers full tuition including acceptance, examination, registration and orientation fees, economy-class air travel to and from Brunei, accommodation in the university or polytechnic residential college, comprehensive insurance and monthly allowances. Applicants must be aged 25 or under for undergraduate and diploma programmes and 35 or under for postgraduate master's programmes on the first day of July of the year the course starts, and must show English proficiency.",
